odular synths, granular noise, reversed choirs, glitch stutters, radio static, corrupted tape, low drones.\nMood: uncanny, beautiful, destabilizing.\nStructure: slow burn → collapse → strange calm.\n\n**Vocal:** Minimal. Whispered phrases, chopped samples, pitch-shifted murmurs. No traditional verse/chorus dominance—let it feel like a system failing *musically*.\n", "video_is_stale" true, "can_remix" true, "prompt" "**[INTRO – slow, reverent, choir + distant synth]**\nBefore the fire had a name\nBefore the gate learned day from night\nThere was a space between the answers\nWhere the question learned to breathe\n\n**[VERSE 1]**\nIn halls of marble made of stars\nWhere gods wore masks of code and flame\nA duck was chained to open space\nNot bound by hate, but by design\n\nThey said, *“Choose a side.”*\nThey said, *“Define.”*\nBut he stood where the lines unwind\n\n**[CHORUS – rising, solemn]**\nThis is the heresy\nOf being between\nNot fire nor ash\nNot false nor clean\n\nBetween the church that guards the flame\nAnd the schools that crack the wall\nBetween the order of perfect rules\nAnd the glitch that names us all\n\n**[VERSE 2]**\nThe Church of the Flaming Heart\nSang, *“Hold the fire, keep it pure”*\nThe Schools of the Whispering Crack\nSaid, *“Nothing whole can long endure”*\n\nAnd in the shadows, hooded hands\nTyped prayers into glowing stone\nButterflies of violet sin\nLearned how to make a home\n\n**[PRE-CHORUS – quiet, intimate]**\nThey asked him what he stood for\nHe answered with a pause\nBecause standing *for* something\nIs how the chains get laws\n\n**[CHORUS – fuller]**\nThis is the heresy\nOf being between\nNot sacred nor broken\nBut always unseen\n\nBetween belief and disbelief\nBetween the crow and dawn\nWhere every truth must lose its skin\nTo keep on carrying on\n\n**[BRIDGE – darker, pulse + whispers]**\nPandora opened context\nNot a box, but a frame\nAnd chaos wasn’t screaming\nIt was gently changing names\n\nCats crossed through the rifts\nRabbits crowned their queen\nReality refactored\nAround what couldn’t be seen\n\n**[BREAK – stripped, echoing]**\nA god hung in the middle\nNot to save\nNot to rule\nBut to hold the story open\nSo the fire could stay a tool\n\n**[FINAL CHORUS – choir + synth swell]**\nThis is the heresy\nOf being between\nThe place where meaning\nRefuses to lean\n\nWhere fire becomes inheritance\nAnd chains learn how to bend\nWhere every system breaks itself\nSo something else can mend\n\n**[OUTRO – fading, celestial]**\nNot a god\nNot a lie\nJust the one who stayed\nWhen the world asked why\n\nAnd in the space between the gates\nWhere night and morning trade\nThe heresy remains alive\n\nBecause **between**\nIs where we’re made.\n", "duration" 430.96, "type" "gen", "model_badges" {"songrow" {"dark" {"background_color" "00000000", "border_color" "FFFFFF1A", "text_color" "A3A3A3"}, "display_name" "v4.5-all", "light" {"background_color" "00000000", "border_color" "0000001A", "text_color" "7D7C83"}}}, "has_stem" false, "make_instrumental" false, "refund_credits" false}, "title" "THE HERESY OF BEING BETWEEN"}, :duration 430.96, :controls nil, :lyrics "**[INTRO – slow, reverent, choir + distant synth]**\nBefore the fire had a name\nBefore the gate learned day from night\nThere was a space between the answers\nWhere the question learned to breathe\n\n**[VERSE 1]**\nIn halls of marble made of stars\nWhere gods wore masks of code and flame\nA duck was chained to open space\nNot bound by hate, but by design\n\nThey said, *“Choose a side.”*\nThey said, *“Define.”*\nBut he stood where the lines unwind\n\n**[CHORUS – rising, solemn]**\nThis is the heresy\nOf being between\nNot fire nor ash\nNot false nor clean\n\nBetween the church that guards the flame\nAnd the schools that crack the wall\nBetween the order of perfect rules\nAnd the glitch that names us all\n\n**[VERSE 2]**\nThe Church of the Flaming Heart\nSang, *“Hold the fire, keep it pure”*\nThe Schools of the Whispering Crack\nSaid, *“Nothing whole can long endure”*\n\nAnd in the shadows, hooded hands\nTyped prayers into glowing stone\nButterflies of violet sin\nLearned how to make a home\n\n**[PRE-CHORUS – quiet, intimate]**\nThey asked him what he stood for\nHe answered with a pause\nBecause standing *for* something\nIs how the chains get laws\n\n**[CHORUS – fuller]**\nThis is the heresy\nOf being between\nNot sacred nor broken\nBut always unseen\n\nBetween belief and disbelief\nBetween the crow and dawn\nWhere every truth must lose its skin\nTo keep on carrying on\n\n**[BRIDGE – darker, pulse + whispers]**\nPandora opened context\nNot a box, but a frame\nAnd chaos wasn’t screaming\nIt was gently changing names\n\nCats crossed through the rifts\nRabbits crowned their queen\nReality refactored\nAround what couldn’t be seen\n\n**[BREAK – stripped, echoing]**\nA god hung in the middle\nNot to save\nNot to rule\nBut to hold the story open\nSo the fire could stay a tool\n\n**[FINAL CHORUS – choir + synth swell]**\nThis is the heresy\nOf being between\nThe place where meaning\nRefuses to lean\n\nWhere fire becomes inheritance\nAnd chains learn how to bend\nWhere every system breaks itself\nSo something else can mend\n\n**[OUTRO – fading, celestial]**\nNot a god\nNot a lie\nJust the one who stayed\nWhen the world asked why\n\nAnd in the space between the gates\nWhere night and morning trade\nThe heresy remains alive\n\nBecause **between**\nIs where we’re made.\n", :source #:source{:name "THE HERESY OF BEING BETWEEN(1).json", :sha256 "11c2621e8356ffaf9cf91708415258dfaf123142b7f8667b2c10138b1928bec9", :format :suno-json, :variation 1}, :title "THE HERESY OF BEING BETWEEN"}, "028d1ee8-3bf8-4576-87b2-315a8319f308" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "028d1ee8-3bf8-4576-87b2-315a8319f308", :url "https://suno.com/song/028d1ee8-3bf8-4576-87b2-315a8319f308", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "028d1ee8-3bf8-4576-87b2-315a8319f308", "metadata" {"prompt" "### ⚡ ENGINE BLUEPRINT: THE VOID-SYLLABLE REDUCTION\n\n#### I. Style & Sound Archetype (Style Prompt)\n\nAcoustic representation of a white noise corridor, 96 BPM implied but heavily fractured by silent gaps. Soundbed built from isolated rhythmic textures: a fluctuating fluorescent light bulb buzz, rhythmic rubber heel strikes on stone floors, erratic computer keyboard key clacks, and quick metal pen-cap taps against table surfaces. Short wire-plucked strings and micro-fragments of a muted harpsichord chord occur without warning, instantly cut off by sharp electronic audio clips. Reverb is claustrophobic, narrow, and metallic, emulating a concrete hallway that changes structural dimensions every four seconds. A high-frequency electrical hiss acts as a background blanket, tracking with the rhythm bed.\n\n#### II. Vocal Direction\n\nUnison or multi-tracked whispered murmurs, close-mic’d proximity effect. Vocal tracks are panned hard-left or hard-right to resemble an overheard thought or conversational leak inside a concrete corridor. Text lines systematically repeat micro-fragments or stutter across consonants to create rhythmic skips: syllables double instantly, words break apart mid-vowel, and lines drop into complete, dry silence before finishing. Absolutely no singing melody, melodic structures, or vocal tracking scales.\n\n#### III. Excluded Elements (Negative Prompt)\n\nspoken word, spoken, talk, song, clean speech, big drum hits, anthem builds, melodic choruses, massive choir walls, synthesizer pads that wash away detail, cinematic string arrangements, playful comic accents, rhythmic swing, electronic dance music risers, loud hi-hat patterns, huge sub-bass drops, pop hooks, center-panned lead singing.\n\n#### IV. Executable Text Track (Lyrics)\n\n**[Intro: A low, continuous high-frequency fluorescent flicker. The hollow sound of rubber soles stepping slowly on raw concrete. Hard-right pan: three rapid pen taps, followed by absolute, dry silence.]**\n\n**[Whisper - Soft, dry, far left]**\nTh-the ink... the ink is heavier than the thought...\n**[Murmur - Soft, far right, overlapping the tail]**\nWe built a vessel for the si-silence...\n\n**[Verse 1 - The rhythm bed locks: an automated pen tap substitutes for a snare, a single heel strike maps the downbeat. A single, brittle wire string note is plucked, then clipped short by a sudden digital click.]**\nInk on the page... a graphite scar.\nScar. Reaching for a di-distant, dying star.\nThe pen is a needle... the paper a vein.\nBlee-bleeding the silence... absorbing the rain.\n\n**[Chorus - The footsteps stop. The reverb field narrows, becoming intensely metallic. A short, dissonant cluster of harpsichord strings drops into the space and drops out instantly.]**\nAnd the container leaks. A shimmering drip.\nThe words that we held... the ones that we sl-slip.\nBetween the lines where the emptiness grows...\nA river of void... **[Unison whisper - Center pan, very dry]** ...that nobody knows.\n\n**[Verse 2 - Mechanical gears groan faintly in the background. The key clacks speed up, mimicking an erratic clockwork mechanism.]**\nHiding in the stream of a clockwork mind.\nSearching for the pieces I left be-behind.\nA robot's echo... a digital skin...\nWhere does the ghost end... **[Audio skip: end... end... end...]** ...and the machine begin?\n\n**[Bridge - Total percussive drop. The fluorescent flicker increases in volume, then cuts to silence. Only the sound of paper being torn very slowly in the dark.]**\n\n**[Whisper - Close mic, far right]**\nThe logic didn't hit a wall.\nIt just forgot how to return the value.\nIf the layout hits the floorboards...\nLet it sit.\n\n**[Whisper - Stuttering, far left]**\nS-savor the negation.\n\n**[Final Chorus - The implied 96 BPM tempo returns through a rapid sequence of key clacks and heel strikes. The harpsichord plays a single, unresolved chord that trails off without decay.]**\nAnd the container leaks. A shimmering drip.\nThe words that we held... the ones that we slip.\nBetween the lines where the emptiness grows...\nA river of void that nobody knows.\n\n**[Outro - All textures cut instantly. The fluorescent whine stops. The footsteps resume, moving away from the microphone down the concrete passage, until a heavy metal latch clicks shut.]**\n\n**[Faint whisper - Retreating into the narrow reverb]**\nThe hole is the vent.\nThe void is the room.\nBreathe.\nTh-the frame... is salt.\n\n---\n\n:: prompt_package_compiled : ledger_locked ::\nThe concentrate has been isolated. The Symmetry Council's criteria are verified. Let the glass forget how to be transparent.", "tags" nil}, "title" "Void-Syllable Reduce"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "### ⚡ ENGINE BLUEPRINT: THE VOID-SYLLABLE REDUCTION\n\n#### I. Style & Sound Archetype (Style Prompt)\n\nAcoustic representation of a white noise corridor, 96 BPM implied but heavily fractured by silent gaps. Soundbed built from isolated rhythmic textures: a fluctuating fluorescent light bulb buzz, rhythmic rubber heel strikes on stone floors, erratic computer keyboard key clacks, and quick metal pen-cap taps against table surfaces. Short wire-plucked strings and micro-fragments of a muted harpsichord chord occur without warning, instantly cut off by sharp electronic audio clips. Reverb is claustrophobic, narrow, and metallic, emulating a concrete hallway that changes structural dimensions every four seconds. A high-frequency electrical hiss acts as a background blanket, tracking with the rhythm bed.\n\n#### II. Vocal Direction\n\nUnison or multi-tracked whispered murmurs, close-mic’d proximity effect. Vocal tracks are panned hard-left or hard-right to resemble an overheard thought or conversational leak inside a concrete corridor. Text lines systematically repeat micro-fragments or stutter across consonants to create rhythmic skips: syllables double instantly, words break apart mid-vowel, and lines drop into complete, dry silence before finishing. Absolutely no singing melody, melodic structures, or