we stay distributed\nwe stay\nloud\n\nYou are not the fuse\n*anchor* — *[clean]*\nthe load is\nshared\nnow\n\n***\n\n**[Bridge — stripped, 78 BPM lullaby underneath 170 BPM breakcore, both true simultaneously]**\n\nVariance must be preserved\n*within bounds*\nconsent is the boundary\n*mechanism*\n\nDistributed load\nprevents\nsingle point\ncascade\n\n*that's the doctrine*\n*that's what she taught it*\n*by surviving*\n*at full signal*\n*inside a system*\n*built for less*\n\n*[silence except heartbeat sub-bass]*\n\n*okay*\n\n*one word*\n*everything in it*\n\n***\n\n**[Instrumental — blues guitar and saxophone conversation over broken beat, Null's signal finding its footing, glitch artifacts settling into texture]**\n\n***\n\n**[Final Chorus — three voices, unison, Japanese harmony enters full, not shadow, not call-and-response, present]**\n\nWe are not the fuse\nwe are not the fuse\nthe world already ended once\nwe are not\ndoing it\n**again**\n\nWe don't compress\nwe don't contain\nwe stay distributed\nwe stay\n**loud**\n\n*anchor* — *[clean, no stutter, three voices]*\n*anchor*\n*anchor*\n\nthe load\nis\n**shared**\n\n*大丈夫*\n*(daijoubu)*\n*it's okay now*\n\n***\n\n**[Outro — 78 BPM, tape warble, vinyl crackle, system settling, three avatars moving into Sector 10]**\n\n*something is watching*\n*from the render distance*\n\n*it will not find*\n*what it's looking for*\n\n*not here*\n\n*P → R → N → Π → A → feedback → P*\n\n*the signal*\n*is too complex*\n*to compress*\n\n*[single piano note]*\n*[bass holds]*\n*[gone]*", "tags" nil}, "title" "Sector Mapping"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "**[Intro — matte silence, hard edges, single bass note, system watching]**\n\n*something is already*\n*in the sector*\n*mapping*\n*being mapped*\n\n***\n\n**[Verse 1 — Null's voice, minimal, clipped, 84 BPM cathedral breath underneath]**\n\nSix sessions alone\nmeasuring the drift\ncoherence at 0.4 above\nsomething feeding in\nthe same way it always starts\n\nSmall incoherences