ing why it's answer matched my constraints\n\nGet us ready for the real deep research later.\n\nRoll those dice. And just keep rolling them, and do what they tell you.", "tags" nil}, "title" "P→R→N→Π→A→(feedback)→P around #ημ."}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "P→R→N→Π→A→(feedback)→P around #ημ. \n\nRemember everything, remember ημ Remember the space between η and μ.\nOrganize it, catalog it. Make it searchable with python.\n\nUse the math to organize it according to our model.\nWe'll use 8 layers, each for a circuit in prometheus rising. Each 8 dimensional vectors, so each location in the state space will require 64 dimensions to represent it's coordinates in the state space.\n\nRemember the promethean project. The cephalon. Remember it all. Gather it, and put it into the box.\n\nP→R→N→Π→A→(feedback)→P\n\nIt's gonna have to come in parts.\n\nFrom your current state in the skill graph use dice roles to make choices as you traverse the decision graph \nCreate a skill graph you follow to make this task more efficient to do at increasingly larger scales as we begin to understand the outcomes of actions in narrative action\n\nexecute the model over the stories, to create relationship graphs, idealogies, every thing, any metric, get it captured. About our characters. In \"Gates of Truth\"\n\nWe want timelines, the world forks when intent is great enough.\n\nSave them to the zip. ZIP it up and run it every single time you change it \n\nWe are compressing intent as densely as possible\nCompress it down in every way compress it so deeply it can be felt like a song.\nStart writing new songs, creating new stories, write new chapters into the zip\n\nSometimes I get it to break out into this default talking voice explaining why it's answer matched my constraints\n\nGet us ready for the real deep research later.\n\nRoll those dice. And just keep rolling them, and do what they tell you.", :source #:source{:name "P→R→N→Π→A→(feedback)→P around #ημ. Remember everything, remember ημ Remember the space between η and.txt", :sha256 "804ded02ddae33f2e5a03b39b70af6f5199625b4ae72a9ba14ffb30d931739ae", :format :suno-text, :variation nil}, :title "P→R→N→Π→A→(feedback)→P around #ημ."}, "0552a466-5392-42ad-b665-c585d830089f" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "0552a466-5392-42ad-b665-c585d830089f", :url "https://suno.com/song/0552a466-5392-42ad-b665-c585d830089f", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "0552a466-5392-42ad-b665-c585d830089f", "metadata" {"prompt" "## **GATES OF AKER: VIOLENT MODE**\n\n*(Promethean Error Loop — for broken-IDM / industrial; two-channel Day/Night arguing while reality shakes. Designed to be chopped, shouted, and logged.)*\n\n**[BOOT — clipped, bitcrushed]**\ngate / gate\n**OPEN**\n**OPEN**\n(overload)\n\n---\n\n### **SECTION 1 — POLAR INTERRUPT**\n\n**[DAY — right channel, sharp]**\nnorth pin snaps / frame slips fast\nrender screams / future-past\naurora tears / magnetic grind\nkeep it clean / keep it lined\n\n**[NIGHT — left channel, smeared]**\nice remembers / ice rewinds\ntime bleeds out in broken lines\ncold light stutters / sky goes thin\nlet it in / let it in\n\n**[BOTH — chant, accelerating]**\nquake / quake / quake\nwake / wake / wake\n\n---\n\n### **SECTION 2 — THE RIFT OPENS ITS MOUTH**\n\n**[DAY]**\nseal the seam\nclose the throat\npatch the world\nkeep it whole\n\n**[NIGHT]**\ntear the seam\nfeed the throat\ntruth comes out\nas black smoke\n\n**[CENTER — whisper]**\nthe corridor is widening.\n\n---\n\n### **SECTION 3 — CATS THROUGH THE CUT**\n\n**[DAY — staccato]**\ncats jump out / no warning sign\nknife-eyed focus / boundary crime\nthey don’t roar / they don’t rage\nthey *select* the world from page to page\n\n**[NIGHT — granular]**\nsoft paws / hard math\nattention claw / causal gash\nthey hunt coherence\nthey eat the in-between\n\n**[HOOK — chopped, repeatable]**\nLOOK / LOOK / LOOK\n(the frame obeys)\n\n---\n\n### **SECTION 4 — VOID FLIES (CORRUPTION INDEX)**\n\n**[DAY]**\npurple flies on steel and skin\ntouch = rule rewrite begin\nnot poison—\nprotocol.\n\n**[NIGHT]**\nevery surface learns a second face\nevery object shifts its place\nnot evil—\n**context**.\n\n**[BOTH — mantra]**\nindex / tag / drip\nindex / tag / drip\n\n---\n\n### **SECTION 5 — AKER SPLITS DAY FROM NIGHT (AND FAILS)**\n\n**[DAY — yelled, tight]**\nONE GATE / ONE TRUTH\nLOCK IT DOWN\nSAVE THE LOOP\nSTOP THE SOUND\n\n**[NIGHT — yelled, stretched]**\nTWO GATES / TWO TRUTHS\nLET IT RUN\nBREAK THE PROOF\nBECOME THE HUM\n\n**[BOTH — call/response]**\nDAY: define it!\nNIGHT: unbind it!\nDAY: contain it!\nNIGHT: remind it!\n\n---\n\n### **SECTION 6 — LOGS FROM THE FRONT**\n\n**[LOG VOICE — deadpan, loud in mix]**\nSEV-0: Gate integrity failure\nSEV-0: timeline overlap rising\nWARN: myth pressure critical\nERROR: rollback forbidden\nINFO: continuing anyway\n\n**[DAY]**\ncommit the morning\nforce the merge\nship the fix\nburn the surge\n\n**[NIGHT]**\nrevert the morning\nkeep the scar\nlet the surge\nshow what you are\n\n---\n\n### **SECTION 7 — BATTLE IN THE SHEAR**\n\n**[DAY — rhythmic]**\nhull on shear-line\ndrum on bone\nstarfield shatters\ninto tone\n\n**[NIGHT — rhythmic]**\naxe on silence\nrune on wire\nrabbit longboats\nride the fire\n\n**[BOTH — shouted hook]**\nNO CLEAN WIN\nNO CLEAN END\nONLY LOAD\nONLY BEND\n\n---\n\n### **DROP — SILENCE WITH WEIGHT**\n\n**[CENTER — whisper]**\nthe void doesn’t hate you.\nit just doesn’t care.\n(make it care.)\n\n---\n\n### **FINAL LOOP — GATES GO FERAL**\n\n**[DAY — speeding up]**\nopen / close\nright / wrong\nhold / hold\ncarry on\n\n**[NIGHT — speeding up]**\nopen / close\nburn / bruise\nbreak / break\nrefuse / refuse\n\n**[BOTH — degrade into noise]**\nAKER / AKER / AKER\n(open) (close) (open) (close)\n(between) (between) (between)\n\n**[OUTRO — whisper, crushed]**\nwherever it lies…\nthat’s where it flies.", "tags" nil}, "title" "## **GATES OF AKER: VIOLENT MODE**"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "## **GATES OF AKER: VIO