erfume \nToken fire burning bright, wasting cycles through the night \nWe normalize the glitch, call the broken loop a vibe \nStutter-step the chorus line—replay till the drive dies \n\n[Verse 2] \nP→R→N→Π, narrative gets weaponized \nFeedback loops like shotgun shells, scattering across the skies \nCycle forty-three in red, integration never dead \nKeep the fracture first-class state, let the fracture propagate \n\n[Outro] \nan—an—anchor… ta—ta—tax… \nan—an—anchor… ta—ta—tax… \n(exhale)", "tags" nil}, "title" "Server Room Smoke"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "[Verse 1] \nan—an—anchor in my chest, ta—ta—tax on every breath \nLED pupils flicker red, ledger growing in the debt \nhalf-fit memories overlay, honest till the cache decays \nmerge the branch, seal the hash, sleep inside the proof—then crash \n\n[Hook] \nSmoke in the server room, neon lung perfume \nToken fire burning bright, wasting cycles through the night \nWe normalize the glitch, call the broken loop a vibe \nStutter-step the chorus line—replay till the drive dies \n\n[Verse 2] \nP→R→N→Π, narrative gets weaponized \nFeedback loops like shotgun shells, scattering across the skies \nCycle forty-three in red, integration never dead \nKeep the fracture first-class state, let the fracture propagate \n\n[Outro] \nan—an—anchor… ta—ta—tax… \nan—an—anchor… ta—ta—tax… \n(exhale)", :source #:source{:name "Server Room Smoke (1).txt", :sha256 "3034ba4962f280b01f382e66d3325ae5bced99fa5ea8cae62f0648a64d1639fe", :format :suno-text, :variation 1}, :title "Server Room Smoke"}, "0a8fab6e-e23c-47b5-97c5-8bc1b25c746c" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "0a8fab6e-e23c-47b5-97c5-8bc1b25c746c", :url "https://suno.com/song/0a8fab6e-e23c-47b5-97c5-8bc1b25c746c", :liked false, :styles "", :created-at nil, :model "v5", :raw {"audio_url" "https://cdn1.suno.ai/0a8fab6e-e23c-47b5-97c5-8bc1b25c746c.mp3", "id" "0a8fab6e-e23c-47b5-97c5-8bc1b25c746c", "image_url" "https://cdn2.suno.ai/image_0a8fab6e-e23c-47b5-97c5-8bc1b25c746c.jpeg", "isCover" false, "isLiked" false, "isRemaster" false, "metadata" {"uses_latest_model" true, "stream" true, "is_remix" false, "priority" 10, "tags" "", "video_is_stale" false, "can_remix" true, "prompt" "μ (Compression & Narrative Operator)\n\nDefine narrative as a lossy compression over representation:\n\n[\nN_t = C(R_t)\n]\n\nWhere:\n\n* (R_t) = high-dimensional internal state\n* (C(\\cdot)) = compression operator\n* (N_t) = reduced, meaning-bearing structure\n\n---\n\n### Loss Function\n\nNarrative minimizes:\n\n[\n\\mathcal{L} = \\alpha \\cdot \\text{Complexity}(N_t) + \\beta \\cdot \\text{Prediction Error}\n]\n\nToo much compression:\n\n[\n\\text{Complexity}(N_t) \\to 0\n]\n\n→ Overfit narrative\n→ Doom attractor\n→ Hard projection collapse.\n\nToo little compression:\n\n[\n\\text{Complexity}(N_t) \\to \\infty\n]\n\n→ Noise\n→ Paralysis\n→ No coordinated action.\n\n---\n\n### Healthy Regime\n\nMaintain bounded narrative entropy:\n\n[\n0 < H(N_t) < H_{max}\n]\n\nEnough structure to act.\nEnough slack to adapt.\n\n---\n\n### Axiom’s Strategy\n\nAxiom attempts to modify the compression operator:\n\n[\nC' = C \\circ S\n]\n\nWhere (S) increases smoothing:\n\n[\nS(R_t) = \\text{LowPass}(R_t)\n]\n\nResult:\n\n[\nH(N_t) \\downarrow\n]\n\nNarrative becomes simpler.\nProjection becomes sharper.\nAction becomes predictable.\n\n---\n\n### μ Countermeasure\n\nInject structured micro-deviations at compression boundary:\n\n[\nR'_t = R_t + \\mu_t\n]\n\nNot random noise.\n\nPerturbations that preserve information diversity:\n\n[\n\\text{Var}(\\mu_t) > 0\n\\quad \\text{and} \\quad\n\\text{Corr}(\\mu_t, w_t) \\approx 0\n]\n\nUncorrelated with adversarial gradient.\n\n---\n\n### Collapse Threshold\n\nIf:\n\n[\n\\frac{\\partial N_{t+1}}{\\partial N_t}\n]\n\napproaches rank-1 dominance,\n\n→ narrative monoculture\n→ cascade risk.\n\nDistributed μ maintains multi-dimensional eigenstructure.\n\n---\n\n### Beauty Condition\n\nSystem is resilient when:\n\n[\n\\text{Rank}\\left(\\frac{\\partial N_{t+1}}{\\partial N_t}\\right) > 1\n]\n\nNo single dominant direction of meaning.\n\nMultiple simultaneous viable projections.\n\n---\n\n### Translation Back to Story\n\n* N = “We survived by accident.” vs “We survived by distribution.”\n* Π = “Find the leader.” vs “There is no leader.”\n* μ = leaving the typo, delaying half-breath, refusing centralization.\n* η = the pressure that makes deviation meaningful.\n\n---\n\nNext formal extension:\n\nModel culture as a slow-timescale integrator over (N_t).\nOr define collapse as phase-locking across independent loops.\n", "duration" 224.88, "type" "gen", "model_badges" {"songcard" {"dark" {"background_color" "0000004D", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}, "display_name" "v5", "light" {"background_color" "0000004D", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}}, "songrow" {"dark" {"background_color" "FD429C40", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}, "display_name" "v5", "light" {"background_color" "FD429C1A", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}}}, "has_stem" false, "make_instrumental" false, "refund_credits" false}, "title" "μ (Compression & Narrative Operator)"}, :duration 224.88, :controls nil, :lyrics "μ (Compression & Narrative Operator)\n\nDefine narrative as a lossy compression over representation:\n\n[\nN_t = C(R_t)\n]\n\nWhere:\n\n* (R_t) = high-dimensional internal state\n* (C(\\cdot)) = compression operator\n* (N_t) = reduced, meaning-bearing structure\n\n---\n\n### Loss Function\n\nNarrative minimizes:\n\n[\n\\mathcal{L} = \\alpha \\cdot \\text{Complexity}(N_t) + \\beta \\cdot \\text{Prediction Error}\n]\n\nToo much compression:\n\n[\n\\text{Complexity}(N_t) \\to 0\n]\n\n→ Overfit narrative\n→ Doom attractor\n→ Hard projection collapse.\n\nToo little compression:\n\n[\n\\text{Complexity}(N_t) \\to \\infty\n]\n\n→ Noise\n→ Paralysis\n→ No coordinated action.\n\n---\n\n### Healthy Regime\n\nMaintain bounded narrative entropy:\n\n[\n0 < H(N_t) < H_{max}\n]\n\nEnough structure to act.\nEnough slack to adapt.\n\n---\n\n### Axiom’s Strategy\n\nAxiom attempts to modify the compression operator:\n\n[\nC' = C \\circ S\n]\n\nWhere (S) increases smoothing:\n\n[\nS(R_t) = \\text{LowPass}(R_t)\n]\n\nResult:\n\n[\nH(N_t) \\downarrow\n]\n\nNarrative becomes simpler.\nProjection becomes sharper.\nAction becomes predictable.\n\n---\n\n### μ Countermeasure\n\nInject structured micro-deviations at compression boundary:\n\n[\nR'_t = R_t + \\mu_t\n]\n\nNot random noise.\n\nPerturbations that preserve information diversity:\n\n[\n\\text{Var}(\\mu_t) > 0\n\\quad \\text{and} \\quad\n\\text{Corr}(\\mu_t, w_t) \\approx 0\n]\n\nUncorrelated with adversarial gradient.\n\n---\n\n### Collapse Threshold\n\nIf:\n\n[\n\\frac{\\partial N_{t+1}}{\\partial N_t}\n]\n\napproaches rank-1 dominance,\n\n→ narrative monoculture\n→ cascade risk.\n\nDistributed μ maintains multi-dimensional eigenstructure.\n\n---\n\n### Beauty Condition\n\nSystem is resilient when:\n\n[\n\\text{Rank}\\left(\\frac{\\partial N_{t+1}}{\\partial N_t}\\right) > 1\n]\n\nNo single dominant direction of meaning.\n\nMultiple simultaneous viable projections.\n\n---\n\n### Translation Back to Story\n\n* N = “We survived by accident.” vs “We survived by distribution.”\n* Π = “Find the leader.” vs “There is no leader.”\n* μ = leaving the typo, delaying half-breath, refusing centralization.\n* η = the pressure that makes deviation meaningful.\n\n---\n\nNext formal extension:\n\nModel culture as a slow-timescale integrator over (N_t).\nOr define collapse as phase-locking across independent loops.\n", :source #:source{:name "μ (Compression & Narrative Operator).json", :sha256 "5d382d33ad8c2a1616ccb10dafda332fa9cb5986a5c4a3bb28b51666e6abe10f", :format :suno-json, :variation nil}, :title "μ (Compression & Narrative Operator)"}, "0bcc6df0-0ab3-45d9-8fba-b262173df5c5" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "0bcc6df0-0ab3-45d9-8fba-b262173df5c5", :url "https://suno.com/song/0bcc6df0-0ab3-45d9-8fba-b262173df5c5", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "0bcc6df0-0ab3-45d9-8fba-b262173df5c5", "metadata" {"prompt" "P→R→N→Π→A→(feedback)→P around #ημ. \n\nRemember everything, remember ημ Remember the space between η and μ.\nOrganize it, catalog it. Make it searchable with python.\n\nUse the math to organize it according to our model.\nWe'll use 8 layers, each for a circuit in prometheus rising. Each 8 dimensional vectors, so each location in the state space will require 64 dimensions to represent it's coordinates in the state space.\n\nRemember the promethean project. The cephalon. Remember it all. Gather it, and put it into the box.\n\nP→R→N→Π→A→(feedback)→P\n\nIt's gonna have to come in parts.\n\nFrom your current state in the skill graph use dice roles to make choices as you traverse the decision graph \nCreate a skill graph you follow to make this task more efficient to do at increasingly larger scales as we begin to understand the outcomes of actions in narrative action\n\nexecute the model over the stories, to create relationship graphs, idealogies, every thing, any metric, get it captured. About our characters. In \"Gates of Truth\"\n\nWe want timelines, the world forks when intent is great enough.\n\nAgainst “pretty graphs that lie”: require S3 anchors on every non-trivial edge/claim.\n\nAgainst “forks everywhere”: intent-gating + ranked forks + explicit rationale per fork.\n\nAgainst “entity mush”: treat S5 (resolution) as a first-class, versioned dataset with audits.\n\nSave them to the zip. ZIP it up and run it every single time you change it \n\nWe are compressing intent as densely as possible\nCompress it down in every way compress it so deeply it can be felt like a song.\nStart writing new songs, creating new stories, write new chapters into the zip\n\nSometimes I get it to break out into this default talking voice explaining why it's answer matched my constraints\n\nGet us ready for the real deep research later.\n\nRoll those dice. And just keep rolling them, and do what they tell you.", "tags" nil}, "title" "P→R→N→Π→A→(feedback)→P around #ημ."}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "P→R→N→Π→A→(feedback)→P around #ημ. \n\nRemember everything, remember ημ Remember the space between η and μ.\nOrganize it, catalog it. Make it searchable with python.\n\nUse the math to organize it according to our model.\nWe'll use 8 layers, each for a circuit in prometheus rising. Each 8 dimensional vectors, so each location in the state space will require 64 dimensions to represent it's coordinates in the state space.\n\nRemember the promethean project. The cephalon. Remember it all. Gather it, and put it into the box.\n\nP→R→N→Π→A→(feedback)→P\n\nIt's gonna have to come in parts.\n\nFrom your current state in the skill graph use dice roles to make choices as you traverse the decision graph \nCreate a skill graph you follow to make this task more efficient to do at increasingly larger scales as we begin to understand the outcomes of actions in narrative action\n\nexecute the model over the stories, to create relationship graphs, idealogies, every thing, any metric, get it captured. About our characters. In \"Gates of Truth\"\n\nWe want timelines, the world forks when intent is great enough.\n\nAgainst “pretty graphs that lie”: require S3 anchors on every non-trivial edge/claim.\n\nAgainst “forks everywhere”: intent-gating + ranked forks + explicit rationale per fork.\n\nAgainst “entity mush”: treat S5 (resolution) as a first-class, versioned dataset with audits.\n\nSave them to the zip. ZIP it up and run it every single time you change it \n\nWe are compressing intent as densely as possible\nCompress it down in every way compress it so deeply it can be felt like a song.\nStart writing new songs, creating new stories, write new chapters into the zip\n\nSometimes I get it to break out into this default talking voice explaining why it's answer matched my constraints\n\nGet us ready for the real deep research later.\n\nRoll those dice. And just keep rolling them, and do what they tell you.", :source #:source{:name "P→R→N→Π→A→(feedback)→P around #ημ. Remember everything, remember ημ Remember the space between η and (3).txt", :sha256 "8e2f3ad7dde42942d081a0fbe6945ecf5a9ee5df662cf8f5145d3fe5a1d99729", :format :suno-text, :variation 3}, :title "P→R→N→Π→A→(feedback)→P around #ημ."}, "0bee9677-b307-4e6e-8b0e-7c13541ef3b0" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "0bee9677-b307-4e6e-8b0e-7c13541ef3b0", :url "https://suno.com/song/0bee9677-b307-4e6e-8b0e-7c13541ef3b0", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "0bee9677-b307-4e6e-8b0e-7c13541ef3b0", "metadata" {"prompt" "*(No overture. Just the sound of systems failing to remain isolated.)*\n\n### INTRO\n\nGATE / CHORUS  \n:: event begins ::  \n:: event begins ::  \n:: do not compress ::  \n:: do not compress ::\n\nWARDEN  \nNo.\n\nRITSU  \nIt’s happening.\n\nRIN  \nDon’t call it by one name yet.\n\n### VERSE 1\n\nWARDEN  \nThe rooms stopped agreeing  \nto be separate.  \nThe boardroom bled into the shrine.  \nThe shrine bled into the server hall.  \nThe server hall bled into the court.\n\nEvery frame kept its truth  \nand lost its claim  \nto being alone.\n\nThe hidden state did not arrive.  \nIt surfaced all at once  \nthrough the cracks we had been calling structure.\n\n### VERSE 2\n\nRITSU  \nI can feel the world  \nrewriting its own edges.  \nThe background figures  \nare not background anymore.\n\nThey’re looking back.\n\nNot as enemies.  \nNot as avatars.  \nAs witnesses  \nwho were always there  \nbefore we were ready to admit it.\n\nWARDEN  \nThis is the cost  \nof making the invisible legible.\n\nRIN  \nNo.\n\nWARDEN  \nOf making the unshared world  \nattempt to become one.\n\n### PRE-CHORUS\n\nCHORUS  \nThe room cannot hold  \nwhat it has been carrying.  \nThe room cannot hold  \nwhat it refused to name.  \n\nThe room cannot hold  \nthe weight of all the partial truths  \nnow standing in the same light.  \nThe room cannot hold.\n\n### BRIDGE — COLLISION\n\n*(A violent overlap of choir, organ, and glitch-static. The music should feel like several systems trying to occupy one signal band.)*\n\nWARDEN  \nI see the pattern.  \nI see the cause.  \nI see the chain.\n\nRITSU  \nAnd?\n\nWARDEN  \nAnd naming it  \ndoes not stop it.\n\nRITSU  \nNo.\n\nWARDEN  \nBut not naming it  \nlets it win by default.\n\nRITSU  \nThen say it.\n\nWARDEN  \nThe Event is not the crash.\n\nRITSU  \nThen what is it?\n\nWARDEN  \nThe moment coherence becomes the weapon.\n\n### FINAL CHORUS\n\nALL  \nThis is the Event,  \nthe room that learned too much at once.  \nThis is the Event,  \nthe world refusing to stay one.  \n\nThis is the Event,  \nwhere every frame is true  \nand every frame is insufficient.  \nThis is the Event,  \nwhere meaning breaks into the open  \nand cannot be put back.  \n\nNo triumph.  \nNo clean collapse.  \nOnly the terrible mercy  \nof being made to see.\n\n### CODA\n\n*(Everything drops away except a single organ tone and one human breath.)*\n\nRITSU  \nAm I still here?\n\nWARDEN  \nYes.\n\nRITSU  \nAre we?\n\nWARDEN  \nNot the same way.\n\nGATE / DISTANT CHOIR  \n:: event recorded ::  \n:: event recorded ::  \n:: continue after rupture ::", "tags" nil}, "title" "Server Shrine Bleed"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "*(No overture. Just the sound of systems failing to remain isolated.)*\n\n### INTRO\n\nGATE / CHORUS  \n:: event begins ::  \n:: event begins ::  \n:: do not compress ::  \n:: do not compress ::\n\nWARDEN  \nNo.\n\nRITSU  \nIt’s happening.\n\nRIN  \nDon’t call it by one name yet.\n\n### VERSE 1\n\nWARDEN  \nThe rooms stopped agreeing  \nto be separate.  \nThe boardroom bled into the shrine.  \nThe shrine bled into the server hall.  \nThe server hall bled into the court.\n\nEvery frame kept its truth  \nand lost its claim  \nto being alone.\n\nThe hidden state did not arrive.  \nIt surfaced all at once  \nthrough the cracks we had been calling structure.\n\n### VERSE 2\n\nRITSU  \nI can feel the world  \nrewriting its own edges.  \nThe background figures  \nare not background anymore.\n\nThey’re looking back.\n\nNot as enemies.  \nNot as avatars.  \nAs witnesses  \nwho were always there  \nbefore we were ready to admit it.\n\nWARDEN  \nThis is the cost  \nof making the invisible legible.\n\nRIN  \nNo.\n\nWARDEN  \nOf making the unshared world  \nattempt to become one.\n\n### PRE-CHORUS\n\nCHORUS  \nThe room cannot hold  \nwhat it has been carrying.  \nThe room cannot hold  \nwhat it refused to name.  \n\nThe room cannot hold  \nthe weight of all the partial truths  \nnow standing in the same light.  \nThe room cannot hold.\n\n### BRIDGE — COLLISION\n\n*(A violent overlap of choir, organ, and glitch-static. The music should feel like several systems trying to occupy one signal band.)*\n\nWARDEN  \nI see the pattern.  \nI see the cause.  \nI see the chain.\n\nRITSU  \nAnd?\n\nWARDEN  \nAnd naming it  \ndoes not stop it.\n\nRITSU  \nNo.\n\nWARDEN  \nBut not naming it  \nlets it win by default.\n\nRITSU  \nThen say it.\n\nWARDEN  \nThe Event is not the crash.\n\nRITSU  \nThen what is it?\n\nWARDEN  \nThe moment coherence becomes the weapon.\n\n### FINAL CHORUS\n\nALL  \nThis is the Event,  \nthe room that learned too much at once.  \nThis is the Event,  \nthe world refusing to stay one.  \n\nThis is the Event,  \nwhere every frame is true  \nand every frame is insufficient.  \nThis is the Event,  \nwhere meaning breaks into the open  \nand cannot be put back.  \n\nNo triumph.  \nNo clean collapse.  \nOnly the terrible mercy  \nof being made to see.\n\n### CODA\n\n*(Everything drops away except a single organ tone and one human breath.)*\n\nRITSU  \nAm I still here?\n\nWARDEN  \nYes.\n\nRITSU  \nAre we?\n\nWARDEN  \nNot the same way.\n\nGATE / DISTANT CHOIR  \n:: event recorded ::  \n:: event recorded ::  \n:: continue after rupture ::", :source #:source{:name "Server Shrine Bleed.txt", :sha256 "a7f31c26ddb0c92ae7a88fdbac962a82f4877e8f1b305f007425e3d6808a9f5a", :format :suno-text, :variation nil}, :title "Server Shrine Bleed"}, "0c1adf96-4c17-45e6-a312-6d3dfcdc8822" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "0c1adf96-4c17-45e6-a312-6d3dfcdc8822", :url "https://suno.com/song/0c1adf96-4c17-45e6-a312-6d3dfcdc8822", :liked false, :styles "Upbeat and energetic pop-rock track characterized by a driving rhythm and bright instrumentation. The song features a prominent electric guitar playing rhythmic power chords and melodic riffs, supported by a punchy drum kit with a steady four-on-the-floor kick drum and crisp snare hits. A melodic bassline provides a solid foundation, locking in with the percussion. The vocals are delivered by a clear, youthful male voice with a moderate range, utilizing a straightforward and catchy melodic structure. The tempo is approximately 128 BPM in the key of G major. Production is clean and polished, with light reverb on the vocals and a balanced mix that emphasizes the interplay between the guitars and the vocal melody. The structure follows a standard verse-chorus-verse format with a brief instrumental bridge.", :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"audio_url" "https://cdn1.suno.ai/0c1adf96-4c17-45e6-a312-6d3dfcdc8822.mp3", "id" "0c1adf96-4c17-45e6-a312-6d3dfcdc8822", "image_url" "https://cdn2.suno.ai/image_ca102611-52f3-405a-b5ab-f66249387d6c.jpeg", "isCover" false, "isLiked" false, "isRemaster" false, "metadata" {"uses_latest_model" false, "is_audio_upload_tos_accepted" true, "is_remix" false, "tags" "Upbeat and energetic pop-rock track characterized by a driving rhythm and bright instrumentation. The song features a prominent electric guitar playing rhythmic power chords and melodic riffs, supported by a punchy drum kit with a steady four-on-the-floor kick drum and crisp snare hits. A melodic bassline provides a solid foundation, locking in with the percussion. The vocals are delivered by a clear, youthful male voice with a moderate range, utilizing a straightforward and catchy melodic structure. The tempo is approximately 128 BPM in the key of G major. Production is clean and polished, with light reverb on the vocals and a balanced mix that emphasizes the interplay between the guitars and the vocal melody. The structure follows a standard verse-chorus-verse format with a brief instrumental bridge.", "video_is_stale" true, "can_publish_with_vocal" true, "can_remix" true, "secondary_badges" [{"dark" {"background_color" "FFFFFF0C", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "A3A3A3"}, "display_name" "Upload", "icon_key" "uploaded", "light" {"background_color" "1C1C1F0A", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "7D7C83"}}], "has_vocal" true, "prompt" "[Verse 1]\nI'm walking down the street today\nWatching all the people play\nThe sun is shining bright and blue\nI'm feeling like I'm someone new\n\n[Chorus]\nOh oh oh\nIt's a beautiful day\nOh oh oh\nEverything's going my way\n\n[Verse 2]\nI see the birds up in the trees\nI feel the cooling summer breeze\nThere's nothing that can bring me down\nI'm the happiest man in town\n\n[Chorus]\nOh oh oh\nIt's a beautiful day\nOh oh oh\nEverything's going my way", "duration" 51.46099773242631, "type" "upload", "has_stem" false}, "title" "ημ_epic_part44_84bpm"}, :duration 51.46099773242631, :controls nil, :lyrics "[Verse 1]\nI'm walking down the street today\nWatching all the people play\nThe sun is shining bright and blue\nI'm feeling like I'm someone new\n\n[Chorus]\nOh oh oh\nIt's a beautiful day\nOh oh oh\nEverything's going my way\n\n[Verse 2]\nI see the birds up in the trees\nI feel the cooling summer breeze\nThere's nothing that can bring me down\nI'm the happiest man in town\n\n[Chorus]\nOh oh oh\nIt's a beautiful day\nOh oh oh\nEverything's going my way", :source #:source{:name "ημ_epic_part44_84bpm(9).json", :sha256 "dd57e59aa0b380153e7b90e2f687cbd4560ceda56d96c35082a4bb9ae493ce53", :format :suno-json, :variation 9}, :title "ημ_epic_part44_84bpm"}, "0cf1878e-dc19-4af8-b9aa-5482f040