ant screams stretched into texture, reversed chants, radio transmissions dissolving into noise.", "can_remix" true, "prompt" "# TITLE: \"Midnight Warehouse Ritual / 真夜中の倉庫儀式\"\n\n---\n\n## STYLE PROMPT\n\n**Genre Fusion:** Post-Industrial Pressure Music × Ritual Glitch Rock × Breath-Guided IDM × Grunge Noise-Ambient × Deconstructed Club Architecture × Somatic Monologue Pop\n\n**Tuning / Tempo:** 432Hz, 88–100 BPM with micro-tempo instability (subtle drift ±2 BPM)\n\n**Key Center:** C minor drifting toward F modal minor, frequent chromatic intrusion (Db, Gb, E natural for tension)\n\n**Rhythmic Architecture:**\n\n* Kick like distant machinery (low, rounded, chest-heavy)\n* Snare as metal impact / warehouse reverb slap\n* Asymmetrical breakcore fragments in transitions\n* Drop sections with half-time collapse feel\n* Silence pockets used as structural reset points\n\n**Texture Palette:**\n\n* Percussive detuned piano clusters (felt-hammer texture)\n* Rusted reverb tails\n* Air-pressure sub bass haze\n* Industrial field recordings (vent hum, chain drag, concrete scrape)\n* Choir pads stretched and granularized\n* Neural flicker glitch bursts in upper frequencies\n* Saturation bloom during emotional peaks\n\n**Vocal Direction:**\n\n* Close-mic breath ASMR verses (intimate, almost confessional)\n* Layered whispered Japanese phrases under English lead lines\n* Chorus expands into distorted choral stack (gender-neutral blend)\n* Occasional spoken internal monologue lines with slight pitch drop\n\n**Mood:** Sacred but mechanical. Vulnerable but resilient. Dark warehouse lit by violet sodium lamps. Emotional catharsis without sentimentality.\n\n---\n\n# LYRICS\n\n## INTRO — Close Breath / Machine Hum\n\n(vent hum, distant metal echo)\n\n息を吸う\nwarehouse air tastes like iron\n吐く\nand the concrete remembers me\n\nNo stained glass here\njust broken skylights\nand stars leaking through the roof.\n\n---\n\n## VERSE 1 — Low Industrial Pulse\n\n床が低く鳴る\nlike a heart too large for its body\n\nMy ribs echo the kick drum\nboom — 空洞 — boom\n\nWe built no cathedral\nwe built pressure\nstacked steel on steel\nuntil the silence cracked.\n\n\"Are you still human?\"\nまだ。\n\"Are you still afraid?\"\n…yes.\n\n---\n\n## PRE-CHORUS — Breath Calibration\n\n吸って — four\nhold — hold\n吐いて — let it fracture\n\nMicro-phase drift in the fluorescent light\n世界が少しズレる\nそれで安定する\n\n---\n\n## CHORUS — Ritual Glitch Pop Lift\n\n真夜中の倉庫で\nwe light the nerve again\n\nKick becomes prayer\nsnare becomes confession\n\nNo nation — no altar — just pulse\njust breath in a steel cathedral\n\n壊れながら\nwe stay intact\n\nMidnight warehouse ritual\nwe glitch but we don’t collapse\n\n---\n\n## POST-CHORUS — Breakcore Fragment\n\namen — cut — amen — cut\nい — き — て — る\n\nwhite noise sparks\nmetallic wings\n\nsub bass rolls like distant thunder\nunder the spine\n\n---\n\n## VERSE 2 — Grunge Noise Bloom\n\nGuitar feedback like neon rain\n錆びた柱に触れる\nmy fingerprints glow\n\nPain is calibration\nnot punishment\n\nI press my palm to cold concrete\nand feel the building breathe.\n\n---\n\n## BRIDGE — Deconstructed Silence\n\n(beat drops out — vent hum only)\n\nListen.\n\nこの沈黙は空っぽじゃない\nit’s loaded.\n\nThe body is architecture.\nThe breath is wiring.\nThe rhythm is survival.\n\n---\n\n## FINAL CHORUS — Expanded Choir / Collapse-Resistant\n\n真夜中の倉庫で\nwe light the nerve again\n\nChoir of static\nchoir of steel\n\nBreak me open\nbut don’t erase me\n\nC minor shadows\nF minor bloom\nchromatic sparks under skin\n\nMidnight warehouse ritual\nstill here\nstill breathing\n\n---\n\n## OUTRO — Silence Pocket\n\n息。\n\nVent hum fades.\n\nConcrete cool.\n\nNo cathedral.\nNo country.\n\nJust pulse.\n", "duration" 435, "type" "gen", "model_badges" {"songrow" {"dark" {"background_color" "00000000", "border_color" "FFFFFF1A", "text_color" "A3A3A3"}, "display_name" "v4.5-all", "light" {"background_color" "00000000", "border_color" "0000001A", "text_color" "7D7C83"}}}, "has_stem" false, "make_instrumental" false, "refu