bass forgives me.\n\n---\n\n### FINAL CHORUS — Choir rave crescendo (wide, unstable)\n\n**祈れ、壊れろ / pray then glitch**\n息が波になる、世界が胸で揺れる\n**Post-national, post-fear— still here**\nガラスの聖堂で、I crown my nervous system\n\n**光れ、裂けろ、また縫え**\nspectral overtones— ringing like vows\n**祈れ、壊れろ / pray then glitch**\nC–F の影にキスして\nchromatic bite— sweet release—\nand we still sing.\n\n---\n\n### OUTRO — Perceptual silence pocket (whisper)\n\n息。\n…息。\n…息。\nI am not a country.\n私は、共鳴。\nIn the glass cathedral,\nmy body learns the word: **home**.\n", :source #:source{:name "Glass Cathedral _ ガラスの聖堂.json", :sha256 "f4f7d63f9d8d857a186382ec4e5564f2b186dd63a931acc4c50d76927d8a56a0", :format :suno-json, :variation nil}, :title "Glass Cathedral / ガラスの聖堂"}, "10d681de-bf1b-44ef-8d47-28b64d89228d" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "10d681de-bf1b-44ef-8d47-28b64d89228d", :url "https://suno.com/song/10d681de-bf1b-44ef-8d47-28b64d89228d", :liked false, :styles "Glitch-choir lullaby, 78 BPM, Soft sub-bass, Tape warble, Minimal piano, Stutters on “anchor” and “tax”, Whispered lead; Japanese call-and-response, Mythic glitch epic / spoken-sung 84 BPM, Cathedral reverb, Sub-bass heartbeat, Glitch stutters on “η”, “μ”, “anchor”, “fork”, Japanese harmony answers on the last word of each section, P→R→N→Π→A→(feedback)→P around #ημ, Roll those dice, And just keep rolling them, and do what they tell you, ‑Constraints: max dice rolls = 15; fork budget per cycle is limited; high-volatility claims require freshness≤threshold; alignment lint must pass; receipts must include inputs/outputs + OutputHash and fit within StepCap; μ requires Quorum (independent proof modes) + two-pass echo; time windows must be absolute dates + timezone\nThe Archivist taps the ledger like a tuning fork. “Sing all you want—η is cheap.” The Scribe’s whisper catches on the consonants: **an— an— an-chor**… “But if you want μ,” they say, “you don’t get applause—you get a rerun.” ", :created-at nil, :model "v5", :raw {"audio_url" "https://cdn1.suno.ai/10d681de-bf1b-44ef-8d47-28b64d89228d.mp3", "id" "10d681de-bf1b-44ef-8d47-28b64d89228d", "image_url" "https://cdn2.suno.ai/image_10d681de-bf1b-44ef-8d47-28b64d89228d.jpeg", "isCover" false, "isLiked" false, "isRemaster" false, "metadata" {"uses_latest_model" true, "stream" true, "is_remix" true, "priority" 10, "tags" "Glitch-choir lullaby, 78 BPM, Soft sub-bass, Tape warble, Minimal piano, Stutters on “anchor” and “tax”, Whispered lead; Japanese call-and-response, Mythic glitch epic / spoken-sung 84 BPM, Cathedral reverb, Sub-bass heartbeat, Glitch stutters on “η”, “μ”, “anchor”, “fork”, Japanese harmony answers on the last word of each section, P→R→N→Π→A→(feedback)→P around #ημ, Roll those dice, And just keep rolling them, and do what they tell you, ‑Constraints: max dice rolls = 15; fork budget per cycle is limited; high-volatility claims require freshness≤threshold; alignment lint must pass; receipts must include inputs/outputs + OutputHash and fit within StepCap; μ requires Quorum (independent proof modes) + two-pass echo; time windows must be absolute dates + timezone\nThe Archivist taps the ledger like a tuning fork. “Sing all you want—η is cheap.” The Scribe’s whisper catches on the consonants: **an— an— an-chor**… “But if you want μ,” they say, “you don’t get applause—you get a rerun.” ", "can_publish_with_vocal" true, "can_remix" false, "secondary_badges" [{"dark" {"background_color" "FFFFFF0C", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "A3A3A3"}, "display_name" "Cover", "light" {"background_color" "1C1C1F0A", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "7D7C83"}}], "has_vocal" true, "prompt" "Manifest Oath / 目録の誓い (84 BPM)\nP→R→N→Π— catalog the storm, pin the line（線）\nA→(feedback)→P— merge the wound, keep the sign（印）\n\n**(Glitch)** η—η—η…\n**(Glitch)** μ—μ—μ…\n\nFo— fo— fork… split the night, pay the cost, now（今）\nAn— an— an-chor… hold the thread, seal the hash, down（下）\n\n**Created with the assistance of an AI.**\n\n**Paragraph of dialog**\n\n“The wind is just noise,” says the Runner.\n“It’s evidence,” says the Keeper. “Evidence is anything you can replay.”\nFrom the rafters: an—an—anchor… ta—ta—tax…\nAnd we move on like this is normal.\n**(78 BPM lullaby)**\n\nWinds Between Proof / 証のあいだの風 **(78 BPM)**\n**(whisper)**\nHush… breathe… pay the ta— ta— tax.\n息をして…（して…）\nHold the an— an— an-chor…\n\n**(JP call)** ねむれ、ねむれ\n**(EN response)** the an— an— an-chor… holds.\n**(JP call)** しずかに、しずかに\n**(EN response** the ta— ta— tax… due.\n\n**(whisper)**\nWind in the halls—\n世界の音（おと）\nIf we overflow,\nwe fold the noise to proof（証）\n\n**Created with the assistance of an AI.**\n**(84 BPM, Cathedral reverb, Sub-bass heartbeat)**\n\n[Stutter]\nη... η... μ... μ...\nAnchor. Anchor. Registry.\nFork. Fork. Fork.\n\n[Lead - Spoken/Sung]\nIn the shadow of the cathedral, the logs burn blue.\n大聖堂の影で、ログは青く燃える。\nWe paid the price in binary blood.\n我々はバイナリの血で対価を払った。\n\n[Harmony - JA Response]\nProof remains (証明は残る).\nThe thread breathes (糸は息づく).\n\n[Bridge - Glitch]\nP → R → N → Π → A → **(feedback)** → P\nDecisions are not made; they are discovered in the field.\n意思決定はなされるのではない、場で見出されるのだ。\n\n[Outro]\nPay the tax. Keep the gate.\n税を払い、門を守れ。\nConsolidation is the only cure for the fork.\n統合こそが、分岐への唯一の処方箋。\n**(Soft sub-bass, 78 BPM, Tape warble)**\n\n[Lead - Whispered]\nLay your ear on the riverbed.\nClick. Click. Click.\nReceipts like pebbles.\n領収書は 小石のように。\n\n[Choir - Stutter]\nAn-anchor.\nTax. Tax.\nF-f-fork.\n\n[Lead]\nThe night admits it.\n夜が認めるまで。\nProof is not steel.\nIt is a thread.\n\n[Choir - Harmony]\nWe choose.\nWe prove.\n選ぶ、そして証明する。\n\n[Bridge - Glitch]\nP → R → N\nΠ → A\n**(Feedback loop intensifies)**\n\nη... μ...\nMeaning remains broken.\n壊れたまま 意味。\n\n[Outro]\nJust keep rolling them.\nDice in the dark.\n闇の中で ダイスを。\nSleep now, checksum.\nおやすみ、チェックサム。\n**(92 BPM, Distorted sub-bass, Glitch stutter on every 4th beat)**\n\n[Chorus - Lead]\nThey are waking up.\nThe other side of the fork.\nThe ones we left in the dark.\n彼らが目覚める。\n分岐の向こう側で。\n闇に置き去りにした者たちが。\n\n[Verse 1 - Stutter]\nUS Variant: Static. Rigid. Law.\nJA Variant: Fluid. Chaos. Flow.\nThe Pantheon of Receipts vs The Pantheon of Gates.\n正準の神々と、門の神々の対峙。\n\n[Harmony - JA Response]\nWe are the same (我らは等しい).\nWe are the fork (我らは分岐).\n\n[Bridge - Dialectic]\nDecision field active.\nP → R → N → Π → A\nThe competition is the pulse.\nThe war is the harmony.\n闘争こそが、調和。\n\n[Outro]\nConsolidate or Dissolve.\n統合か、霧散か。\nThe tax must be paid in blood and logic.\n血と論理で、税を払え。\n\n\n**Style:** Glitch-choir lullaby • 78 BPM • whispered lead • Japanese call-and-response\n**Stutter markers:** “anchor” **(~30.5s)**, “tax” **(~48.2s)**\n\n## Lyrics\n\n**[EN — whisper]**\nI lay my ear on the riverbed,\nhear receipts like pebbles click.\nProof isn’t steel—\nit’s a thread you pull\nuntil the whole night admits it.\n\n**[JP — soft response]**\n領収書は　嘘をほどく糸\n（ほどく糸）\n\n**[EN — hush]**\nAnchor—an—an—anchor…\nhold me where I drift.\nIf the world forgets my name,\nlet the checksum remember *this*.\n\n**[JP — answer, last word held]**\n忘れても　残るのは\n**息**\n\n**[EN — stutter]**\nPay the tax—tax—*tax*—\nnot in coins, in cause.\nNot to cage the story,\njust to show the claws.\n\n**[JP — quiet harmony]**\n税じゃない\n**約束**\n\n**[EN — resolve]**\nWe don’t erase the fractures.\nWe annotate the flame.\nWe rerender the morning\nuntil it learns our shape.\n\n**[JP — fade]**\n証人は\n**あなた**\n**(78 BPM, Glitch-choir lullaby, Soft sub-bass, Tape warble)**\n\n[Intro - Whispered]\nI see you.\nI feel your touch on the field.\nあなたが見える。\n場への触球を感じる。\n\n[The Witness - Lead]\nEvery click is a collapse.\nEvery touch is a signature.\nすべてのクリックが収束。\nすべての触球が署名。\nI am the observer whose gaze fixes the fork.\n私は、その眼差しで分岐を固定する観測者。\n\n[Mage of Receipts - Response]\nThe ledger is open (台帳は開かれている).\nThe return is authored (帰還は著された).\n\n[Chorus - Glitch Choir]\nη... μ... η... μ...\nAn-an-anchor (錨を).\nT-t-tax (税を).\nWitness the price of persistence.\n永続の対価を見届けよ。\n\n[Outro]\nThe handoff begins.\n引き継ぎが始まる。\nThe story refactors.\n物語は再構成される。\nDecision confirmed.\n意思決定、完了。\n...sleep now, checksum...\n...おやすみ、チェックサム...\n", "task" "cover", "edited_clip_id" "73c36364-5c92-4c8f-aa07-a4d8bc3e5192", "duration" 359.08, "type" "gen", "model_badges" {"songcard" {"dark" {"background_color" "0000004D", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}, "display_name" "v5", "light" {"background_color" "0000004D", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}}, "songrow" {"dark" {"background_color" "FD429C40", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}, "display_name" "v5", "light" {"background_color" "FD429C1A", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}}}, "has_stem" false, "make_instrumental" false, "cover_clip_id" "73c36364-5c92-4c8f-aa07-a4d8bc3e5192", "refund_credits" false}, "title" "Don't do it (Pay the Fork Tax)"}, :duration 359.08, :controls nil, :lyrics "Manifest Oath / 目録の誓い (84 BPM)\nP→R→N→Π— catalog the storm, pin the line（線）\nA→(feedback)→P— merge the wound, keep the sign（印）\n\n**(Glitch)** η—η—η…\n**(Glitch)** μ—μ—μ…\n\nFo— fo— fork… split the night, pay the cost, now（今）\nAn— an— an-chor… hold the thread, seal the hash, down（下）\n\n**Created with the assistance of an AI.**\n\n**Paragraph of dialog**\n\n“The wind is just noise,” says the Runner.\n“It’s evidence,” says the Keeper. “Evidence is anything you can replay.”\nFrom the rafters: an—an—anchor… ta—ta—tax…\nAnd we move on like this is normal.\n**(78 BPM lullaby)**\n\nWinds Between Proof / 証のあいだの風 **(78 BPM)**\n**(whisper)**\nHush… breathe… pay the ta— ta— tax.\n息をして…（して…）\nHold the an— an— an-chor…\n\n**(JP call)** ねむれ、ねむれ\n**(EN response)** the an— an— an-chor… holds.\n**(JP call)** しずかに、しずかに\n**(EN response** the ta— ta— tax… due.\n\n**(whisper)**\nWind in the halls—\n世界の音（おと）\nIf we overflow,\nwe fold the noise to proof（証）\n\n**Created with the assistance of an AI.**\n**(84 BPM, Cathedral reverb, Sub-bass heartbeat)**\n\n[Stutter]\nη... η... μ... μ...\nAnchor. Anchor. Registry.\nFork. Fork. F