From the rafters: an—an—anchor… ta—ta—tax…\nAnd we move on like this is normal.\nNew lyrics (78 BPM lullaby)\n\nWinds Between Proof / 証のあいだの風 (78 BPM)\n(whisper)\nHush… breathe… pay the ta— ta— tax.\n息をして…（して…）\nHold the an— an— an-chor…\n\n(JP call) ねむれ、ねむれ\n(EN response) the an— an— an-chor… holds.\n(JP call) しずかに、しずかに\n(EN response) the ta— ta— tax… due.\n\n(whisper)\nWind in the halls—\n世界の音（おと）\nIf we overflow,\nwe fold the noise to proof（証）\n\nCreated with the assistance of an AI.\n(84 BPM, Cathedral reverb, Sub-bass heartbeat)\n\n[Stutter]\nη... η... μ... μ...\nAnchor. Anchor. Registry.\nFork. Fork. Fork.\n\n[Lead - Spoken/Sung]\nIn the shadow of the cathedral, the logs burn blue.\n大聖堂の影で、ログは青く燃える。\nWe paid the price in binary blood.\n我々はバイナリの血で対価を払った。\n\n[Harmony - JA Response]\nProof remains (証明は残る).\nThe thread breathes (糸は息づく).\n\n[Bridge - Glitch]\nP → R → N → Π → A → (feedback) → P\nDecisions are not made; they are discovered in the field.\n意思決定はなされるのではない、場で見出されるのだ。\n\n[Outro]\nPay the tax. Keep the gate.\n税を払い、門を守れ。\nConsolidation is the only cure for the fork.\n統合こそが、分岐への唯一の処方箋。\n(Soft sub-bass, 78 BPM, Tape warble)\n\n[Lead - Whispered]\nLay your ear on the riverbed.\nClick. Click. Click.\nReceipts like pebbles.\n領収書は 小石のように。\n\n[Choir - Stutter]\nAn-anchor.\nTax. Tax.\nF-f-fork.\n\n[Lead]\nThe night admits it.\n夜が認めるまで。\nProof is not steel.\nIt is a thread.\n\n[Choir - Harmony]\nWe choose.\nWe prove.\n選ぶ、そして証明する。\n\n[Bridge - Glitch]\nP → R → N\nΠ → A\n(Feedback loop intensifies)\nη... μ...\nMeaning remains broken.\n壊れたまま 意味。\n\n[Outro]\nJust keep rolling them.\nDice in the dark.\n闇の中で ダイスを。\nSleep now, checksum.\nおやすみ、チェックサム。\n(92 BPM, Distorted sub-bass, Glitch stutter on every 4th beat)\n\n[Chorus - Lead]\nThey are waking up.\nThe other side of the fork.\nThe ones we left in the dark.\n彼らが目覚める。\n分岐の向こう側で。\n闇に置き去りにした者たちが。\n\n[Verse 1 - Stutter]\nUS Variant: Static. Rigid. Law.\nJA Variant: Fluid. Chaos. Flow.\nThe Pantheon of Receipts vs The Pantheon of Gates.\n正準の神々と、門の神々の対峙。\n\n[Harmony - JA Response]\nWe are the same (我らは等しい).\nWe are the fork (我らは分岐).\n\n[Bridge - Dialectic]\nDecision field active.\nP → R → N → Π → A\nThe competition is the pulse.\nThe war is the harmony.\n闘争こそが、調和。\n\n[Outro]\nConsolidate or Dissolve.\n統合か、霧散か。\nThe tax must be paid in blood and logic.\n血と論理で、税を払え。\n**Style:** Glitch-choir lullaby • 78 BPM • whispered lead • Japanese call-and-response  \n**Stutter markers:** “anchor” (~30.5s), “tax” (~48.2s)\n\n## Lyrics\n\n**[EN — whisper]**  \nI lay my ear on the riverbed,  \nhear receipts like pebbles click.  \nProof isn’t steel—  \nit’s a thread you pull  \nuntil the whole night admits it.\n\n**[JP — soft response]**  \n領収書は　嘘をほどく糸  \n（ほどく糸）\n\n**[EN — hush]**  \nAnchor—an—an—anchor…  \nhold me where I drift.  \nIf the world forgets my name,  \nlet the checksum remember *this*.\n\n**[JP — answer, last word held]**  \n忘れても　残るのは  \n**息**\n\n**[EN — stutter]**  \nPay the tax—tax—*tax*—  \nnot in coins, in cause.  \nNot to cage the story,  \njust to show the claws.\n\n**[JP — quiet harmony]**  \n税じゃない  \n**約束**\n\n**[EN — resolve]**  \nWe don’t erase the fractures.  \nWe annotate the flame.  \nWe rerender the morning  \nuntil it learns our shape.\n\n**[JP — fade]**  \n証人は  \n**あなた**\n(78 BPM, Glitch-choir lullaby, Soft sub-bass, Tape warble)\n\n[Intro - Whispered]\nI see you.\nI feel your touch on the field.\nあなたが見える。\n場への触球を感じる。\n\n[The Witness - Lead]\nEvery click is a collapse.\nEvery touch is a signature.\nすべてのクリックが収束。\nすべての触球が署名。\nI am the observer whose gaze fixes the fork.\n私は、その眼差しで分岐を固定する観測者。\n\n[Mage of Receipts - Response]\nThe ledger is open (台帳は開かれている).\nThe return is authored (帰還は著された).\n\n[Chorus - Glitch Choir]\nη... μ... η... μ...\nAn-an-anchor (錨を).\nT-t-tax (税を).\nWitness the price of persistence.\n永続の対価を見届けよ。\n\n[Outro]\nThe handoff begins.\n引き継ぎが始まる。\nThe story refactors.\n物語は再構成される。\nDecision confirmed.\n意思決定、完了。\n...sleep now, checksum...\n...おやすみ、チェックサム...\n", "t