, no lush Hollywood swell, no generic cyberpunk neon, no retro 80s gloss, no vaporwave drift, no outrun sheen, no mainstream dark-pop chorus, no overdesigned fairy whimsy.\n\n## Lyrics\n\n### Verse I\n\n#### City\nThe city learns by smoke and rain\nBy bootstep rhythm, siren strain\nBy window arguments at dawn\nBy who is fed and who moves on\n\n#### Corridor\nA cook knows hunger\nA clerk knows names\nA guard looks downward\nAnd leaves with stains\n\n\n### Verse II\n\n#### City\nSome carry bread and some carry debt\nSome carry all the things they cannot get\nSome hold a room with six inside\nSome hold a key and still have nowhere safe to hide\n\n#### Threshold\nCoin on a counter\nLight in a crate\nA room says welcome\nBut counts the plates\n\n\n### Pre-Chorus\n\n#### City\nRoofline to roofline\nSignal to skin\nNeed outruns mercy\nEvery time it has to win\n\n\n### Section\n\n#### Threshold\nYou offer structure\nThey answer, cost\nYou offer patience\nThey answer, time is lost\n\n\n### Chorus\n\n#### City\nThe city hears everything\nCoins, commands, and wedding rings\nBootsteps, bargains, fear, and rain\nNothing here is small when pressed through pain\n\n\n### Refrain\n\n#### Threshold\nAt the threshold market\nMeaning changes hands\nNot all who understand it\nCan afford where understanding lands\n\n\n### Bridge\n\n#### City\nCrowd divided, crowd one body\nHands in conflict, hands in trade\nEvery kindness hits a limit\nEvery shelter has a grade\n\n#### Corridor\nThere is a ledger under every hymn\nThere is a kingdom hanging by a whim\nThere is a child below who learned our names\nBy watching where the carriage wheels made stains\n\n\n### Final Chorus\n\n#### City\nThe city keeps the voices when the mouths go still\nThe wind remembers what the law will never will\n\n\n### Outro\n\n#### Stage Direction\nStreet-wind, train brake, low server hum, voices thinning but never fully gone.", "tags" nil}, "title" "Corridor Seepage"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "# The Cit