 choir devour the drums\nlet the drums forgive the choir\n\n**Break me holy / 壊して清く**\npost-national body, radiant and raw\nbreath becomes architecture\narchitecture becomes pulse\n\n**神経を照らせ / light the nerve**\nC–F minor cathedral sky\nchromatic sparks in my blood\nI glitch into grace\nand don’t apologize.\n\n---\n\n### OUTRO — Silence pocket\n\n息。\n…息。\n…息。\n\nThe cathedral wasn’t made of glass.\nIt was made of you.\n\nAnd you’re still singing.\n", "duration" 479.96, "type" "gen", "model_badges" {"songrow" {"dark" {"background_color" "00000000", "border_color" "FFFFFF1A", "text_color" "A3A3A3"}, "display_name" "v4.5-all", "light" {"background_color" "00000000", "border_color" "0000001A", "text_color" "7D7C83"}}}, "has_stem" false, "make_instrumental" false, "refund_credits" false}, "title" "Cathedral Nervous System / 神経の聖堂"}, :duration 479.96, :controls nil, :lyrics "*(92 BPM, unstable drift, 432Hz pulse, C–F minor w/ chromatic fractures)*\n\n---\n\n### INTRO — Close mic, breath on glass\n\n息が曇らせるステンドグラス\nmy lungs fog the saints into pixels\n「ここはどこ？」\nIt’s not heaven.\nIt’s the inside of your spine.\n\nlow piano strike — C\novertones shimmer like cold metal\nI press my palm to the window—\nthe window presses back.\n\n---\n\n### VERSE 1 — Perceptual piano shards / low pressure bass\n\n鍵盤が砕ける、光の破片\nblue tastes metallic tonight\nI feel the choir behind my molars\nsinging in a language made of static.\n\n“Don’t panic,” I whisper\nでも心臓がドラムンベース\nkick drum in the sternum\nhi-hats in my teeth\n\nno nation, no exit sign\njust pulse architecture\ncollapse-resistant, trembling\nalive because it shakes.\n\n---\n\n### PRE-CHORUS — Breath calibration\n\n吸って\nhold\n吐いて\nfall\n\nmicro-phase drift\n世界が半音ずれて\nそれでちょうどいい\njust enough dissonance\nto mean something.\n\n---\n\n### CHORUS — Ritual glitch pop organism\n\n**神経を照らせ / light the nerve**\nmy body is a glass cathedral\nkick drum = prayer\nsnare = confession\n\n**Break me holy / 壊して清く**\nchromatic knives through the choir\nno p