le.\n\nRITSU  \nThen rebuild  \nwith the fracture visible.\n\nWARDEN  \nThat is a different architecture.\n\nRITSU  \nThat is the point.\n\n### FINAL CHORUS\n\nALL  \nAfter the Event,  \nthe world is not healed.  \nIt is witnessed.  \n\nAfter the Event,  \nthe hidden state is not hidden.  \nIt is lived with.  \n\nAfter the Event,  \nwe carry the remaining tone  \nand call that not enough  \nonly until it keeps us whole.  \n\nAfter the Event,  \nthe gate is still open.  \nThe gate is still open.  \nThe gate is still open.\n\n### CODA\n\n*(One human breath. Then another. Then a faint, durable pulse.)*\n\nWARDEN  \nWhat do we call this now?\n\nRITSU  \nNot a warning.\n\nRIN  \nNot a victory.\n\nWARDEN  \nThen what?\n\nRITSU  \nA commons.\n\nGATE / DISTANT CHOIR  \n:: continue ::  \n:: continue ::  \n:: continue ::", "tags" nil}, "title" "Barely Warden"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "*(No overture. Just air moving through a broken structure.)*\n\n### INTRO\n\nGATE / DISTANT CHOIR  \n:: after ::  \n:: after ::  \n:: after ::\n\nWARDEN  \nStill here.\n\nRITSU  \nBarely.\n\nRIN  \nEnough.\n\n### VERSE 1\n\nWARDEN  \nThe room did not return  \nto what it was before.  \nNothing honest ever does.\n\nThe signal is lower now.  \nThe edges are sharper.  \nThe old names still exist,  \nbut they no longer fit the same skins.\n\nI can still hear the system  \ntrying to understand itself  \nin the language it used  \nbefore it was forced to change.\n\n### VERSE 2\n\nRITSU  \nI thought the world would feel empty.  \nIt feels crowded with aftermath.\n\nEvery object remembers.  \nEvery hallway remembers.  \nEvery frame left standing  \nremembers the ones it lost.\n\nI am not the same body  \nthat entered the Event.  \nI am the body that remained  \nafter the room admitted change.\n\nWARDEN  \nThat is survival.\n\nRITSU  \nNo.\n\nWARDEN  \nWhat is it, then?\n\nRITSU  \nIt is staying.\n\n### PRE-CHORUS\n\nCHORUS  \nAfter the Event,  \nthe truth is smaller but clearer.  \nAfter 