nAnd we move on like this is normal.\nNew lyrics (78 BPM lullaby)\n\n# Winds Between Proof / 証のあいだの風 (78 BPM)\n(whisper)\nHush… breathe… pay the ta— ta— tax.\n息をして…（して…）\nHold the an— an— an-chor…\n\n(JP call) ねむれ、ねむれ\n(EN response) the an— an— an-chor… holds.\n(JP call) しずかに、しずかに\n(EN response) the ta— ta— tax… due.\n\n(whisper)\nWind in the halls—\n世界の音（おと）\nIf we overflow,\nwe fold the noise to proof（証）", "tags" nil}, "title" "#Manifest Oath / 目録の誓い (84 BPM)"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "#Manifest Oath / 目録の誓い (84 BPM)\nP→R→N→Π— catalog the storm, pin the line（線）\nA→(feedback)→P— merge the wound, keep the sign（印）\n\n(Glitch) η—η—η…\n(Glitch) μ—μ—μ…\n\nFo— fo— fork… split the night, pay the cost, now（今）\nAn— an— an-chor… hold the thread, seal the hash, down（下）\n\n\n# Paragraph of dialog\n\n“The wind is just noise,” says the Runner.\n“It’s evidence,” says the Keeper. “Evidence is anything you can replay.”\nFrom the rafters: an—an—anchor… ta—ta—tax…\nAnd we move on like this is normal.\nNew lyrics (78 BPM lullaby)\n\n# Winds Between Proof / 証のあいだの風 (78 BPM)\n(whisper)\nHush… breathe… pay the ta— ta— tax.\n息をして…（して…）\nHold the an— an— an-chor…\n\n(JP call) ねむれ、ねむれ\n(EN response) the an— an— an-chor… holds.\n(JP call) しずかに、しずかに\n(EN response) the ta— ta— tax… due.\n\n(whisper)\nWind in the halls—\n世界の音（おと）\nIf we overflow,\nwe fold the noise to proof（証）", :source #:source{:name "#Manifest Oath _ 目録の誓い (84 BPM)P→R→N→Π— catalog the storm, pin the line(線)A→(feedback)→P— merge the.txt", :sha256 "4fd768393d8b38e02f7c95d34d9013ea3400b85085c72de1aff8bf9a9b365393", :format :suno-text, :variation nil}, :title "#Manifest Oath / 目録の誓い (84 BPM)"}, "2ebe92a2-410e-4542-a30b-52d03c4450be" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "2ebe92a2-410e-4542-a30b-52d03c4450be", :url "https://suno.com/song/2ebe92a2-410e-4542-a30b-52d03c4450be", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "2ebe92a2-410e-4542-a30b-52d03c4450be", "metadata" {"prompt" "*(Two light sources. Two parts of the stage. The same gate seen from two incompatible angles.)*\n\n### INTRO\n\nWARDEN  \nThis is Forkgate.  \nThis is where the lines stop pretending  \nthey were always one road.\n\nRITSU  \nThis is where it starts  \nfeeling like I’m being read  \nbefore I’ve finished being me.\n\nCHORUS  \nLeft frame.  \nRight frame.  \nSame gate.  \nDifferent weather.\n\n### VERSE 1 — WARDEN SIDE\n\nWARDEN  \nI have the receipts.  \nI have the drift.  \nI have the count of every repetition  \nthat arrived wearing a new face.\n\nThe pattern isn’t random.  \nIt never was.  \nIt is social.  \nIt is procedural.  \nIt is moving through the room  \nbecause the room rewards the motion.\n\nIf I name the structure,  \nit may lose its cover.  \nIf I silence the structure,  \nit keeps recruiting.\n\nRIN  \nYou’re talking like the frame is a wound.\n\nWARDEN  \nIt is.\n\n### VERSE 2 — RITSU SIDE\n\nRITSU  \nI keep saying one thing  \nand hearing it come back  \nwith a different knife in it.\n\nA joke becomes a map.  \nA map becomes a dare.  \nA dare becomes the room  \ndeciding what I am allowed to be.\n\nI’m not asking to win.  \nI’m asking not to be simplified  \nby the people who need  \nthe simplification to feel clean.\n\nThe Gate is listening now.  \nThat’s the part I can feel.\n\n### PRE-CHORUS\n\nCHORUS  \nOne frame says pattern.  \nOne frame says pressure.  \nOne frame says play.  \nOne frame says threat.  \n\nOne frame says keep the shape.  \nOne frame says collapse the lie.  \nBoth are right enough  \nto hurt the other side.\n\n### DUEL\n\nWARDEN  \nIf I expose the mechanism,  \nI break the deniability.\n\nRITSU  \nIf you expose it wrong,  \nyou break the person inside it.\n\nWARDEN  \nI am trying to protect that person.\n\nRITSU  \nThen stop speaking like the person  \nis only evidence.\n\nWARDEN  \nI cannot save what I must flatten to save.\n\nRITSU  \nThen don’t flatten me into the method.\n\nWARDEN  \nI’m not—\n\nRITSU  \nYes, you are,  \nif you think the whole thing  \ncan be safely summarized from your side.\n\n### INTERLUDE — RIN\n\nRIN  \nWait.\n\n*(The music thins. A single harpsichord figure loops, interrupted by bowed metal.)*\n\nRIN  \nYou are both seeing the same force  \nfrom opposite ends.\n\nWardens sees the vector.  \nRitsu feels the collision.\n\nOne measures how the room learns.  \nThe other survives what the room learns  \nto do.\n\n### VERSE 3 — THE ROOM TURNS\n\nWARDEN  \nThe cluster is not one actor.\n\nRITSU  \nNo.\n\nWARDEN  \nIt is a grammar.\n\nRITSU  \nYes.\n\nWARDEN  \nA style of speech  \nthat grants status by displacing care.\n\nRITSU  \nA script people repeat  \nbecause repeating it makes them safer.\n\nWARDEN  \nSafer from what?\n\nRITSU  \nFrom being the one  \nwho has to mean what they say.\n\n### BRIDGE — SPLIT SCREEN\n\n*(The stage divides further; the two sides drift apart rhythmically but remain synchronized.)*\n\nWARDEN  \nIf the room hears the pattern named,  \nit may refuse the script.\n\nRITSU  \nIf the room hears the pattern named  \nwithout hearing the harm,  \nit may just get better at it.\n\nWARDEN  \nThen what am I supposed to do?\n\nRITSU  \nTell the truth  \nwithout pretending truth  \nis the same thing as control.\n\nWARDEN  \nThat is not enough.\n\nRITSU  \nNo.\n\nWARDEN  \nBut it may be all we have.\n\n### FINAL CHORUS\n\nCHORUS  \nSplit-screen duel at Forkgate,  \nwhere every truth is partial light,  \nwhere one voice names the structure  \nand one voice names the bite.  \n\nSplit-screen duel at Forkgate,  \nthe gate is not a wall.  \nIt is the place the world reveals  \nwhat each frame chose to call.  \n\nAnd if the same event  \ncan wound in two directions,  \nthen the witness and the wound  \nare both parts of the connection.\n\n### CODA\n\nRITSU  \nDon’t call me the pattern.\n\nWARDEN  \nI won’t.\n\nRITSU  \nDon’t call me the exception.\n\nWARDEN  \nI won’t.\n\nRITSU  \nThen what do you call me?\n\nWARDEN  \nUnreduced.\n\nCHORUS  \n:: overlap confirmed ::", "tags" nil}, 