f", :format :suno-text, :variation 1}, :title "The Render"}, "31ddc907-1bc6-4303-ad10-60347f5fd7d6" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "31ddc907-1bc6-4303-ad10-60347f5fd7d6", :url "https://suno.com/song/31ddc907-1bc6-4303-ad10-60347f5fd7d6", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "31ddc907-1bc6-4303-ad10-60347f5fd7d6", "metadata" {"prompt" "# The City Hears Everything\n\n## Role\nThe city as living frame. The crowd, the struggle, the unequal room, with corridor seepage and outsider contact at the edges.\n\n## Style Prompt\nLayered chorus, urgent pulse, street wind textures, low percussion, bowed strings, crowded call-and-response, cheap-phone crowd grain, motion through pressure not speed. Hushed ensemble, plucked strings cut by buffer clicks, service-hall footsteps, low strings under breath, murmured prose, close-mic secrecy. Bright but restrained threshold piece, delicate chimes, hand percussion, plucked motifs, pauses that feel like negotiation, polite glitches, open harmonies.\n\n## Excluded Style\nNo EDM drop, no trailer braams, no tavern bounce, no pop-ballad belting, no symphonic metal, no glossy neon, no soft haze, no triumphant snare march, no festival build, no lush Hollywood swell, no generic cyberpunk neon, no retro 80s gloss, no vaporwave drift, no outrun sheen, no mainstream dark-pop chorus, no overdesigned fairy whimsy.\n\n## Lyrics\n\n### Verse I\n\n#### City\nThe city learns by smoke and rain\nBy bootstep rhythm, siren strain\nBy window arguments at dawn\nBy who is fed and who moves on\n\n#### Corridor\nA cook knows hunger\nA clerk knows names\nA guard looks downward\nAnd leaves with stains\n\n\n### Verse II\n\n#### City\nSome carry bread and some carry debt\nSome carry all the things they cannot get\nSome hold a room with six inside\nSome hold a key and still have nowhere safe to hide\n\n#### Threshold\nCoin on a counter\nLight in a crate\nA room says welcome\nBut counts the plates\n\n\n### Pre-Chorus\n\n#### City\nRoofline to roofline\nSignal to skin\nNeed outruns mercy\nEvery time it has to win\n\n\n### Section\n\n#### Threshold\nYou offer structure\nThey answer, cost\nYou offer patience\nThey answer, time is lost\n\n\n### Chorus\n\n#### City\nThe city hears everything\nCoins, commands, and wedding rings\nBootsteps, bargains, fear, and rain\nNothing here is small when pressed through pain\n\n\n### Refrain\n\n#### Threshold\nAt the threshold market\nMeaning changes hands\nNot all who understand it\nCan afford where understanding lands\n\n\n### Bridge\n\n#### City\nCrowd divided, crowd one body\nHands in conflict, hands in trade\nEvery kindness hits a limit\nEvery shelter has a grade\n\n#### Corridor\nThere is a ledger under every hymn\nThere is a kingdom hanging by a whim\nThere is a child below who learned our names\nBy watching where the carriage wheels made stains\n\n\n### Final Chorus\n\n#### City\nThe city keeps the voices when the mouths go still\nThe wind remembers what the law will never will\n\n\n### Outro\n\n#### Stage Direction\nStreet-wind, train brake, low server hum, voices thinning but never fully gone.", "tags" nil}, "title" "Corridor Seepage"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "# The City Hears Everything\n\n## Role\nThe city as living frame. The crowd, the struggle, the unequal room, with corridor seepage and outsider contact at the edges.\n\n## Style Prompt\nLayered chorus, urgent pulse, street wind textures, low percussion, bowed strings, crowded call-and-response, cheap-phone crowd grain, motion through pressure not speed. Hushed ensemble, plucked strings cut by buffer clicks, service-hall footsteps, low strings under breath, murmured prose, close-mic secrecy. Bright but restrained threshold piece, delicate chimes, hand percussion, plucked motifs, pauses that feel like negotiation, polite glitches, open harmonies.\n\n## Excluded Style\nNo EDM drop, no trailer braams, no tavern bounce, no pop-ballad belting, no symphonic metal, no glossy neon, no soft haze, no