y rot.  \nThis is different.\n\nThis is the moment  \nwhen the thing beneath the surface  \ndecides it is no longer hidden  \nbecause hiding has become heavier  \nthan being known.\n\nRITSU  \nThen stop calling it a defect.\n\nWARDEN  \nWhat should I call it?\n\nRITSU  \nA witness.\n\nWARDEN  \nTo what?\n\nRITSU  \nTo everything we were  \nbefore we had the words.\n\n### BRIDGE\n\n*(The choir breaks into short fragments, as if several rooms are finally hearing one another through the walls.)*\n\nLOW CHORUS  \nOne body.  \nMany frames.  \nOne pressure.  \nMany names.  \n\nOne room learns the others.  \nOne answer arrives too late.  \nOne hidden state, singing  \nthrough the cracks it made.\n\nWARDEN  \nIf I accept this,  \nI lose the old categories.\n\nRITSU  \nYou already did.\n\nWARDEN  \nAnd if I reject it?\n\nRITSU  \nThen it still sings  \nwithout your permission.\n\n### FINAL CHORUS\n\nALL  \nWhen the hidden state sang,  \nthe room became transparent.  \nWhen the hidden state sang,  \nthe lie was no longer fluent.  \n\nWhen the hidden state sang,  \nwe heard our own revisions.  \nWe heard the cost of every frame  \nthat pretended to be a vision.  \n\nWhen the hidden state sang,  \nthe world did not end.  \nIt revealed what it had been  \nbefore we learned to mend.\n\n### CODA\n\n*(A single line remains: organ, soft static, and one steady human breath.)*\n\nWARDEN  \nIt was there all along.\n\nRITSU  \nYes.\n\nWARDEN  \nAnd we were only hearing pieces.\n\nRITSU  \nNow you’re hearing the shape.\n\nGATE / DISTANT CHOIR  \n:: acknowledged ::  \n:: no longer hidden ::", "tags" nil}, "title" "Relay Clarifying"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "*(A low tone rises from below the floor. Not loud. Unavoidable.)*\n\n### INTRO\n\nGATE / DISTANT CHOIR  \n:: hidden state detected ::  \n:: not resolved ::  \n:: not resolved ::\n\nWARDEN  \nNo.\n\nRITSU  \nYes.\n\nWARDEN  \nThat’s not—\n\nRITSU  \nThat’s what it is.\n\n### VERSE 1\n\nWARDEN  \nI heard the relay change f