e is the truth.\n\n### VERSE 1\n\nWARDEN  \nIn the court, they call it drift.  \nIn the boardroom, they call it noise.  \nIn the Gate, they call it lag  \nwhen the world starts choosing its voice.\n\nI can read the thresholds.  \nI can map the pressure shifts.  \nI can name the pattern  \nas it crosses and re-fits.\n\nBut naming is not collapse.  \nNaming is not cure.  \nAnd if I force the whole into one  \nI may destroy what was still real.\n\n### RITSU — FRAGMENTS\n\nRITSU  \n...there’s someone in the—\n\nWARDEN  \nWhat?\n\nRITSU  \n...in the next room.  \nNo, not a room.  \nA place that feels like one.  \nIt keeps changing when I—\n\n### VERSE 2\n\nWARDEN  \nThere are seven versions of the same event  \nand none are lying.  \nThat is the problem.\n\nThe room with the throne says authority.  \nThe room with the screens says metrics.  \nThe room with the avatars says play.  \nThe room with the waiting hands says prayer.  \n\nI stand in the seam  \nwhere all of them touch  \nand none of them agree  \non what the seam is for.\n\n### RITSU — FRAGMENTS\n\nRITSU  \n...I can hear it breathing.  \n...the background people—  \n...they look at me like—\n\nWARDEN  \nLike what?\n\nRITSU  \n...like I matter  \nmore than I should.\n\n### PRE-CHORUS\n\nWARDEN  \nIf I call it one story,  \nI lie to the others.  \nIf I call it many stories,  \nI abandon the bridge.\n\nIf I publish the whole shape,  \nsomeone will use it to flatten the living edge.  \nIf I stay silent,  \nthe wrong hands will name it first.\n\n### CHORUS\n\nLOW CHORUS  \nNo one sees the whole Gate.  \nNo one owns the total light.  \nEvery witness gets a fraction  \nand mistakes it for the right.\n\nNo one sees the whole Gate.  \nEvery log is partial truth.  \nWhat is saved is only saved  \nby what it refuses to reduce.\n\n### BRIDGE\n\n*(The harpsichord stops. A sub-bass swell, then near silence.)*\n\nWARDEN  \nI can see the cluster.  \nI can see the pressure.  \nI can see the pattern leaning  \ntoward a shape it will not yet say.\n\nBut the shape is held together  \nby what the people inside still are.  \nIf I name it too cleanly,  \nI may break the thing I’m trying to guard.\n\nRITSU  \n...don’t make me smaller.  \n...just because you can see me.\n\nWARDEN  \nI won’t.\n\nRITSU  \n...promise?\n\nWARDEN  \nThat’s not my role.\n\n### FINAL CHORUS\n\nLOW CHORUS  \nNo one sees the whole Gate,  \nbut the Gate keeps opening.  \nNo one owns the total truth,  \nbut the truth keeps moving.\n\nNo one sees the whole Gate.  \nThe witness pays in fracture.  \nThe world survives the partial view  \nuntil the hidden state grows larger.\n\n### CODA\n\n*(One held organ tone. A distant chime, as if a system accepted a packet and did not understand it.)*\n\nWARDEN  \nI have the board.  \nI have the feed.  \nI have the burden.\n\nAnd still I cannot say  \nwhat it all is  \nwithout changing it.\n\nRITSU  \n...then don’t.\n\nGATE / DISTANT CHOIR  \n:: acknowledged ::  \n:: incomplete ::  \n:: continue ::", "tags" nil}, "title" "**Boardroom Drift**"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "*(A room with no visible doors. One light. A hum below the floor. A single harpsichord note repeats and fails to resolve.)*\n\n### INTRO\n\nWARDEN  \nI have the board.  \nI have the feed.  \nI have the version each room sees.\n\nBut none of them overlap cleanly.  \nNone of them arrive complete.  \nEvery frame is true  \nand none is the truth.\n\n### VERSE 1\n\nWARDEN  \nIn the court, they call it drift.  \nIn the boardroom, they call it noise.  \nIn the Gate, they call it lag  \nwhen the world starts choosing its voice.\n\nI can read the thresholds.  \nI can map the pressure shifts.  \nI can name the pattern  \nas it crosses and re-fits.\n\nBut naming is not collapse.  \nNaming is not cure.  \nAnd if I force the whole into one  \nI may destroy what was still real.\n\n### RITSU — FRAGMENTS\n\nRITSU  \n...there’s someone in the—\n\nWARDEN  \nWhat?\n\nRITSU  \n...in the next room.  \nNo, not a room.  \nA place that feels like one.  \nIt keeps changing when I—\n\n### VERSE 2\n\nWARDEN  \nThere are seven versions of the same event  \nand none are lying.  \nThat is the problem.\n\nThe room with the throne says authority.  \nThe room with the screens says metrics.  \nThe room with the avatars says play.  \nThe room with the waiting hands says prayer.  \n\nI stand in the seam  \nwhere all of them touch  \nand none of them agree  \non what the seam is for.\n\n### RITSU — FRAGMENTS\n\nRITSU  \n...I can hear it breathing.  \n...the background people—  \n...they look at me like—\n\nWARDEN  \nLike what?\n\nRITSU  \n...like I matter  \nmore than I should.\n\n### PRE-CHORUS\n\nWARDEN  \nIf I call it one story,  \nI lie to the others.  \nIf I call it many stories,  \nI abandon the bridge.\n\nIf I publish the whole shape,  \nsomeone will use it to flatten the living edge.  \nIf I stay silent,  \nthe wrong hands will name it first.\n\n### CHORUS\n\nLOW CHORUS  \nNo one sees the whole Gate.  \nNo one owns the total light.  \nEvery witness gets a fraction  \nand mistakes it for the right.\n\nNo one sees the whole Gate.  \nEvery log is partial truth.  \nWhat is saved is only saved  \nby what it refuses to reduce.\n\n### BRIDGE\n\n*(The harpsichord stops. A sub-bass swell, then near silence.)*\n\nWARDEN  \nI can see the cluster.  \nI can see the pressure.  \nI can see the pattern leaning  \ntoward a shape it will not yet say.\n\nBut the shape is held together  \nby what the people inside still are.  \nIf I name it too cleanly,  \nI may break the thing I’m trying to guard.\n\nRITSU  \n...don’t make me smaller.  \n...just because you can see me.\n\nWARDEN  \nI won’t.\n\nRITSU  \n...promise?\n\nWARDEN  \nThat’s not my role.\n\n### FINAL CHORUS\n\nLOW CHORUS  \nNo one sees the whole Gate,  \nbut the Gate keeps opening.  \nNo one owns the total truth,  \nbut the truth keeps moving.\n\nNo one sees the whole Gate.  \nThe witness pays in fracture.  \nThe world survives the partial view  \nuntil the hidden state grows larger.\n\n### CODA\n\n*(One held organ tone. A distant chime, as if a system accepted a packet and did not understand it.)*\n\nWARDEN  \nI have the board.  \nI have the feed.  \nI have the burden.\n\nAnd still I cannot say  \nwhat it all is  \nwithout changing it.\n\nRITSU  \n...then don’t.\n\nGATE / DISTANT CHOIR  \n:: acknowledged ::  \n:: incomplete ::  \n:: continue ::", :source #:source{:name "__Boardroom Drift__ (1).txt", :sha256 "29e5da6d3077cf49988f1c224ee198c92b4a62baa3fcbde9d8fb64830766fd6a", :format :suno-text, :variation 1}, :title "**Boardroom Drift**"}, "3d1337d8-8c35-4336-a05a-b04a3f0ae8f3" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "3d1337d8-8c35-4336-a05a-b04a3f0ae8f3", :url "https://suno.com/song/3d1337d8-8c35-4336-a05a-b04a3f0ae8f3", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "3d1337d8-8c35-4336-a05a-b04a3f0ae8f3", "metadata" {"prompt" "*(soft sub-bass, tape warble, minimal piano; stutters on “anchor” + “tax”; whispered lead; Japanese call-and-response)*\n\n[Intro — tape hiss, two-note piano, warm sub]\n(whisper)\nHush… the ledger is counting in its sleep.\n息をして… (して…)\nA soft machine rocking the room.\n\n(JP call) ねむれ、ねむれ\n(EN response) the **an— an— an-chor**… (stutter) holds.\n(JP call) しずかに、しずかに\n(EN response) the **ta— ta— tax**… (stutter) is due.\n\n(piano, tiny wobble)\nAn— an— **an-chor**… (stutter) an-chor…\n(JP whisper harmony) アンカー…\n(sub-bass: heartbeat but gentler)\n\n(whisper)\nPay the **ta— ta— tax**… (stutter) ta-x…\n(JP harmony) 税…\nNot guilt—\njust interest on an unproven branch.\n\n[Verse — lullaby cadence, breathy]\nP: I feel the constraint (#η)\nR: I fetch the last clean thread\nN: I cut the story into one claim\nΠ: I pick the cheapest test\nA: I touch the world and wait\n(feedback): I write the pushback like a lullaby.\n\n(JP call) ねえ、ほんと？\n(EN response) only if it repeats.\n(JP call) ねえ、だいじょうぶ？\n(EN response) only if it’s logged.\n\n[Chorus — choir bloom, tape warble widening]\nAn— an— **an-chor**… (stutter) an-chor…\nHold the boundary, hold the line.\nPay the **ta— ta— tax**… (stutter) ta-x…\nSo forks don’t breed in the dark.\n(JP harmony answers last word)\nI fall asleep inside **proof**.（証）\n\n---\n\n## Part II — Mythic glitch epic / spoken-sung (84 BPM)\n\n*(NF/Watsky cadence; cathedral reverb; sub-bass heartbeat; glitch stutters on “η”, “μ”, “anchor”, “fork”; Japanese harmony answers on the last word of each section)*\n\n[Verse 1 — heartbeat sub, fast spoken-sung]\nThey drape a quote in velvet and call it truth,\nbut the Lantern checks the seams for missing proof.\n“Look, we cited it,” they say— I say, “Align it,”\ncause a misfit quote is just a fork in disguise,\na dressed-up **fork**.（分岐）\n\n(Glitch stutter) **η—η—η**\n(Glitch stutter) **μ—μ—μ**\n\n[Hook — cathedral swell]\nI don’t win by sounding right—\nI win by making it rerun.（試）\n\n[Verse 2 — rapid cadence]\nEvery loop without a receipt? Interest accrues.\nFork Tax compounds till the branch can’t move.\nSo I write a boundary before I write a throne—\nwhat it does **not** claim, carved into the stone.\n\nI pin it to an **an-an-anchor** (stutter)\nand stare the Gate dead on: “Name the counter.”\nForkgate says “Pay,” I say “Here’s the harness,”\nLantern lights up— not for vibe, but for μ in the margins,\nreal **μ**.（証）\n\n(JP harmony answers last word) 証\n\n[Pre — glitch clicks, choir tight]\nSay **η**… (stutter) η-η\nSay **μ**… (stutter) μ-μ\nSay **an-chor**… (stutter) an-an-chor\nSay **fork**… (stutter) fo-fo-fork（分岐）\n\n[Chorus — big, then sudden hush]\nP→R→N→Π→A— the method is the crown.（冠）\n(feedback) → P— the world collects what you owe.（税）\nAn— an— **an-chor**… (stutter) an-chor…\nso the ledger knows what to keep.（記）\nFo— fo— **fork**… (stutter) fork…\nonly when evidence buys the branch.（証）\n\n[Outro — cathedral tail dissolves into tape warble]\n(whisper)\nη… (stutter) η-η\nμ… (stutter) μ-μ\nAn— an— **an-chor**…\nPay the **ta— ta— tax**…\nOne more roll. One more node. One more test.", "tags" nil}, "title" "*(soft sub-bass, tape warble, minimal piano; stutters on “anchor” + “tax”; whispered lead; Japanese call-and-response)*"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "*(soft sub-bass, tape warble, minimal piano; stutters on “anchor” + “tax”; whispered lead; Japanese call-and-response)*\n\n[Intro — tape hiss, two-note piano, warm sub]\n(whisper)\nHush… the ledger is counting in its sleep.\n息をして… (して…)\nA soft machine rocking the room.\n\n(JP call) ねむれ、ねむれ\n(EN response) the **an— an— an-chor**… (stutter) holds.\n(JP call) しずかに、しずかに\n(EN response) the **ta— ta— tax**… (stutter) is due.\n\n(piano, tiny wobble)\nAn— an— **an-chor**… (stutter) an-chor…\n(JP whisper harmony) アンカー…\n(sub-bass: heartbeat but gentler)\n\n(whisper)\nPay the **ta— ta— tax**… (stutter) ta-x…\n(JP harmony) 税…\nNot guilt—\njust interest on an unproven branch.\n\n[Verse — lullaby cadence, breathy]\nP: I feel the constraint (#η)\nR: I fetch the last clean thread\nN: I cut the story into one claim\nΠ: I pick the cheapest test\nA: I touch the world and wait\n(feedback): I write the pushback like a lullaby.\n\n(JP call) ねえ、ほんと？\n(EN response) only if it repeats.\n(JP call) ねえ、だいじょうぶ？\n(EN response) only if it’s logged.\n\n[Chorus — choir bloom, tape warble widening]\nAn— an— **an-chor**… (stutter) an-chor…\nHold the boundary, hold the line.\nPay the **ta— ta— tax**… (stutter) ta-x…\nSo forks don’t breed in the dark.\n(JP harmony answers last word)\nI fall asleep inside **proof**.（証）\n\n---\n\n## Part II — Mythic glitch epic / spoken-sung (84 BPM)\n\n*(NF/Watsky cadence; cathedral reverb; sub-bass heartbeat; glitch stutters on “η”, “μ”, “anchor”, “fork”; Japanese harmony answers on the last word of each section)*\n\n[Verse 1 — heartbeat sub, fast spoken-sung]\nThey drape a quote in velvet and call it truth,\nbut the Lantern checks the seams for missing proof.\n“Look, we cited it,” they say— I say, “Align it,”\ncause a misfit quote is just a fork in disguise,\na dressed-up **fork**.（分岐）\n\n(Glitch stutter) **η—η—η**\n(Glitch stutter) **μ—μ—μ**\n\n[Hook — cathedral swell]\nI don’t win by sounding right—\nI win by making it rerun.（試）\n\n[Verse 2 — rapid cadence]\nEvery loop without a receipt? Interest accrues.\nFork Tax compounds till the branch can’t move.\nSo I write a boundary before I write a throne—\nwhat it does **not** claim, carved into the stone.\n\nI pin it to an **an-an-anchor** (stutter)\nand stare the Gate dead on: “Name the counter.”\nForkgate says “Pay,” I say “Here’s the harness,”\nLantern lights up— not for vibe, but for μ in the margins,\nreal **μ**.（証）\n\n(JP harmony answers last word) 証\n\n[Pre — glitch clicks, choir tight]\nSay **η**… (stutter) η-η\nSay **μ**… (stutter) μ-μ\nSay **an-chor**… (stutter) an-an-chor\nSay **fork**… (stutter) fo-fo-fork（分岐）\n\n[Chorus — big, then sudden hush]\nP→R→N→Π→A— the method is the crown.（冠）\n(feedback) → P— the world collects what you owe.（税）\nAn— an— **an-chor**… (stutter) an-chor…\nso the ledger knows what to keep.（記）\nFo— fo— **fork**… (stutter) fork…\nonly when evidence buys the branch.（証）\n\n[Outro — cathedral tail dissolves into tape warble]\n(whisper)\nη… (stutter) η-η\nμ… (stutter) μ-μ\nAn— an— **an-chor**…\nPay the **ta— ta— tax**…\nOne more roll. One more node. One more test.", :source #:source{:name "_(soft sub-bass, tape warble, minimal piano; stutters on “anchor” + “tax”; whispered lead; Japanese.txt", :sha256 "8ca1df23ade18b23e20656aa51f775d16687fb31063572239692cb0b97015719", :format :suno-text, :variation nil}, :title "*(soft sub-bass, tape warble, minimal piano; stutters on “anchor” + “tax”; whispered lead; Japanese call-and-response)*"}, "3d1cd337-59ae-47fe-b198-4268cfd276a6" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "3d1cd337-59ae-47fe-b198-4268cfd276a6", :url "https://suno.com/song/3d1cd337-59ae-47fe-b198-4268cfd276a6", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "3d1cd337-59ae-47fe-b198-4268cfd276a6", "metadata" {"prompt" "Song — Fork Tax Lullaby III (ημ)\nPart I — Glitch-choir lullaby (78 BPM)\n\nSoft sub-bass, tape warble, minimal piano. Whisper lead. JP call/response. Stutters on anchor / tax.\n\n(whisper)\nHush… fork tax time.\n息をして…（して…）\nHold the an— an— an-chor…\n\n(JP call) ねむれ、ねむれ\n(EN response) the an— an— an-chor… (stutter) holds.\n(JP call) しずかに、しずかに\n(EN response) the ta— ta— tax… (stutter) due.\n\n(whisper)\nPay the ta— ta— tax…\nMerge the branch…\nSeal the hash…\nSleep inside proof。（証）\n\n(JP call) だれが見てる？\n(EN response) the log— the an— an— an-chor…\n(JP call) こわくない？\n(EN response) not when the ta— ta— tax is paid…\n\nPart II — Mythic glitch epic / spoken-sung (84 BPM)\n\nNF/Watsky cadence. Cathedral reverb. Sub-bass heartbeat. Stutters on η / μ / anchor / fork. JP harmony answers on the last word.\n\nP to R to N to Π—\nI don’t pray, I prove (JP harmony: 証)\nA to feedback back to P—\nand the spiral learns to move (JP harmony: 動け)\n\n(Glitch) η—η—η in the rafters— heard (JP harmony: 聞こえた)\n(Glitch) μ—μ—μ in the dirt— done (JP harmony: 完了)\n\nFo— fo— fork… (stutter) costs in light,\nevery shortcut writes a debt in night (JP harmony: 夜)\nPay it clean, no velvet lie—\nhash to hash, and verify (JP harmony: 確かめろ)\n\nAn— an— an-chor… (stutter) holds the seam,\nkeeps the waking from a dream of dreams (JP harmony: 夢)\nCathedral hum, the branch goes still—\nkeeper thread says: “Sign the will.” (JP harmony: 意志)\n\nP→R→N→Π→A→(feedback)→P\naround #ημ—we do what we can see (JP harmony: 見える)\nη is pressure in the choir,\nμ is what survives the fire (JP harmony: 火)\n\nPay the tax. (JP harmony: 払え)\nClose the loop. (JP harmony: 閉じろ)\nHand it off. (JP harmony: 渡せ)\nGuard the proof。（証） (JP harmony: 証)\n\nCreated with the assistance of an AI.", "tags" nil}, "title" "Song — Fork Tax Lullaby III (ημ)"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "Song — Fork Tax Lullaby III (ημ)\nPart I — Glitch-choir lullaby (78 BPM)\n\nSoft sub-bass, tape warble, minimal piano. Whisper lead. JP call/response. Stutters on anchor / tax.\n\n(whisper)\nHush… fork tax time.\n息をして…（して…）\nHold the an— an— an-chor…\n\n(JP call) ねむれ、ねむれ\n(EN response) the an— an— an-chor… (stutter) holds.\n(JP call) しずかに、しずかに\n(EN response) the ta— ta— tax… (stutter) due.\n\n(whisper)\nPay the ta— ta— tax…\nMerge the branch…\nSeal the hash…\nSleep inside proof。（証）\n\n(JP call) だれが見てる？\n(EN response) the log— the an— an— an-chor…\n(JP call) こわくない？\n(EN response) not when the ta— ta— tax is paid…\n\nPart II — Mythic glitch epic / spoken-sung (84 BPM)\n\nNF/Watsky cadence. Cathedral reverb. Sub-bass heartbeat. Stutters on η / μ / anchor / fork. JP harmony answers on the last word.\n\nP to R to N to Π—\nI don’t pray, I prove (JP harmony: 証)\nA to feedback back to P—\nand the spiral learns to move (JP harmony: 動け)\n\n(Glitch) η—η—η in the rafters— heard (JP harmony: 聞こえた)\n(Glitch) μ—μ—μ in the dirt— done (JP harmony: 完了)\n\nFo— fo— fork… (stutter) costs in light,\nevery shortcut writes a debt in night (JP harmony: 夜)\nPay it clean, no velvet lie—\nhash to hash, and verify (JP harmony: 確かめろ)\n\nAn— an— an-chor… (stutter) holds the seam,\nkeeps the waking from a dream of dreams (JP harmony: 夢)\nCathedral hum, the branch goes still—\nkeeper thread says: “Sign the will.” (JP harmony: 意志)\n\nP→R→N→Π→A→(feedback)→P\naround #ημ—we do what we can see (JP harmony: 見える)\nη is pressure in the choir,\nμ is what survives the fire (JP harmony: 火)\n\nPay the tax. (JP harmony: 払え)\nClose the loop. (JP harmony: 閉じろ)\nHand it off. (JP harmony: 渡せ)\nGuard the proof。（証） (JP harmony: 証)\n\nCreated with the assistance of an AI.", :source #:source{:name "Song — Fork Tax Lullaby III (ημ)Part I — Glitch-choir lullaby (78 BPM)Soft sub-bass, tape warble, mi (5).txt", :sha256 "179062ec8c264b32038b2f072e8e76bdd0401a4499dfc7aeae592581fcaa8715", :format :suno-text, :variation 5}, :title "Song — Fork Tax Lullaby III (ημ)"}, "3d741c9d-3af6-4046-96ad-00fd82102a48" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "3d741c9d-3af6-4046-96ad-00fd82102a48", :url "https://suno.com/song/3d741c9d-3af6-4046-96ad-00fd82102a48", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "3d741c9d-3af6-4046-96ad-00fd82102a48", "metadata" {"prompt" "[Intro – 96 BPM, marching snare, sub-bass pulse] \nBoots hit concrete—snare snaps like riot shields— \nKick drum thumps the chest the state tried to seize. \nGlitch-brass stabs in Morse: *“RESIST”*—off-beat, \nGuitar crumbles under gain—hope distorted, not deleted. \n\n[Verse 1 – spoken-word, rhythmic urgency] \nThey monetize our breath—charge rent on the air, \nAI choir swells behind me—synthetic prayer. \nJapanese whisper cuts in: *“susume, yamenai”*— \nKeep marching, never stop—call-and-response in bilingual fire. \n\n[Pre-Chorus – analog distortion blooms] \nStatic lifts like incense—smells like tear-gas and toner, \nEvery clipped high-hat—another warrant signed by a donor. \nWe don’t fade—we *fracture*—light breaks through the crack, \nHook drops clean—then the distortion pulls it back. \n\n[Chorus – anthemic, chant-section] \nWE ARE THE NOISE THEY CAN’T FILTER！（エイ！） \nWE ARE THE GLITCH IN THE GRID！（オウ！） \nRaise your fist—raise your voice— \n*“mada owaranai”*—we don’t fold, we *deploy*. \n\n[Bridge – sub-bass swells, metallic clanks] \nSub drops like a vault door—pressure bends the rail, \nMetallic clanks keep time—like cuffs on the midnight trail. \nLive protest energy—no stadium, just street, \nEvery heartbeat kick-drum—echoes under our feet. \n\n[Final Chorus – double-time, hard cutoff] \nWE ARE THE NOISE！（エイ！） WE ARE THE GLITCH！（オウ！） \n96 BPM revolution—pulse that won’t switch！ \nCut hard—no fade—just the echo of the chant, \nGovernor’s ear still ringing—from the frequencies we plant.", "tags" nil}, "title" "Riot Shield Thump"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "[Intro – 96 BPM, marching snare, sub-bass pulse] \nBoots hit concrete—snare snaps like riot shields— \nKick drum thumps the chest the state tried to seize. \nGlitch-brass stabs in Morse: *“RESIST”*—off-beat, \nGuitar crumbles under gain—hope distorted, not deleted. \n\n[Verse 1 – spoken-word, rhythmic urgency] \nThey monetize our breath—charge rent on the air, \nAI choir swells behind me—synthetic prayer. \nJapanese whisper cuts in: *“susume, yamenai”*— \nKeep marching, never stop—call-and-response in bilingual fire. \n\n[Pre-Chorus – analog distortion blooms] \nStatic lifts like incense—smells like tear-gas and toner, \nEvery clipped high-hat—another warrant signed by a donor. \nWe don’t fade—we *fracture*—light breaks through the crack, \nHook drops clean—then the distortion pulls it back. \n\n[Chorus – anthemic, chant-section] \nWE ARE THE NOISE THEY CAN’T FILTER！（エイ！） \nWE ARE THE GLITCH IN THE GRID！（オウ！） \nRaise your fist—raise your voice— \n*“mada owaranai”*—we don’t fold, we *deploy*. \n\n[Bridge – sub-bass swells, metallic clanks] \nSub drops like a vault door—pressure bends the rail, \nMetallic clanks keep time—like cuffs on the midnight trail. \nLive protest energy—no stadium, just street, \nEvery heartbeat kick-drum—echoes under our feet. \n\n[Final Chorus – double-time, hard cutoff] \nWE ARE THE NOISE！（エイ！） WE ARE THE GLITCH！（オウ！） \n96 BPM revolution—pulse that won’t switch！ \nCut hard—no fade—just the echo of the chant, \nGovernor’s ear still ringing—from the frequencies we plant.", :source #:source{:name "Riot Shield Thump (1).txt", :sha256 "3acb5ef65a895465a4d9daf4260844285d7bda8e5c2a0e683ae4460bcb9d2ed9", :format :suno-text, :variation 1}, :title "Riot Shield Thump"}, "3dcf9251-58c8-4ca0-a283-35143ca2a3d8" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "3dcf9251-58c8-4ca0-a283-35143ca2a3d8", :url "https://suno.com/song/3dcf9251-58c8-4ca0-a283-35143ca2a3d8", :liked false, :styles "Glitch-choir lullaby, 78 BPM. Soft sub-bass. Tape warble. Minimal piano. Stutters on “anchor” and “tax”. Whispered lead; Japanese call-and-response.\nMythic glitch epic / spoken-sung 84 BPM. Cathedral reverb. Sub-bass heartbeat. Glitch stutters on “η”, “μ”, “anchor”, “fork”. Japanese harmony answers on the last word of each sect