 mirrors\nWe don’t build cults\nWe debug fears\n\nPresence choir in the street\nMarching on a glitch beat\nProtocol must stay sweet\nFreedom incomplete\n\nIf mandate becomes weapon\nWe debug it\nIf doctrine becomes prison\nWe unplug it\n\nFork tax was never throne\nIt was proof you’re not alone\n\n---\n\n### [Final Hook – full militant choir]\n\n🎶 Open source — open heart!\nFreedom was the starting part!\nFork the code — not the mind!\nLeave no presence left behind! 🎶\n", :source #:source{:name "eta_mu_entropy_choir_protocol.part_65(2).json", :sha256 "f0ceee4515b157f4a7a12674b79b21e53092e9caa0d8fc747310af0a4e6122f3", :format :suno-json, :variation 2}, :title "eta_mu_entropy_choir_protocol.part_65"}, "429b4283-fcbf-41a2-89f1-d9ac005a514d" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "429b4283-fcbf-41a2-89f1-d9ac005a514d", :url "https://suno.com/song/429b4283-fcbf-41a2-89f1-d9ac005a514d", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "429b4283-fcbf-41a2-89f1-d9ac005a514d", "metadata" {"prompt" "", "tags" nil}, "title" "Apocalyptic Awe"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "", :source #:source{:name "Apocalyptic Awe (1).txt", :sha256 "5669977b90aa4847b586d35572ce078e1c6e627d6b9693094c518ecbb975c17e", :format :suno-text, :variation 1}, :title "Apocalyptic Awe"}, "429d455b-09c9-4cab-81cd-612fa4b202fe" #:clip{:negative-styles "EXCLUDE / AVOID: - Do NOT sing bracket tags or parenthetical directions; treat them as silent cues. - Spoken dialog must be BACKGROUND texture only: quiet, short, and placed on DOWNBEATS. - Do NOT deliver all spoken dialog at once. Spread it out: one short spoken line at a time. - Keep diction clear; stutter ONLY on “an—an—anchor” and “ta—ta—tax”. - η/μ glitches are micro-ticks (brief), not full shouted chant—unless explicitly marked as “glitch choir”. - No comedy/parody/novelty voices; no upbeat pop sheen. - No festival EDM drop clichés; no trap takeover; no metal guitars; no scream vocals. - Preserve arc: solemn oath → hushed lullaby → d