xed **me**.\n\n**[OUTRO — calm, glowing]**\ngate.open…\ngate.close…\nbetween… between…\n(soft chant fading) nu… nu… nu…\nand in the crack where the whisper hides—\nthe duck still carries fire.\n", :source #:source{:name "NU (THE HERESY OF BEING BETWEEN).json", :sha256 "2402387bc5a635fbee48515a8e1ec6811499741993d618ff1f6e13fe943cce34", :format :suno-json, :variation nil}, :title "NU (THE HERESY OF BEING BETWEEN)"}, "453fda63-2231-4760-b82a-1b4ceedca538" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "453fda63-2231-4760-b82a-1b4ceedca538", :url "https://suno.com/song/453fda63-2231-4760-b82a-1b4ceedca538", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "453fda63-2231-4760-b82a-1b4ceedca538", "metadata" {"prompt" "[singer A]\nThe city hears through brick and steam\nThrough broken sleep and market screams\nThrough alley prayer and factory cough\nThrough all the names the rich rubbed off\n\nSome carry bread and some carry debt\nSome carry all the things they cannot get\nSome hold a room with six inside\nSome hold a key and still have nowhere safe to hide\n\nWindow to window\nWire to wire\nNeed moves quicker\nThan the language of desire\n\n[transition]\n\n[singer B]\nTray against marble\nKey against lock\nInk on the margin\nTick of the clock\n\nA cook knows hunger\nA clerk knows names\nA guard looks downward\nAnd leaves with stains\n\nSoft treason travels\nHand over hand\nNot through the anthem\nBut through what was planned\n\nThrough the service hall\nThrough the papers thin\nWhat the court keeps out\nStill finds a way in\n\n[transition]\n\n[singer A]\nThe city hears everything\nCoins, commands, and wedding rings\nBootsteps, bargains, fear, and rain\nNothing here is small when pressed through pain\nThe city keeps the voices when the mouths go still\nThe wind remembers what the law will never will\n\nCrowd divided, crowd one body\nHands in conflict, hands in trade\nEvery kindness hits a limit\nEvery shelter has a grade\n\nThe city hears everything\nThe lifted voice, th