ythm Design:**\n\n* Subdued, distant kick (heartbeat feel)\n* Minimal brushed snare or soft metallic taps\n* Sparse glitch accents like flickering fluorescent lights\n* Long silence pockets between phrases\n\n**Texture Palette:**\n\n* Felt piano (close mic, audible hammer noise)\n* Low warehouse reverb tail fading into emptiness\n* Airy choir pads stretched almost beyond recognition\n* Soft sub-bass warmth instead of pressure\n* Field recording: faint wind through broken windows\n\n**Vocal Direction:**\n\n* Intimate lead vocal, nearly whispered\n* Japanese harmony layers answering English lines\n* No aggressive stacking; emotional restraint\n\n**Mood:** Dawn after intensity. Emotional recalibration. Cool concrete, pale light, breath steadying. Vulnerable but grounded.\n\n---\n\n# LYRICS\n\n## INTRO — Dawn Air\n\n(soft wind through broken glass)\n\n息を吸う\ncolder now\n\nThe warehouse is quiet.\nNo lights.\nNo choir.\n\nJust dust\nand morning.\n\n---\n\n## VERSE 1\n\nLast night we burned like neon veins\n今はただの静かな床\n\nConcrete remembers everything\nbut it doesn’t judge.\n\nI trace the cracks with my finger\nlike constellations that survived\n\n\"Are you still here?\"\n\nまだ。\n\n---\n\n## PRE-CHORUS\n\n吸って — steady\n吐いて — slower\n\nThe body returns to itself\n\n神経が静まる\nlike water after stones\n\n---\n\n## CHORUS\n\nAfter the ritual\nwe are only breath\n\nNo altar\nno anthem\njust pulse under skin\n\n儀式のあとで\nwe stay\n\nNot shining\nNot breaking\n\nJust alive.\n\n---\n\n## VERSE 2\n\nPiano notes fall like pale light\n鍵盤がやわらかく鳴る\n\nThe chromatic knives are gone\nonly warmth remains\n\nI used to think transcendence\nhad to be loud\n\nBut maybe it’s this —\n\nstaying.\n\n---\n\n## BRIDGE — Silence Embrace\n\n(beat drops out)\n\nListen.\n\nThe quiet isn’t empty.\n\nこの静けさは\n痛みの裏側じゃない\n\nIt’s what’s left\nwhen fear dissolves.\n\n---\n\n## FINAL CHORUS\n\nAfter the ritual\nwe are only breath\n\nWarehouse sky turning silver\n\n儀式のあとで\nwe remain\n\nC minor shadow\nF minor bloom\n\nNo