ation-mindfuck/ c", "can_remix" true, "negative_tags" "Against “pretty graphs that lie”: require S3 anchors on every non-trivial edge/claim. Against “forks everywhere”: intent-gating + ranked forks + explicit rationale per fork. Against “entity mush”: treat S5 (resolution) as a first-class, versioned dataset with audits.If an edge has no anchor → it’s invalid output (fail the build next pass).  If forks proliferate → tighten intent ontology + require event-backed intent.  If entity mush returns → treat alias merges as reviewed inputs, not derived guessesIf an intent event can’t be anchored → treat it as invalid output (drop it / fail build next pass).  If intent feels “over-saturated” (too many 255s) → adjust the strength curve in the analyzer (still stays 0..255).If a graph edge has no anchor → treat it as not real (drop it / fail builds next iteration).  If forks explode → raise the intent threshold + require explicit rationale per fork.  If entities blur → keep S5 resolution as versioned inputs (aliases/merges are reviewed deltas)..", "prompt" "# songbook — ημ (intent compression you can feel)\n\nthese are **original** songs written to encode the box constraints as music:\nanchors over vibes, forks gated by intent, and s5 resolution as ritual.\n\neach song includes:\n- a production prompt (suno-friendly)\n- lyrics\n- an “anchor refrain” (a line you can cite as the song’s thesis)\n\n---\n\n## 1) between η and μ\n\n**style prompt:** mythic glitch-choral synth ballad. 84 bpm. cathedral reverb. soft sub-bass heartbeat. sparse drums that arrive late. whispered english + japanese harmony. glitch-stutters on “η” and “μ”.\n\n**anchor refrain:** *no claim without anchor.*\n\n**lyrics**\n\n[verse]\ni said a word and the world left a tail,\nreverb made of things i cannot tell.\nη in the muscle, hidden in the bone,\nμ in the motion, the proof in the stone.\n\n[pre]\nif it can’t be pointed to,\nit can’t be used to move you.\n\n[chorus]\nno claim without anchor,\nno crown without weight.\nbetween η and μ\nis where liars congregate.\nso i sing the checksum,\ni sing the gate:\nno claim without anchor,\nno claim without anchor.\n\n[bridge — 日本語]\n見えない状態(η) 震える胸\n行動の証(μ) 石の上へ\n曖昧を捨てて 立つよ ここで\n「根拠(アンカー)なし」じゃ 進めないって\n\n---\n\n## 2) pretty graphs lie\n\n**style prompt:** industrial glitch-rap. 96 bpm half-time. distorted bass, clipped snares, harsh hi-hats. spoken delivery with sharp pauses. crowd-chant hook.\n\n**anchor refrain:** *edges are claims. claims need receipts.*\n\n**lyrics**\n\n[verse]\nyou drew me a graph with a halo of nodes,\nbut where’s the bolt that broke the road?\nwhere’s the sentence, where’s the scene,\nwhere’s the witness in between?\n\n[hook]\nedges are claims—(say it)\nclaims need receipts—(prove it)\npretty graphs lie—(burn it)\nanchors, or sleep.\n\n\n\n(see songbook_eta_mu.md for full set.)\n", "duration" 189.76, "type" "gen", "model_badges" {"songcard" {"dark" {"background_color" "0000004D", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}, "display_name" "v5", "light" {"background_color" "0000004D", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}}, "songrow" {"dark" {"background_color" "FD429C40", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}, "display_name" "v5", "light" {"background_color" "FD429C1A", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}}}, "has_stem" false, "make_instrumental" false, "refund_credits" false}, "title" "Intent is now **compressed densely** and"}, :duration 189.76, :controls nil, :lyrics "# songbook — ημ (intent compression you can feel)\n\nthese are **original** songs written to encode the box constraints as music:\nanchors over vibes, forks gated by intent, and s5 resolution as ritual.\n\neach song includes:\n- a production prompt (suno-friendly)\n- lyrics\n- an “anchor refrain” (a line you can cite as the song’s thesis)\n\n---\n\n## 1) between η and μ\n\n**style prompt:** mythic glitch-choral synth ballad. 84 bpm. cathedral reverb. soft sub-bass heartbeat. sparse drums that arr