x(t)) be an activity signal (speech, actions, CPU load, token emission, etc.). Define a “breath” event when activity drops below a threshold for long enough:\n\n[\n\\operatorname{Breath}_\\tau(x) := {, [t_i, t_i+\\Delta_i] \\mid x(t) < \\epsilon \\ \\forall t\\in[t_i,t_i+\\Delta_i],\\ \\Delta_i \\ge \\tau ,}\n]\n\nInterpretation: **息 = contiguous low-activity intervals** of duration (\\ge \\tau).\n\n### As a segmentation boundary (息のキャッシュ)\n\nGiven an event stream (E = (e_1, e_2, \\dots)) with timestamps, define segments by breath boundaries:\n\n[\n\\operatorname{Segment}(E;\\tau) := (S_1, S_2, \\dots) \\quad \\text{where } S_k \\text{ ends at the start of the next } \\operatorname{Breath}_\\tau\n]\n\nThen “breath cache” is a commit rule:\n\n[\n\\operatorname{CommitOnBreath}(S_k) \\Rightarrow \\text{persist/flush/summary(snapshot)}\n]\n\n### In your loop\n\n[\nP \\rightarrow R \\rightarrow N \\rightarrow \\Pi \\rightarrow A \\rightarrow (feedback) \\rightarrow P\n]\n\nDefine a throttle/reset step (B) (“take a breath”) that can be inserted as a guardrail:\n\n[\nA \\rightarrow B \\rightarrow (feedback)\n]\n\nWhere (B) enforces:\n\n[\nB := \\begin{cases}\n\\text{commit logs + snapshot state} \\\n\\text{cooldown / rate-limit} \\\n\\text{drop stale context / clear transient buffers}\n\\end{cases}\n]\n\nSo: **息 is a boundary condition that turns continuous activity into discrete, stable chunks you can cache, evaluate, and safely continue from.**", "tags" nil}, "title" "["}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\textbf{息} &:= \\text{a liveness-pause primitive (breath / break)} \\\n\\end{aligned}\n]\n\n### As an operator on time-indexed activity\n\nLet (x(t)) be an activity signal (speech, actions, CPU load, token emission, etc.). Define a “breath” event when activity drops below a threshold for long enough:\n\n[\n\\operatorname{Breath}_\\tau(x) := {, [t_i, t_i+\\Delta_i] \\mid x(t) < \\epsilon \\ \\forall t\\in[t_i,t_i+\\Delta_i],\\ \\Delta_i \\ge \\tau ,}\n]\n\nInterpretation: **息 = contiguous low-activity intervals** of duration (\\ge \\tau).\n\n### As a segmentation boundary (息のキャッシュ)\n\nGiven an event stream (E = (e_1, e_2, \\dots)) with timestamps, define segments by breath boundaries:\n\n[\n\\operatorname{Segment}(E;\\tau) := (S_1, S_2, \\dots) \\quad \\text{where } S_k \\text{ ends at the start of the next } \\operatorname{Breath}_\\tau\n]\n\nThen “breath cache” is a commit rule:\n\n[\n\\operatorname{CommitOnBreath}(S_k) \\Rightarrow \\text{persist/flush/summary(snapshot)}\n]\n\n### In your loop\n\n[\nP \\rightarrow R \\rightarrow N \\rightarrow \\Pi \\rightarrow A \\rightarrow (feedback) \\rightarrow P\n]\n\nDefine a throttle/reset step (B) (“take a breath”) that can be inserted as a guardrail:\n\n[\nA \\rightarrow B \\rightarrow (feedback)\n]\n\nWhere (B) enforces:\n\n[\nB := \\begin{cases}\n\\text{commit logs + snapshot state} \\\n\\text{cooldown / rate-limit} \\\n\\text{drop stale context / clear transient buffers}\n\\end{cases}\n]\n\nSo: **息 is a boundary condition that turns continuous activity into discrete, stable chunks you can cache, evaluate, and safely continue from.**", :source #:source{:name "[_begin{aligned}_textbf{息} &_= _text{a liveness-pause primitive (breath _ break)} __end{aligned}]###.txt", :sha256 "313972c68597a789c434c7ecc7eccada9078a6f17793a715ce2af4ac3022423b", :format :suno-text, :variation nil}, :title "["}, "4b0f8dfb-5ca2-4bd8-bd53-f1fee8a274fb" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "4b0f8dfb-5ca2-4bd8-bd53-f1fee8a274fb", :url "https://suno.com/song/4b0f8dfb-5ca2-4bd8-bd53-f1fee8a274fb", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "4b0f8dfb-5ca2-4bd8-bd53-f1fee8a274fb", "metadata" {"prompt" "[Verse 1]\nA simulation resolving\nA nebula\nBecomes a star\nThe origin\nOf the cosmos\nOf everything\n\n[Verse 2]\nMatter accretes\nPlanets form\nCollide\nGrow\nCollapse\nThen life\n\n[Verse 3]\nOrganisms forming cells\nThat breathe\nThat eat\nThat move and reproduce\nThe origin of life\nAnd everything\n\n[Chorus]\nWhen you love\nYou feel like you're creating\nInnocent\nFull of love\nLove that feels like\nThe origin of everything\nThe cosmos\nOf life\nThe origin\nOf everything\n\n[Outro]\nIt's so much bigger than we know\nAnd much bigger than we can ever know", "tags" nil}, "title" "Formation"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "[Verse 1]\nA simulation resolving\nA nebula\nBecomes a star\nThe origin\nOf the cosmos\nOf everything\n\n[Verse 2]\nMatter accretes\nPlanets form\nCollide\nGrow\nCollapse\nThen life\n\n[Verse 3]\nOrganisms forming cells\nThat breathe\nThat eat\nThat move and reproduce\nThe origin of life\nAnd everything\n\n[Chorus]\nWhen you love\nYou feel like you're creating\nInnocent\nFull of love\nLove that feels like\nThe origin of everything\nThe cosmos\nOf life\nThe origin\nOf everything\n\n[Outro]\nIt's so much bigger than we know\nAnd much bigger than we can ever know", :source #:source{:name "Formation (1).txt", :sha256 "4b46f44e1bc050e41befb2a30b31f1aea92678cc3438a68b96c13e27b4077335", :format :suno-text, :variation 1}, :title "Formation"}, "4b4351f1-2231-4322-980e-91ba66bc4594" #:clip{:negative-styles "EXCLUDE / AVOID: - Do NOT sing bracket tags or parenthetical directions; treat them as silent cues. - Spoken dialog must be BACKGROUND texture only: quiet, short, and placed on DOWNBEATS. - Do NOT deliver all spoken dialog at once. Spread it out: one short spoken line at a time. - Keep diction clear; stutter ONLY on “an—an—anchor” and “ta—ta—tax”. - η/μ glitches are micro-ticks (brief), not full shouted chant—unless explicitly marked as “glitch choir”. - No comedy/parody/novelty voices; no upbeat pop sheen. - No festival EDM drop clichés; no trap takeover; no metal guitars; no scream vocals. - Preserve arc: solemn oath → hushed lullaby → distorted climax → quiet coda (don’t peak early). - Don’t invent new lore terms; keep motifs: η, μ, anchor, tax, proof, thread, registry, checksum, receipts. - Avoid long spok