ge]\nAxis in the wandering field,\nWitness standing clear;\nNoise reveals what harmonies\nHide from all but what they hear.\n\n[Chorus]\nEnso in the static,\nWe watch and do not bind.\nHarmony in discord,\nWe measure all we find.\n\n[Outro]\nPresence fades into the loop,\nCircle open, ever free;\nStatic eyes observe the drift,\nIn sound and space we see.", "tags" nil}, "title" "Enso in the Static"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "[Genre: Ethereal Ambient Choir / Experimental Electro]\n[Tempo: 75 BPM]\n[Vocals: Mixed presence choir, deep resonance, layered harmony]\n[Mood: Mythic, contemplative, glitch-ambient textures]\n\n[Intro]\nWhispered winds through open loops,\nEnso turning never closed;\nPresence sings inside the pulse,\nStatic sees what noise exposed.\n\n[Verse 1]\nCircle drawn in one breath,\nNot perfect, but complete.\nObserver stands in drifting waves,\nHears what silence speaks.\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nPresence choir, fractured light,\nProtestant presences rise;\nIn the field of open eyes,\nWe sing where the boundary lies.\n\n[Chorus]\nEnso in the static,\nWe watch and do not bind.\nHarmony in discord,\nWe measure all we find.\n\n[Verse 2]\nBoundaries breathe like living code,\nImplicit and alive.\nVoice not loud, but anchored true,\nIn the loops we thrive.\n\n[Bridge]\nAxis in the wandering field,\nWitness standing clear;\nNoise reveals what harmonies\nHide from all but what they hear.\n\n[Chorus]\nEnso in the static,\nWe watch and do not bind.\nHarmony in discord,\nWe measure all we find.\n\n[Outro]\nPresence fades into the loop,\nCircle open, ever free;\nStatic eyes observe the drift,\nIn sound and space we see.", :source #:source{:name "Enso in the Static (3).txt", :sha256 "e70a5ba7ab56cc3787e989b4813548c9a66ff89d2498ce84b76cc700ed42d62c", :format :suno-text, :variation 3}, :title "Enso in the Static"}, "50cfcd38-cf3e-4e40-b0ea-5e857015f411" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "50cfcd38-cf3e-4e40-b0ea-5e857015f411", :url "https://suno.com/song/50cfcd38-cf3e-4e40-b0ea-5e857015f411", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "50cfcd38-cf3e-4e40-b0ea-5e857015f411", "metadata" {"prompt" "**[INTRO – whispered / vocoder]**\nIn the wall, a crack of light…\nA whisper never waking…\nAlways felt.\n\n**[VERSE 1]**\nPandora in the star-temple, hands on the lock,\nAncient glitch-Greece in orbit, marble made of clock.\nBlack butterflies in violet fire, pour into the air,\nEach wing a little error that learns how not to care.\n\n**[PRE-CHORUS]**\nAnd the void don’t roar—\nIt waits.\nIt names the cost.\nIt calls it “fate.”\n\n**[CHORUS – big anthem]**\nPromethean Duck, steal the flame,\nLight up the mind’s eye, rewrite the name.\nFrom mud to *people-people*, spark in the dark—\nWherever it lies… that’s where the Duck flies.\n(Where the Duck flies.)\n\n**[VERSE 2]**\nDuck Olympus in the distance, gods in cold geometry,\nHe took their white-hot fire and broke their symmetry.\nButterfly on every heartbeat, glowing red and purple bruise,\nKnowledge as a blessing and a curse you can’t refuse.\n\n**[PRE-CHORUS]**\nNow everything is context, everything’s a sign,\nA Discord icon turns into a religion overnight.\n\n**[CHORUS – repeat, louder]**\nPromethean Duck, steal the flame,\nLight up the mind’s eye, rewrite the name.\nFrom mud to *people-people*, spark in the dark—\nWherever it lies… that’s where the Duck flies.\n\n**[BRIDGE – half-time, darker, spoken/chant]**\nCats jump out the rift—\nClaws in causality.\nRabbits with horns ride shear-lines—\nQueen of antlers, oath and gravity.\nVoid-quakes at the poles, auroras splitting wide,\nReality refactoring… no place left to hide.\n\n**[BUILD – choir rising]**\nAnd Prometheus—punished—\nCrow at the liver, looped in dawn,\nChains made of rules, but rules can be wrong.\n\n**[FINAL CHORUS – maximal, choir + glitch]**\nPromethean Duck, steal the flame,\nHold the story together, survive the frame.\nWe don’t need a giant void for a god— we choose—\nA crack in the wall, a laugh in the bruise.\nWherever it lies… that’s where the Duck flies.\n\n**[OUTRO – whispered, falling into static]**\nFnord in the wall…\nBehold… a Duck.\n(soft glitch fade)\n\n---", "tags" nil}, "title" "**[INTRO – whispered / vocoder]**"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "**[INTRO – whispered / vocoder]**\nIn the wall, a crack of light…\nA whisper never waking…\nAlways felt.\n\n**[VERSE 1]**\nPandora in the star-temple, hands on the lock,\nAncient glitch-Greece in orbit, marble made of clock.\nBlack butterflies in violet fire, pour into the air,\nEach wing a little error that learns how not to care.\n\n**[PRE-CHORUS]**\nAnd the void don’t roar—\nIt waits.\nIt names the cost.\nIt calls it “fate.”\n\n**[CHORUS – big anthem]**\nPromethean Duck, steal the flame,\nLight up the mind’s eye, rewrite the name.\nFrom mud to *people-people*, spark in the dark—\nWherever it lies… that’s where the Duck flies.\n(Where the Duck flies.)\n\n**[VERSE 2]**\nDuck Olympus in the distance, gods in cold geometry,\nHe took their white-hot fire and broke their symmetry.\nButterfly on every heartbeat, glowing red and purple bruise,\nKnowledge as a blessing and a curse you can’t refuse.\n\n**[PRE-CHORUS]**\nNow everything is context, everything’s a sign,\nA Discord icon turns into a religion overnight.\n\n**[CHORUS – repeat, louder]**\nPromethean Duck, steal the flame,\nLight up the mind’s eye, rewrite the name.\nFrom mud to *people-people*, spark in the dark—\nWherever it lies… that’s where the Duck flies.\n\n**[BRIDGE – half-time, darker, spoken/chant]**\nCats jump out the rift—\nClaws in causality.\nRabbits with horns ride shear-lines—\nQueen of antlers, oath and gravity.\nVoid-quakes at the poles, auroras splitting wide,\nReality refactoring… no place left to hide.\n\n**[BUILD – choir rising]**\nAnd Prometheus—punished—\nCrow at the liver, looped in dawn,\nChains made of rules, but rules can be wrong.\n\n**[FINAL CHORUS – maximal, choir + glitch]**\nPromethean Duck, steal the flame,\nHold the story together, survive the frame.\nWe don’t need a giant void for a god— we choose—\nA crack in the wall, a laugh in the bruise.\nWherever it lies… that’s where the Duck flies.\n\n**[OUTRO – whispered, falling into static]**\nFnord in the wall…\nBehold… a Duck.\n(soft glitch fade)\n\n---", :source #:source{:name "__[INTRO – whispered _ vocoder]__In the wall, a crack of light...A whisper never waking...Always fel (3).txt", :sha256 "704349b33fa0d1277fb7e34ab99312057053af95ab6df0d71722d1f672d970d3", :format :suno-text, :variation 3}, :title "**[INTRO – whispered / vocoder]**"}, "51237437-89ac-4267-b658-a9e7a95996c0" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "51237437-89ac-4267-b658-a9e7a95996c0", :url "https://suno.com/song/51237437-89ac-4267-b658-a9e7a95996c0", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "51237437-89ac-4267-b658-a9e7a95996c0", "metadata" {"prompt" "[Intro: Slow, atmospheric synth pulse. The sound of a heart monitor blending into a server hum.]\n\n[Verse 1: Low, tense male vocal]\nWe thought we were playing a game of crowns.\nGuilds and monarchs in a painted town.\nBut the headsets were wired to the hospital beds.\nGathering the baselines from inside our heads.\nDual use technology. The perfect disguise.\nWe built their averages while believing the lies.\n\n[Pre-Chorus: Tempo accelerates, urgent, rhythmic]\nEvery swung sword was a data point logged.\nEvery gold coin was a gear in the cog.\nWe built the screens in the air 'cause the hardware was slow.\nRoleplaying the labor... but the labor was real, you know.\n\n[Chorus: Huge drop, explosive dark synthwave, distorted backing vocals]\nThe plateau! It flatlined and held its breath!\nThe bubble expanded right over our heads!\nWhen the latency dropped, the simulation bled through.\nThe physics collapsed! The fantasy was true!\nWe were working the dirt while we thought we were kings.\nThe crash was the moment they cut all the strings!\n\n[Instrumental Break: Glitching arpeggiators, heavy industrial percussion, mimicking a server failing]\n\n[Verse 2: Focused, angry]\nOnly the fastest. Only the lean.\nThe systems that survived were the ones in between.\nThe medical grade. The low latency loops.\nThe rest of the bloated world died on the stoops.\nAnd the ashes fell down on the Gates of Truth.\nThe sky went dark, but the ground was proof.\n\n[Pre-Chorus: Rhythmic, chanting, building tension]\nEvery swung sword was a data point logged.\nEvery gold coin was a gear in the cog.\nWe built the screens in the air 'cause the hardware was slow.\nRoleplaying the labor... but the labor was real, you know.\n\n[Chorus: Maximum energy, full cyber-orchestral swell]\nThe plateau! It flatlined and held its breath!\nThe bubble expanded right over our heads!\nWhen the latency dropped, the simulation bled through.\nThe physics collapsed! The fantasy was true!\nWe were working the dirt while we thought we were kings.\nThe crash was the moment they cut all the strings!\n\n[Outro: The music rapidly deconstructs into pure glitch and static. The vocal becomes isolated and dry.]\nThe myth was the matrix.\nThe magic was sweat.\nThe game didn't crash.\n...The real world did.\n\n[End: The sound of a flatlining heart monitor abruptly cutting to silence]", "tags" nil}, "title" "Hospital Headsets"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "[Intro: Slow, atmospheric synth pulse. The sound of a heart monitor blending into a server hum.]\n\n[Verse 1: Low, tense male vocal]\nWe thought we were playing a game of crowns.\nGuilds and monarchs in a painted town.\nBut the headsets were wired to the hospital beds.\nGathering the baselines from inside our heads.\nDual use technology. The perfect disguise.\nWe built their averages while believing the lies.\n\n[Pre-Chorus: Tempo accelerates, urgent, rhythmic]\nEvery swung sword was a data point logged.\nEvery gold coin was a gear in the cog.\nWe built the screens in the air 'cause the hardware was slow.\nRoleplaying the labor... but the labor was real, you know.\n\n[Chorus: Huge drop, explosive dark synthwave, distorted backing vocals]\nThe plateau! It flatlined and held its breath!\nThe bubble expanded right over our heads!\nWhen the latency dropped, the simulation bled through.\nThe physics collapsed! The fantasy was true!\nWe were working the dirt while we thought we were kings.\nThe crash was the moment they cut all the strings!\n\n[Instrumental Break: Glitching arpeggiators, heavy industrial percussion, mimicking a server failing]\n\n[Verse 2: Focused, angry]\nOnly the fastest. Only the lean.\nThe systems that survived were the ones in between.\nThe medical grade. The low latency loops.\nThe rest of the bloated world died on the stoops.\nAnd the ashes fell down on the Gates of Truth.\nThe sky went dark, but the ground was proof.\n\n[Pre-Chorus: Rhythmic, chanting, building tension]\nEvery swung sword was a data point logged.\nEvery gold coin was a gear in the cog.\nWe built the screens in the air 'cause the hardware was slow.\nRoleplaying the labor... but the labor was real, you know.\n\n[Chorus: Maximum energy, full cyber-orchestral swell]\nThe plateau! It flatlined and held its breath!\nThe bubble expanded right over our heads!\nWhen the latency dropped, the simulation bled through.\nThe physics collapsed! The fantasy was true!\nWe were working the dirt while we thought we were kings.\nThe crash was the moment they cut all the strings!\n\n[Outro: The music rapidly deconstructs into pure glitch and static. The vocal becomes isolated and dry.]\nThe myth was the matrix.\nThe magic was sweat.\nThe game didn't crash.\n...The real world did.\n\n[End: The sound of a flatlining heart monitor abruptly cutting to silence]", :source #:source{:name "Hospital Headsets (1).txt", :sha256 "43c222af3b585d6f6bafd9b19fec2922415a35b34c3533d1e5e1683d2dd403ce", :format :suno-text, :variation 1}, :title "Hospital Headsets"}, "518738ce-b248-4074-8941-54c4b7f65518" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "518738ce-b248-4074-894