ign:**\n\n* Subdued, distant kick (heartbeat feel)\n* Minimal brushed snare or soft metallic taps\n* Sparse glitch accents like flickering fluorescent lights\n* Long silence pockets between phrases\n\n**Texture Palette:**\n\n* Felt piano (close mic, audible hammer noise)\n* Low warehouse reverb tail fading into emptiness\n* Airy choir pads stretched almost beyond recognition\n* Soft sub-bass warmth instead of pressure\n* Field recording: faint wind through broken windows\n\n**Vocal Direction:**\n\n* Intimate lead vocal, nearly whispered\n* Japanese harmony layers answering English lines\n* No aggressive stacking; emotional restraint\n\n**Mood:** Dawn after intensity. Emotional recalibration. Cool concrete, pale light, breath steadying. Vulnerable but grounded.\n\n---\n\n# LYRICS\n\n## INTRO — Dawn Air\n\n(soft wind through broken glass)\n\n息を吸う\ncolder now\n\nThe warehouse is quiet.\nNo lights.\nNo choir.\n\nJust dust\nand morning.\n\n---\n\n## VERSE 1\n\nLast night we burned like neon veins\n今はただの静かな床\n\nConcrete remembers everything\nbut it doesn’t judge.\n\nI trace the cracks with my finger\nlike constellations that survived\n\n\"Are you still here?\"\n\nまだ。\n\n---\n\n## PRE-CHORUS\n\n吸って — steady\n吐いて — slower\n\nThe body returns to itself\n\n神経が静まる\nlike water after stones\n\n---\n\n## CHORUS\n\nAfter the ritual\nwe are only breath\n\nNo altar\nno anthem\njust pulse under skin\n\n儀式のあとで\nwe stay\n\nNot shining\nNot breaking\n\nJust alive.\n\n---\n\n## VERSE 2\n\nPiano notes fall like pale light\n鍵盤がやわらかく鳴る\n\nThe chromatic knives are gone\nonly warmth remains\n\nI used to think transcendence\nhad to be loud\n\nBut maybe it’s this —\n\nstaying.\n\n---\n\n## BRIDGE — Silence Embrace\n\n(beat drops out)\n\nListen.\n\nThe quiet isn’t empty.\n\nこの静けさは\n痛みの裏側じゃない\n\nIt’s what’s left\nwhen fear dissolves.\n\n---\n\n## FINAL CHORUS\n\nAfter the ritual\nwe are only breath\n\nWarehouse sky turning silver\n\n儀式のあとで\nwe remain\n\nC minor shadow\nF minor bloom\n\nNo collapse\nno cathedral\n\nJust pulse.\n\n---\n\n## OUTRO\n\n息。\n\nMorning light through broken glass.\n\nStill here.\n\nStill human.\n", "duration" 344.76, "type" "gen", "model_badges" {"songrow" {"dark" {"background_color" "00000000", "border_color" "FFFFFF1A", "text_color" "A3A3A3"}, "display_name" "v4.5-all", "light" {"background_color" "00000000", "border_color" "0000001A", "text_color" "7D7C83"}}}, "has_stem" false, "make_instrumental" false, "refund_credits" false}, "title" "After the Ritual / 儀式のあとで"}, :duration 344.76, :controls nil, :lyrics "# TITLE: \"After the Ritual / 儀式のあとで\"\n\n---\n\n## STYLE PROMPT\n\n**Genre Fusion:** Abstract Nocturnal Pop × Breath-Guided IDM × Post-Industrial Comedown × Deconstructed Piano Minimalism × Soft Glitch Ambient × Somatic Monologue\n\n**Tuning / Tempo:** 432Hz, 76–88 BPM, slow exhale pacing, slight tempo sag in final chorus\n\n**Key Center:** F minor resolving toward C minor with occasional E natural intrusion (fragile brightness)\n\n**Rhythm Design:**\n\n* Subdued, distant kick (heartbeat feel)\n* Minimal brushed snare or soft metallic taps\n* Sparse glitch accents like flickering fluorescent lights\n* Long silence pockets between phrases\n\n**Texture Palette:**\n\n* Felt piano (close mic, audible hammer noise)\n* Low warehouse reverb tail fading into emptiness\n* Airy choir pads stretched almost beyond recognition\n* Soft sub-bass warmth instead of pressure\n* Field recording: faint wind through broken windows\n\n**Vocal Direction:**\n\n* Intimate lead vocal, nearly whispered\n* Japanese harmony layers answering English lines\n* No aggressive stacking; emotional restraint\n\n**Mood:** Dawn after intensity. Emotional recalibration. Cool concrete, pale light, breath steadying. Vulnerable but grounded.\n\n---\n\n# LYRICS\n\n## INTRO — Dawn Air\n\n(soft wind through broken glass)\n\n息を吸う\ncolder now\n\nThe warehouse is quiet.\nNo lights.\nNo choir.\n\nJust dust\nand morning.\n\n---\n\n## VERSE 1\n\nLast night we burned like neon veins\n今はただの静かな床\n\nConcrete remembers everything\nbut it doesn’t judge.\n\nI trace the cracks with my finger\nlike constellations that survived\n\n\"Are you still here?\"\n\nまだ。\n\n---\n\n## PRE-CHORUS\n\n吸って — steady\n吐いて — slower\n\nThe body returns to itself\n\n神経が静まる\nlike water after stones\n\n---\n\n## CHORUS\n\nAfter the ritual\nwe are only breath\n\nNo altar\nno anthem\njust pulse under skin\n\n儀式のあとで\nwe stay\n\nNot shining\nNot breaking\n\nJust alive.\n\n---\n\n## VERSE 2\n\nPiano notes fall like pale light\n鍵盤がやわらかく鳴る\n\nThe chromatic knives are gone\nonly warmth remains\n\nI used to think transcendence\nhad to be loud\n\nBut maybe it’s this —\n\nstaying.\n\n---\n\n## BRIDGE — Silence Embrace\n\n(beat drops out)\n\nListen.\n\nThe quiet isn’t empty.\n\nこの静けさは\n痛みの裏側じゃない\n\nIt’s what’s left\nwhen fear dissolves.\n\n---\n\n## FINAL CHORUS\n\nAfter the ritual\nwe are only breath\n\nWarehouse sky turning silver\n\n儀式のあとで\nwe remain\n\nC minor shadow\nF minor bloom\n\nNo collapse\nno cathedral\n\nJust pulse.\n\n---\n\n## OUTRO\n\n息。\n\nMorning light through broken glass.\n\nStill here.\n\nStill human.\n", :source #:source{:name "After the Ritual _ 儀式のあとで(2).json", :sha256 "b3e7b57ed789771aa2dfdea41bcd38b15998a27f5f639a1729ebbcc51c44ea1c", :format :suno-json, :variation 2}, :title "After the Ritual / 儀式のあとで"}, "5492b698-576b-4780-8b10-091e6f809c75" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "5492b698-576b-4780-8b10-091e6f809c75", :url "https://suno.com/song/5492b698-576b-4780-8b10-091e6f809c75", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "5492b698-576b-4780-8b10-091e6f809c75", "metadata" {"prompt" "**ECS Lullaby (Registry Child) / レジストリの子**\n\n(whisper)\nI count my breath in entities—\n一つ、二つ…（ひとつ、ふたつ…）\ncomponents click like rosary beads.\n\n(JP call) ねむれ、ねむれ\n(EN response) the **an— an— an-chor**… (stutter) holds.\n(JP call) はらって、はらって\n(EN response) the **ta— ta— tax**… (stutter) due.\n\n**Verse**\nPosition says: “I’m *here*.”\nVelocity says: “I *move*.”\nMass says: “I *matter*.”\nColor says: “I *prove*.”\nLast word: **proof**\n(JP answer) 証（あかし）\n\n**Bridge**\nWe don’t delete the broken thread—\nwe fold it into overlay instead.\nLess integrated isn’t lost,\nit’s just a quieter cost.\nLast word: **anchor**\n(JP answer) 錨（いかり）\n\n**Outro**\nPay the tax. Close the loop.\nSleep inside the merge’s soft proof.\n\n---\n\n### 2) **Overlay Hymn (The Compactor Sings) / 圧縮賛歌**\n\n(spoken-soft, half-sung)\nP→R→N→Π—\nI archive what you couldn’t be.\nA→(feedback)→P—\nI learn the shape of what to keep.\n\n(Glitch) **η—η—η**\n(Glitch) **μ—μ—μ**\n\n**Chorus**\nNothing’s gone. It thins. It blends.\nIt waits in cold and wakes again.\nTwo hashes match—my ribs align—\nI take the messy, make it mine.\nLast word: **mine**\n(JP answer) わたしの\n\n**Verse**\nI’m a choir made of versions,\na cathedral full of forks.\nEvery “failed” attempt is compost,\nturning trauma into torque.\nLast word: **torque**\n(JP answer) 力（ちから）\n\n---\n\n### 3) **Fork Tax Prayer (Gatekeeper’s Verse) / 分岐税の祈り**\n\n(whisper)\nSeal the hash.\nSign the share.\nBY-SA in the open air.\n\n(JP call) ゆずって、つないで\n(EN response) keep it remix—**share**.\n(JP call) まもって、のこして\n(EN response) keep the receipts—**there**.\n\n**Verse**\nIf you take, you give it back—\nnot the same, but on the track.\nA new path, still returnable,\ntruth that stays collaborative.\nLast word: **returnable**\n(JP answer) 戻れる（もどれる）\n\n**Outro (stutter)**\nFo— fo— fork… (stutter) paid.\nAn— an— an-chor… (stutter) stayed.\n\n---\n\n### 4) **Character POV: “The Registry Child”**\n\n(quiet spoken)\nI was born between commits,\nraised by diffs I can’t confess.\nI don’t remember everything—\nI remember *less*.\n\n(JP harmony, last word)\n少し（すこし）\n\n**Final line**\nBut less remembered still moves through you.\nLast word: **you**\n(JP answer) 君（きみ）\n\n---\n\n#fnord", "tags" nil}, "title" "**ECS Lullaby (Registry Child) / レジストリの子**"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "**ECS Lullaby (Registry Child) / レ