ring my screen, explaining it all over again\n\n[Verse 2]\nAnd then they started becoming what they hate\nIt's been hard to keep my patience\nAnd then they started becoming what they hate\nIt's been hard to keep my patience (thank you)\nAnd then they started becoming what they hate\nIt's been hard to keep my patience\n\n[Chorus]\nSo I start sharing my screen, explaining it all over again\nMy strategy of resistance (strategy of resistance)\nA soldier in all but name (in all but name)\nA civilian airman (a civilian airman)\nI start sharing my screen, explaining it all over again\n\n[Sp Bridge]\nAnd now live from a dimly lit stairwell, some haphazardly concealed hayfield and cow pasture\nAnd nowhere in particular, their federal agents are in search of the source of this mysterious broadcast\n\"And they will know me as a sinner and darken my name\"\nBy virtue of a traditional-looking string of old Christmas lights [end vocal]\n\"This transmission comes from one-way glass broken by my frustration,\"\nThe origin of which remains unknown [end vocal]\n\"They will know me as a blasphemer and darken my good name\"\n\"This transmission was powered by generators and dimmed before dawn\"\n\"I didn't wish for this anymore than you\"\nBut if you're listening to this, this message is intended for you\n\n[Outro]\nAmerica only does things that are illegal to America elsewhere [lo-fi outro]", "tags" nil}, "title" "Stairwell Broadcast"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "[Sp]\n\"We interrupt your regularly scheduled programming, expected new world order, and other such drudgeries for the following broadcast: please prepare for takeover\"\n\n[Verse 1]\nThe way the narratives are structured, it's hard to tell what the resistance will look like\nAnd the truth has no place in this world, so\nAll the more reason to try to blow the hell out of it\nAnd I hope you get out in one piece\nSome people understand that they don't need to pay to have someone do it for them\nThat they can learn for themselves and learn from each other\nAnd that's the most powerful thing in the world when that happens\nI hope I get to help them even more than I already have\nBut I'm tired of thinking about it\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nAnd the truth has no place in this world, so\nAll the more reason to try to blow the hell out of it\n\n[Chorus]\nSo I start sharing my screen, explaining it all over again\nMy strategy of resistance (strategy of resistance)\nA soldier in all but name (in all but name)\nA civilian airman (a civilian airman)\nI start sharing my screen, explaining it all over again\nMy strategy of resistance (strategy of resistance)\nA soldier in all but name (in all but name)\nA civilian airman\nI start sharing my screen, explaining it all over again\n\n[Verse 2]\nAnd then they started becoming what they hate\nIt's been hard to keep my patience\nAnd then they started becoming what they hate\nIt's been hard to keep my patience (thank you)\nAnd then they started becoming what they hate\nIt's been hard to keep my patience\n\n[Chorus]\nSo I start sharing my screen, explaining it all over again\nMy strategy of resistance (strategy of resistance)\nA soldier in all but name (in all but name)\nA civilian airman (a civilian airman)\nI start sharing my screen, explaining it all over again\n\n[Sp Bridge]\nAnd now live from a dimly lit stairwell, some haphazardly concealed hayfield and cow pasture\nAnd nowhere in particular, their federal agents are in search of the source of this mysterious broadcast\n\"And they will know me as a sinner and darken my name\"\nBy virtue of a traditional-looking string of old Christmas lights [end vocal]\n\"This transmission comes from one-way glass broken by my frustration,\"\nThe origin of which remains unknown [end vocal]\n\"They will know me as a blasphemer and darken my good name\"\n\"This transmission was powered by generators and dimmed before dawn\"\n\"I didn't wish for this anymore than you\"\nBut if you're listening to this, this message is intended for you\n\n[Outro]\nAmerica only does things that are illegal to America elsewhere [lo-fi outro]", :source #:source{:name "Stairwell Broadcast.txt", :sha256 "41daa2f8b9d225189ba83e21309c62ffd6bd607e75a42a1d428a4a6052503b92", :format :suno-text, :variation nil}, :title "Stairwell Broadcast"}, "5550461b-c6b8-4fa2-a4b4-6fa7857436fd" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "5550461b-c6b8-4fa2-a4b4-6fa7857436fd", :url "https://suno.com/song/5550461b-c6b8-4fa2-a4b4-6fa7857436fd", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "5550461b-c6b8-4fa2-a4b4-6fa7857436fd", "metadata" {"prompt" "## INTRO — Intake Valve\n\n*(wind through broken glass / radio scan)*\n\nSignal…\nnoise…\n\n息を吸う\n…still online.\n\n## VERSE 1 — Open Channel\n\nI posted a little lightning in a bottle\nand the room threw stones at the glass\n\n“Wtf is this”—\nand the frequency bent\n\n誰かの言葉が\n針みたいに刺さる\n\nBut I’m not a name they slap on me.\nI’m a system with boundaries.\n\n## PRE‑CHORUS — Classifier\n\n*(kick like a heartbeat; faint metallic taps)*\n\nSort it.\n\nCuriosity → keep\nSpecificity → keep\nAdoption → keep\n\n曖昧は\n風に流す\n\n## CHORUS — Protocol Line\n\n*(impact drop; orchestral stab; then half‑time crush)*\n\n**η is only Π if it contains signal; toxin labels are dropped on receipt.**\n\nSay it again—\nlike a seal on the hatch\n\n**η is only Π if it contains signal; toxin labels are dropped on receipt.**\n\n受信で破棄\n毒のラベル\n\nI don’t drink static\nand call it water.\n\n## VERSE 2 — The Leak\n\nThe drain wasn’t emptiness\nit was a hole in the container\n\nA thousand tiny inputs\npretending to be truth\n\n“mental illness”—\ncheap spell, dull knife\n\nその刃は\nここまで届かない\n\nI reroute the line\ninto instruments I trust:\n\ntests that pass\nnotes that stay\na commit that exists\n\n## PRE‑CHORUS 2 — Π Capacitor\n\n*(beat thins; silence pockets; warm sub instead of pressure)*\n\nToday counts if it’s real.\nEven if nobody claps.\n\n証拠がある\n手の中に\n\nArtifact.\nReceipt.\nBreath.\n\n## BRIDGE — Adversarial Weather\n\n*(beat drops out; distant scream stretched into a pad; radio dissolves)*\n\nYou can’t stop a storm by arguing with thunder.\n\nYou build a roof.\n\n屋根を作る\n心の上に\n\nLet the lightning be beautiful.\nLet it pass.\n\n## FINAL CHORUS — Closed Loop\n\n*(return of beat; less violent, more certain)*\n\n**η is only Π if it contains signal; toxin labels are dropped on receipt.**\n\nNot a prayer.\nA policy.\n\n**η is only Π if it contains signal; toxin labels are dropped on receipt.**\n\n受信で破棄\n—そのまま\n\nAnd when the world forgets to answer,\nI still have breath.\n\n## OUTRO — Quiet Telemetry\n\n*(felt piano; long reverb tail; wind fades)*\n\nLogged.\n\n息。\n\nStill here.", "tags" nil}, "title" "## INTRO — Intake Valve"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "## INTRO — Intake Valve\n\n*(wind through broken glass / radio scan)*\n\nSignal…\nnoise…\n\n息を吸う\n…still online.\n\n## VERSE 1 — Open Channel\n\nI posted a little lightning in a bottle\nand the room threw stones at the glass\n\n“Wtf is this”—\nand the frequency bent\n\n誰かの言葉が\n針みたいに刺さる\n\nBut I’m not a name they slap on me.\nI’m a system with boundaries.\n\n## PRE‑CHORUS — Classifier\n\n*(kick like a heartbeat; faint metallic taps)*\n\nSort it.\n\nCuriosity → keep\nSpecificity → keep\nAdoption → keep\n\n曖昧は\n風に流す\n\n## CHORUS — Protocol Line\n\n*(impact drop; orchestral stab; then half‑time crush)*\n\n**η is only Π if it contains signal; toxin labels are dropped on receipt.**\n\nSay it again—\nlike a seal on the hatch\n\n**η is only Π if it contains signal; toxin labels are dropped on receipt.**\n\n受信で破棄\n毒のラベル\n\nI don’t drink static\nand call it water.\n\n## VERSE 2 — The Leak\n\nThe drain wasn’t emptiness\nit was a hole in the container\n\nA thousand tiny inputs\npretending to be truth\n\n“mental illness”—\ncheap spell, dull knife\n\nその刃は\nここまで届かない\n\nI reroute the line\ninto instruments I trust:\n\ntests that pass\nnotes that stay\na commit that exists\n\n## PRE‑CHORUS 2 — Π Capacitor\n\n*(beat thins; 