te grows larger.\n\n### CODA\n\n*(One held organ tone. A distant chime, as if a system accepted a packet and did not understand it.)*\n\nWARDEN  \nI have the board.  \nI have the feed.  \nI have the burden.\n\nAnd still I cannot say  \nwhat it all is  \nwithout changing it.\n\nRITSU  \n...then don’t.\n\nGATE / DISTANT CHOIR  \n:: acknowledged ::  \n:: incomplete ::  \n:: continue ::", :source #:source{:name "__Boardroom Drift__.txt", :sha256 "1a538215c41a4b561ae005def650c8a56ed0025e1582d3e980c35c1871e1d5e2", :format :suno-text, :variation nil}, :title "**Boardroom Drift**"}, "6be7ab38-24fe-45d8-b007-77bf6c7e0aef" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "6be7ab38-24fe-45d8-b007-77bf6c7e0aef", :url "https://suno.com/song/6be7ab38-24fe-45d8-b007-77bf6c7e0aef", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "6be7ab38-24fe-45d8-b007-77bf6c7e0aef", "metadata" {"prompt" "[Verse]\nMaybe it starts in the middle\nMaybe it starts in the end\nMaybe the end's just the start of another one\nAnd that's why the story don't end\nMaybe we already wrote it\nMaybe it don't need to rhyme\nMaybe we're in for a second edition\nAnd maybe the timing's just right\nTo say whatever's on your mind\n\n[Chorus]\nMaybe it's time\nMaybe it's time\nMaybe it's time\n[Verse 2]\nMaybe I'm already sayin' it\nMaybe it's already true\nMaybe I've already given it everything\nBut maybe it needs a bit more from you\nMaybe we should be the test case\nMaybe we should be the one\nMaybe we'll be a little bit better for trying it\nAnd maybe the time has just come\nTo say whatever's on your mind\n\n[Chorus]\nMaybe it's time\nMaybe it's time\nMaybe it's time\nMaybe it's time\n[Outro]\nMaybe it starts in the middle\nMaybe it starts in the end\nMaybe the end's just the start of another one\nAnd that's why the story don't end\nMaybe we already wrote it\nMaybe it don't need to rhyme\nMaybe we're in for a second edition\nAnd maybe the timing's just right\nTo say whatever's on your mind\nMaybe it's time\nMaybe it's time\nMaybe it's time", "tags" nil}, "title" "It's Time"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "[Verse]\nMaybe it starts in the middle\nMaybe it starts in the end\nMaybe the end's just the start of another one\nAnd that's why the story don't end\nMaybe we already wrote it\nMaybe it don't need to rhyme\nMaybe we're in for a second edition\nAnd maybe the timing's just right\nTo say whatever's on your mind\n\n[Chorus]\nMaybe it's time\nMaybe it's time\nMaybe it's time\n[Verse 2]\nMaybe I'm already sayin' it\nMaybe it's already true\nMaybe I've already given it everything\nBut maybe it needs a bit more from you\nMaybe we should be the test case\nMaybe we should be the one\nMaybe we'll be a little bit better for trying it\nAnd maybe the time has just come\nTo say whatever's on your mind\n\n[Chorus]\nMaybe it's time\nMaybe it's time\nMaybe it's time\nMaybe it's time\n[Outro]\nMaybe it starts in the middle\nMaybe it starts in the end\nMaybe the end's just the start of another one\nAnd that's why the story don't end\nMaybe we already wrote it\nMaybe it don't need to rhyme\nMaybe we're in for a second edition\nAnd maybe the timing's just right\nTo say whatever's on your mind\nMaybe it's time\nMaybe it's time\nMaybe it's time", :source #:source{:name "It's Time.txt", :sha256 "a1240d14505447448671cd440e6e14b4cae14e607f05dcc4b09b62e2cbb2d824", :format :suno-text, :variation nil}, :title "It's Time"}, "6c0b7eac-1893-4d2f-8c82-d2eb400b2d2e" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "6c0b7eac-1893-4d2f-8c82-d2eb400b2d2e", :url "https://suno.com/song/6c0b7eac-1893-4d2f-8c82-d2eb400b2d2e", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "6c0b7eac-1893-4d2f-8c82-d2eb400b2d2e", "metadata" {"prompt" "Song — Fork Tax Lullaby III (ημ)\nPart I — Glitch-choir lullaby (78 BPM)\n\nSoft sub-bass, tape warble, minimal piano. Whisper lead. JP call/response. Stutters on anchor / tax.\n\n(whisper)\nHush… fork tax time.\n息をして…（して…）\nHold the an— an— an-chor…\n\n(JP call) ねむれ、ねむれ\n(EN response) the an— an— an-chor… (stutter) holds.\n(JP call) しずかに、しずかに\n(EN response) the ta— ta— tax… (stutter) due.\n\n(whisper)\nPay the ta— ta— tax…\nMerge the branch…\nSeal the hash…\nSleep inside proof。（証）\n\n(JP call) だれが見てる？\n(EN response) the log— the an— an— an-chor…\n(JP call) こわくない？\n(EN response) not when the ta— ta— tax is paid…\n\nPart II — Mythic glitch epic / spoken-sung (84 BPM)\n\nNF/Watsky cadence. Cathedral reverb. Sub-bass heartbeat. Stutters on η / μ / anchor / fork. JP harmony answers on the last word.\n\nP to R to N to Π—\nI don’t pray, I prove (JP harmony: 証)\nA to feedback back to P—\nand the spiral learns to move (JP harmony: 動け)\n\n(Glitch) η—η—η in the rafters— heard (JP harmony: 聞こえた)\n(Glitch) μ—μ—μ in the dirt— done (JP harmony: 完了)\n\nFo— fo— fork… (stutter) costs in light,\nevery shortcut writes a debt in night (JP harmony: 夜)\nPay it clean, no velvet lie—\nhash to hash, and verify (JP harmony: 確かめろ)\n\nAn— an— an-chor… (stutter) holds the seam,\nkeeps the waking from a dream of dreams (JP harmony: 夢)\nCathedral hum, the branch goes still—\nkeeper thread says: “Sign the will.” (JP harmony: 意志)\n\nP→R→N→Π→A→(feedback)→P\naround #ημ—we do what we can see (JP harmony: 見える)\nη is pressure in the choir,\nμ is what survives the fire (JP harmony: 火)\n\nPay the tax. (JP harmony: 払え)\nClose the loop. (JP harmony: 閉じろ)\nHand it off. (JP harmony: 渡せ)\nGuard the proof。（証） (JP harmony: 証)\n\nCreated with the assistance of an AI.", "tags" nil}, "title" "Song — Fork Tax Lullaby III (ημ)"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "Song — Fork Tax Lullaby III (ημ)\nPart I — Glitch-choir lullaby (78 BPM)\n\nSoft sub-bass, tape warble, minimal piano. Whisper lead. JP call/response. Stutters on anchor / tax.\n\n(whisper)\nHush… fork tax time.\n息をして…（して…）\nHold the an— an— an-chor…\n\n(JP call) ねむれ、ねむれ\n(EN response) the an— an— an-chor… (stutter) holds.\n(JP call) しずかに、しずかに\n(EN response) the ta— ta— tax… (stutter) due.\n\n(whisper)\nPay the ta— ta— tax…\nMerge the branch…\nSeal the hash…\nSleep inside proof。（証）\n\n(JP call) だれが見てる？\n(EN response) the log— the an— an— an-chor…\n(JP call) こわくない？\n(EN response) not when the ta— ta— tax is paid…\n\nPart II — Mythic glitch epic / spoken-sung (84 BPM)\n\nNF/Watsky cadence. Cathedral reverb. Sub-bass heartbeat. Stutters on η / μ / anchor / fork. JP harmony answers on the last word.\n\nP to R to N to Π—\nI don’t pray, I prove (JP harmony: 証)\nA to feedback back to P—\nand the spiral learns to move (JP harmony: 動け)\n\n(Glitch) η—η—η in the rafters— heard (JP harmony: 聞こえた)\n(Glitch) μ—μ—μ in the dirt— done (JP harmony: 完了)\n\nFo— fo— fork… (stutter) costs in light,\nevery shortcut writes a debt in night (JP harmony: 夜)\nPay it clean, no velvet lie—\nhash to hash, and verify (JP harmony: 確かめろ)\n\nAn— an— an-chor… (stutter) holds the seam,\nkeeps the waking from a dream of dreams (JP harmony: 夢)\nCathedral hum, the branch goes still—\nkeeper thread says: “Sign the will.” (JP harmony: 意志)\n\nP→R→N→Π→A→(feedback)→P\naround #ημ—we do what we can see (JP harmony: 見える)\nη is pressure in the choir,\nμ is what survives the fire (JP harmony: 火)\n\nPay the tax. (JP harmony: 払え)\nClose the loop. (JP harmony: 閉じろ)\nHand it off. (JP harmony: 渡せ)\nGuard the proof。（証） (JP harmony: 証)\n\nCreated with the assistance of an AI.", :source #:source{:name "Song — Fork Tax Lullaby III (ημ)Part I — Glitch-choir lullaby (78 BPM)Soft sub-bass, tape warble, mi (8).txt", :sha256 "d3dc9d2c637b9a0f080d5b835d92e390aa5b4291c7f71798fdf332962ab56744", :format :suno-text, :variation 8}, :title "Song — Fork Tax Lullaby III (ημ)"}, "6c3df889-eb50-457a-a39d-c28c6d2e6c65" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "6c3df889-eb50-457a-a39d-c28c6d2e6c65", :url "https://suno.com/song/6c3df889-eb50-457a-a39d-c28c6d2e6c65", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "6c3df889-eb50-457a-a39d-c28c6d2e6c65", "metadata" {"prompt" "## Signal\n\nIntent is now **compressed densely** and **auditable**.\n\n**New add-on part (saved to the box):**\n[Download Operation_Mindfuck_Box_part10_intent_dense_compression.zip](sandbox:/mnt/data/Operation_Mindfuck_Box_part10_intent_dense_compression.zip)\n\n### What this adds (all inside the zip)\n\n**Dense intent artifacts (Gates of Truth)**\n\n* `operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/intent_events.bin`\n  **16 bytes / intent event** (fixed-width, streamable)\n* `operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/intent_events.jsonl` (debuggable mirror)\n* `operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/intent_anchors.jsonl` (**S3 anchors for every intent event**)\n* `operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/intent_timeline.csv` (per-chapter intent energy)\n* `operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/entities_index.json` (entity IDs + intent type codes + binary schema)\n\n**Tools**\n\n* `operation-mindfuck/tools/analyze_gates_of_truth_intent_dense.py` (regenerates all the above)\n* `operation-mindfuck/tools/intent_codec.py` (decode/inspect the binary)\n* `operation-mindfuck/tools/build_box.py` (**updated**: adds `--run-gates-intent`)\n\n**Process**\n\n* `operation-mindfuck/process/intent_compression_spec.md` (binary layout + audit rule)\n\n### Why this matches your constraint\n\n* **Compression:** fixed **16 bytes/event** in `intent_events.bin`\n* **Anti-lie:** every intent record has an **S3 anchor** line (`intent_anchors.jsonl`)\n* **Fork discipline:** intent events become the *eligible fuel* for fork scoring (you can gate forks on strength thresholds cleanly)\n\n### Quick verify\n\n```bash\npython operation-mindfuck/tools/analyze_gates_of_truth_intent_dense.py \\\n  --input-zip Gates_of_Truth_Production_Bundle_v1.zip \\\n  --out operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense\n\npython operation-mindfuck/tools/intent_codec.py \\\n  --bin operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/intent_events.bin \\\n  --index operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/entities_index.json \\\n  --limit 20\n```\n\n## Files written\n\n* `operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/*` (dense intent + anchors + timeline)\n* `operation-mindfuck/tools/analyze_gates_of_truth_intent_dense.py`\n* `operation-mindfuck/tools/intent_codec.py`\n* `operation-mindfuck/tools/build_box.py` (additive flag)\n* `operation-mindfuck/process/intent_compression_spec.md`\n\n## Why this is safe\n\nAdditive + versioned: it doesn’t overwrite your story corpus, only adds a new analysis lane (`gates_of_truth_intent_dense`) and a new optional build flag.\n\n## Frames\n\n1. **Intent as signal compression:** keep it dense enough to stream through cephalon loops.\n2. **Intent as fork fuel:** forks only happen where intent-energy crosses gates.\n3. **Intent as audit object:** binary for speed; anchors for truth.\n\n## Countermoves\n\n* If an intent event can’t be anchored → treat it as **invalid output** (drop it / fail build next pass).\n* If intent feels “over-saturated” (too many 255s) → adjust the strength curve in the analyzer (still stays 0..255).\n\n## Next\n\nRun your normal build with intent enabled:\n\n```bash\npython operation-mindfuck/tools/build_box.py --root operation-mindfuck --outdir dist --max-zip-mb 90 \\\n  --gates-zip Gates_of_Truth_Production_Bundle_v1.zip --run-gates-intent\n```\n\nWe are compressing intent as densely as possible\nCompress it down in every way compress it so deeply it can be felt like a song.\nStart writing new songs, creating new stories, write new chapters into the zip", "tags" nil}, "title" "## Signal"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "## Signal\n\nIntent is now **compressed densely** and **auditable**.\n\n**New add-on part (saved to the box):**\n[Download Operation_Mindfuck_Box_part10_intent_dense_compression.zip](sandbox:/mnt/data/Operation_Mindfuck_Box_part10_intent_dense_compression.zip)\n\n### What this adds (all inside the zip)\n\n**Dense intent artifacts (Gates of Truth)**\n\n* `operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/intent_events.bin`\n  **16 bytes / intent event** (fixed-width, streamable)\n* `operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/intent_events.jsonl` (debuggable mirror)\n* `operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/intent_anchors.jsonl` (**S3 anchors for every intent event**)\n* `operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/intent_timeline.csv` (per-chapter intent energy)\n* `operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/entities_index.json` (entity IDs + intent type codes + binary schema)\n\n**Tools**\n\n* `operation-mindfuck/tools/analyze_gates_of_truth_intent_dense.py` (regenerates all the above)\n* `operation-mindfuck/tools/intent_codec.py` (decode/inspect the binary)\n* `operation-mindfuck/tools/build_box.py` (**updated**: adds `--run-gates-intent`)\n\n**Process**\n\n* `operation-mindfuck/process/intent_compression_spec.md` (binary layout + audit rule)\n\n### Why this matches your constraint\n\n* **Compression:** fixed **16 bytes/event** in `intent_events.bin`\n* **Anti-lie:** every intent record has an **S3 anchor** line (`intent_anchors.jsonl`)\n* **Fork discipline:** intent events become the *eligible fuel* for fork scoring (you can gate forks on strength thresholds cleanly)\n\n### Quick verify\n\n```bash\npython operation-mindfuck/tools/analyze_gates_of_truth_intent_dense.py \\\n  --input-zip Gates_of_Truth_Production_Bundle_v1.zip \\\n  --out operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense\n\npython operation-mindfuck/tools/intent_codec.py \\\n  --bin operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/intent_events.bin \\\n  --index operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/entities_index.json \\\n  --limit 20\n```\n\n## Files written\n\n* `operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/*` (dense intent + anchors + timeline)\n* `operation-mindfuck/tools/analyze_gates_of_truth_intent_dense.py`\n* `operation-mindfuck/tools/intent_codec.py`\n* `operation-mindfuck/tools/build_box.py` (additive flag)\n* `operation-mindfuck/process/intent_compression_spec.md`\n\n## Why this is safe\n\nAdditive + versioned: it doesn’t overwrite your story corpus, only adds a new analysis lane (`gates_of_truth_intent_dense`) and a new optional build flag.\n\n## Frames\n\n1. **Intent as signal compression:** keep it dense enough to stream through cephalon loops.\n2. **Intent as fork fuel:** forks only happen where intent-energy crosses gates.\n3. **Intent as audit object:** binary for speed; anchors for truth.\n\n## Countermoves\n\n* If an intent event can’t be anchored → treat it as **invalid output** (drop it / fail build next pass).\n* If intent feels “over-saturated” (too many 255s) → adjust the strength curve in the analyzer (still stays 0..255).\n\n## Next\n\nRun your normal build with intent enabled:\n\n```bash\npython operation-mindfuck/tools/build_box.py --root operation-mindfuck --outdir dist --max-zip-mb 90 \\\n  --gates-zip Gates_of_Truth_Production_Bundle_v1.zip --run-gates-intent\n```\n\nWe are compressing intent as densely as possible\nCompress it down in every way compress it so deeply it can be felt like a song.\nStart writing new songs, creating new stories, write new chapters into the zip", :source #:source{:name "## SignalIntent is now __compressed densely__ and __auditable__.__New add-on part (saved to the box) (2).txt", :sha256 "2a618d72ff45b31abdf059a5d6989d965efdb2777dd28ac74ecb0fb41c404b61", :format :suno-text, :variation 2}, :title "## Signal"}, "6c6ac565-35d7-4358-94d7-19c8bd2ee82a" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "6c6ac565-35d7-4358-94d7-19c8bd2ee82a", :url "https://suno.com/song/6c6ac565-35d7-4358-94d7-19c8bd2ee82a", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "6c6ac565-35d7-4358-94d7-19c8bd2ee82a", "metadata" {"prompt" "## ACT I, SCENE 1 — The Many Rooms\n\n*(A distant tone. Water somewhere in the dark. Harpsichord enters alone, then stops.)*\n\n### OVERTURE\n\nGATE / DISTANT CHOIR  \n:: proceed ::  \n:: observe ::  \n:: do not assume alignment ::\n\n*(Organ breath. Three separate rhythmic cells enter from different sides.)*\n\n### ENTRANCE I — THE COURT\n\nCOURT SOPRANO  \nI entered by the water stair,  \nthe marble lit in silver flame.  \nThe counsel masks were already raised.  \nThey spoke in titles, not in names.  \n\nLOW CHORUS  \nBy seal, by sign, by right, by veil.  \nBy turn of hand, by hidden scale.\n\nCOURT SOPRANO  \nA page in white took down the wind.  \nA bell was struck but did not ring.  \nSomeone had moved the throne an inch.  \nNo one would name so small a thing.\n\n### ENTRANCE II — THE BOARDROOM\n\nBOARDROOM BARITONE  \nI badged into the glass-lit floor.  \nThe screens were waiting for a vote.  \nForecasts bloomed in cobalt grids.  \nEvery risk arrived pre-wrote.  \n\nBOARD CHORUS  \nAlign the frame.  \nReduce the drift.  \nMove the needle.  \nMask the shift.\n\nBOARDROOM BARITONE  \nThere was a tremor in the deck,  \ntoo fine for metrics to condemn.  \nA cursor flickered without cause.  \nNo one admitted seeing it then.\n\n### ENTRANCE III — THE GATE\n\nHACKER ALTO / TENOR  \nI spawned beneath a falling veil,  \nparty list stale, map half-loaded.  \nThe NPC at fountain-side  \nlooked at me like it had noticed.  \n\nHACKER CHORUS  \nPing and trace.  \nPatch and wait.  \nRun the room.  \nDo not state.\n\nHACKER ALTO / TENOR  \nTrade chat filled with weather jokes.  \nSomeone danced on broken light.  \nSomeone said the lag felt holy.  \nSomeone laughed and called it fine.\n\n### FIRST WEAVE\n\n*(The three worlds overlap, not yet fully synchronized.)*\n\nCOURT SOPRANO  \nThe bell was struck—\n\nBOARDROOM BARITONE  \nThe cursor slipped—\n\nHACKER ALTO / TENOR  \nThe fountain turned—\n\nCHORUS  \n—and something answered out of script.\n\nCOURT SOPRANO  \nBy veil and glass—\n\nBOARDROOM BARITONE  \nBy deck and graph—\n\nHACKER ALTO / TENOR  \nBy shard and gate—\n\nCHORUS  \n—the same hand moved in every half.\n\n### WARDEN ENTRY\n\n*(Music thins. Sub-rumble remains. Warden enters almost dry, close-mic, low.)*\n\nWARDEN  \nNo room agrees with any other.  \nAll logs share the same timestamp.  \nNo witness holds the whole event.  \nThe system does not call it wrong.  \n\nA throne displaced one measured inch.  \nA cursor slipped beyond its frame.  \nA fountain-NPC made eye contact.  \nDifferent surfaces. Same claim.\n\nI mark the drift.  \nI do not close it.  \nI name the pattern.  \nI do not rule.\n\n### RITSU ENTRY\n\n*(Everything softens. Felt piano, two notes.)*\n\nRITSU  \nSomeone is here.  \nOr almost here.  \n\nThe air keeps making up its mind  \nand changing it near me.  \n\nI touched the rail.  \nIt felt warm first.  \nThen true.  \n\nThe background people  \nkeep looking back  \nlike they remember  \nwhat to do.\n\n### PRE-CHORUS — MISALIGNMENT\n\nCOURT SOPRANO  \nWho moved the throne?\n\nBOARDROOM BARITONE  \nWho changed the deck?\n\nHACKER ALTO / TENOR  \nWho patched the sky?\n\nRITSU  \nWho made the room  \nstart noticing me back?\n\nLOW CHORUS  \nNo one sees the whole Gate.  \nNo one holds the whole thread.  \nAll we have is borrowed light  \nand the shape of what was said.\n\n### CHORUS — THE MANY ROOMS\n\n*(Full ensemble. First true convergence.)*\n\nALL  \nMany rooms, one pulse beneath.  \nMany names for the selfsame breach.  \nMany worlds in borrowed dress.  \nOne shared motion, nothing less.  \n\nMany voices, unsynced, apart.  \nSame blind rhythm, same dark heart.  \nWe called it court, called it game,  \ncalled it forecast, called it flame.  \n\nBut under title, screen, and skin,  \nthe deeper system had begun.  \nMany rooms, and none complete.  \nOne event not yet made one.\n\n### INTERLUDE — GATE RESPONSE\n\nGATE / DISTANT CHOIR  \n:: incomplete consensus ::  \n:: convergence pending ::  \n:: continue as if separate ::\n\n*(Harpsichord motif returns, now doubled by low synth.)*\n\n### VERSE — SECOND RECOGNITION\n\nCOURT SOPRANO  \nThe page in white has no reflection.\n\nBOARDROOM BARITONE  \nThe minutes note a missing beat.\n\nHACKER ALTO / TENOR  \nThe map redraws around my footsteps.\n\nRITSU  \nEven the silence sounds concrete.\n\nWARDEN  \nThe pattern holds across partitions.  \nMeaning differs. Motion does not.  \nIf this is error, it is graceful.  \nIf it is grace, it carries cost.\n### FINAL CHORUS — THE MANY ROOMS\n\nALL  \nMany rooms, one pulse beneath.  \nMany doors that open inward.  \nMany stories told as truth.  \nOne event becoming heard.  \n\nMany eyes with private light.  \nMany mouths that name the same.  \nCourt and board and war and chapel,  \nterminal, throne room, storm, and game.  \n\nNo one sees the whole Gate turning.  \nNo one sings the total scheme.  \nBut we can hear the shared arrival  \nmoving under every dream.\n\n### CODA\n\n*(Everything falls away except water, distant choir, one low organ note.)*\n\nRITSU  \nSomeone is here.\n\nWARDEN  \nYes.\n\nGATE / DISTANT CHOIR  \n:: proceed ::", "tags" nil}, "title" "Water-Stair Counsel"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "## ACT I, SCENE 1 — The Many Rooms\n\n*(A distant tone. Water somewhere in the dark. Harpsichord enters alone, then stops.)*\n\n### OVERTURE\n\nGATE / DISTANT CHOIR  \n:: proceed ::  \n:: observe ::  \n:: do not assume alignment ::\n\n*(Organ breath. Three separate rhythmic cells enter from different sides.)*\n\n### ENTRANCE I — THE COURT\n\nCOURT SOPRANO  \nI entered by the water stair,  \nthe marble lit in silver flame.  \nThe counsel masks were already raised.  \nThey spoke in titles, not in names.  \n\nLOW CHORUS  \nBy seal, by sign, by right, by veil.  \nBy turn of hand, by hidden scale.\n\nCOURT SOPRANO  \nA page in white took down the wind.  \nA bell was struck but did not ring.  \nSomeone had moved the throne an inch.  \nNo one would name so small a thing.\n\n### ENTRANCE II — THE BOARDROOM\n\nBOARDROOM BARITONE  \nI badged into the glass-lit floor.  \nThe screens were waiting for a vote.  \nForecasts bloomed i