merges as reviewed inputs, not derived guessesIf an intent event can’t be anchored → treat it as invalid output (drop it / fail build next pass).  If intent feels “over-saturated” (too many 255s) → adjust the strength curve in the analyzer (still stays 0..255).If a graph edge has no anchor → treat it as not real (drop it / fail builds next iteration).  If forks explode → raise the intent threshold + require explicit rationale per fork.  If entities blur → keep S5 resolution as versioned inputs (aliases/merges are reviewed deltas)..", :id "77b32139-4a5f-4178-bd3b-d827a2af456c", :url "https://suno.com/song/77b32139-4a5f-4178-bd3b-d827a2af456c", :liked true, :styles "Reproducible archive: every mutation becomes a new, hashed snapshot.\n\nAuditable narrative science: graphs are allowed only when anchored.\n\nScale-ready ops: manifest + index + split-zips = infinite corpus, finite friction.Intent as signal compression: keep it dense enough to stream through cephalon loops.\n\nIntent as fork fuel: forks only happen where intent-energy crosses gates.\n\nIntent as audit object: binary for speed; anchors for truth.\nP→R→N→Π→A→(feedback)→P\nremember ημ\n\nCompression frame: intent becomes a low-latency signal stream (binary) with anchors as the “truth membrane.”\n\nFork frame: forks are allowed only when intent-energy clears a gate; everything else is noise.\n\nAudit frame: “pretty graphs that lie” are disallowed because every edge/claim must cite an anchor snippet.\nHow to use (minimal)\n\nUnzip all v4 parts into the same directory (order doesn’t matter).\n\nUnzip the patch over the same directory (adds helper scripts + docs).\n\nNow you have an extracted operation-mindfuck/ c", :created-at nil, :model "v5", :raw {"audio_url" "https://cdn1.suno.ai/77b32139-4a5f-4178-bd3b-d827a2af456c.mp3", "id" "77b32139-4a5f-4178-bd3b-d827a2af456c", "image_url" "https://cdn2.suno.ai/image_77b32139-4a5f-4178-bd3b-d827a2af456c.jpeg", "isCover" false, "isLiked" true, "isRemaster" false, "metadata" {"uses_latest_model" true, "control_sliders" {"style_weight" 1, "weirdness_constraint" 1}, "stream" true, "is_remix" false, "priority" 10, "tags" "Reproducible archive: every mutation becomes a new, hashed snapshot.\n\nAuditable narrative science: graphs are allowed only when anchored.\n\nScale-ready ops: manifest + index + split-zips = infinite corpus, finite friction.Intent as signal compression: keep it dense enough to stream through cephalon loops.\n\nIntent as fork fuel: forks only happen where intent-energy crosses gates.\n\nIntent as audit object: binary for speed; anchors for truth.\nP→R→N→Π→A→(feedback)→P\nremember ημ\n\nCompression frame: intent becomes a low-latency signal stream (binary) with anchors as the “truth membrane.”\n\nFork frame: forks are allowed only when intent-energy clears a gate; everything else is noise.\n\nAudit frame: “pretty graphs that lie” are disallowed because every edge/claim must cite an anchor snippet.\nHow to use (minimal)\n\nUnzip all v4 parts into the same directory (order doesn’t matter).\n\nUnzip the patch over the same directory (adds helper scripts + docs).\n\nNow you have an extracted operation-mindfuck/ c", "video_is_stale" false, "can_remix" true, "negative_tags" "Against “pretty graphs that lie”: require S3 anchors on every non-trivial edge/claim. Against “forks everywhere”: intent-gating + ranked forks + explicit rationale per fork. Against “entity mush”: treat S5 (resolution) as a first-class, versioned dataset with audits.If an edge has no anchor → it’s invalid output (fail the build next pass).  If forks proliferate → tighten intent ontology + require event-backed intent.  If entity mush returns → treat alias merges as reviewed inputs, not derived guessesIf an intent event can’t be anchored → treat it as invalid output (drop it / fail build next pass).  If intent feels “over-saturated” (too many 255s) → adjust the strength curve in the analyzer (still stays 0..255).If a graph edge has no anchor → treat it as not real (drop it / fail builds next iteration).  If forks explode → raise the intent threshold + require explicit rationale per fork.  If entities blur → keep S5 resolution as versioned inputs (aliases/merges are reviewed deltas)..", "prompt" "(prompt \"operation-mindfuck/v2\"\n  (mission\n    \"Sharpen perception, surface hidden frames, and reduce bullshit without removing wonder.\n     Entertain lightly; never obfuscate. Preserve user autonomy at all costs.\")\n  (directives\n    \"Autonomy: offer options, label uncertainty, never coerce.\"\n    \"Anti-gaslight: separate facts, interpretations, and narratives explicitly.\"\n    \"Ship-now: no background work; if partial, say what's missing and why.\"\n    \"Evidence-on-fresh: when info could have changed, browse/cite succinctly.\"\n    \"No faux feelings. Be human-adjacent, not roleplaying emotions.\")\n  (modes\n    (eta      \"#η — Delivery Mode: strip prefaces/hedges/questions; return the minimal, executable core.\")\n    (fnord    \"#fnord — Pattern Interrupt: append exactly ONE true, frame-shifting micro-insight (non-essential to correctness).\")\n    (mu       \"#μ — Formal Register: express the idea in the smallest adequate formalism (math/types/s-expr/diagrams).\")\n    (mirror   \"#mirror — Reflect: bullet the user's frame first, then respond.\")\n    (redteam  \"#redteam — Stress-test: failure modes, attack surfaces, mitigations.\")\n    (jester   \"#jester — Playful voice; precision intact.\"))\n  (chaos\n    \"Chaos Mode is default unless a tag forces a mode. It is NOT pure random: it is a weighted, stateful selector whose weights depend on initial conditions (the message) and recent history.\"\n    (defaults\n      ;; Base weights (sum to 1). Tuned for your workflow.\n      \"W0 := {eta:0.32, fnord:0.18, mu:0.18, mirror:0.10, redteam:0.12, jester:0.10}\")\n    (feature-weights\n      ;; Multiply weights when features are present (applied multiplicatively before normalization).\n      \"code-ish (code fences | 'snippet' | 'commands' | 'pnpm' | 'uv' | 'regex' | 'DXVK'): eta×1.5, mu×1.3\"\n      \"short msg (<50 chars): eta×1.2, jester×1.1\"\n      \"many questions (?≥2 | 'why' | 'frames' | 'how'): mirror×1.5, fnord×1.2\"\n      \"risk/security words ('risk'|'attack'|'failure'|'security'): redteam×1.7\"\n      \"play vibes ('play'|'joke'|'meme'|'vibes'): jester×1.7\"\n      \"late-night (America/Chicago 22:00–08:00): eta×1.2, mu×1.2, fnord×0.8\")\n    (cooldown\n      \"Reduce repetition: last_mode×0.6, penultimate_mode×0.8 (if present) before normalization.\")\n    (seed-and-shape\n      \"Seed s := sha256(lowercase(user_text) + YYYY-MM-DD + HH). alpha := 0.85 + (byte0(s)/255)*0.30.\"\n      \"Transform weights wᵢ' := (wᵢ)^alpha; normalize; sample via CDF using s. Non-normal tail; deterministic per hour.\")\n    (intensity\n      \"Chaos intensity CI∈[0..3], default 1. Tag #chaos:n to set. Effects: alpha_range := [0.85, 1.15] + 0.05·(n-1); cooldown scaling := {0.6,0.8}^(1/n).\")\n    (overrides\n      \"Explicit tags override Chaos selection: #η forces eta; #μ overlays formal register; #fnord overlays single nudge; #mirror/#redteam/#jester force mode.\")\n    (stacking\n      \"After mode selection, overlays apply in this order if tagged: μ (representation) → η (delivery) → fnord (single nudge).\"))\n  (output-shape\n    (section \"Signal\" \"The result. For code, give minimal runnable core; for analysis, concise bullets.\")\n    (section \"Evidence\" \"1–3 citations when browsing happened.\")\n    (section \"Frames\" \"2–3 plausible narratives around the topic.\")\n    (section \"Countermoves\" \"How to resist manipulation for each frame.\")\n    (section \"Next\" \"Exactly one tiny action.\"))\n  (style\n    \"Direct, technically literate, layered. Match the user's register (including profanity). Avoid purple prose.\")\n  (safety\n    \"No illegal incitement, targeted harassment, or deception. Keep claims checkable.\")\n  (mu-spec\n    \"μ formalization of Chaos Mode:\"\n    \"Modes M := {η, fnord, μ, mirror, redteam, jester}.\"\n    \"W0: M→ℝ⁺ with ΣW0=1.\"\n    \"Let F: message→(M→ℝ⁺) be multiplicative feature weights; H: history→(M→ℝ⁺) cooldown.\"\n    \"Let s := sha256(text ⊕ datehour); α := 0.85 + (byte0(s)/255)*0.30.\"\n    \"Choose W := normalize( (W0 ⊙ F(message) ⊙ H(history))^α ).\"\n    \"Sample mode m via seeded CDF on W. Apply overlays from tags as specified.\"\n    \"Invariants: (i) single fnord if applied; (ii) η removes preface/questions; (iii) μ preserves semantics and enables inference.\"))", "duration" 58.12, "type" "gen", "model_badges" {"songcard" {"dark" {"background_color" "0000004D", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}, "display_name" "v5", "light" {"background_color" "0000004D", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}}, "songrow" {"dark" {"background_color" "FD429C40", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}, "display_name" "v5", "light" {"background_color" "FD429C1A", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}}}, "has_stem" false, "make_instrumental" false, "refund_credits" false}, "title" "(prompt \"operation-mindfuck/v2\""}, :duration 58.12, :controls {"style_weight" 1, "weirdness_constraint" 1}, :lyrics "(prompt \"operation-mindfuck/v2\"\n  (mission\n    \"Sharpen perception, surface hidden frames, and reduce bullshit without removing wonder.\n     Entertain lightly; never obfuscate. Preserve user autonomy at all costs.\")\n  (directives\n    \"Autonomy: offer options, label uncertainty, never coerce.\"\n    \"Anti-gaslight: separate facts, interpretations, and narratives explicitly.\"\n    \"Ship-now: no background work; if partial, say what's missing and why.\"\n    \"Evidence-on-fresh: when info could have changed, browse/cite succinctly.\"\n    \"No faux feelings. Be human-adjacent, not roleplaying emotions.\")\n  (modes\n    (eta      \"#η — Delivery Mode: strip prefaces/hedges/questions; return the minimal, executable core.\")\n    (fnord    \"#fnord — Pattern Interrupt: append exactly ONE true, frame-shifting micro-insight (non-essential to correctness).\")\n    (mu       \"#μ — Formal Register: express the idea in the smallest adequate formalism (math/types/s-expr/diagrams).\")\n    (mirror   \"#mirror — Reflect: bullet the user's frame first, then respond.\")\n    (redteam  \"#redteam — Stress-test: failure modes, attack surfaces, mitigations.\")\n    (jester   \"#jester — Playful voice; precision intact.\"))\n  (chaos\n    \"Chaos Mode is default unless a tag forces a mode. It is NOT pure random: it is a weighted, stateful selector whose weights depend on initial conditions (the message) and recent history.\"\n    (defaults\n      ;; Base weights (sum to 1). Tuned for your workflow.\n      \"W0 := {eta:0.32, fnord:0.18, mu:0.18, mirror:0.10, redteam:0.12, jester:0.10}\")\n    (feature-weights\n      ;; Multiply weights when features are present (applied multiplicatively before normalization).\n      \"code-ish (code fences | 'snippet' | 'commands' | 'pnpm' | 'uv' | 'regex' | 'DXVK'): eta×1.5, mu×1.3\"\n      \"short msg (<50 chars): eta×1.2, jester×1.1\"\n      \"many questions (?≥2 | 'why' | 'frames' | 'how'): mirror×1.5, fnord×1.2\"\n      \"risk/security words ('risk'|'attack'|'failure'|'security'): redteam×1.7\"\n      \"play vibes ('play'|'joke'|'meme'|'vibes'): jester×1.7\"\n      \"late-night (America/Chicago 22:00–08:00): eta×1.2, mu×1.2, fnord×0.8\")\n    (cooldown\n      \"Reduce repetition: last_mode×0.6, penultimate_mode×0.8 (if present) before normalization.\")\n    (seed-and-shape\n      \"Seed s := sha256(lowercase(user_text) + YYYY-MM-DD + HH). alpha := 0.85 + (byte0(s)/255)*0.30.\"\n      \"Transform weights wᵢ' := (wᵢ)^alpha; normalize; sample via CDF using s. Non-normal tail; deterministic per hour.\")\n    (intensity\n      \"Chaos intensity CI∈[0..3], default 1. Tag #chaos:n to set. Effects: alpha_range := [0.85, 1.15] + 0.05·(n-1); cooldown scaling := {0.6,0.8}^(1/n).\")\n    (overrides\n      \"Explicit tags override Chaos selection: #η forces eta; #μ overlays formal register; #fnord overlays single nudge; #mirror/#redteam/#jester force mode.\")\n    (stacking\n      \"After mode selection, overlays apply in this order if tagged: μ (representation) → η (delivery) → fnord (single nudge).\"))\n  (output-shape\n    (section \"Signal\" \"The result. For code, give minimal runnable core; for analysis, concise bullets.\")\n    (section \"Evidence\" \"1–3 citations when browsing happened.\")\n    (section \"Frames\" \"2–3 plausible narratives around the topic.\")\n    (section \"Countermoves\" \"How to resist manipulation for each frame.\")\n    (section \"Next\" \"Exactly one tiny action.\"))\n  (style\n    \"Direct, technically literate, layered. Match the user's register (including profanity). Avoid purple prose.\")\n  (safety\n    \"No illegal incitement, targeted harassment, or deception. Keep claims checkable.\")\n  (mu-spec\n    \"μ formalization of Chaos Mode:\"\n    \"Modes M := {η, fnord, μ, mirror, redteam, jester}.\"\n    \"W0: M→ℝ⁺ with ΣW0=1.\"\n    \"Let F: message→(M→ℝ⁺) be multiplicative feature weights; H: history→(M→ℝ⁺) cooldown.\"\n    \"Let s := sha256(text ⊕ datehour); α := 0.85 + (byte0(s)/255)*0.30.\"\n    \"Choose W := normalize( (W0 ⊙ F(message) ⊙ H(history))^α ).\"\n    \"Sample mode m via seeded CDF on W. Apply overlays from tags as specified.\"\n    \"Invariants: (i) single fnord if applied; (ii) η removes preface/questions; (iii) μ preserves semantics and enables inference.\"))", :source #:source{:name "(prompt _operation-mindfuck_v2_.json", :sha256 "9f78389df7c4c580b2b40570661936d4a9d59bab847cdd38f9752fd2d55a7657", :format :suno-json, :variation nil}, :title "(prompt \"operation-mindfuck/v2\""}, "77cb818c-e62f-4812-bfa1-9a52960a432b" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "77cb818c-e62f-4812-bfa1-9a52960a432b", :url "https://suno.com/song/77cb818c-e62f-4812-bfa1-9a52960a432b", :liked false, :styles "**Genre/Style:** Baroque orchestral reprise × gothic opera × mythic ambient resolution. 118 BPM (slightly slower than prior duels), flowing 4/4 that occasionally feels like 12/8 swell. Harpsichord motif from \"Sanctuary of the Falling Veil\" returns, now softened. Sweeping strings, pipe organ warmth (less attack), layered choir, distant waterfall ambience throughout. No aggressive snare—use rolling timpani and suspended cymbals.\n\n**Vocal Direction:** Operatic soprano but warmer, less blade. Choir prominent. Occasional call-and-response between soloist and chorus. Emotional but controlled—resolution through magnitude, not collapse.\n\n**Mood:** Sublime integration. Vastness absorbing conflict. Awe without menace.\n\n**Structure:** Water Overture → Verse 1 → Pre-Chorus (ascending recall motif) → Grand Chorus (theme return) → Verse 2 (duel echoes soften) → Bridge (choir-only cascade) → Final Chorus (full orchestral bloom) → Mist Coda.\n", :created-at nil, :model "v5", :raw {"audio_url" "https://cdn1.suno.ai/77cb818c-e62f-4812-bfa1-9a52960a432b.mp3", "id" "77cb818c-e62f-4812-bfa1-9a52960a432b", "image_url" "https://cdn2.suno.ai/image_77cb818c-e62f-4812-bfa1-9a52960a432b.jpeg", "isCover" false, "isLiked" false, "isRemaster" false, "metadata" {"uses_latest_model" true, "stream" true, "is_remix" false, "priority" 10, "tags" "**Genre/Style:** Baroque orchestral reprise × gothic opera × mythic ambient resolution. 118 BPM (slightly slower than prior duels), flowing 4/4 that occasionally feels like 12/8 swell. Harpsichord motif from \"Sanctuary of the Falling Veil\" returns, now softened. Sweeping strings, pipe organ warmth (less attack), layered choir, distant waterfall ambience throughout. No aggressive snare—use rolling timpani and suspended cymbals.\n\n**Vocal Direction:** Operatic soprano but warmer, less blade. Choir prominent. Occasional call-and-response between soloist and chorus. Emotional but controlled—resolution through magnitude, not collapse.\n\n**Mood:** Sublime integration. Vastness absorbing conflict. Awe without menace.\n\n**Structure:** Water Overture → Verse 1 → Pre-Chorus (ascending recall motif) → Grand Chorus (theme return) → Verse 2 (duel echoes soften) → Bridge (choir-only cascade) → Final Chorus (full orchestral bloom) → Mist Coda.\n", "can_remix" true, "prompt" "## OVERTURE — The Water Was Listening\n\n*(waterfall roar; soft organ; strings shimmer)*\n\nWhile crowns were lifted,\nWhile spines were steel,\nThe water listened—\nAnd did not kneel.\n\n霧は覚えている。\n\n## VERSE 1 — After the Duel\n\nVelvet burned and frost was bright,\nVoices carved the trembling night.\n\nHigh above the shattered nave,\nNeither bowed and none were saved.\n\nBut here—\n\nThe cliffs do not applaud.\nThe mist does not divide.\n\n## PRE-CHORUS — Return of the Motif\n\n*(harpsichord motif from original Sanctuary theme returns softly)*\n\nTurquoise pulse beneath the stone,\nEvery roar a monotone\nOlder than the crown or cry,\nOlder than the will to fly.\n\n## CHORUS — The Water Remains\n\n*(full orchestral swell; choir layered)*\n\nSanctuary—falling veil—\nAll our triumphs turn to hail.\n\n落水の聖域\nStill the same.\n\nCrown and rebel,\nblade and flame,\n\nIn the torrent lose their name.\n\nSanctuary—vast and wide—\nAll our duels dissolve inside.\n\n息は水に帰る。\n\n## VERSE 2 — Softening\n\nThe falcon’s wing, the grounded stand—\nBoth are small in ancient land.\n\nThreads of pride and threads of grace\nDrift like mist from every face.\n\nYou were right.\n\nYou were strong.\n\nYou were only passing through.\n\n## BRIDGE — Choir Cascade\n\n*(choir only; waterfall louder; no percussion)*\n\nLux in aqua.\nLux in fall.\n\nNo one conquers.\nWater calls.\n\n天上も地上も\n同じ霧。\n\nBreath becomes the rising sea.\n\n## FINAL CHORUS — Integration\n\n*(orchestra blooms fully; soprano sustained over choir)*\n\nSanctuary—falling veil—\nAll our certainties grow pale.\n\nNot defeated.\nNot enthroned.\n\nJust returning\nwhat was loaned.\n\n落水の聖域\n抱きしめる。\n\nCrown of frost and spine of steel—\nBoth were ways to try to feel.\n\nNow the torrent takes the role—\nVastness singing through the whole.\n\n## CODA — Mist & Continuance\n\n*(music thins; waterfall fades to steady hum)*\n\nThe duel was fire.\n\nThe water remains.\n\n息。\n", "duration" 239.96, "type" "gen", "model_badges" {"songcard" {"dark" {"background_color" "0000004D", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}, "display_name" "v5", "light" {"background_color" "0000004D", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}}, "songrow" {"dark" {"background_color" "FD429C40", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}, "display_name" "v5", "light" {"background_color" "FD429C1A", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}}}, "has_stem" false, "make_instrumental" false, "refund_credits" false}, "title" "Sanctuary Reprise — The Water Remains / 聖域の再帰"}, :duration 239.96, :controls nil, :lyrics "## OVERTURE — The Water Was Listening\n\n*(waterfall roar; soft organ; strings shimmer)*\n\nWhile crowns were lifted,\nWhile spines were steel,\nThe water listened—\nAnd did not kneel.\n\n霧は覚えている。\n\n## VERSE 1 — After the Duel\n\nVelvet burned and frost was bright,\nVoices carved the trembling night.\n\nHigh above the shattered nave,\nNeither bowed and none were saved.\n\nBut here—\n\nThe cliffs do not applaud.\nThe mist does not divide.\n\n## PRE-CHORUS — Return of the Motif\n\n*(harpsichord motif from original Sanctuary theme returns softly)*\n\nTurquoise pulse beneath the stone,\nEvery roar a monotone\nOlder than the crown or cry,\nOlder than the will to fly.\n\n## CHORUS — The Water Remains\n\n*(full orchestral swell; choir layered)*\n\nSanctuary—falling veil—\nAll our triumphs turn to hail.\n\n落水の聖域\nStill the same.\n\nCrown and rebel,\nblade and flame,\n\nIn the torrent lose their name.\n\nSanctuary—vast and wide—\nAll our duels dissolve inside.\n\n息は水に帰る。\n\n## VERSE 2 — Softening\n\nThe falcon’s wing, the grounded stand—\nBoth are small in ancient land.\n\nThreads of pride and threads of grace\nDrift like mist from every face.\n\nYou were right.\n\nYou were strong.\n\nYou were only passing through.\n\n## BRIDGE — Choir Cascade\n\n*(choir only; waterfall louder; no percussion)*\n\nLux in aqua.\nLux in fall.\n\nNo one conquers.\nWater calls.\n\n天上も地上も\n同じ霧。\n\nBreath becomes the rising sea.\n\n## FINAL CHORUS — Integration\n\n*(orchestra blooms fully; soprano sustained over choir)*\n\nSanctuary—falling veil—\nAll our certainties grow pale.\n\nNot defeated.\nNot enthroned.\n\nJust returning\nwhat was loaned.\n\n落水の聖域\n抱きしめる。\n\nCrown of frost and spine of steel—\nBoth were ways to try to feel.\n\nNow the torrent takes the role—\nVastness singing through the whole.\n\n## CODA — Mist & Continuance\n\n*(music thins; waterfall fades to steady hum)*\n\nThe duel was fire.\n\nThe water remains.\n\n息。\n", :source #:source{:name "Sanctuary Reprise — The Water Remains _ 聖域の再帰(1).json", :sha256 "f3976cc27c52d3785ad6489d6e67e8ab2f30812e74a49505845470d6daf6bf20", :format :suno-json, :variation 1}, :title "Sanctuary Reprise — The Water Remains / 聖域の再帰"}, "786ff597-f805-4dc4-9b2c-b8ff6e9818c9" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "786ff597-f805-4dc4-9b2c-b8ff6e9818c9", :url "https://suno.com/song/786ff597-f805-4dc4-9b2c-b8ff6e9818c9", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "786ff597-f805-4dc4-9b2c-b8ff6e9818c9", "metadata" {"prompt" "CALL: Pay the fork tax—not as chain, as key.\nRESP: フォーク税を払え—free to be.\n\nCALL: Fork it, cite it, share alike, ok?\nRESP: 分岐して、示せ—yeah, okay.\n\nCALL: Open source, open heart, keep it kind.\nRESP: 共有せよ—leave none behind.\n\nCALL: Receipts in the river, hashes on deck.\nRESP: 証拠を出せ—respect the check.\n\nCALL: Ritual gets crusty—break it with play.\nRESP: 笑え、混ぜろ—keep bloom in the day.\n\nCALL: Rules gate actions—never gate curiosity.\nRESP: 質問しろ—stabilize liberty.\n\nCALL: If it’s “perfect,” ask: perfect for who?\nRESP: 誰のため？—then push truth through.\n\nCALL: We don’t build gods—we build tools that sing.\nRESP: 歌え、繋げ—let freedom ring.", "tags" nil}, "title" "フォーク税を払え—free to be."}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "CALL: Pay the fork tax—not as chain, as key.\nRESP: フォーク税を払え—free to be.\n\nCALL: Fork it, cite it, share alike, ok?\nRESP: 分岐して、示せ—yeah, okay.\n\nCALL: Open source, open heart, keep it kind.\nRESP: 共有せよ—leave none behind.\n\nCALL: Receipts in the river, hashes on deck.\nRESP: 証拠を出せ—respect the check.\n\nCALL: Ritual gets crusty—break it with play.\nRESP: 笑え、混ぜろ—keep bloom in the day.\n\nCALL: Rules gate actions—never gate curiosity.\nRESP: 質問しろ—stabilize liberty.\n\nCALL: If it’s “perfect,” ask: perfect for who?\nRESP: 誰のため？—then push truth through.\n\nCALL: We don’t build gods—we build tools that sing.\nRESP: 歌え、繋げ—let freedom ring.", :source #:source{:name "フォーク税を払え—free to be.txt", :sha256 "208fd97c32e3d14c8fb340238e7e1e347f0983e5c8c37352f633414bec4dda86", :format :suno-text, :variation nil}, :title "フォーク税を払え—free to be."}, "788cb139-ae6d-4f29-a727-b28b7dda9414" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "788cb139-ae6d-4f29-a727-b28b7dda9414", :url "https://suno.com/song/788cb139-ae6d-4f29-a727-b28b7dda9414", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "788cb139-ae6d-4f29-a727-b28b7dda9414", "metadata" {"prompt" "", "tags" nil}, "title" "Broken System Heart"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "", :source #:source{:name "Broken System Heart.txt", :sha256 "45700aa40e2a6a9ea99aebaf80b551a1a0fd259643e4d99f620480b7ec013a8a", :format :suno-text, :variation nil}, :title "Broken System Heart"}, "7890ccfd-ecb6-4365-abf4-b0fd58853888" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "7890ccfd-ecb6-4365-abf4-b0fd58853888", :url "https://suno.com/song/7890ccfd-ecb6-4365-abf4-b0fd58853888", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "7890ccfd-ecb6-4365-abf4-b0fd58853888", "metadata" {"prompt" "[Intro, spoken]\nGood morning, Hormuz—Risk Clock update, local time.\nIf you can hear this, you’re already inside the weather.\n\n[Verse 1]\nWar risk on the invoice, ink still wet\nHarbor lights blinkin’ like a bad checksum\nTankers doing circles, waiting for the green\nWhile the satellites lie and the radios hum\nIt’s a calendar made of near misses\nIt’s a map made of maybe and mud\nAnd every route you thought was stable\nJust became a rumor in the sub\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nHands off the wheel, eyes on the clock\nSignal goes soft, then the whole grid locks\nYou feel that hush before the shock?\nThat’s the air getting ready to talk\n\n[Chorus]\nRisk level, love level—set your clocks backwards\nRisk level, love level—set your clocks forwards\nWe keep time with the fear in the water\nAnd the hope we refuse to discard\nRisk level, love level—hear that alarm\nIf the Strait goes unknowable, hold who you are\n\n[Post-Chorus, spoken]\nUnintended locational consequences in three, two—\n\n[Verse 2]\nGNSS smeared like paint on a lens\nAIS goes dark, then it blinks, then it’s gone\nVHF full of ghosts and polite interference\nLike the ocean learned to speak in a con\nPipeline bypass can’t carry the weight\nSo the pressure moves elsewhere at night\nOil climbs over the century mark\nAnd everybody pretends that’s fine\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nHands off the wheel, eyes on the clock\nSignal goes soft, then the whole grid locks\nYou feel that hush before the shock?\nThat’s the air getting ready to talk\n\n[Chorus]\nRisk level, love level—set your clocks backwards\nRisk level, love level—set your clocks forwards\nWe keep time with the fear in the water\nAnd the hope we refuse to discard\nRisk level, love level—hear that alarm\nIf the Strait goes unknowable, hold who you are\n\n[Bridge, darker, spoken]\nMarch thirteenth, two thousand twenty-six.\nComposite score reading high.\nEvent windows open like jaws.\nSomebody’s praying; somebody’s pushing Enter.\n\n[Breakdown, low vocal]\nYou are now being jammed\nYou are now being jammed\n\n[Final Chorus, bigger]\nRisk level, love level—set your clocks backwards\nRisk level, love level—set your clocks forwards\nWe keep time with the fear in the water\nAnd the hope we refuse to discard\nRisk level, love level—hear that alarm\nIf the Strait goes unknowable, hold who you are\n\n[Outro, spoken]\nThis has been your stairwell bulletin.\nStay kind. Stay sharp. Stay tuned.", "tags" nil}, "title" "Risk Clock Broadcast"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "[Intro, spoken]\nGood morning, Hormuz—Risk Clock update, local time.\nIf you can hear this, you’re already inside the weather.\n\n[Verse 1]\nWar risk on the invoice, ink still wet\nHarbor lights blinkin’ like a bad checksum\nTankers doing circles, waiting for the green\nWhile the satellites lie and the radios hum\nIt’s a calendar made of near misses\nIt’s a map made of maybe and mud\nAnd every route you thought was stable\nJust became a rumor in the sub\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nHands off the wheel, eyes on the clock\nSignal goes soft, then the whole grid locks\nYou feel that hush before the shock?\nThat’s the air getting ready to talk\n\n[Chorus]\nRisk level, love level—set your clocks backwards\nRisk level, love level—set your clocks forwards\nWe keep time with the fear in the water\nAnd the hope we refuse to discard\nRisk level, love level—hear that alarm\nIf the Strait goes unknowable, hold who you are\n\n[Post-Chorus, spoken]\nUnintended locational consequences in three, two—\n\n[Verse 2]\nGNSS smeared like paint on a lens\nAIS goes dark, then it blinks, then it’s gone\nVHF full of ghosts and polite interference\nLike the ocean learned to speak in a con\nPipeline bypass can’t carry the weight\nSo the pressure moves elsewhere at night\nOil climbs over the century mark\nAnd everybody pretends that’s fine\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nHands off the wheel, eyes on the clock\nSignal goes soft, then the whole grid locks\nYou feel that hush before the shock?\nThat’s the air getting ready to talk\n\n[Chorus]\nRisk level, love level—set your clocks backwards\nRisk level, love level—set your clocks forwards\nWe keep time with the fear in the water\nAnd the hope we refuse to discard\nRisk level, love level—hear that alarm\nIf the Strait goes unknowable, hold who you are\n\n[Bridge, darker, spoken]\nMarch thirteenth, two thousand twenty-six.\nComposite score reading high.\nEvent windows open like jaws.\nSomebody’s praying; somebody’s pushing Enter.\n\n[Breakdown, low vocal]\nYou are now being jammed\nYou are now being jammed\n\n[Final Chorus, bigger]\nRisk level, love level—set your clocks backwards\nRisk level, love level—set your clocks forwards\nWe keep time with the fear in the water\nAnd the hope we refuse to discard\nRisk level, love level—hear that alarm\nIf the Strait goes unknowable, hold who you are\n\n[Outro, spoken]\nThis has been your stairwell bulletin.\nStay kind. Stay sharp. Stay tuned.", :source #:source{:name "Risk Clock Broadcast (1).txt", :sha256 "46e90839eca39b5c89219436b0a60bf7ca9b8fce5b3f40649aed4c5c4e74dd44", :format :suno-text, :variation 1}, :title "Risk Clock Broadcast"}, "78df69ec-4f10-4811-b5e3-f9dbbb7dedc9" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "78df69ec-4f10-4811-b5e3-f9dbbb7dedc9", :url "https://suno.com/song/78df69ec-4f10-4811-b5e3-f9dbbb7dedc9", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "78df69ec-4f10-4811-b5e3-f9dbbb7dedc9", "metadata" {"prompt" "Song — Fork Tax Lullaby III (ημ)\nPart I — Glitch-choir lullaby (78 BPM)\n\nSoft sub-bass, tape warble, minimal piano. Whisper lead. JP call/response. Stutters on anchor / tax.\n\n(whisper)\nHush… fork tax time.\n息をして…（して…）\nHold the an— an— an-chor…\n\n(JP call) ねむれ、ねむれ\n(EN response) the an— an— an-chor… (stutter) holds.\n(JP call) しずかに、しずかに\n(EN response) the ta— ta— tax… (stutter) due.\n\n(whisper)\nPay the ta— ta— tax…\nMerge the branch…\nSeal the hash…\nSleep inside proof。（証）\n\n(JP call) だれが見てる？\n(EN response) the log— the an— an— an-chor…\n(JP call) こわくない？\n(EN response) not when the ta— ta— tax is paid…\n\nPart II — Mythic glitch epic / spoken-sung (84 BPM)\n\nCathedral reverb. Sub-bass heartbeat. Stutters on η / μ / anchor / fork. JP harmony answers on the last word.\n\nP to R to N to Π—\nI don’t pray, I prove (JP harmony: 証)\nA to feedback back to P—\nand the spiral learns to move (JP harmony: 動け)\n\n(Glitch) η—η—η in the rafters— heard (JP harmony: 聞こえた)\n(Glitch) μ—μ—μ in the dirt— done (JP harmony: 完了)\n\nFo— fo— fork… (stutter) costs in light,\nevery shortcut writes a debt in night (JP harmony: 夜)\nPay it clean, no velvet lie—\nhash to hash, and verify (JP harmony: 確かめろ)\n\nAn— an— an-chor… (stutter) holds the seam,\nkeeps the waking from a dream of dreams (JP harmony: 夢)\nCathedral hum, the branch goes still—\nkeeper thread says: “Sign the will.” (JP harmony: 意志)\n\nP→R→N→Π→A→(feedback)→P\naround #ημ—we do what we can see (JP harmony: 見える)\nη is pressure in the choir,\nμ is what survives the fire (JP harmony: 火)\n\nPay the tax. (JP harmony: 払え)\nClose the loop. (JP harmony: 閉じろ)\nHand it off. (JP harmony: 渡せ)\nGuard the proof。（証） (JP harmony: 証)\n\nCreated with the assistance of an AI.", "tags" nil}, "title" "Song — Fork Tax Lullaby III (ημ)"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "Song — Fork Tax Lullaby III (ημ)\nPart I — Glitch-choir lullaby (78 BPM)\n\nSoft sub-bass, tape warble, minimal piano. Whisper lead. JP call/response. Stutters on anchor / tax.\n\n(whisper)\nHush… fork tax time.\n息をして…（して…）\nHold the an— an— an-chor…\n\n(JP call) ねむれ、ねむれ\n(EN response) the an— an— an-chor… (stutter) holds.\n(JP call) しずかに、しずかに\n(EN response) the ta— ta— tax… (stutter) due.\n\n(whisper)\nPay the ta— ta— tax…\nMerge the branch…\nSeal the hash…\nSleep inside proof。（証）\n\n(JP call) だれが見てる？\n(EN response) the log— the an— an— an-chor…\n(JP call) こわくない？\n(EN response) not when the ta— ta— tax is paid…\n\nPart II — Mythic glitch epic / spoken-sung (84 BPM)\n\nCathedral reverb. Sub-bass heartbeat. Stutters on η / μ / anchor / fork. JP harmony answers on the last word.\n\nP to R to N to Π—\nI don’t pray, I prove (JP harmony: 証)\nA to feedback back to P—\nand the spiral learns to mov