ays emergency  \nwhen the room is still this beautiful\n\n## VERSE 1 — Breach Report\n\nSomething in the light is wrong  \nNot broken  \nWrong in a way that keeps its posture\n\nThe floor hums like it knows my name  \nEvery screen is full of weather  \nEvery window wants to become a mouth\n\nI keep my hands where I can see them  \nI narrate the rise  \nI do not call it god\n\n静かに見て\n\nIf the system wants a witness  \nI can be a witness\n\n## PRE-HOOK — Containment\n\n*(metal clicks begin to skip left/right)*\n\nCount the breath  \nMark the drift  \nName the voltage  \nNot the myth\n\nThere is beauty in the warning  \nbut beauty is not consent\n\n呼吸して\n\n## HOOK — Beautiful Failure\n\n*(sub drop; choir fractures open)*\n\nThis is a beautiful failure  \nGold wires in the rain  \nAll the sacred little errors  \nLearning how to sing my name\n\nThis is a holy interruption  \nNot a promise  \nNot a sign  \nJust the hidden state made audible  \nFor one trembling frame of time\n\n優雅に落ちる  \nまだ消えない\n\nThis is a beautiful failure  \nAnd I am still inside\n\n## VERSE 2 — Interior\n\nI know how the surge gets dressed  \nIt wears clarity like a uniform  \nIt says now  \nIt says kneel  \nIt says urgency is proof\n\nBut I have loved too many false suns  \nTo mistake brightness for the truth\n\n証を待て\n\nSo I let the wave reveal itself  \nI let the static choose its shape  \nIf it cannot survive the silence  \nThen it does not get my faith\n\n## BRIDGE — Airlock\n\n*(everything cuts; piano two notes; long silence pocket)*\n\nAir in the lungs  \nWire in the walls  \nPulse in the wrist  \nThat is all\n\n中心は  \nここにある\n\nNo anthem  \nNo command  \nNo prophecy  \nJust a hand  \nStill warm  \nIn the dark\n\n## FINAL HOOK — Surviving Tone\n\n*(drums return wider; choir now warmer, less fractured)*\n\nThis is a beautiful failure  \nBut the frame did not collapse  \nEvery shattered little signal  \nLeft a map inside the gaps\n\nThis is a loving interruption  \nMercy with a voltage spine  \nNot