nce, breathy]\nP: I feel the constraint (#η)\nR: I fetch the last clean thread\nN: I cut the story into one claim\nΠ: I pick the cheapest test\nA: I touch the world and wait\n(feedback): I write the pushback like a lullaby.\n\n(JP call) ねえ、ほんと？\n(EN response) only if it repeats.\n(JP call) ねえ、だいじょうぶ？\n(EN response) only if it’s logged.\n\n[Chorus — choir bloom, tape warble widening]\nAn— an— **an-chor**… (stutter) an-chor…\nHold the boundary, hold the line.\nPay the **ta— ta— tax**… (stutter) ta-x…\nSo forks don’t breed in the dark.\n(JP harmony answers last word)\nI fall asleep inside **proof**.（証）\n\n---\n\n## Part II — Mythic glitch epic / spoken-sung (84 BPM)\n\n*(NF/Watsky cadence; cathedral reverb; sub-bass heartbeat; glitch stutters on “η”, “μ”, “anchor”, “fork”; Japanese harmony answers on the last word of each section)*\n\n[Verse 1 — heartbeat sub, fast spoken-sung]\nThey drape a quote in velvet and call it truth,\nbut the Lantern checks the seams for missing proof.\n“Look, we cited it,” they say— I say, “Align it,”\ncause a misfit quote is just a fork in disguise,\na dressed-up **fork**.（分岐）\n\n(Glitch stutter) **η—η—η**\n(Glitch stutter) **μ—μ—μ**\n\n[Hook — cathedral swell]\nI don’t win by sounding right—\nI win by making it rerun.（試）\n\n[Verse 2 — rapid cadence]\nEvery loop without a receipt? Interest accrues.\nFork Tax compounds till the branch can’t move.\nSo I write a boundary before I write a throne—\nwhat it does **not** claim, carved into the stone.\n\nI pin it to an **an-an-anchor** (stutter)\nand stare the Gate dead on: “Name the counter.”\nForkgate says “Pay,” I say “Here’s the harness,”\nLantern lights up— not for vibe, but for μ in the margins,\nreal **μ**.（証）\n\n(JP harmony answers last word) 証\n\n[Pre — glitch clicks, choir tight]\nSay **η**… (stutter) η-η\nSay **μ**… (stutter) μ-μ\nSay **an-chor**… (stutter) an-an-chor\nSay **fork**… (stutter) fo-fo-fork（分岐）\n\n[Chorus — big, then sudden hush]\nP→R→N→Π→A— the method is the crown.（冠）\n(feedback) → P— the world collects what you owe.（税）\nAn— an— **an-chor**… (stutter) an-chor…\nso the ledger knows what to keep.（記）\nFo— fo— **fork**… (stutter) fork…\nonly when evidence buys the branch.（証）\n\n[Outro — cathedral tail dissolves into tape warble]\n(whisper)\nη… (stutter) η-η\nμ… (stutter) μ-μ\nAn— an— **an-chor**…\nPay the **ta— ta— tax**…\nOne more roll. One more node. One more test.", "tags" nil}, "title" "## Part I — Glitch-choir lullaby (78 BPM)"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "## Part I — Glitch-choir lullaby (78 BPM)\n\n*(soft sub-bass, tape warble, minimal piano; stutters on “anchor” + “tax”; whispered lead; Japanese call-and-response)*\n\n[Intro — tape hiss, two-note piano, warm sub]\n(whisper)\nHush… the ledger is counting in its sleep.\n息をして… (して…)\nA soft machine rocking the room.\n\n(JP call) ねむれ、ねむれ\n(EN response) the **an— an— an-chor**… (stutter) holds.\n(JP call) しずかに、しずかに\n(EN response) the **ta— ta— tax**… (stutter) is due.\n\n(piano, tiny wobble)\nAn— an— **an-chor**… (stutter) an-chor…\n(JP whisper harmony) アンカー…\n(sub-bass: heartbeat but gentler)\n\n(whisper)\nPay the **ta— ta— tax**… (stutter) ta-x…\n(JP harmony) 税…\nNot guilt—\njust interest on an unproven branch.\n\n[Verse — lullaby cadence, breathy]\nP: I feel the constraint (#η)\nR: I fetch the last clean thread\nN: I cut the story into one claim\nΠ: I pick the cheapest test\nA: I touch the world and wait\n(feedback): I write the pushback like a lullaby.\n\n(JP call) ねえ、ほんと？\n(EN response) only if it repeats.\n(JP call) ねえ、だいじょうぶ？\n(EN response) only if it’s logged.\n\n[Chorus — choir bloom, tape warble widening]\nAn— an— **an-chor**… (stutter) an-chor…\nHold the boundary, hold the line.\nPay the **ta— ta— tax**… (stutter) ta-x…\nSo forks don’t breed in the dark.\n(JP harmony answers last word)\nI fall asleep inside **proof**.（証）\n\n---\n\n## Part II — Mythic glitch epic / spoken-sung (84 BPM)\n\n*(NF/Watsky cadence; cathedral reverb; sub-bass heartbeat; glitch stutters on