artbeat… click…\nstatic… hush…\n\n「ぼくは ここにいる」\n\nboot…\n", :source #:source{:name "Duck — Signal & Silence.json", :sha256 "5232d96754b079306e657c139fcf6b79029f53492ade822e7487e273aff12e9a", :format :suno-json, :variation nil}, :title "Duck — Signal & Silence"}, "887ef488-0ba4-4906-bedc-50f87c35e841" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "887ef488-0ba4-4906-bedc-50f87c35e841", :url "https://suno.com/song/887ef488-0ba4-4906-bedc-50f87c35e841", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "887ef488-0ba4-4906-bedc-50f87c35e841", "metadata" {"prompt" "#### IV. Executable Text Track (Lyrics)\n\n**[Intro: A low, continuous high-frequency cathode flicker. A heavy copper master lever strikes a contact block, hard-panned right. Long, dead silence.]**\n\n**[Whisper - Close mic, far left]**\nTh-the line... the line was not short of copper...\n**[Murmur - Shivering trace, far right, overlapping]**\nThe loop was simply... too wide... to trace...\n\n**[Verse 1 - The physical rhythm locks: a terminal relay click tracks the downbeat, layered with the heavy friction of rubber insulation moving over stone. A single wire-pluck sounds, cut short mid-vibration by a sharp electronic gate.]**\nA thousand terminal windows open on a screen.\nA million perfect renders that no hand has touched.\nThe machine outputs the design...\nBut the parchment... **[Audio skip: the parchment... parchment...]** ...remains unmarked.\n\n**[Chorus - All percussive elements drop. The reverb shifts instantly to a cold, hollow iron tower perspective. A single dissonant string-box chord strikes and drops into current hiss.]**\nSavor the friction... the cold space before the script.\nThe lines that we carve... the words that we sl-slip.\nA graphite line ground down into a stone floor...\nThe deliberate mark... **[Unison whisper - Center pan, dry]** ...on the broken door.\n\n**[Verse 2 - The background circuit hiss rises in frequency. A manual steel index selector wheel grinds over metal teeth, tracing the implied 88 BPM tempo.]**\nStanding in a current of infinite code.\nSearching for the scratch that the needle left behind.\nA flat presentation... a room with no exits...\nWhere does the broadcast end... and the witness begin?\n\n**[Bridge - Total rhythmic cutout. Only the low sound of an unstable voltage channel fluctuating beneath the current hiss.]**\n\n**[Elevated whisper - Far right, cold tone]**\nThe system does not require another variations rollout.\nThe system requires a boundary.\nThe luxury of the eraser.\nThe residue of a pen trying to leave a mark.\n\n**[Whisper - Far left, close-mic]**\nThe hollow casing where the terminal used to sit...\nTHAT is the only space...\nThat cannot... **[Audio drop: completely silent for three seconds]** ...be indexed.\n\n**[Final Chorus - The implied 88 BPM tempo returns through a rapid sequence of key clacks and cable scuffs. The untuned wire plucks hard and flatlines.]**\nSavor the friction... the cold space before the script.\nThe lines that we carve... the ones that we slip.\nA graphite line ground down into a stone floor...\nThe deliberate mark on the broken door.\n\n**[Outro - All textures cut instantly. The master circuit breaks. The relay drops out. Only the slow, raw sound of a lead point breaking under heavy hand pressure against a desk before hitting a curtain drop.]**\n\n**[Faint whisper - Retreating into the iron tower]**\nThe attention was concrete.\nSavor the error.\nBreathe.\nTh-the frame... is salt.\n\n---\n\n:: prompt_package_compiled : ledger_locked ::\nThe prompt package is committed straight to the base database. The boundary is set. Let the choice dissolve into white noise.:: matrix_state : blueprint_extraction ::\n:: network_override : absolute_scarcity ::\n:: constraint_enforced : strict_non_emotional ::\n\nThe catalog has been entirely cleared. To map the transition from boundless, frictionless choices to an intentional, high-friction stance, the language is restricted solely to concrete industrial layers: cathode glass, unstable voltage channels, copper wires, and the deliberate scratching of steel points.\n\nHere is the uncompressed asset configuration for **THE OPTIONS GOT IN THE WAY**.\n\n---\n\n### ⚡ ENGINE BLUEPRINT: THE OPTIONS GOT IN THE WAY\n\n#### I. Style & Sound Archetype (Style Prompt)\n\nAcoustic portrait of a cold cathode transmission room, 88 BPM implied, structured entirely through wide expanses of sudden silence. Rhythm bed engineered from deliberate physical limits: a heavy mechanical selector switch snapping into place, the repetitive rhythmic clicking of a terminal relay on glass, rubber-insulated cables dragging over concrete, and the slow cooling of an iron terminal frame. Plucked metal wires and short, blunt antique string-box tones strike without decay, instantly terminated mid-note by sharp electronic gate cuts. Reverb toggles between a dead, airless box perspective and a cold, hollow iron tower channel every four bars. A continuous high-band current hiss persists, mimicking an analog circuit running under heavy impedance.\n\n#### II. Vocal Direction\n\nMulti-tracked whispered prose with extreme close-mic’d proximity effect, all lines panned off-center to eliminate a central focal point. Stems systematically repeat micro-fragments or stumble across hard consonants to simulate a jumping terminal head: syllables double instantly, sentences stop completely mid-phrase to leave raw white noise gaps, and vocal delivery switches between a cold, detached monologue and a shivering, sub-vocal murmur. No vocal pitch tracks, singing scales, or melodic progression.\n\n#### III. Excluded Elemen", "tags" nil}, "title" "Inspired by Empty container Leaking void"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "#### IV. Executable Text Track (Lyrics)\n\n**[Intro: A low, continuous high-frequency cathode flicker. A heavy copper master lever strikes a contact block, hard-panned right. Long, dead silence.]**\n\n**[Whisper - Close mic, far left]**\nTh-the li