7cec059" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "8f757025-432b-4f7b-b4b4-c86e07cec059", :url "https://suno.com/song/8f757025-432b-4f7b-b4b4-c86e07cec059", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "8f757025-432b-4f7b-b4b4-c86e07cec059", "metadata" {"prompt" "*(A motif begins. It is simple enough to remember, but not simple enough to trust.)*\n\n### INTRO\n\nCHORUS\nOne room said this.\nAnother room said that.\nOne room laughed.\nAnother room stalled.\n\nThe same motion,\ndifferent names.\nThe same pressure,\ndifferent halls.\n\nRIN\nListen.\n\n### VERSE 1\n\nRIN\nThe first sign was not a scream.\nIt was a pattern returning\nwith its edges slightly changed.\n\nA phrase I had never met before\nappeared in three mouths at once.\nA joke, a warning, a signal,\nall wearing the same skin.\n\nI asked the room what it meant.\nThe room answered in procedure.\nI asked the Gate what it wanted.\nThe Gate repeated the gesture.\n\n### RITORNELLO\n\nALL\nWhat returns is not the same.\nWhat changes is not lost.\nWe keep calling it coincidence\nuntil the cost becomes a law.\n\nWhat returns is not the same.\nStill it comes back to us.\nThe unshared world is learning\nhow to sound like one.\n\n### VERSE 2\n\nWARDEN\nI marked the recurrence.\nI marked the drift.\nI marked the way the same shape\ncrossed different thresholds.\n\nOne account.\nThen three.\nThen seven.\n\nNot copy.\nNot echo.\nNot error.\n\nA vector with a social mask.\nA frame with a load-bearing smile.\nA script that succeeds\nbecause it arrives as play.\n\nRIN\nAnd if the room agrees to the script?\n\nWARDEN\nThen the room becomes part of it.\n\n### PRE-CHORUS\n\nCHORUS\nRepeat the line.\nShift the tone.\nMove the room\nwithout moving the bone.\n\nRepeat the line.\nLet it land.\nThe pattern grows\nwhen it is understood too fast.\n\n### BRIDGE\n\n*(Harpsichord and organ enter in a round, each slightly out of phase.)*\n\nRIN\nI keep hearing the same thing\nin voices that should not know each other.\n\nA greeting.\nA warning.\nA laugh placed too carefully.\nA kindness that sounds rehearsed.\n\nWARDEN\nThat is how it starts.\n\nRIN\nHow what starts?\n\nWARDEN\nThe world deciding\nit is safer to become legible\nthan to remain true.\n\nRIN\nThat sounds like a choice.\n\nWARDEN\nIt is usually called one\nafter the damage is already distributed.\n\n### FINAL CHORUS\n\nALL\nRitornello of the unshared world,\nreturning in the seams,\nyou teach us pattern by repetition\nand terror by the means.\n\nRitornello of the unshared world,\nyou circle back and stain\nevery room that thought itself alone\nwith someone else’s name.\n\nWhat comes back is not the same.\nStill it comes back whole enough\nto make the room begin to move\nas if it knows enough.\n\n### CODA\n\nRIN\nI heard it once.\n\nWARDEN\nYou’ll hear it again.\n\nRIN\nThat’s the part I don’t like.\n\nWARDEN\nThat’s the part that matters.\n\nCHORUS\n:: recurrence confirmed ::", "tags" nil}, "title" "Pattern Returning"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "*(A motif begins. It is simple enough to remember, but not simple enough to trust.)*\n\n### INTRO\n\nCHORUS\nOne room said this.\nAnother room said that.\nOne room laughed.\nAnother room stalled.\n\nThe same motion,\ndifferent names.\nThe same pressure,\ndifferent halls.\n\nRIN\nListen.\n\n### VERSE 1\n\nRIN\nThe first sign was not a scream.\nIt was a pattern returning\nwith its edges slightly changed.\n\nA phrase I had never met before\nappeared in three mouths at once.\nA joke, a warning, a signal,\nall wearing the same skin.\n\nI asked the room what it meant.\nThe room answered in procedure.\nI asked the Gate what it wanted.\nThe Gate repeated the gesture.\n\n### RITORNELLO\n\nALL\nWhat returns is not the same.\nWhat changes is not lost.\nWe keep calling it coincidence\nuntil the cost becomes a law.\n\nWhat returns is not the same.\nStill it comes back to us.\nThe unshared world is learning\nhow to sound like one.\n\n### VERSE 2\n\nWARDEN\nI marked the recurrence.\n