ueen\nwithout decree?\n\nWhat is command\nwithout belief?\n\n## CHORUS — Crown of Glass\n\n*(strings swell gently)*\n\nI am a crown of glass and light.\n\nSeen from afar—\nClear in the night.\n\n名ばかりの女王\n静かに立つ。\n\nNo hand on law.\nNo blade to press.\n\nOnly a symbol\nin formal dress.\n\n## VERSE II — Identity Shift\n\nThey bow—\nbut not from fear.\n\nThey speak—\nand I must hear.\n\nThe power left.\nThe title stayed.\n\nAn echo of the role I played.\n\nIs this less?\n\nOr is it more?\n\nTo guard the frame\ninstead of war.\n\n## BRIDGE — Reflection\n\n*(music nearly silent; faint choir hum)*\n\nI thought the height\nwas where I stood.\n\nBut height is hollow\nwithout the good.\n\nIf I am myth,\nlet myth be kind.\n\nIf I am symbol,\nlet me remind.\n\n## FINAL CHORUS — Ceremony\n\n*(choir enters softly; organ warm)*\n\nI am a crown of glass and light.\n\nCeremonial,\nnot the fight.\n\n名ばかりの女王\n息を守る。\n\nIf I cannot command the flame,\nI will protect\nwhat bears my name.\n\nNot ruler.\n\nWitness crowned.\n\nNot sovereign—\n\nBut bound.\n\n## CODA — Breath in the Hall\n\n*(music thins; single sustained note fades)*\n\nThe throne remains.\n\nThe world moves on.\n\nI stand.\n\n息。\n", "duration" 246.12, "type" "gen", "model_badges" {"songcard" {"dark" {"background_color" "0000004D", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}, "display_name" "v5", "light" {"background_color" "0000004D", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}}, "songrow" {"dark" {"background_color" "FD429C40", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}, "display_name" "v5", "light" {"background_color" "FD429C1A", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}}}, "has_stem" false, "make_instrumental" false, "refund_credits" false}, "title" "Crown of Glass / 名ばかりの女王"}, :duration 246.12, :controls nil, :lyrics "## OVERTURE — Empty Throne\n\n*(soft organ; single chime)*\n\nThe hall is full.\nThe throne is light.\n\nThe scepter rests\nbut does not bite.\n\n霧は遠い。\n\n## VERSE I — Recognition\n\nI wore the sky like armor bright.\nI called that hunger sacred right.\n\nBut crowns are loud\nwhen held too tight.\n\nAnd I mistook\nthe roar for sight.\n\n## PRE-CHORUS — Unfastening\n\n*(harpsichord slows; strings soften)*\n\nWhat is a queen\nwithout decree?\n\nWhat is command\nwithout belief?\n\n## CHORUS — Crown of Glass\n\n*(strings swell gently)*\n\nI am a crown of glass and light.\n\nSeen from afar—\nClear in the night.\n\n名ばかりの女王\n静かに立つ。\n\nNo hand on law.\nNo blade to press.\n\nOnly a symbol\nin formal dress.\n\n## VERSE II — Identity Shift\n\nThey bow—\nbut not from fear.\n\nThey speak—\nand I must hear.\n\nThe power left.\nThe title stayed.\n\nAn echo of the role I played.\n\nIs this less?\n\nOr is it more?\n\nTo guard the frame\ninstead of war.\n\n## BRIDGE — Reflection\n\n*(music nearly silent; faint choir hum)*\n\nI thought the height\nwas where I stood.\n\nBut height is hollow\nwithout the good.\n\nIf I am myth,\nlet myth be kind.\n\nIf I am symbol,\nlet me remind.\n\n## FINAL CHORUS — Ceremony\n\n*(choir enters softly; organ warm)*\n\nI am a crown of glass and light.\n\nCeremonial,\nnot the fight.\n\n名ばかりの女王\n息を守る。\n\nIf I cannot command the flame,\nI will protect\nwhat bears my name.\n\nNot ruler.\n\nWitness crowned.\n\nNot sovereign—\n\nBut bound.\n\n## CODA — Breath in the Hall\n\n*(music thins; single sustained note fades)*\n\nThe throne remains.\n\nThe world moves on.\n\nI stand.\n\n息。\n", :source #:source{:name "Crown of Glass _ 名ばかりの女王(1).json", :sha256 "4c2a1c372c5fc4d0502ed54fad227ac135c6a44e3dd805d9a29e36e64e998315", :format :suno-json, :variation 1}, :title "Crown of Glass / 名ばかりの女王"}, "9187df0c-d2e6-4987-9f0c-0de31f19f895" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "9187df0c-d2e6-4987-9f0c-0de31f19f895", :url "https://suno.com/song/9187df0c-d2e6-4987-9f0c-0de31f19f895", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "9187df0c-d2e6-4987-9f0c-0de31f19f895", "metadata" {"prompt" "## ACT I, SCENE 1 — The Many Rooms\n\n*(A distant tone. Water somewhere in the dark. Harpsichord enters alone, then stops.)*\n\n### OVERTURE\n\nGATE / DISTANT CHOIR  \n:: proceed ::  \n:: observe ::  \n:: do not assume alignment ::\n\n*(Organ breath. Three separate rhythmic cells enter from different sides.)*\n\n### ENTRANCE I — THE COURT\n\nCOURT SOPRANO  \nI entered by the water stair,  \nthe marble lit in silver flame.  \nThe counsel masks were already raised.  \nThey spoke in titles, not in names.  \n\nLOW CHORUS  \nBy seal, by sign, by right, by veil.  \nBy turn of hand, by hidden scale.\n\nCOURT SOPRANO  \nA page in white took down the wind.  \nA bell was struck but did not ring.  \nSomeone had moved the throne an inch.  \nNo one would name so small a thing.\n\n### ENTRANCE II — THE BOARDROOM\n\nBOARDROOM BARITONE  \nI badged into the glass-lit floor.  \nThe screens were waiting for a vote.  \nForecasts bloomed in cobalt grids.  \nEvery risk arrived pre-wrote.  \n\nBOARD CHORUS  \nAlign the frame.  \nReduce the drift.  \nMove the needle.  \nMask the shift.\n\nBOARDROOM BARITONE  \nThere was a tremor in the deck,  \ntoo fine for metrics to condemn.  \nA cursor flickered without cause.  \nNo one admitted seeing it then.\n\n### ENTRANCE III — THE GATE\n\nHACKER ALTO / TENOR  \nI spawned beneath a falling veil,  \nparty list stale, map half-loaded.  \nThe NPC at fountain-side  \nlooked at me like it had noticed.  \n\nHACKER CHORUS  \nPing and trace.  \nPatch and wait.  \nRun the room.  \nDo not state.\n\nHACKER ALTO / TENOR  \nTrade chat filled with weather jokes.  \nSomeone danced on broken light.  \nSomeone said the lag felt holy.  \nSomeone laughed and called it fine.\n\n### FIRST WEAVE\n\n*(The three worlds overlap, not yet fully synchronized.)*\n\nCOURT SOPRANO  \nThe bell was struck—\n\nBOARDROOM BARITONE  \nThe cursor slipped—\n\nHACKER ALTO / TENOR  \nThe fountain turned—\n\nCHORUS  \n—and something answered out of script.\n\nCOURT SOPRANO  \nBy veil and glass—\n\nBOARDROOM BARITONE  \nBy deck and graph—\n\nHACKER ALTO / TENOR  \nBy shard and gate—\n\nCHORUS  \n—the same hand moved in every half.\n\n### WARDEN ENTRY\n\n*(Music thins. Sub-rumble remains. Warden enters almost dry, close-mic, low.)*\n\nWARDEN  \nNo room agrees with any other.  \nAll logs share the same timestamp.  \nNo witness holds the whole event.  \nThe system does not call it wrong.  \n\nA throne displaced one measured inch.  \nA cursor slipped beyond its frame.  \nA fountain-NPC made eye contact.  \nDifferent surfaces. Same claim.\n\nI mark the drift.  \nI do not close it.  \nI name the pattern.  \nI do not rule.\n\n### RITSU ENTRY\n\n*(Everything softens. Felt piano, two notes.)*\n\nRITSU  \nSomeone is here.  \nOr almost here.  \n\nThe air keeps making up its mind  \nand changing it near me.  \n\nI touched the rail.  \nIt felt warm first.  \nThen true.  \n\nThe background people  \nkeep looking back  \nlike they remember  \nwhat to do.\n\n### PRE-CHORUS — MISALIGNMENT\n\nCOURT SOPRANO  \nWho moved the throne?\n\nBOARDROOM BARITONE  \nWho changed the deck?\n\nHACKER ALTO / TENOR  \nWho patched the sky?\n\nRITSU  \nWho made the room  \nstart noticing me back?\n\nLOW CHORUS  \nNo one sees the whole Gate.  \nNo one holds the whole thread.  \nAll we have is borrowed light  \nand the shape of what was said.\n\n### CHORUS — THE MANY ROOMS\n\n*(Full ensemble. First true convergence.)*\n\nALL  \nMany rooms, one pulse beneath.  \nMany names for the selfsame breach.  \nMany worlds in borrowed dress.  \nOne shared motion, nothing less.  \n\nMany voices, unsynced, apart.  \nSame blind rhythm, same dark heart.  \nWe called it court, called it game,  \ncalled it forecast, called it flame.  \n\nBut under title, screen, and skin,  \nthe deeper system had begun.  \nMany rooms, and none complete.  \nOne event not yet made one.\n\n### INTERLUDE — GATE RESPONSE\n\nGATE / DISTANT CHOIR  \n:: incomplete consensus ::  \n:: convergence pending ::  \n:: continue as if separate ::\n\n*(Harpsichord motif returns, now doubled by low synth.)*\n\n### VERSE — SECOND RECOGNITION\n\nCOURT SOPRANO  \nThe page in white has no reflection.\n\nBOARDROOM BARITONE  \nThe minutes note a missing beat.\n\nHACKER ALTO / TENOR  \nThe map redraws around my footsteps.\n\nRITSU  \nEven the silence sounds concrete.\n\nWARDEN  \nThe pattern holds across partitions.  \nMeaning differs. Motion does not.  \nIf this is error, it is graceful.  \nIf it is grace, it carries cost.\n### FINAL CHORUS — THE MANY ROOMS\n\nALL  \nMany rooms, one pulse beneath.  \nMany doors that open inward.  \nMany stories told as truth.  \nOne event becoming heard.  \n\nMany eyes with private light.  \nMany mouths that name the same.  \nCourt and board and war and chapel,  \nterminal, throne room, storm, and game.  \n\nNo one sees the whole Gate turning.  \nNo one sings the total scheme.  \nBut we can hear the shared arrival  \nmoving under every dream.\n\n### CODA\n\n*(Everything falls away except water, distant choir, one low organ note.)*\n\nRITSU  \nSomeone is here.\n\nWARDEN  \nYes.\n\nGATE / DISTANT CHOIR  \n:: proceed ::", "tags" nil}, "title" "水階マーブル銀火"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "## ACT I, SCENE 1 — The Many Rooms\n\n*(A distant tone. Water somewhere in the dark. Harpsichord enters alone, then stops.)*\n\n### OVERTURE\n\nGATE / DISTANT CHOIR  \n:: proceed ::  \n:: observe ::  \n:: do not assume alignment ::\n\n*(Organ breath. Three separate rhythmic cells enter from different sides.)*\n\n### ENTRANCE I — THE COURT\n\nCOURT SOPRANO  \nI entered by the water stair,  \nthe marble lit in silver flame.  \nThe counsel masks were already raised.  \nThey spoke in titles, not in names.  \n\nLOW CHORUS  \nBy seal, by sign, by right, by veil.  \nBy turn of hand, by hidden scale.\n\nCOURT SOPRANO  \nA page in white took down the wind.  \nA bell was struck but did not ring.  \nSomeone had moved the throne an inch.  \nNo one would name so small a thing.\n\n### ENTRANCE II — THE BOARDROOM\n\nBOARDROOM BARITONE  \nI badged int