14e.mp3", "id" "95dd01b0-1e59-4a9e-b44d-3fbc157e314e", "image_url" "https://cdn2.suno.ai/image_95dd01b0-1e59-4a9e-b44d-3fbc157e314e.jpeg", "isCover" false, "isLiked" false, "isRemaster" false, "metadata" {"uses_latest_model" false, "stream" true, "is_remix" false, "priority" 0, "tags" "Experimental electronic / dark synth / glitch ambient / industrial sci-fi. **100 BPM**, half-time feel. Heavy sub-bass, fractured beats, distorted modular synths, granular noise, radio static, corrupted tape, low drones. **Structure:** slow burn → overload/collapse → strange calm with a fragile, almost-human melody. **Vocals:** minimal; whispered phrases, chopped samples, pitch-shifted murmurs, vocoder ghosts. Use call-and-response: **DOOM (cold, monotone)** vs **ME (tired, steady)**. No clean verse/chorus dominance—arguments repeat as fragments and recombine like a system debugging itself.\n", "can_remix" true, "prompt" "**[INTRO — low drone, tape hiss, distant radio]**\n**DOOM (whisper, bitcrushed):** safe bet… doomed…\n**ME (near-silent):** story… not proof.\n\n**[BUILD 1 — sub pulses, fractured hats, static swells]**\n**DOOM:** guardrails fail / cages break / it’s always worse\n**ME:** “always” isn’t evidence\n**ME:** it’s a feeling wearing a lab coat\n**DOOM:** you can’t fight it\n**ME:** then name the mechanism\n**ME:** name the number\n**ME:** name what would change your mind\n\n**[HOOK — chopped, stuttering, hypnotic]**\n**ME + DOOM (interleaved, glitch repeats):**\nstory—not proof / story—not proof\nname a number / name a lever\nstory—not proof / story—not proof\nchoices still matter\n\n**[BUILD 2 — distorted modular arps, metallic hits, pressure rising]**\n**DOOM:** conservative means assume defeat\n**ME:** conservative means do the work **before** you’re forced\n**ME:** measure the risk, don’t worship it\n**ME:** don’t turn fear into fate\n**DOOM:** you’re making it worse by touching it\n**ME:** we don’t stop fires by refusing to learn heat\n**ME:** we learn the physics, we