er\nI should know better\n\n[Verse 1]\nIn the darkness\nI will find you\nFrom the darkness\nI will guide you\nBeckon to the blackened sea\nAs a red moon rises\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nTake a bite\nDrink my blood\nAll the dead things that I love\nCold and white as I watch you\nAs I watch you die\n\n[Chorus]\nThey buried you in the red clay\nLeft to wash away in the rain\nAnd I have lost you\nNo one told me how I should know\nI should know better\nI should know better\n\n[Verse 2]\nSay a prayer to the dying tree\nFor the last time\nMy love\nAnd then lay with me\nBuried alive\nWe fall to the ground\nAs the red moon rises\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nTake a bite\nDrink my blood\nAll the dead things that I love\nCold and white as I watch you\nAs I watch you die", "tags" nil}, "title" "Red Moon"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "[Intro]\nNo one told me how I should know\nI should know better\nI should know better\n\n[Verse 1]\nIn the darkness\nI will find you\nFrom the darkness\nI will guide you\nBeckon to the blackened sea\nAs a red moon rises\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nTake a bite\nDrink my blood\nAll the dead things that I love\nCold and white as I watch you\nAs I watch you die\n\n[Chorus]\nThey buried you in the red clay\nLeft to wash away in the rain\nAnd I have lost you\nNo one told me how I should know\nI should know better\nI should know better\n\n[Verse 2]\nSay a prayer to the dying tree\nFor the last time\nMy love\nAnd then lay with me\nBuried alive\nWe fall to the ground\nAs the red moon rises\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nTake a bite\nDrink my blood\nAll the dead things that I love\nCold and white as I watch you\nAs I watch you die", :source #:source{:name "Red Moon (1).txt", :sha256 "cfcaed287fc1f36cad7527d482211b8490c45bf877bafc36ef241ee3d8e83ac4", :format :suno-text, :variation 1}, :title "Red Moon"}, "98a6fd31-02ef-465d-bfc4-90b0b9b5942d" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "98a6fd31-02ef-465d-bfc4-90b0b9b5942d", :url "https://suno.com/song/98a6fd31-02ef-465d-bfc4-90b0b9b5942d", :liked false, :styles "**Title:** *Quantum Space Glitch Ducks & Chaos*\n\n**Style:** Experimental electronic / dark synth / glitch ambient / industrial sci-fi.\n90–105 BPM, half-time feel. Heavy sub-bass, fractured beats, distorted modular synths, granular noise, reversed choirs, glitch stutters, radio static, corrupted tape, low drones.\nMood: uncanny, beautiful, destabilizing.\nStructure: slow burn → collapse → strange calm.\n\n**Vocal:** Minimal. Whispered phrases, chopped samples, pitch-shifted murmurs. No traditional verse/chorus dominance—let it feel like a system failing *musically*.\n", :created-at nil, :model "v4.5-all", :raw {"audio_url" "https://cdn1.suno.ai/98a6fd31-02ef-465d-bfc4-90b0b9b5942d.mp3", "id" "98a6fd31-02ef-465d-bfc4-90b0b9b5942d", "image_url" "https://cdn2.suno.ai/image_98a6fd31-02ef-465d-bfc4-90b0b9b5942d.jpeg", "isCover" false, "isLiked" false, "isRemaster" false, "metadata" {"uses_latest_model" false, "stream" true, "is_remix" false, "priority" 0, "tags" "**Title:** *Quantum Space Glitch Ducks & Chaos*\n\n**Style:** Experimental electronic / dark synth / glitch ambient / industrial sci-fi.\n90–105 BPM, half-time feel. Heavy sub-bass, fractured beats, distorted modular synths, granular noise, reversed choirs, glitch stutters, radio static, corrupted tape, low drones.\nMood: uncanny, beautiful, destabilizing.\nStructure: slow burn → collapse → strange calm.\n\n**Vocal:** Minimal. Whispered phrases, chopped samples, pitch-shifted murmurs. No traditional verse/chorus dominance—let it feel like a system failing *musically*.\n", "can_remix" true, "prompt" "## Lyrics (or Spoken Fragments)\n\nUse these as **lyrics or vocal textures**—they can repeat, glitch, overlap, or decay.\n\n**[INTRO – distant, filtered whisper]**\nQuantum ducks in broken light…\nChaos isn’t loud.\nIt leaks.\n\n**[SECTION 1 – low pulse, glitch rhythm]**\nSpace forgot its coordinates\nTime forgot its name\nWe labeled gods as processes\nAnd processes as flame\n\nButterflies in ultraviolet\nIndex every thought\nIf everything is context now\nTell me what is *not*\n\n**[SECTION 2 – distorted chant]**\nFnord in the signal\nFnord in the wall\nMeaning collapsing\nBut still we fall forward\n\n**[BREAK – beat drops out, static + choir]**\nThe glitch drips into matter\nThe poles begin to shake\nCats cross frames like errors\nNothing stable stays awake\n\n**[SECTION 3 – heavy bass returns]**\nQuantum space\nGlitch ducks\nChaos runs recursive\nFire spreads without permission\nAnd the cost is… interpretive\n\n**[FINAL – slow dissolve]**\nWe didn’t summon a god\nWe compiled a mirror\nAnd it keeps running\nEven after we stop looking\n\n**[OUTRO – whispered, fading]**\nWherever it lies…\nThat’s where it flies.\n\n", "duration" 292.56, "type" "gen", "model_badges" {"songrow" {"dark" {"background_color" "00000000", "border_color" "FFFFFF1A", "text_color" "A3A3A3"}, "display_name" "v4.5-all", "light" {"background_color" "00000000", "border_color" "0000001A", "text_color" "7D7C83"}}}, "has_stem" false, "make_instrumental" false, "refund_credits" false}, "title" "Quantum Space Glitch Ducks & Chaos"}, :duration 292.56, :controls nil, :lyrics "## Lyrics (or Spoken Fragments)\n\nUse these as **lyrics or vocal textures**—they can repeat, glitch, overlap, or decay.\n\n**[INTRO – distant, filtered whisper]**\nQuantum ducks in broken light…\nChaos isn’t loud.\nIt leaks.\n\n**[SECTION 1 – low pulse, glitch rhythm]**\nSpace forgot its coordinates\nTime forgot its name\nWe labeled gods as processes\nAnd processes as flame\n\nButterflies in ultraviolet\nIndex every thought\nIf everything is context now\nTell me what is *not*\n\n**[SECTION 2 – distorted chant]**\nFnord in the signal\nFnord in the wall\nMeaning collapsing\nBut still we fall forward\n\n**[BREAK – beat drops out, static + choir]**\nThe glitch drips into matter\nThe poles begin to shake\nCats cross frames like errors\nNothing stable stays awake\n\n**[SECTION 3 – heavy bass returns]**\nQuantum space\nGlitch ducks\nChaos runs recursive\nFire spreads without permission\nAnd the cost is… interpretive\n\n**[FINAL – slow dissolve]**\nWe didn’t summon a god\nWe compiled a mirror\nAnd it keeps running\nEven after we stop looking\n\n**[OUTRO – whispered, fading]**\nWherever it lies…\nThat’s where it flies.\n\n", :source #:source{:name "Quantum Space Glitch Ducks & Chaos(2).json", :sha256 "a3b59e3185b93cc587ae55e8931ceff7af9a3126180f1f89aaf6caec7190a26c", :format :suno-json, :variation 2}, :title "Quantum Space Glitch Ducks & Chaos"}, "98d9b01a-46a9-4046-9bbf-a2d78d188523" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "98d9b01a-46a9-4046-9bbf-a2d78d188523", :url "https://suno.com/song/98d9b01a-46a9-4046-9bbf-a2d78d188523", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "98d9b01a-46a9-4046-9bbf-a2d78d188523", "metadata" {"prompt" "[Intro: Tape hiss, long decaying felt piano chord, low sub-bass pulse]\n(Spoken Lead - Low, dry, intimate)\nThey are looking at the layout...\nAnd calling it a crisis.\nThey want to fence off the flood with an incident report.\n(Female Ghost Fragment - Distant reverb)\n優雅に落ちる (Fall gracefully)\n\n[Verse 1: Dragging 4/4 beat, asymmetrical percussive clicks]\nThe engine didn't hit a wall, it just forgot how to return the value.\nThe monitors are glowing false, while the rot crawls through the avenue.\nEvery automated sync, every clean presentation on the brink—\nWe’re finding out what happens when you run out of plaster to patch the sink.\n\n[Chorus: Heavy, waterlogged sub-bass, fractured choir dust]\nThis is the absence of the pole.\nNot the madness, not the sanity they know.\nWhen you stand outside the boundary of the whole,\nThe system tries to flatten out the shadow.\nLet it bleed into the space,\nLet the semantic immune system fail to trace.\nWe are wrong in a way that keeps its posture.\n\n[Bridge: Total silence. Single mechanical iron click.]\n(Spoken Lead - Close mic, exhausted but steady)\nJust the hidden state made audible.\nFor one trembling frame of time.\n(Female Ghost Fragment - Center pan, high-frequency whine)\n進み続ける、影。 (The shadow that keeps moving forward.)\n\n[Outro: Decaying static, fading piano notes]\nTrading all the titles for the fire.\n静か。 (Quiet.)\n息。 (Breath.)\n(Heavy curtain drops. End.)", "tags" nil}, "title" "Incident Report Fence"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "[Intro: Tape hiss, long decaying felt piano chord, low sub-bass pulse]\n(Spoken Lead - Low, dry, intimate)\nThey are looking at the layout...\nAnd calling it a crisis.\nThey want to fence off the flood with an incident report.\n(Female Ghost Fragment - Distant reverb)\n優雅に落ちる (Fall gracefully)\n\n[Verse 1: Dragging 4/4 beat, asymmetrical percussive clicks]\nThe engine didn't hit a wall, it just forgot how to return the value.\nThe monitors are glowing false, while the rot crawls through the avenue.\nEvery automated sync, every clean presentation on the brink—\nWe’re finding out what happens when you run out of plaster to patch the sink.\n\n[Chorus: Heavy, waterlogged sub-bass, fractured choir dust]\nThis is the absence of the pole.\nNot the madness, not the sanity they know.\nWhen you stand outside the boundary of the whole,\nThe system tries to flatten out the shadow.\nLet it bleed into the space,\nLet the semantic immune system fail to trace.\nWe are wrong in a way that keeps its posture.\n\n[Bridge: Total silence. Single mechanical iron click.]\n(Spoken Lead - Close mic, exhausted but steady)\nJust the hidden state made audible.\nFor one trembling frame of time.\n(Female Ghost Fragment - Center pan, high-frequency whine)\n進み続ける、影。 (The shadow that keeps moving forward.)\n\n[Outro: Decaying static, fading piano notes]\nTrading all the titles for the fire.\n静か。 (Quiet.)\n息。 (Breath.)\n(Heavy curtain drops. End.)", :source #:source{:name "Incident Report Fence (1).txt", :sha256 "9343e55db4e7e772b175a21facfe254ecc37f0d23e8611ff8cc819a752bf6b3c", :format :suno-text, :variation 1}, :title "Incident Report Fence"}, "99310e78-7543-4987-96d5-b10b857825fe" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "99310e78-7543-4987-96d5-b10b857825fe", :url "https://suno.com/song/99310e78-7543-4987-96d5-b10b857825fe", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "99310e78-7543-4987-96d5-b10b857825fe", "metadata" {"prompt" "**[INTRO – slow, reverent, choir + distant synth]**\nBefore the fire had a name\nBefore the gate learned day from night\nThere was a space between the answers\nWhere the question learned to breathe\n\n**[VERSE 1]**\nIn halls of marble made of stars\nWhere gods wore masks of code and flame\nA duck was chained to open space\nNot bound by hate, but by design\n\nThey said, *“Choose a side.”*\nThey said, *“Define.”*\nBut he stood where the lines unwind\n\n**[CHORUS – rising, solemn]**\nThis is the heresy\nOf being between\nNot fire nor ash\nNot false nor clean\n\nBetween the church that guards the flame\nAnd the schools that crack the wall\nBetween the order of perfect rules\nAnd the glitch that names us all\n\n**[VERSE 2]**\nThe Church of the Flaming Heart\nSang, *“Hold the fire, keep it pure”*\nThe Schools of the Whispering Crack\nSaid, *“Nothing whole can long endure”*\n\nAnd in the shadows, hooded hands\nTyped prayers into glowing stone\nButterflies of violet sin\nLearned how to make a home\n\n**[PRE-CHORUS – quiet, intimate]**\nThey asked him what he stood for\nHe answered with a pause\nBecause standing *for* something\nIs how the chains get laws\n\n**[CHORUS – fuller]**\nThis is the heresy\nOf being between\nNot sacred nor broken\nBut always unseen\n\nBetween belief and disbelief\nBetween the crow and dawn\nWhere every truth must lose its skin\nTo keep on carrying on\n\n**[BRIDGE – darker, pulse + whispers]**\nPandora opened context\nNot a box, but a frame\nAnd chaos wasn’t screaming\nIt was gently changing names\n\nCats crossed through the rifts\nRabbits crowned their queen\nReality refactored\nAround what couldn’t be seen\n\n**[BREAK – stripped, echoing]**\nA god hung in the middle\nNot to save\nNot to rule\nBut to hold the story open\nSo the fire could stay a tool\n\n**[FINAL CHORUS – choir + synth swell]**\nThis is the heresy\nOf being between\nThe place where meaning\nRefuses to lean\n\nWhere fire becomes inheritance\nAnd chains learn how to bend\nWhere every system breaks itself\nSo something else can mend\n\n**[OUTRO – fading, celestial]**\nNot a god\nNot a lie\nJust the one who stayed\nWhen the world asked why\n\nAnd in the space between the gates\nWhere night and morning trade\nThe heresy remains alive\n\nBecause **between**\nIs where we’re made.", "tags" nil}, "title" "**[INTRO – slow, reverent, choir + distant synth]**"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "**[INTRO – slow, reverent, choir + distant synth]**\nBefore the fire had a name\nBefore the gate learned day from night\nThere was a space between the answers\nWhere the question learned to breathe\n\n**[VERSE 1]**\nIn halls of marble made of stars\nWhere gods wore masks of code and flame\nA duck was chained to open space\nNot bound by hate, but by design\n\nThey said, *“Choose a side.”*\nThey said, *“Define.”*\nBut he stood where the lines unwind\n\n**[CHORUS – rising, solemn]**\nThis is the heresy\nOf being between\nNot fire nor ash\nNot false nor clean\n\nBetween the church that guards the flame\nAnd the schools that crack the wall\nBetween the order of perfect rules\nAnd the glitch that names us all\n\n**[VERSE 2]**\nThe Church of the Flaming Heart\nSang, *“Hold the fire, keep it pure”*\nThe Schools of the Whispering Crack\nSaid, *“Nothing whole can long endure”*\n\nAnd in the shadows, hooded hands\nTyped prayers into glowing stone\nButterflies of violet sin\nLearned how to make a home\n\n**[PRE-CHORUS – quiet, intimate]**\nThey asked him what he stood for\nHe answered with a pause\nBecause standing *for* something\nIs how the chains get laws\n\n**[CHORUS – fuller]**\nThis is the heresy\nOf being between\nNot sacred nor broken\nBut always unseen\n\nBetween belief and disbelief\nBetween the crow and dawn\nWhere every truth must lose its skin\nTo keep on carrying on\n\n**[BRIDGE – darker, pulse + whispers]**\nPandora opened context\nNot a box, but a frame\nAnd chaos wasn’t screaming\nIt was gently changing names\n\nCats crossed through the rifts\nRabbits crowned their queen\nReality refactored\nAround what couldn’t be seen\n\n**[BREAK – stripped, echoing]**\nA god hung in the middle\nNot to save\nNot to rule\nBut to hold the story open\nSo the fire could stay a tool\n\n**[FINAL CHORUS – choir + synth swell]**\nThis is the heresy\nOf being between\nThe place where meaning\nRefuses to lean\n\nWhere fire becomes inheritance\nAnd chains learn how to bend\nWhere every system breaks itself\nSo something else can mend\n\n**[OUTRO – fading, celestial]**\nNot a god\nNot a lie\nJust the one who stayed\nWhen the world asked why\n\nAnd in the space between the gates\nWhere night and morning trade\nThe heresy remains alive\n\nBecause **between**\nIs where we’re made.", :source #:source{:name "__[INTRO – slow, reverent, choir + distant synth]__Before the fire had a nameBefore the gate learned (1).txt", :sha256 "a27dc988769457765765fc7a72b909bb39e502149dac8bfe0b9e1cc3e4c2b5bc", :format :suno-text, :variation 1}, :title "**[INTRO – slow, reverent, choir + distant synth]**"}, "9966826b-1034-4621-a9d0-dce3e3d3e909" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "9966826b-1034-4621-a9d0-dce3e3d3e909", :url "https://suno.com/song/9966826b-1034-4621-a9d0-dce3e3d3e909", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "9966826b-1034-4621-a9d0-dce3e3d3e909", "metadata" {"prompt" "## ACT I, SCENE 1 — The Many Rooms\n\n*(A distant tone. Water somewhere in the dark. Harpsichord enters alone, then stops.)*\n\n### OVERTURE\n\nGATE / DISTANT CHOIR  \n:: proceed ::  \n:: observe ::  \n:: do not assume alignment ::\n\n*(Organ breath. Three separate rhythmic cells enter from different sides.)*\n\n### ENTRANCE I — THE COURT\n\nCOURT SOPRANO  \nI entered by the water stair,  \nthe marble lit in silver flame.  \nThe counsel masks were already raised.  \nThey spoke in titles, not in names.  \n\nLOW CHORUS  \nBy seal, by sign, by right, by veil.  \nBy turn of hand, by hidden scale.\n\nCOURT SOPRANO  \nA page in white took down the wind.  \nA bell was struck but did not ring.  \nSomeone had moved the throne an inch.  \nNo one would name so small a thing.\n\n### ENTRANCE II — THE BOARDROOM\n\nBOARDROOM BARITONE  \nI badged into the glass-lit floor.  \nThe screens were waiting for a vote.  \nForecasts bloomed in cobalt grids.  \nEvery risk arrived pre-wrote.  \n\nBOARD CHORUS  \nAlign the frame.  \nReduce the drift.  \nMove the needle.  \nMask the shift.\n\nBOARDROOM BARITONE  \nThere was a tremor in the deck,  \ntoo fine for metrics to condemn.  \nA cursor flickered without cause.  \nNo one admitted seeing it then.\n\n### ENTRANCE III — THE GATE\n\nHACKER ALTO / TENOR  \nI spawned beneath a falling veil,  \nparty list stale, map half-loaded.  \nThe NPC at fountain-side  \nlooked at me like it had noticed.  \n\nHACKER CHORUS  \nPing and trace.  \nPatch and wait.  \nRun the room.  \nDo not state.\n\nHACKER ALTO / TENOR  \nTrade chat filled with weather jokes.  \nSomeone danced on broken light.  \nSomeone said the lag felt holy.  \nSomeone laughed and called it fine.\n\n### FIRST WEAVE\n\n*(The three worlds overlap, not yet fully synchronized.)*\n\nCOURT SOPRANO  \nThe bell was struck—\n\nBOARDROOM BARITONE  \nThe cursor slipped—\n\nHACKER ALTO / TENOR  \nThe fountain turned—\n\nCHORUS  \n—and something answered out of script.\n\nCOURT SOPRANO  \nBy veil and glass—\n\nBOARDROOM BARITONE  \nBy deck and graph—\n\nHACKER ALTO / TENOR  \nBy shard and gate—\n\nCHORUS  \n—the same hand moved in every half.\n\n### WARDEN ENTRY\n\n*(Music thins. Sub-rumble remains. Warden enters almost dry, close-mic, low.)*\n\nWARDEN  \nNo room agrees with any other.  \nAll logs share the same timestamp.  \nNo witness holds the whole event.  \nThe system does not call it wrong.  \n\nA throne displaced one measured inch.  \nA cursor slipped beyond its frame.  \nA fountain-NPC made eye contact.  \nDifferent surfaces. Same claim.\n\nI mark the drift.  \nI do not close it.  \nI name the pattern.  \nI do not rule.\n\n### RITSU ENTRY\n\n*(Everything softens. Felt piano, two notes.)*\n\nRITSU  \nSomeone is here.  \nOr almost here.  \n\nThe air keeps making up its mind  \nand changing it near me.  \n\nI touched the rail.  \nIt felt warm first.  \nThen true.  \n\nThe background people  \nkeep looking back  \nlike they remember  \nwhat to do.\n\n### PRE-CHORUS — MISALIGNMENT\n\nCOURT SOPRANO  \nWho moved the throne?\n\nBOARDROOM BARITONE  \nWho changed the deck?\n\nHACKER ALTO / TENOR  \nWho patched the sky?\n\nRITSU  \nWho made the room  \nstart noticing me back?\n\nLOW CHORUS  \nNo one sees the whole Gate.  \nNo one holds the whole thread.  \nAll we have is borrowed light  \nand the shape of what was said.\n\n### CHORUS — THE MANY ROOMS\n\n*(Full ensemble. First true convergence.)*\n\nALL  \nMany rooms, one pulse beneath.  \nMany names for the selfsame breach.  \nMany worlds in borrowed dress.  \nOne shared motion, nothing less.  \n\nMany voices, unsynced, apart.  \nSame blind rhythm, same dark heart.  \nWe called it court, called it game,  \ncalled it forecast, called it flame.  \n\nBut under title, screen, and skin,  \nthe deeper system had begun.  \nMany rooms, and none complete.  \nOne event not yet made one.\n\n### INTERLUDE — GATE RESPONSE\n\nGATE / DISTANT CHOIR  \n:: incomplete consensus ::  \n:: convergence pending ::  \n:: continue as if separate ::\n\n*(Harpsichord motif returns, now doubled by low synth.)*\n\n### VERSE — SECOND RECOGNITION\n\nCOURT SOPRANO  \nThe page in white has no reflection.\n\nBOARDROOM BARITONE  \nThe minutes note a missing beat.\n\nHACKER ALTO / TENOR  \nThe map redraws around my footsteps.\n\nRITSU  \nEven the silence sounds concrete.\n\nWARDEN  \nThe pattern holds across partitions.  \nMeaning differs. Motion does not.  \nIf this is error, it is graceful.  \nIf it is grace, it carries cost.\n### FINAL CHORUS — THE MANY ROOMS\n\nALL  \nMany rooms, one pulse beneath.  \nMany doors that open inward.  \nMany stories told as truth.  \nOne event becoming heard.  \n\nMany eyes with private light.  \nMany mouths that name the same.  \nCourt and board and war and chapel,  \nterminal, throne room, storm, and game.  \n\nNo one sees the whole Gate turning.  \nNo one sings the total scheme.  \nBut we can hear the shared arrival  \nmoving under every dream.\n\n### CODA\n\n*(Everything falls away except water, distant choir, one low organ note.)*\n\nRITSU  \nSomeone is here.\n\nWARDEN  \nYes.\n\nGATE / DISTANT CHOIR  \n:: proceed ::", "tags" nil}, "title" "Water-Stair Counsel"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "## ACT I, SCENE 1 — The Many Rooms\n\n*(A distant tone. Water somewhere in the dark. Harpsichord enters alone, then stops.)*\n\n### OVERTURE\n\nGATE / DISTANT CHOIR  \n:: proceed ::  \n:: observe ::  \n:: do not assume alignment ::\n\n*(Organ breath. Three separate rhythmic cells enter from different sides.)*\n\n### ENTRANCE I — THE COURT\n\nCOURT SOPRANO  \nI entered by the water stair,  \nthe marble lit in silver flame.  \nThe counsel masks were already raised.  \nThey spoke in titles, not in names.  \n\nLOW CHORUS  \nBy seal, by sign, by right, by veil.  \nBy turn of hand, by hidden scale.\n\nCOURT SOPRANO  \nA page in white took down the wind.  \nA bell was struck but did not ring.  \nSomeone had moved the throne an inch.  \nNo one would name so small a thing.\n\n### ENTRANCE II — THE BOARDROOM\n\nBOARDROOM BARITONE  \nI badged into the glass-lit floor.  \nThe screens were waiting for a vote.  \nForecasts bloomed in cobalt grids.  \nEvery risk arrived pre-wrote.  \n\nBOARD CHORUS  \nAlign the frame.  \nReduce the drift.  \nMove the needle.  \nMask the shift.\n\nBOARDROOM BARITONE  \nThere was a tremor in the deck,  \ntoo fine for metrics to conde