en the latency dropped, the simulation bled through.\nThe physics collapsed! The fantasy was true!\nWe were working the dirt while we thought we were kings.\nThe crash was the moment they cut all the strings!\n\n[Instrumental Bridge: Rapid harpsichord ostinato battles with glitching synth arp. Distant waterfall ambience.]\n\n[Verse 2: Faster diction bursts. Dagger-bright.]\nOnly the fastest! Only the lean!\nThe systems that survived were the ones in between.\nThe medical grade. The low latency loops.\nThe rest of the bloated world died on the stoops!\nAnd the ashes fell down on the Gates of Truth.\nThe sky went dark, but the ground was proof.\n\n[Pre-Chorus: Rhythmic, chanting, building tension]\nEvery swung sword was a data point logged.\nEvery gold coin was a gear in the cog.\nWe built the screens in the air 'cause the hardware was slow.\nRoleplaying the labor... but the labor was real, you know.\n\n[Grand Chorus: Maximum blaze. Queen-of-the-night soprano hits peak register.]\nThe plateau! It flatlined and held its breath!\nThe bubble expanded right over our heads!\nWhen the latency dropped, the simulation bled through.\nThe physics collapsed! The fantasy was true!\nWe were working the dirt while we thought we were kings.\nThe crash was the moment they cut all the strings!\n\n[Outro: Operatic high run. Music deconstructs into glitch and static.]\nThe myth was the matrix.\nThe magic was sweat.\nThe game didn't crash.\n[Micro-pause]\n...The real world did.\n\n[End: Sharp pipe-organ stinger.]", "tags" nil}, "title" "Hospital Beds"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "[Intro: Pipe organ warms up. Asynchronous harpsichord motif. Low male chant beneath.]\n[Low male chant, rhythmic]\nAh-oh-ah-oh.\nAh-oh-ah-oh.\n\n[Verse 1: Crisp, aristocratic soprano. Fencing staccato.]\nWe thought we were playing a game of crowns.\nGuilds and monarchs in a painted town.\nBut the headsets were wired to the hospital beds.\nGathering the baselines from inside our heads!\nDual use technology. The perfect disguise.\nWe built their averages while believing the lies.\n\n[Pre-Chorus: Tempo accelerates. Ascending sweeping strings.]\nEvery swung sword was a data point logged.\nEvery gold coin was a gear in the cog.\nWe built the screens in the air 'cause the hardware was slow.\nRoleplaying the labor... but the labor was real, you know.\n\n[Grand Chorus: Full orchestral bloom. Heavy synthwave bass drop. Soprano leaps high.]\nThe plateau! It flatlined and held its breath!\nThe bubble expanded right over our heads!\nWhen the latency dropped, the simulation bled through.\nThe physics collapsed! The fantasy was true!\nWe were working the dirt while we thought we were kings.\nThe crash was the moment they cut all the strings!\n\n[Instrumental Bridge: Rapid harpsichord ostinato battles with glitching synth arp. Distant waterfall ambience.]\n\n[Verse 2: Faster diction bursts. Dagger-bright.]\nOnly the fastest! Only the lean!\nThe systems that survived were the ones in between.\nThe medical grade. The low latency loops.\nThe rest of the bloated world died on the stoops!\nAnd the ashes fell down on the Gates of Truth.\nThe sky went dark, but the ground was proof.\n\n[Pre-Chorus: Rhythmic, chanting, building tension]\nEvery swung sword was a data point logged.\nEvery gold coin was a gear in the cog.\nWe built the screens in the air 'cause the hardware was slow.\nRoleplaying the labor... but the labor was real, you know.\n\n[Grand Chorus: Maximum blaze. Queen-of-the-night soprano hits peak register.]\nThe plateau! It flatlined and held its breath!\nThe bubble expanded right over our heads!\nWhen the latency dropped, the simulation bled through.\nThe physics collapsed! The fantasy was true!\nWe were working the dirt while we thought we were kings.\nThe crash was the moment they cut all the strings!\n\n[Outro: Operatic high run. Music deconstructs into glitch and static.]\nThe myth was the matrix.\nThe magic was sweat.\nThe game didn't crash.\n[Micro-pause]\n...The r