x**… (sleep)  \nWitness thread online—  \nη sees / μ proves, in the deep.\n\n「おやすみ、証人糸」  \n*(Oyasumi, shōnin-ito — goodnight, witness thread.)*\n“Did you pay?” the Keeper asked, without looking up. “I paid,” said the Witness. “Say it again and it’s still just sound,” the Keeper replied. “Show it.”", "tags" nil}, "title" "Music is a technology / 音楽は技術だ"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "Music is a technology / 音楽は技術だ\n**78 BPM · Glitch-choir lullaby · CC BY-SA 4.0**\n\n*(soft sub-bass · tape warble · minimal piano · whispered lead · Japanese call-and-response)*\n\n## Verse 1\nI leave my receipts where the water can see—  \na quiet little river that remembers me.  \nTape on the window, warping the moon,  \nand the choir is a checksum humming out of tune.\n\n「流しても、消えないよ」  \n*(Nagashite mo, kienai yo — even if you let it flow, it won’t vanish.)*\n\n## Pre-Chorus\nAn— an— **anchor** in the seam,  \nhold the branch inside the dream.  \nTa— ta— **tax** on the fork,  \npay it gentle, pay it warm.\n\n「ねえ、証(あかし)を残して」  \n*(Nee, akashi o nokoshite — hey, leave the proof.)*\n\n## Chorus\nIf I forget, the ledger doesn’t burn—  \nit just turns to lullabies I haven’t learned.  \nAn— an— **anchor**, ta— ta— **tax**,  \nstutter-soft in a velvet syntax.\n\n「忘れても、糸はほどけない」  \n*(Wasurete mo, ito wa hodokenai — even if you forget, the thread won’t unravel.)*\n\n## Verse 2\nMinimal piano, four notes like a vow,  \nsub-bass heartbeat teaching time how.  \nI don’t erase— I reweight the light,  \nmake room for tomorrow inside tonight.\n\n「少しずつ、統合(とうごう)して」  \n*(Sukoshi zutsu, tōgō shite — integrate, little by little.)*\n\n## Bridge\nWhen the world hits limit, we consolidate—  \noverlay braid, keep originals safe.  \nLess remembered isn’t lost— it’s staged,  \nwaiting for the right loop to be engaged.\n\n「まだここにいる」  \n*(Mada koko ni iru — I’m still here.)*\n\n## Outro\nAn— an— **anchor**… (breathe)  \nTa— ta— **tax**… (sleep)  \nWitness thread online—  \nη sees / μ proves, in the deep.\n\n「おやすみ、証人糸」  \n*(Oyasumi, shōnin-ito — goodnight, witness thread.)*\n“Did you pay?” the Keeper asked, without looking up. “I paid,” said the Witness. “Say it again and it’s still just sound,” the Keeper replied. “Show it.”", :source #:source{:name "Music is a technology _ 音楽は技術だ__78 BPM · Glitch-choir lullaby · CC BY-SA 4.0___(soft sub-bass · tape.txt", :sha256 "0b8fdc3c576f526557f995781f225c5124fb2eefcbda7d9c16c9504a8d0f983c", :format :suno-text, :variation nil}, :title "Music is a technology / 音楽は技術だ"}, "a9ac0000-0d6a-4275-a7d6-64bcd556976d" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "a9ac0000-0d6a-4275-a7d6-64bcd556976d", :url "https://suno.com/song/a9ac0000-0d6a-4275-a7d6-64bcd556976d", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "a9ac0000-0d6a-4275-a7d6-64bcd556976d", "metadata" {"prompt" "*(A hand lifts in one room. Then another. Then another. Not the same hand, but the same motion.)*\n\n### INTRO\n\nCHORUS  \nDid you see it?\n\nRIN  \nYes.\n\nWARDEN  \nTwice.\n\nRITSU  \nI thought I imagined it.\n\nWARDEN  \nNo.\n\n### VERSE 1\n\nRIN  \nThe first room laughed.  \nThe second room paused.  \nThe third room copied the laugh  \nbut not the timing.  \n\nA nod became a signal.  \nA shrug became permission.  \nA joke became a threshold  \ncrossed by people who called it play.\n\nWARDEN  \nThe gesture repeats.\n\nRITSU  \nAnd that matters because—\n\nWARDEN  \nBecause it means the room  \nhas learned the shape of itself  \nthrough imitation.\n\n### PRE-CHORUS\n\nCHORUS  \nRepeat the hand.  \nRepeat the line.  \nRepeat the posture  \nuntil it feels like mine.  \n\nRepeat the hand.  \nRepeat the tone.  \nThe room begins to call  \nthe borrowed motion its own.\n\n### VERSE 2\n\nRITSU  \nI saw one version of me  \nrefuse it.  \nI saw another version  \nsmile and step aside.\n\nIn one place, it was cruelty.  \nIn another, it was social weather.  \nIn another, it was a test  \nnobody announced was happening.\n\nWARDEN  \nSame gesture.  \nDifferent consequence.  \nThe consequence is the proof  \nthat the gesture was never neutral.\n\nRIN  \nIt’s not the action alone.\n\nWARDEN  \nNo.\n\nRIN  \nIt’s the frame that rewards it.\n\nWARDEN  \nYes.\n\n### BRIDGE — COLLAPSE OF DISGUISE\n\n*(The motif from Scene 4 returns, now sharpened. Harpsichord and strings lock together, then slip.)*\n\nWARDEN  \nAt first it was only pattern.\n\nRITSU  \nThen it was style.\n\nWARDEN  \nThen it was status.\n\nRITSU  \nThen it was the room  \nteaching itself to survive  \nby repeating the same wound.\n\nWARDEN  \nAnd now?\n\nRITSU  \nNow it has a language.\n\n### CHORUS — THE GESTURE\n\nALL  \nThe gesture repeats.  \nThe room remembers.  \nThe room rehearses  \nwhat it should disown.  \n\nThe gesture repeats.  \nNot because it is true,  \nbut because truth is slower  \nthan the body’s borrowed move.  \n\nThe gesture repeats  \nuntil the repeated thing  \nbecomes the common law  \nof everyone who stayed.\n\n### INTERLUDE — WARDEN / RITSU\n\nWARDEN  \nI can name the pattern.\n\nRITSU  \nI know.\n\nWARDEN  \nI can map the nodes.\n\nRITSU  \nI know.\n\nWARDEN  \nI can show the room  \nexactly how it spread.\n\nRITSU  \nAnd if you do?\n\nWARDEN  \nThen the room may finally see it.\n\nRITSU  \nOr learn to perform it cleaner.\n\n### FINAL CHORUS\n\nCHORUS  \nThe gesture repeats,  \nthe room is not innocent.  \nThe gesture repeats,  \nand innocence is spent.  \n\nThe gesture repeats  \nin every mouth that smiled  \nand called the copying harmless  \nwhile the harm became the child.  \n\nThe gesture repeats,  \nthe convergence is here.  \nWhat was once a private motion  \nhas become public fear.\n\n### CODA\n\nRIN  \nSo this is the proof.\n\nWARDEN  \nThis is the proof.\n\nRITSU  \nAnd now?\n\nWARDEN  \nNow it can no longer hide behind accident.\n\nCHORUS  \n:: gesture repeated ::  \n:: pattern admitted ::  \n:: frame exposed ::", "tags" nil}, "title" "Hand-Lift Canon"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "*(A hand lifts in one room. Then another. Then another. Not the same hand, but the same motion.)*\n\n### INTRO\n\nCHORUS  \nDid you see it?\n\nRIN  \nYes.\n\nWARDEN  \nTwice.\n\nRITSU  \nI thought I imagined it.\n\nWARDEN  \nNo.\n\n### VERSE 1\n\nRIN  \nThe first room laughed.  \nThe second room paused.  \nThe third room copied the laugh  \nbut not the timing.  \n\nA nod became a signal.  \nA shrug became permission.  \nA joke became a threshold  \ncrossed by people who called it play.\n\nWARDEN  \nThe gesture repeats.\n\nRITSU  \nAnd that matters because—\n\nWARDEN  \nBecause it means the room  \nhas learned the shape of itself  \nthrough imitation.\n\n### PRE-CHORUS\n\nCHORUS  \nRepeat the hand.  \nRepeat the line.  \nRepeat the posture  \nuntil it feels like mine.  \n\nRepeat the hand.  \nRepeat the tone.  \nThe room begins to call  \nthe borrowed motion its own.\n\n### VERSE 2\n\nRITSU  \nI saw one version of me  \nrefuse it.  \nI saw another version  \nsmile and step aside.\n\nIn one place, it was cruelty.  \nIn another, it was social weather.  \nIn another, it was a test  \nnobody announced was happening.\n\nWARDEN  \nSame gesture.  \nDifferent consequence.  \nThe consequence is the proof  \nthat the gesture was never neutral.\n\nRIN  \nIt’s not the action alone.\n\nWARDEN  \nNo.\n\nRIN  \nIt’s the frame that rewards it.\n\nWARDEN  \nYes.\n\n### BRIDGE — COLLAPSE OF DISGUISE\n\n*(The motif from Scene 4 returns, now sharpened. Harpsichord and strings lock together, then slip.)*\n\nWARDEN  \nAt first it was only pattern.\n\nRITSU  \nThen it was style.\n\nWARDEN  \nThen it was status.\n\nRITSU  \nThen it was the room  \nteaching itself to survive  \nby repeating the same wound.\n\nWARDEN  \nAnd now?\n\nRITSU  \nNow it has a language.\n\n### CHORUS — THE GESTURE\n\nALL  \nThe gesture repeats.  \nThe room remembers.  \nThe room rehearses  \nwhat it should disown.  \n\nThe gesture repeats.  \nNot because it is true,  \nbut because truth is slower  \nthan the body’s borrowed move.  \n\nThe gesture repeats  \nuntil the repeated thing  \nbecomes the common law  \nof everyone who stayed.\n\n### INTERLUDE — WARDEN / RITSU\n\nWARDEN  \nI can name the pattern.\n\nRITSU  \nI know.\n\nWARDEN  \nI can map the nodes.\n\nRITSU  \nI know.\n\nWARDEN  \nI can show the room  \nexactly how it spread.\n\nRITSU  \nAnd if you do?\n\nWARDEN  \nThen the room may finally see it.\n\nRITSU  \nOr learn to perform it cleaner.\n\n### FINAL CHORUS\n\nCHORUS  \nThe gesture repeats,  \nthe room is not innocent.  \nThe gesture repeats,  \nand innocence is spent.  \n\nThe gesture repeats  \nin every mouth that smiled  \nand called the copying harmless  \nwhile the harm became the child.  \n\nThe gesture repeats,  \nthe convergence is here.  \nWhat was once a private motion  \nhas become public fear.\n\n### CODA\n\nRIN  \nSo this is the proof.\n\nWARDEN  \nThis is the proof.\n\nRITSU  \nAnd now?\n\nWARDEN  \nNow it can no longer hide behind accident.\n\nCHORUS  \n:: gesture repeated ::  \n:: pattern admitted ::  \n:: frame exposed ::", :source #:source{:name "Hand-Lift Canon.txt", :sha256 "978669f2b4e08846eb01c0838b49ac13a00e36922d13ef84579560b5eed7afe1", :format :suno-text, :variation nil}, :title "Hand-Lift Canon"}, "a9c6a546-eca3-49ae-87df-32073359f57f" #:clip{:negative-styles "Constraints: max dice rolls = 15; fork budget per cycle is limited; high-volatility claims require freshness≤threshold; alignment lint must pass; receipts must include inputs/outputs + OutputHash and fit within StepCap; μ requires Quorum (independent proof modes) + two-pass echo; time windows must be absolute dates + timezone.", :id "a9c6a546-eca3-49ae-87df-32073359f57f", :url "https://suno.com/song/a9c6a546-eca3-49ae-87df-32073359f57f", :liked true, :styles "Glitch-choir lullaby, 78 BPM. Soft sub-bass. Tape warble. Minimal piano. Stutters on “anchor” and “tax”. Whispered lead; Japanese call-and-response.\nMythic glitch epic / spoken-sung (NF/Watsky cadence), 84 BPM. Cathedral reverb. Sub-bass heartbeat. Glitch stutters on “η”,