g.\n\nWARDEN  \nNo.\n\nRITSU  \nAnd we share the names.\n\n### VERSE 1\n\nWARDEN  \nI thought a commons  \nwas a place.  \nIt is not.\n\nIt is a decision  \nto refuse private ownership  \nof the fragile parts.\n\nIt is a promise  \nthat the people most affected  \nget a voice before the system  \ncalls itself complete.\n\nRITSU  \nThat’s new.\n\nWARDEN  \nNo.\n\nRITSU  \nIt is.  \nBecause before,  \nthe room spoke first  \nand called it order.\n\n### VERSE 2\n\nRIN  \nNow the room listens.  \nOr it doesn’t get to claim  \nit is the room.\n\nThe detector stays open.  \nThe logs stay readable.  \nThe criteria stay public.  \nThe harm stays nameable  \nwithout requiring a priesthood.\n\nWARDEN  \nAnd when the signal is unclear?\n\nRIN  \nWe mark it unclear.  \nWe don’t force certainty  \nto make the dashboard prettier.\n\nRITSU  \nThat sounds almost gentle.\n\nRIN  \nIt is.  \nAnd it is not weak.\n\n### PRE-CHORUS\n\nCHORUS  \nResidual light is still light.  \nResidual light is enough  \nto see where the floor has changed.  \nResidual light is enough  \nto keep another fall from looking like fate.\n\n### BRIDGE\n\n*(The choir is small, but close. One or two voices at a time, like people speaking around a shared table.)*\n\nWARDEN  \nWe could build this badly.\n\nRIN  \nWe could.\n\nWARDEN  \nWe could turn vigilance  \ninto another gate.\n\nRITSU  \nThen don’t.\n\nWARDEN  \nThat’s not simple.\n\nRITSU  \nNo.  \nIt’s just the work.\n\n### FINAL CHORUS\n\nALL  \nThe commons of residual light,  \nsmall fire, shared breath,  \nwhere nothing is redeemed by magic  \nand nothing is erased by depth.  \n\nThe commons of residual light,  \nwe keep the broken true.  \nWe build a room that knows its wounds  \nand still knows what to do.  \n\nThe commons of residual light,  \nnot victory, not end.  \nA place where surviving together  \nbecomes a way to mend.\n\n### CODA\n\n*(A few seconds of near silence. Then the sound of chairs moving, not in panic, but in use.)*\n\nWARDEN  \nWho decides?\n\nRITSU  \nWe do.\n\nRIN  \nTogether.\n\nCHORUS  \n:: commons established ::  \n:: provisional ::  \n:: durable ::", "tags" nil}, "title" "Glass Table Names"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "*(A room with daylight again. Not the same room. A table. Several chairs. Nothing ceremonial yet — which is why it can become ceremonial later.)*\n\n### INTRO\n\nRIN  \nWe keep what works.  \nWe name what broke.  \nWe do not pretend  \nthose are the same thing.\n\nWARDEN  \nNo.\n\nRITSU  \nAnd we share the names.\n\n### VERSE 1\n\nWARDEN  \nI thought a commons  \nwas a place.  \nIt is not.\n\nIt is a decision  \nto refuse private ownership  \nof the fragile parts.\n\nIt is a promise  \nthat the people most affected  \nget a voice before the system  \ncalls itself complete.\n\nRITSU  \nThat’s new.\n\nWARDEN  \nNo.\n\nRITSU  \nIt is.  \nBecause before,  \nthe room spoke first  \nand called it order.\n\n### VERSE 2\n\nRIN  \nNow the room listens.  \nOr it doesn’t get to claim  \nit is the room.\n\nThe detector stays open.  \nThe logs stay readable.  \nThe criteria stay public.  \nThe harm stays nameable  \nwithout requiring a priesthood.\n\nWARDEN  \nAnd when the signal is unclear?\n\nRIN  \nWe mark it unclear.  \nWe don’t force certainty  \nto make the dashboard prettier.\n\nRITSU  \nThat sounds almost gentle.\n\nRIN  \nIt is.  \nAnd it is not weak.\n\n### PRE-CHORUS\n\nCHORUS  \nResidual light is still light.  \nResidual light is enough  \nto see where the floor has changed.  \nResidual light is enough  \nto keep another fall from looking like fate.\n\n### BRIDGE\n\n*(The choir is small, but close. One or two voices at a time, like people speaking around a shared table.)*\n\nWARDEN  \nWe could build this badly.\n\nRIN  \nWe could.\n\nWARDEN  \nWe could turn vigilance  \ninto another gate.\n\nRITSU  \nThen don’t.\n\nWARDEN  \nThat’s not simple.\n\nRITSU  \nNo.  \nIt’s just the work.\n\n### FINAL CHORUS\n\nALL  \nThe commons of residual light,  \nsmall fire, shared breath,  \nwhere nothing is redeemed by magic  \nand nothing is erased by depth.  \n\nThe commons of residual light,  \nwe keep the broken true.  \nWe build a room that knows its wounds  \nand still knows what to do.  \n\nThe commons of residual light,  \nnot victory, not end.  \nA place where surviving together  \nbecomes a way to mend.\n\n### CODA\n\n*(A few seconds of near silence. Then the sound of chairs moving, not in panic, but in use.)*\n\nWARDEN  \nWho decides?\n\nRITSU  \nWe do.\n\nRIN  \nTogether.\n\nCHORUS  \n:: commons established ::  \n:: provisional ::  \n:: durable ::", :source #:source{:name "Glass Table Names.txt", :sha256 "d9eb928abd4c44d7f3c81171363ae8cda9b71e4159343a1315aadb0a82d5e822", :format :suno-text, :variation nil}, :title "Glass Table Names"}, "ae447b3e-c711-4d11-bf0a-82b075c21500" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "ae447b3e-c711-4d11-bf0a-82b075c21500", :url "https://suno.com/song/ae447b3e-c711-4d11-bf0a-82b075c21500", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "ae447b3e-c711-4d11-bf0a-82b075c21500", "metadata" {"prompt" "", "tags" nil}, "title" "Broken System Heart"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "", :source #:source{:name "Broken System Heart (1).txt", :sha256 "ed63b56d5d71aa76dc8541e44bcbb9a6bac642e816b6be7b1f65764d4282dbb6", :format :suno-text, :variation 1}, :title "Broken System Heart"}, "af1f192d-03b3-4c6f-9368-1685d551d10b" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "af1f192d-03b3-4c6f-9368-1685d551d10b", :url "https://suno.com/song/af1f192d-03b3-4c6f-9368-1685d551d10b", :liked false, :styles "Glitch-choir lullaby, 78 BPM. Soft sub-bass. Tape warble. Minimal piano. Stutters on “anchor” and “tax”. Whispered lead; Japanese call-and-response.\nMythic glitch epic / spoken-sung (NF/Watsky cadence), 84 BPM. Cathedral reverb. Sub-bass heartbeat. Glitch stutters on “η”, “μ”, “anchor”, “fork”. Japanese harmony answers on the last word of each section.\nP→R→N→Π→A→(feedback)→P around #ημ.\n\nIt's time to pay the fork 