 machines can diff, gate, and re-echo.\n- If the system can’t answer “what is the current world state?” without vibes, it will drift.\n\nInputs:\n- `analysis/world/*.md`\n- `analysis/constraints/*.md`\n\nOutputs:\n- `analysis/world/world_state_ledger.jsonl`\n  - one JSON object per source doc (kind=world|constraints)\n  - includes `id`, `seed`, `kv`, `notes`, and `file`\n- `analysis/world/world_state.json`\n  - `{ last_id, seed, merged }` where `merged` is the latest overlay\n\nDeterminism:\n- Ledger is rebuilt deterministically from file contents.\n- Sorting: by `id` then `kind`.\n- Snapshot: merges in that order (constraints can override world).\n\nCLI:\n- `node program/world_state_ledger.js --root . --emit`\n\nSuggested gate usage:\n- Run ledger build as a pre-step for any “announcement” or “revalidation” cycle.\n- Consume `world_state.json.merged` as the canonical config surface for tools.\n\nSafety:\n- Additive only; does not mutate source docs.\n- Output files are derived artifacts; can be deleted and rebuilt any time.", "tags" nil}, "title" "# Feature — World State Ledger (μ-world)"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "# Feature — World State Ledger (μ-world)\n\nGoal:\nConvert the living narrative of the world (markdown updates + constraints) into a queryable, checkable state.\n\nWhy:\n- η can describe anything.\n- μ must serialize to something machines can diff, gate, and re-echo.\n- If the system can’t answer “what is the current world state?” without vibes, it will drift.\n\nInputs:\n- `analysis/world/*.md`\n- `analysis/constraints/*.md`\n\nOutputs:\n- `analysis/world/world_state_ledger.jsonl`\n  - one JSON object per source doc (kind=world|constraints)\n  - includes `id`, `seed`, `kv`, `notes`, and `file`\n- `analysis/world/world_state.json`\n  - `{ last_id, seed, merged }` where `merged` is the latest overlay\n\nDeterminism:\n- Ledger is rebuilt deterministically from file contents.\n- Sorting: by `id` then `kind`.\n- Snapshot: merges in that order (