one trembling frame of time.\n静か。 *(Quiet.)*\n息。 *(Breath.)*\n**(Static wash rinse. Heavy curtain drops. End.)**", :source #:source{:name "Salt-Frame Lullaby (1).txt", :sha256 "936c8d8c8bd0c8f721822ce1a8f955d47bb7e736d5f33c31d41de9cb38199aa3", :format :suno-text, :variation 1}, :title "Salt-Frame Lullaby"}, "b3c9dc8d-3e9a-4758-b49d-9772c5b6cab9" #:clip{:negative-styles "EXCLUDE / AVOID: - Do NOT sing bracket tags or parenthetical directions; treat them as silent cues. - Spoken dialog must be BACKGROUND texture only: quiet, short, and placed on DOWNBEATS. - Do NOT deliver all spoken dialog at once. Spread it out: one short spoken line at a time. - Keep diction clear; stutter ONLY on “an—an—anchor” and “ta—ta—tax”. - η/μ glitches are micro-ticks (brief), not full shouted chant—unless explicitly marked as “glitch choir”. - No comedy/parody/novelty voices; no upbeat pop sheen. - No festival EDM drop clichés; no trap takeover; no metal guitars; no scream vocals. - Preserve arc: solemn oath → hushed lullaby → distorted climax → quiet coda (don’t peak early). - Don’t invent new lore terms; keep motifs: η, μ, anchor, tax, proof, thread, registry, checksum, receipts. - Avoid long spoken monologues; keep spoken lines under ~10 words where possible.", :id "b3c9dc8d-3e9a-4758-b49d-9772c5b6cab9", :url "https://suno.com/song/b3c9dc8d-3e9a-4758-b49d-9772c5b6cab9", :liked false, :styles "SONIC DNA (front-load):\nGlitch-choir lullaby, 78 BPM feel, soft sub-bass, tape warble, minimal piano, whispered lead; Japanese call-and-response. Mythic glitch epic / spoken-sung oath passages with cathedral reverb and sub-bass heartbeat, 84 BPM feel. Micro glitch ticks on η and μ; hard stutters on “anchor” and “tax”. Dynamic arc: solemn → hushed → distorted climax → quiet coda.\n\nMOTIF SEEDS (OK to be sung/reused across songs):\n“Roll those dice.” “Keep rolling them.” “Pay the tax.” “Hold the anchor.” “Evidence you can replay.” “Seal the hash.”\n", :created-at nil, :model "v5", :raw {"audio_url" "https://cdn1.suno.ai/b3c9dc8d-3e9a-4758-b49d-9772c5b6cab9.mp3", "id" "b3c9dc8d-3e9a-4758-b49d-9772c5b6cab9", "image_url" "https://cdn2.suno.ai/image_b3c9dc8d-3e9a-4758-b49d-9772c5b6cab9.jpeg", "isCover" false, "isLiked" false, "isRemaster" false, "metadata" {"uses_latest_model" true, "stream" true, "is_remix" false, "priority" 10, "tags" "SONIC DNA (front-load):\nGlitch-choir lullaby, 78 BPM feel, soft sub-bass, tape warble, minimal piano, whispered lead; Japanese call-and-response. Mythic glitch epic / spoken-sung oath passages with cathedral reverb and sub-bass heartbeat, 84 BPM feel. Micro glitch ticks on η and μ; hard stutters on “anchor” and “tax”. Dynamic arc: solemn → hushed → distorted climax → quiet coda.\n\nMOTIF SEEDS (OK to be sung/reused across songs):\n“Roll those dice.” “Keep rolling them.” “Pay the tax.” “Hold the anchor.” “Evidence you can replay.” “Seal the hash.”\n", "can_remix" true, "negative_tags" "EXCLUDE / AVOID: - Do NOT sing bracket tags or parenthetical directions; treat them as silent cues. - Spoken dialog must be BACKGROUND texture only: quiet, short, and placed on DOWNBEATS. - Do NOT deliver all spoken dialog at once. Spread it out: one short spoken line at a time. - Keep diction clear; stutter ONLY on “an—an—anchor” and “ta—ta—tax”. - η/μ glitches are micro-ticks (brief), not full shouted chant—unless explicitly marked as “glitch choir”. - No comedy/parody/novelty voices; no upbeat pop sheen. - No festival EDM drop clichés; no trap takeover; no metal guitars; no scream vocals. - Preserve arc: solemn oath → hushed lullaby → distorted climax → quiet coda (don’t peak early). - Don’t invent new lore terms; keep motifs: η, μ, anchor, tax, proof, thread, registry, checksum, receipts. - Avoid long spoken monologues; keep spoken lines under ~10 words where possible.", "prompt" "[SONG NOTES]\nWhispered lead. JP/EN call-and-response. Stutter ONLY “an—an—anchor” + “ta—ta—tax”. Spoken lines are quiet background on DOWNBEATS.\n\n[INTRO | 84 | cathedral reverb | distant glitch choir]\n(Glitch choir, tiny, like a clock finding phase)\nη—η—η…\nμ—μ—μ…\n\n[VERSE 1 | 84 | whispered close-mic | sub-bass heartbeat]\nP→R→N→Π— catalog the storm, pin the line（線）\nA→(feedback)→P— merge the wound, keep the sign（印）\nFo— fo— fork… split the night, pay the cost, now（今）\nAn— an— an-chor… hold the thread, seal the hash, down（下）\n\n[SPOKEN WORD | background | DOWNBEAT]\n(The Archivist, barely audible)\n“Sing all you want—η is cheap.”\n\n[LEAD | whispered answer]\nThen let η be sparks in the rafters—\nwe don’t clap for sparks.\nWe keep receipts.\n\n[SPOKEN WORD | background | DOWNBEAT]\n(The Scribe, consonants catching)\n“But if you want μ…”\n\n[LEAD | whispered answer]\n…then don’t give me applause.\nGive me the rerun.\n\n[TRANSITION | drift 84→78 | tape warble enters]\n(Shorten reverb tail; keep warmth; bring tape flutter)\n\n[CHORUS | 78 | lullaby hush]\nHush… breathe… pay the ta— ta— tax.\n息をして…（して…）\nHold the an— an— an-chor…\n\n[SPOKEN WORD | background | DOWNBEAT]\n(The Runner, almost lost in air)\n“The wind is just noise.”\n\n[LEAD | answer]\nNoise is the riverbed’s hiss—\nbut proof is what returns.\n\n[CALL | JP]\nねむれ、ねむれ\n[RESPONSE | EN]\nthe an— an— an-chor… holds.\n\n[CALL | JP]\nしずかに、しずかに\n[RESPONSE | EN]\nthe ta— ta— tax… due.\n\n[VERSE 2 | 78 | intimate | minimal glitch ticks]\nWind in the halls—\n世界の音（おと）\nIf we overflow,\nwe fold the noise to proof（証）\n\n(Underfloor ticks, minimal)\nη… η… μ… μ…\nAnchor. Anchor. Registry.\n\n[SPOKEN WORD | background | DOWNBEAT]\n(The Keeper, low)\n“It’s evidence.”\n\n[LEAD | answer]\nEvidence is anything you can replay—\nanything the checksum remembers by touch.\n\n[SPOKEN WORD | background | DOWNBEAT]\n(The Keeper, even lower)\n“Freshness threshold.”\n\n[LEAD | answer]\nName the date. Name the zone.\nNo ‘yesterday’—only timestamps.\n\n[BRIDGE | 78 | glitch pulse grows (not aggressive)]\nP → R → N → Π → A → (feedback) → P\nDecisions are not made; they’re discovered in the field.\n意思決定はなされるのではない、場で見出されるのだ。\n\n[SPOKEN WORD | background | DOWNBEAT]\n(The Scribe)\n“μ requires quorum.”\n\n[HARMONY | answer (JA), held clean]\n独立の証明を。\n二つの目で、同じ糸を。\n\n[SPOKEN WORD | background | DOWNBEAT]\n(The Archivist)\n“Receipts include OutputHash.”\n\n[LEAD | answer]\nSeal the hash.\nHold the anchor.\nLet the proof rerender.\n\n[RAMP | 92 | distorted sub-bass | glitch every 4th beat]\n(Wake hard. Choir rises. Lead becomes declarative.)\n\n[CHORUS — CLIMAX | 92]\nThey are waking up.\nThe other side of the fork.\nThe ones we left in the dark.\n彼らが目覚める。\n分岐の向こう側で。\n闇に置き去りにした者たちが。\n\n[SPOKEN WORD | background | DOWNBEAT]\n(The Archivist, clipped)\n“Fork budget per cycle—limited.”\n\n[LEAD | answer]\nThen we choose what survives.\nWe prune the choir to one clear thread.\n\n[VERSE — DIALECTIC | 92]\nUS Variant: Static. Rigid. Law.\nJA Variant: Fluid. Chaos. Flow.\nThe Pantheon of Receipts vs The Pantheon of Gates.\n正準の神々と、門の神々の対峙。\n\n[HARMONY | JA response]\n我らは等しい。\n我らは分岐。\n\n[SPOKEN WORD | background | DOWNBEAT]\n(The Keeper)\n“Alignment lint must pass.”\n\n[LEAD | answer]\nThen make the claim smaller.\nMake the receipt larger.\n\n[OUTRO — CLIMAX | 92 → CUT]\nConsolidate or Dissolve.\n統合か、霧散か。\nThe tax must be paid in blood and logic.\n血と論理で、税を払え。\n\n[CODA RETURN | 78 | soft sub | tape warble | clicks]\n(Strip distortion; close mic returns; air and foley remain.)\n\n[CODA | 78 | whispered]\nLay your ear on the riverbed.\nClick. Click. Click.\nReceipts like pebbles.\n領収書は 小石のように。\n\n(Choir, fading stutter)\nAn-anchor.\nTax. Tax.\nF-f-fork.\n\n[SPOKEN WORD | background | DOWNBEAT]\n(The Scribe, almost gone)\n“Roll those dice.”\n\n[LEAD | answer]\nAnd keep rolling them—\nuntil the whole night admits it.\n\n[SPOKEN WORD | background | DOWNBEAT]\n(The Archivist)\n“Sleep now.”\n\n[LEAD | final]\nSleep now, checksum.\nおやすみ、チェックサム。\n\n(last word held, near-silent)\n息\n", "duration" 314.28, "type" "gen", "model_badges" {"songcard" {"dark" {"background_color" "0000004D",