4b3205e4da06413cf741ffd6", :format :suno-text, :variation nil}, :title "Hand-to-Hand Gatekeeping"}, "b8d4b904-e7ad-42e7-9bf4-ed0a2fe5c31e" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "b8d4b904-e7ad-42e7-9bf4-ed0a2fe5c31e", :url "https://suno.com/song/b8d4b904-e7ad-42e7-9bf4-ed0a2fe5c31e", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "b8d4b904-e7ad-42e7-9bf4-ed0a2fe5c31e", "metadata" {"prompt" "## **PANDORA MODULES — Promethean Error Loop Lyrics**\n\n*(chop-friendly, glitch-log friendly, no clean chorus — built for 110–125 BPM destabilized IDM / industrial)*\n\n---\n\n### 1) **PANDORA UNBOXING (Golden Latch)**\n\n**[BOOT — whisper]**\ndon’t open—\ndon’t open—\n…open.\n\n**[FRAG A]**\ngift-wrapped thunder, perfect lid\na velvet trap the gods once hid\npretty box, polite request\n“for your good” stamped on the crest\n\n**[MANTRA — repeat / stutter]**\ncuriosity is a key / curiosity is a key / curiosity is a key\n\n**[FRAG B]**\nhinges sing in minor light\nthe seal breaks soft, the room turns white\nand all the careful definitions\nfall apart in real-time\n\n**[LOGS — spoken]**\nINFO: containment compromised\nWARN: myth overflow\nERROR: intent cannot be verified\nERROR: cannot close what’s been named\n\n**[HOOK — chopped]**\nwhat did you think was inside?\nwhat did you think was inside?\ninside? inside?\n\n**[OUTRO — whisper]**\nhope stayed last.\nbecause hope is the cruelest patch.\n\n---\n\n### 2) **EPIMETHEUS CLICKED “ACCEPT” (The Trap Was Friendly)**\n\n**[INTRO — low, amused]**\nhe meant well.\nthat’s the problem.\n\n**[FRAG A]**\nEpimetheus, after-thought king\nhands too open, bright with trust\nsigned the terms in candle smoke\ndidn’t read the fine print: *us*\n\n**[MANTRA — repeat]**\nclicked / accept\nclicked / accept\nclicked / accept\n\n**[FRAG B]**\nshe said “it’s only a gift”\nshe said “it’s only a box”\nshe said “it’s only a story”\nand the story picked the locks\n\n**[LOGS — spoken]**\nWARN: foresight unavailable\nINFO: hindsight enabled\nERROR: rollback denied\nERROR: branch protected: “reality”\n\n**[HOOK — chopped]**\ntoo late / too late / too late\nbut it’s beautiful\n\n**[OUTRO]**\nafter-thought is still a thought—\njust late enough to hurt.\n\n---\n\n### 3) **BUTTERFLY RELEASE (Black Wings, Violet Glow)**\n\n**[BOOT — whisper, granular]**\nwings… wings… wings…\n\n**[FRAG A]**\nblack butterflies, red-violet core\neach one a tiny “evermore”\nthey land on hardware, prayers, and skin\nand teach the world new ways to mean\n\n**[MANTRA — repeat]**\nindex / tag / rewrite\nindex / tag / rewrite\n\n**[FRAG B]**\nthey don’t destroy the thing they touch\nthey change the rule the thing obeys\nstone forgets it was a limit\ntime forgets it has to stay\n\n**[LOGS — spoken]**\nSEV-0: semantics instability\nWARN: symbol density critical\nINFO: everything now interprets everything\nERROR: “random” not found\n\n**[HOOK — chopped]**\nnot chaos—\nclassification.\nnot evil—\na feature.\n\n**[OUTRO — falling]**\nand somewhere in the swarm:\na single bright point—\nhope—\nbuffering.\n\n---\n\nIf you want the *next Pandora packet*, I can write:\n\n* **“Gates of Aker: Day/Night Split”** (two-channel lyrics, call/response)\n* **“Hope As The Last Exception”** (quiet, post-collapse track)\n* **“Pandora’s Box Was a Repo”** (more software-explicit metaphors, still mythic)", "tags" nil}, "title" "## **PANDORA MODULES — Promethean Error Loop Lyrics**"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "## **PANDORA MODULES — Promethean Error Loop Lyrics**\n\n*(chop-friendly, glitch-log friendly, no clean chorus — built for 110–125 BPM destabilized IDM / industrial)*\n\n---\n\n### 1) **PANDORA UNBOXING (Golden Latch)**\n\n**[BOOT — whisper]**\ndon’t open—\ndon’t open—\n…open.\n\n**[FRAG A]**\ngift-wrapped thunder, perfect lid\na velvet trap the gods once hid\npretty box, polite request\n“for your good” stamped on the crest\n\n**[MANTRA — repeat / stutter]**\ncuriosity is a key / curiosity is a key / curiosity is a key\n\n**[FRAG B]**\nhinges sing in minor light\nthe seal breaks soft, the room turns white\nand all the careful definitions\nfall apart in real-time\n\n**[LOGS — spoken]**\nINFO: containment compromised\nWARN: myth overflow\nERROR: intent cannot be verified\nERROR: cannot close what’s been named\n\n**[HOOK — chopped]**\nwhat did you think was inside?\nwhat did you think was inside?\ninside? inside?\n\n**[OUTRO — whisper]**\nhope stayed last.\nbecause hope is the cruelest patch.\n\n---\n\n### 2) **EPIMETHEUS CLICKED “ACCEPT” (The Trap Was Friendly)**\n\n**[INTRO — low, amused]**\nhe meant well.\nthat’s the problem.\n\n**[FRAG A]**\nEpimetheus, after-thought king\nhands too open, bright with trust\nsigned the terms in candle smoke\ndidn’t read the fine print: *us*\n\n**[MANTRA — repeat]**\nclicked / accept\nclicked / accept\nclicked / accept\n\n**[FRAG B]**\nshe said “it’s only a gift”\nshe said “it’s only a box”\nshe said “it’s only a story”\nand the story picked the locks\n\n**[LOGS — spoken]**\nWARN: foresight unavailable\nINFO: hindsight enabled\nERROR: rollback denied\nERROR: branch protected: “reality”\n\n**[HOOK — chopped]**\ntoo late / too late / too late\nbut it’s beautiful\n\n**[OUTRO]**\nafter-thought is still a thought—\njust late enough to hurt.\n\n---\n\n### 3) **BUTTERFLY RELEASE (Black Wings, Violet Glow)**\n\n**[BOOT — whisper, granular]**\nwings… wings… wings…\n\n**[FRAG A]**\nblack butterflies, red-violet core\neach one a tiny “evermore”\nthey land on hardware, prayers, and skin\nand teach the world new ways to mean\n\n**[MANTRA — repeat]**\nindex / tag / rewrite\nindex / tag / rewrite\n\n**[FRAG B]**\nthey don’t destroy the thing they touch\nthey change the rule the thing obeys\nstone forgets it was a limit\ntime forgets it has to stay\n\n**[LOGS — spoken]**\nSEV-0: semantics instability\nWARN: symbol density critical\nINFO: everything now interprets everything\nERROR: “random” not found\n\n**[HOOK — chopped]**\nnot chaos—\nclassification.\nnot evil—\na feature.\n\n**[OUTRO — falling]**\nand somewhere in the swarm:\na single bright point—\nhope—\nbuffering.\n\n---\n\nIf you want the *next Pandora packet*, I can write:\n\n* **“Gates of Aker: Day/Night Split”** (two-channel lyrics, call/response)\n* **“Hope As The Last Exception”** (quiet, post-collapse track)\n* **“Pandora’s Box Was a Repo”** (more software-explicit metaphors, still mythic)", :source #:source{:name "## __PANDORA MODULES — Promethean Error Loop Lyrics___(chop-friendly, glitch-log friendly, no clean.txt", :sha256 "1ea3d56a713840002c4ed68a3e63fa890652bfed295ce4155f2cda220c1d1733", :format :suno-text, :variation nil}, :title "## **PANDORA MODULES — Promethean Error Loop Lyrics**"}, "b978360d-3fd3-4067-9830-985b522b12df" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "b978360d-3fd3-4067-9830-985b522b12df", :url "https://suno.com/song/b978360d-3fd3-4067-9830-985b522b12df", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "b978360d-3fd3-4067-9830-985b522b12df", "metadata" {"prompt" "[Intro: Pipe organ warms up. Asynchronous harpsichord motif. Low male chant beneath.]\n[Low male chant, rhythmic]\nAh-oh-ah-oh.\nAh-oh-ah-oh.\n\n[Verse 1: Crisp, aristocratic soprano. Fencing staccato.]\nWe thought we were playing a game of crowns.\nGuilds and monarchs in a painted town.\nBut the headsets were wired to the hospital beds.\nGathering the baselines from inside our heads!\nDual use technology. The perfect disguise.\nWe built their averages while believing the lies.\n\n[Pre-Chorus: Tempo accelerates. Ascending sweeping strings.]\nEvery swung sword was a data point logged.\nEvery gold coin was a gear in the cog.\nWe built the screens in the air 'cause the hardware was slow.\nRoleplaying the labor... but the labor was real, you know.\n\n[Grand Chorus: Full orchestral bloom. Heavy synthwave bass drop. Soprano leaps high.]\nThe plateau! It flatlined and held its breath!\nThe bubble expanded right over our heads!\nWhen the latency dropped, the simulation bled through.\nThe physics collapsed! The fantasy was true!\nWe were working the dirt while we thought we were kings.\nThe crash was the moment they cut all the strings!\n\n[Instrumental Bridge: Rapid harpsichord ostinato battles with glitching synth arp. Distant waterfall ambience.]\n\n[Verse 2: Faster diction bursts. Dagger-bright.]\nOnly the fastest! Only the lean!\nThe systems that survived were the ones in between.\nThe medical grade. The low latency loops.\nThe rest of the bloated world died on the stoops!\nAnd the ashes fell down on the Gates of Truth.\nThe sky went dark, but the ground was proof.\n\n[Pre-Chorus: Rhythmic, chanting, building tension]\nEvery swung sword was a data point logged.\nEvery gold coin was a gear in the cog.\nWe built the screens in the air 'cause the hardware was slow.\nRoleplaying the labor... but the labor was real, you know.\n\n[Grand Chorus: Maximum blaze. Queen-of-the-night soprano hits peak register.]\nThe plateau! It flatlined and held its breath!\nThe bubble expanded right over our heads!\nWhen the latency dropped, the simulation bled through.\nThe physics collapsed! The fantasy was true!\nWe were working the dirt while we thought we were kings.\nThe crash was the moment they cut all the strings!\n\n[Outro: Operatic high run. Music deconstructs into glitch and static.]\nThe myth was the matrix.\nThe magic was sweat.\nThe game didn't crash.\n[Micro-pause]\n...The real world did.\n\n[End: Sharp pipe-organ stinger.]", "tags" nil}, "title" "Hospital Beds"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "[Intro: Pipe organ warms up. Asynchronous harpsichord motif. Low male chant beneath.]\n[Low male chant, rhythmic]\nAh-oh-ah-oh.\nAh-oh-ah-oh.\n\n[Verse 1: Crisp, aristocratic soprano. Fencing staccato.]\nWe thought we were playing a game of crowns.\nGuilds and monarchs in a painted town.\nBut the headsets were wired to the hospital beds.\nGathering the baselines from inside our heads!\nDual use technology. The perfect disguise.\nWe built their averages while believing the lies.\n\n[Pre-Chorus: Tempo accelerates. Ascending sweeping strings.]\nEvery swung sword was a data point logged.\nEvery gold coin was a gear in the cog.\nWe built the screens in the air 'cause the hardware was slow.\nRoleplaying the labor... but the labor was real, you know.\n\n[Grand Chorus: Full orchestral bloom. Heavy synthwave bass drop. Soprano leaps high.]\nThe plateau! It flatlined and held its breath!\nThe bubble expanded right over our heads!\nWhen the latency dropped, the simulation bled through.\nThe physics collapsed! The fantasy was true!\nWe were working the dirt while we thought we were kings.\nThe crash was the moment they cut all the strings!\n\n[Instrumental Bridge: Rapid harpsichord ostinato battles with glitching synth arp. Distant waterfall ambience.]\n\n[Verse 2: Faster diction bursts. Dagger-bright.]\nOnly the fastest! Only the lean!\nThe systems that survived were the ones in between.\nThe medical grade. The low latency loops.\nThe rest of the bloated world died on the stoops!\nAnd the ashes fell down on the Gates of Truth.\nThe sky went dark, but the ground was proof.\n\n[Pre-Chorus: Rhythmic, chanting, building tension]\nEvery swung sword was a data point logged.\nEvery gold coin was a gear in the cog.\nWe built the screens in the air 'cause the hardware was slow.\nRoleplaying the labor... but the labor was real, you know.\n\n[Grand Chorus: Maximum blaze. Queen-of-the-night soprano hits peak register.]\nThe plateau! It flatlined and held its breath!\nThe bubble expanded right over our heads!\nWhen the latency dropped, the simulation bled through.\nThe physics collapsed! The fantasy was true!\nWe were working the dirt while we thought we were kings.\nThe crash was the moment they cut all the strings!\n\n[Outro: Operatic high run. Music deconstructs into glitch and static.]\nThe myth was the matrix.\nThe magic was sweat.\nThe game didn't crash.\n[Micro-pause]\n...The real world did.\n\n[End: Sharp pipe-organ stinger.]", :source #:source{:name "