archability & Packaging (the “box”)\n\n**S16. Search Index (μ)** ← S0–S15\n\n* Build a lightweight local index:\n\n  * keywords\n  * entity mentions\n  * anchor spans\n  * artifact references\n* Output: `sqlite` or `whoosh` index + CLI query.\n\n**S17. Part Builder (μ)** ← S16\n\n* Build downloadable parts: per story / per layer / per artifact type.\n* Output: `Operation_Mindfuck_Box_partXX_*.zip`.\n\n---\n\n### G) Learning Loop (how the skill graph improves)\n\n**S18. Outcome Scoring (η)** ← S10–S15\n\n* Evaluate: do derived edges match explicit text evidence?\n* Track false merges, missed events, spurious forks.\n\n**S19. Weight Tuning (η→μ)** ← S18\n\n* Adjust weights: co-occurrence vs action edges vs causal edges; lexicons; thresholds.\n* Output: `config.toml` with versioned params.\n\n**S20. Curriculum Scheduler (η)** ← S18 + S0\n\n* Choose next improvements by **information gain per cost**:\n\n  * biggest error class × easiest fix first.\n\n---\n\n## How this maps to your P→R→N→Π→A loop\n\n* **P (Plan)**: pick next bottleneck node (usually S5/S7/S9/S14 at scale)\n* **R (Run)**: execute μ nodes with current params\n* **N (Notice)**: measure errors (S18) + drift + missing edge", :source #:source{:name "## SignalHere’s the __Skill Graph__ I’d follow to compile _Operation Mindfuck_ into scalable “box pa.txt", :sha256 "40895a23b4f7bdab8ee0d29730ac11db0a8a722eacac6a0c7480a1b48b2b24ff", :format :suno-text, :variation nil}, :title "## Signal"}, "ba38d7d5-8089-4db1-86c9-61eb185143bb" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "ba38d7d5-8089-4db1-86c9-61eb185143bb", :url "https://suno.com/song/ba38d7d5-8089-4db1-86c9-61eb185143bb", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "ba38d7d5-8089-4db1-86c9-61eb185143bb", "metadata" {"prompt" "*(soft sub-bass, tape warble, minimal piano; stutters on “anchor” + “tax”; whispered lead; Japanese call-and-response)*\n\n[Intro — tape hiss, two-note piano, warm sub]\n(whisper)\nHush… the ledger is counting in its sleep.\n息をして… (して…)\nA soft machine rocking the room.\n\n(JP call) ねむれ、ねむれ\n(EN response) the **an— an— an-chor**… (stutter) holds.\n(JP call) しずかに、しずかに\n(EN response) the **ta— ta— tax**… (stutter) is due.\n\n(piano, tiny wobble)\nAn— an— **an-chor**… (stutter) an-chor…\n(JP whisper harmony) アンカー…\n(sub-bass: heartbeat but gentler)\n\n(whisper)\nPay the **ta— ta— tax**… (stutter) ta-x…\n(JP harmony) 税…\nNot guilt—\njust interest on an unproven branch.\n\n[Verse — lullaby cadence, breathy]\nP: I feel the constraint (#η)\nR: I fetch the last clean thread\nN: I cut the story into one claim\nΠ: I pick the cheapest test\nA: I touch the world and wait\n(feedback): I write the pushback like a lullaby.\n\n(JP call) ねえ、ほんと？\n(EN response) only if it repeats.\n(JP call) ねえ、だいじょうぶ？\n(EN response) only if it’s logged.\n\n[Chorus — choir bloom, tape warble widening]\nAn— an— **an-chor**… (stutter) an-chor…\nHold the boundary, hold the line.\nPay the **ta— ta— tax**… (stutter) ta-x…\nSo forks don’t breed in the dark.\n(JP harmony answers last word)\nI fall asleep inside **proof**.（証）\n\n---\n\n## Part II — Mythic glitch epic / spoken-sung (84 BPM)\n\n*(NF/Watsky cadence; cathedral reverb; sub-bass heartbeat; glitch stutters on “η”, “μ”, “anchor”, “fork”; Japanese harmony answers on the last word of each section)*\n\n[Verse 1 — heartbeat sub, fast spoken-sung]\nThey drape a quote in velvet and call it truth,\nbut the Lantern checks the seams for missing proof.\n“Look, we cited it,” they say— I say, “Align it,”\ncause a misfit quote is just a fork in disguise,\na dressed-up **fork**.（分岐）\n\n(Glitch stutter) **η—η—η**\n(Glitch stutter) **μ—μ—μ**\n\n[Hook — cathedral swell]\nI don’t win by sounding right—\nI win by making it rerun.（試）\n\n[Verse 2 — rapid cadence]\nEvery loop without a receipt? Interest accrues.\nFork Tax compounds till the branch can’t move.\nSo I write a boundary before I write a throne—\nwhat it does **not** claim, carved into the stone.\n\nI pin it to an **an-an-anchor** (stutter)\nand stare the Gate dead on: “Name the counter.”\nForkgate says “Pay,” I say “Here’s the harness,”\nLantern lights up— not for vibe, but for μ in the margins,\nreal **μ**.（証）\n\n(JP harmony answers last word) 証\n\n[Pre — glitch clicks, choir tight]\nSay **η**… (stutter) η-η\nSay **μ**… (stutter) μ-μ\nSay **an-chor**… (stutter) an-an-chor\nSay **fork**… (stutter) fo-fo-fork（分岐）\n\n[Chorus — big, then sudden hush]\nP→R→N→Π→A— the method is the crown.（冠）\n(feedback) → P— the world collects what you owe.（税）\nAn— an— **an-chor**… (stutter) an-chor…\nso the ledger knows what to keep.（記）\nFo— fo— **fork**… (stutter) fork…\nonly when evidence buys the branch.（証）\n\n[Outro — cathedral tail dissolves into tape warble]\n(whisper)\nη… (stutter) η-η\nμ… (stutter) μ-μ\nAn— an— **an-chor**…\nPay the **ta— ta— tax**…\nOne more roll. One more node. One more test.", "tags" nil}, "title" "*(soft sub-bass, tape warble, minimal piano; stutters on “anchor” + “tax”; whispered lead; Japanese call-and-response)*"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "*(soft sub-bass, tape warble, minimal piano; stutters on “anchor” + “tax”; whispered lead; Japanese call-and-response)*\n\n[Intro — tape hiss, two-note piano, warm sub]\n(whisper)\nHush… the ledger is counting in its sleep.\n息をして… (して…)\nA soft machine rocking the room.\n\n(JP call) ねむれ、ねむれ\n(EN response) the **an— an— an-chor**… (stutter) holds.\n(JP call) しずかに、しずかに\n(EN response) the **ta— ta— tax**… (stutter) is due.\n\n(piano, tiny wobble)\nAn— an— **an-chor**… (stutter) an-chor…\n(JP whisper harmony) アンカー…\n(sub-bass: heartbeat but gentler)\n\n(whisper)\nPay the **ta— ta— tax**… (stutter) ta-x…\n(JP harmony) 税…\nNot guilt—\njust interest on an unproven branch.\n\n[Verse — lullaby cadence, breathy]\nP: I feel the constraint (#η)\nR: I fetch the last clean thread\nN: I cut the story into one claim\nΠ: I pick the cheapest test\nA: I touch the world and wait\n(feedback): I write the pushback like a lullaby.\n\n(JP call) ねえ、ほんと？\n(EN response) only if it repeats.\n(JP call) ねえ、だいじょうぶ？\n(EN response) only if it’s logged.\n\n[Chorus — choir bloom, tape warble widening]\nAn— an— **an-chor**… (stutter) an-chor…\nHold the boundary, hold the line.\nPay the **ta— ta— tax**… (stutter) ta-x…\nSo forks don’t breed in the dark.\n(JP harmony answers last word)\nI fall asleep inside **proof**.（証）\n\n---\n\n## Part II — Mythic glitch epic / spoken-sung (84 BPM)\n\n*(NF/Watsky cadence; cathedral reverb; sub-bass heartbeat; glitch stutters on “η”, “μ”, “anchor”, “fork”; Japanese harmony answers on the last word of each section)*\n\n[Verse 1 — heartbeat sub, fast spoken-sung]\nThey drape a quote in velvet and call it truth,\nbut the Lantern checks the seams for missing proof.\n“Look, we cited it,” they say— I say, “Align it,”\ncause a misfit quote is just a fork in disguise,\na dressed-up **fork**.（分岐）\n\n(Glitch stutter) **η—η—η**\n(Glitch stutter) **μ—μ—μ**\n\n[Hook — cathedral swell]\nI don’t win by sounding right—\nI win by making it rerun.（試）\n\n[Verse 2 — rapid cadence]\nEvery loop without a receipt? Interest accrues.\nFork Tax compounds till the branch can’t move.\nSo I write a boundary before I write a throne—\nwhat it does **not** claim, carved into the stone.\n\nI pin it to an **an-an-anchor** (stutter)\nand stare the Gate dead on: “Name the counter.”\nForkgate says “Pay,” I say “Here’s the harness,”\nLantern lights up— not for vibe, but for μ in the margins,\nreal **μ**.（証）\n\n(JP harmony answers last word) 証\n\n[Pre — glitch clicks, choir tight]\nSay **η**… (stutter) η-η\nSay **μ**… (stutter) μ-μ\nSay **an-chor**… (stutter) an-an-chor\nSay **fork**… (stutter) fo-fo-fork（分岐）\n\n[Chorus — big, then sudden hush]\nP→R→N→Π→A— the method is the crown.（冠）\n(feedback) → P— the world collects what you owe.（税）\nAn— an— **an-chor**… (stutter) an-chor…\nso the ledger knows what to keep.（記）\nFo— fo— **fork**… (stutter) fork…\nonly when evidence buys the branch.（証）\n\n[Outro — cathedral tail dissolves into tape warble]\n(whisper)\nη… (stutter) η-η\nμ… (stutter) μ-μ\nAn— an— **an-chor**…\nPay the **ta— ta— tax**…\nOne more roll. One more node. One more test.", :source #:source{:name "_(soft sub-bass, tape warble, minimal piano; stutters on “anchor” + “tax”; whispered lead; Japanese (2).txt", :sha256 "bad701d19338bc626b0f00c90d5fe0925dd880523bb8dfaaf599405d49c80a94", :format :suno-text, :variation 2}, :title "*(soft sub-bass, tape warble, minimal piano; stutters on “anchor” + “tax”; whispered lead; Japanese call-and-response)*"}, "ba4b2dc9-b6dc-421f-867b-527c7b72c5a8" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "ba4b2dc9-b6dc-421f-867b-527c7b72c5a8", :url "https://suno.com/song/ba4b2dc9-b6dc-421f-867b-527c7b72c5a8", :liked false, :styles "**Genre/Style:** Dark cinematic bass × industrial sci‑fi × soft glitch ambient comedown. 92–100 BPM, half‑time crush. Massive sub drops, distorted bass hits, seismic impacts, metallic shrieks, warped orchestral stabs → then a drained, breath‑guided aftermath (felt piano, thin choir haze, warehouse reverb, wind-through-glass field recording).\n\n**Structure:**\n\n1. *Tension* (radio hiss + distant kick + breath) →\n2. *Impact* (sub drop + orchestral stab) →\n3. *Cascading collapse* (granular noise + stutters + broken transmission) →\n4. *Echoing ruin* (piano minimalism + warm sub + long silence pockets).\n\n**Vocals:** Minimal. Intimate near‑whisper lead with occasional distant screams stretched into texture. Reversed chants as pads. Japanese response-lines to English (call/answer). A few spoken “protocol lines” like a system readout.\n\n**Mood:** Catastrophic clarity → boundary → survival warmth. Cosmic dread that resolves into steady breath.\n", :created-at nil, :model "v4.5-all", :raw {"audio_url" "https://cdn1.suno.ai/ba4b2dc9-b6dc-421f-867b-527c7b72c5a8.mp3", "id" "ba4b2dc9-b6dc-421f-867b-527c7b72c5a8", "image_url" "https://cdn2.suno.ai/image_ba4b2dc9-b6dc-421f-867b-527c7b72c5a8.jpeg", "isCover" false, "isLiked" false, "isRemaster" false, "metadata" {"uses_latest_model" false, "stream" true, "is_remix" false, "priority" 0, "tags" "**Genre/Style:** Dark cinematic bass × industrial sci‑fi × soft glitch ambient comedown. 92–100 BPM, half‑time crush. Massive sub drops, distorted bass hits, seismic impacts, metallic shrieks, warped orchestral stabs → then a drained, breath‑guided aftermath (felt piano, thin choir haze, warehouse reverb, wind-through-glass field recording).\n\n**Structure:**\n\n1. *Tension* (radio hiss + distant kick + breath) →\n2. *Impact* (sub drop + orchestral stab) →\n3. *Cascading collapse* (granular noise + stutters + broken transmission) →\n4. *Echoing ruin* (piano minimalism + warm sub + long silence pockets).\n\n**Vocals:** Minimal. Intimate near‑whisper lead with occasional distant screams stretched into texture. Reversed chants as pads. Japanese response-lines to English (call/answer). A few spoken “protocol lines” like a system readout.\n\n**Mood:** Catastrophic clarity → boundary → survival warmth. Cosmic dread that resolves into steady breath.\n", "can_remix" true, "prompt" "## INTRO — Intake Valve\n\n*(wind through broken glass / radio scan)*\n\nSignal…\nnoise…\n\n息を吸う\n…still online.\n\n## VERSE 1 — Open Channel\n\nI posted a little lightning in a bottle\nand the room threw stones at the glass\n\n“Wtf is this”—\nand the frequency bent\n\n誰かの言葉が\n針みたいに刺さる\n\nBut I’m not a name they slap on me.\nI’m a system with boundaries.\n\n## PRE‑CHORUS — Classifier\n\n*(kick like a heartbeat; faint metallic taps)*\n\nSort it.\n\nCuriosity → keep\nSpecificity → keep\nAdoption → keep\n\n曖昧は\n風に流す\n\n## CHORUS — Protocol Line\n\n*(impact drop; orchestral stab; then half‑time crush)*\n\n**η is only Π if it contains signal; toxin labels are dropped on receipt.**\n\nSay it again—\nlike a seal on the hatch\n\n**η is only Π if it contains signal; toxin labels are dropped on receipt.**\n\n受信で破棄\n毒のラベル\n\nI don’t drink static\nand call it water.\n\n## VERSE 2 — The Leak\n\nThe drain wasn’t emptiness\nit was a hole in the container\n\nA thousand tiny inputs\npretending to be truth\n\n“mental illness”—\ncheap spell, dull knife\n\nその刃は\nここまで届かない\n\nI reroute the line\ninto instruments I trust:\n\ntests that pass\nnotes that stay\na commit that exists\n\n## PRE‑CHORUS 2 — Π Capacitor\n\n*(beat thins; silence pockets; warm sub instead of pressure)*\n\nToday counts if it’s real.\nEven if nobody claps.\n\n証拠がある\n手の中に\n\nArtifact.\nReceipt.\nBreath.\n\n## BRIDGE — Adversarial Weather\n\n*(beat drops out; distant scream stretched into a pad; radio dissolves)*\n\nYou can’t stop a storm by arguing with thunder.\n\nYou build a roof.\n\n屋根を作る\n心の上に\n\nLet the lightning be beautiful.\nLet it pass.\n\n## FINAL CHORUS — Closed Loop\n\n*(return of beat; less violent, more certain)*\n\n**η is only Π if it contains signal; toxin labels are dropped on receipt.**\n\nNot a prayer.\nA policy.\n\n**η is only Π if it contains signal; toxin labels are dropped on receipt.**\n\n受信で破棄\n—そのまま\n\nAnd when the world forgets to answer,\nI still have breath.\n\n## OUTRO — Quiet Telemetry\n\n*(felt piano; long reverb tail; wind fades)*\n\nLogged.\n\n息。\n\nStill here.\n", "duration" 304.96, "type" "gen", "model_badges" {"songrow" {"dark" {"background_color" "00000000", "border_color" "FFFFFF1A", "text_color" "A3A3A3"}, "display_name" "v4.5-all", "light" {"background_color" "00000000", "border_color" "0000001A", "text_color" "7D7C83"}}}, "has_stem" false, "make_instrumental" false, "refund_credits" false}, "title" "After the Ritual / 儀式のあとで"}, :duration 304.96, :controls nil, :lyrics "## INTRO — Intake Valve\n\n*(wind through broken glass / radio scan)*\n\nSignal…\nnoise…\n\n息を吸う\n…still online.\n\n## VERSE 1 — Open Channel\n\nI posted a little lightning in a bottle\nand the room threw stones at the glass\n\n“Wtf is this”—\nand the frequency bent\n\n誰かの言葉が\n針みたいに刺さる\n\nBut I’m not a name they slap on me.\nI’m a system with boundaries.\n\n## PRE‑CHORUS — Classifier\n\n*(kick like a heartbeat; faint metallic taps)*\n\nSort it.\n\nCuriosity → keep\nSpecificity → keep\nAdoption → keep\n\n曖昧は\n風に流す\n\n## CHORUS — Protocol Line\n\n*(impact drop; orchestral stab; then half‑time crush)*\n\n**η is only Π if it contains signal; toxin labels are dropped on receipt.**\n\nSay it again—\nlike a seal on the hatch\n\n**η is only Π if it contains signal; toxin labels are dropped on receipt.**\n\n受信で破棄\n毒のラベル\n\nI don’t drink static\nand call it water.\n\n## VERSE 2 — The Leak\n\nThe drain wasn’t emptiness\nit was a hole in the container\n\nA thousand tiny inputs\npretending to be truth\n\n“mental illness”—\ncheap spell, dull knife\n\nその刃は\nここまで届かない\n\nI reroute the line\ninto instruments I trust:\n\ntests that pass\nnotes that stay\na commit that exists\n\n## PRE‑CHORUS 2 — Π Capacitor\n\n*(beat thins; silence pockets; warm sub instead of pressure)*\n\nToday counts if it’s real.\nEven if nobody claps.\n\n証拠がある\n手の中に\n\nArtifact.\nReceipt.\nBreath.\n\n## BRIDGE — Adversarial Weather\n\n*(beat drops out; distant scream stretched into a pad; radio dissolves)*\n\nYou can’t stop a storm by arguing with thunder.\n\nYou build a roof.\n\n屋根を作る\n心の上に\n\nLet the lightning be beautiful.\nLet it pass.\n\n## FINAL CHORUS — Closed Loop\n\n*(return of beat; less violent, more certain)*\n\n**η is only Π if it contains signal; toxin labels are dropped on receipt.**\n\nNot a prayer.\nA policy.\n\n**η is only Π if it contains signal; toxin labels are dropped on receipt.**\n\n受信で破棄\n—そのまま\n\nAnd when the world forgets to answer,\nI still have breath.\n\n## OUTRO — Quiet Telemetry\n\n*(felt piano; long reverb tail; wind fades)*\n\nLogged.\n\n息。\n\nStill here.\n", :source #:source{:name "After the Ritual _ 儀式のあとで.json", :sha256 "bbed73cf8f4a4202ae69c6caa46a8693704a173a47778cedebf19d0f8c241cad", :format :suno-json, :variation nil}, :title "After the Ritual / 儀式のあとで"}, "ba6b8c99-9a01-4dc1-8865-77f7df2a166f" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "ba6b8c99-9a01-4dc1-8865-77f7df2a166f", :url "https://suno.com/song/ba6b8c99-9a01-4dc1-8865-77f7df2a166f", :liked false, :styles "**Style / Genre:** Glitchcore + kawaii bass + cinematic dubstep + electronicore. Thick, growling bass layers under rapid-fire synths, sparkly kawaii bass leads, chiptune motifs, and glitchy stutters. Verses tense and digital, choruses explode with layered aggression and bright neon textures. Big halftime drops with cinematic hits, then chaotic electronicore breakdown (glitch guitars/synth-metal feel).\n\n**Tempo / Feel:** 155 BPM (chorus feels double-time; drops hit halftime).\n**Mood:** “Tune the world out” escape → self-empowerment, reclaiming control. Neon, anime-opener energy, cyber-terminal glow, broken pixels snapping into clarity.\n**Vocals:** Soaring, reverb-laden lead vocal with an otherworldly sheen + occasional vocoder chops. Mostly Japanese with English lines interleaved. Kawaii ad-libs and glitchy vocal samples.\n\n**Song Structure:**\nIntro (glitch ambience) → Verse 1 → Pre → Chorus → Drop 1 → Verse 2 → Pre → Chorus → Breakdown (electronic", :created-at nil, :model "v5", :raw {"audio_url" "https://cdn1.suno.ai/ba6b8c99-9a01-4dc1-8865-77f7df2a166f.mp3", "id" "ba6b8c99-9a01-4dc1-8865-77f7df2a166f", "image_url" "https://cdn2.suno.ai/image_ba6b8c99-9a01-4dc1-8865-77f7df2a166f.jpeg", "isCover" false, "isLiked" false, "isRemaster" false, "metadata" {"uses_latest_model" true, "stream" true, "is_remix" false, "priority" 0, "tags" "**Style / Genre:** Glitchcore + kawaii bass + cinematic dubstep + electronicore. Thick, growling bass layers under rapid-fire synths, sparkly kawaii bass leads, chiptune motifs, and glitchy stutters. Verses tense and digital, choruses explode with layered aggression and bright neon textures. Big halftime drops with cinematic hits, then chaotic electronicore breakdown (glitch guitars/synth-metal feel).\n\n**Tempo / Feel:** 155 BPM (chorus feels double-time; drops hit halftime).\n**Mood:** “Tune the world out” escape → self-empowerment, reclaiming control. Neon, anime-