dsound_lullaby_part41_78bpm(4).json", :sha256 "5b0b7feb7f16dc97da3871d465957c8cce94bb01f7c8ad410d8c84fb9aa73fff", :format :suno-json, :variation 4}, :title "ημ_worldsound_lullaby_part41_78bpm"}, "bbfecdba-3702-4f77-862c-e2180fe60772" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "bbfecdba-3702-4f77-862c-e2180fe60772", :url "https://suno.com/song/bbfecdba-3702-4f77-862c-e2180fe60772", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "bbfecdba-3702-4f77-862c-e2180fe60772", "metadata" {"prompt" "# 🎤 **“Don’t Blame the Whole Crowd”**\n\n*(lo-fi protest rap / spoken word — calm, steady beat)*\n\n**[Intro – spoken]**\nYeah…\nDiscord philosophers at 5 PM again.\nSame fight, different server.\nSame old loop.\n\n**[Verse 1]**\nEverybody got a hot take, keyboard flame,\nTurn a whole group into a punchline name.\nOne bad headline, whole culture blamed,\nThen we wonder why the whole damn chat’s inflamed.\n\nHistory echoes in the words we drop,\nYou think it's just slang but the meaning don’t stop.\nEvery insult got a shadow it drags,\nLike smoke in the room when the powder keg cracks.\n\nI ain’t here to censor, I ain’t here to preach,\nJust tired of watching every convo breach.\nWe start with AI, trials, code, and the stack,\nTen minutes later it’s identity attacks.\n\n**[Chorus]**\nDon’t blame the whole crowd for the sins of a few,\nThat’s the oldest bad logic the world ever knew.\nIf you want a real fight, bring facts to the floor—\nNot a lazy old stereotype war.\n\nDon’t blame the whole crowd, that road’s been walked,\nEvery empire burned where that logic talked.\nWe can argue all night, we can disagree loud—\nJust don’t blame the whole damn crowd.\n\n**[Verse 2]**\nYou say it’s just a word, just slang, just a joke,\nBut language got history tied in the smoke.\nMeanings evolve but scars still remain,\nLike graffiti on walls after decades of rain.\n\nYou wanna roast companies? Cool, I’m in,\nCriticize power, that’s where we begin.\nBut when blame starts drifting to blood or a name,\nThat’s where the signal dissolves into flame.\n\nSee the real debate’s buried under the noise,\nSame tired bait with the same tired toys.\nEverybody swinging but nobody scores,\nJust the echo of keyboards and rhetorical wars.\n\n**[Chorus]**\nDon’t blame the whole crowd for the sins of a few,\nThat’s the oldest bad logic the world ever knew.\nIf you want a real fight, bring facts to the floor—\nNot a lazy old stereotype war.\n\nDon’t blame the whole crowd, that road’s been walked,\nEvery empire burned where that logic talked.\nWe can argue all night, we can disagree loud—\nJust don’t blame the whole damn crowd.\n\n**[Bridge – spoken]**\nLook…\nYou can hate a policy.\nYou can hate a company.\nYou can hate a government.\n\nBut when you start hating a whole people…\nYou’re not arguing anymore.\n\nYou’re just lighting matches.\n\n**[Verse 3]**\nSo step back, breathe, let the static clear,\nNot every disagreement needs a spear.\nWe’re all just ghosts in a server at night,\nTrying to make sense of a world in a fight.\n\nArgue the system, the rules, the machine,\nThe policies written behind the screen.\nThat’s a battle worth fighting, that’s ground worth loud—\nJust don’t blame the whole damn crowd.\n\n**[Outro – quiet]**\nSame server tomorrow.\nDifferent argument.\nHopefully… better signal. 🎧", "tags" nil}, "title" "Don’t Blame the Whole Crowd”"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "# 🎤 **“Don’t Blame the Whole Crowd”**\n\n*(lo-fi protest rap / spoken word — calm, steady beat)*\n\n**[Intro – spoken]**\nYeah…\nDiscord philosophers at 5 PM again.\nSame fight, different server.\nSame old loop.\n\n**[Verse 1]**\nEverybody got a hot take, keyboard flame,\nTurn a whole group into a punchline name.\nOne bad headline, whole culture blamed,\nThen we wonder why the whole damn chat’s inflamed.\n\nHistory echoes in the words we drop,\nYou think it's just slang but the meaning don’t stop.\nEvery insult got a shadow it drags,\nLike smoke in the room when the powder keg cracks.\n\nI ain’t here to censor, I ain’t here to preach,\nJust tired of watching every convo breach.\nWe start with AI, trials, code, and the stack,\nTen minutes later it’s identity attacks.\n\n**[Chorus]**\nDon’t blame the whole crowd for the sins of a few,\nThat’s the oldest bad logic the world ever knew.\nIf you want a real fight, bring facts to the floor—\nNot a lazy old stereotype war.\n\nDon’t blame the whole crowd, that road’s been walked,\nEvery empire burned where that logic talked.\nWe can argue all night, we can disagree loud—\nJust don’t blame the whole damn crowd.\n\n**[Verse 2]**\nYou say it’s just a word, just slang, just a joke,\nBut language got history tied in the smoke.\nMeanings evolve but scars still remain,\nLike graffiti on walls after decades of rain.\n\nYou wanna roast companies? Cool, I’m in,\nCriticize power, that’s where we begin.\nBut when blame starts drifting to blood or a name,\nThat’s where the signal dissolves into flame.\n\nSee the real debate’s buried under the noise,\nSame tired bait with the same tired toys.\nEverybody swinging but nobody scores,\nJust the echo of keyboards and rhetorical wars.\n\n**[Chorus]**\nDon’t blame the whole crowd for the sins of a few,\nThat’s the oldest bad logic the world ever knew.\nIf you want a real fight, bring facts to the floor—\nNot a lazy old stereotype war.\n\nDon’t blame the whole crowd, that road’s been walked,\nEvery empire burned where that logic talked.\nWe can argue all night, we can disagree loud—\nJust don’t blame the whole damn crowd.\n\n**[Bridge – spoken]**\nLook…\nYou can hate a policy.\nYou can hate a company.\nYou can hate a government.\n\nBut when you start hating a whole people…\nYou’re not arguing anymore.\n\nYou’re just lighting matches.\n\n**[Verse 3]**\nSo step back, breathe, let the static clear,\nNot every disagreement needs a spear.\nWe’re all just ghosts in a server at night,\nTrying to make sense of a world in a fight.\n\nArgue the system, the rules, the machine,\nThe policies written behind the screen.\nThat’s a battle worth fighting, that’s ground worth loud—\nJust don’t blame the whole damn crowd.\n\n**[Outro – quiet]**\nSame server tomorrow.\nDifferent argument.\nHopefully… better signal. 🎧", :source #:source{:name "Don’t Blame the Whole Crowd” (1).txt", :sha256 "773b91813a63c0574f0ad1c31bfc54c884387e4dd395abd3882c6389a9fc6c09", :format :suno-text, :variation 1}, :title "Don’t Blame the Whole Crowd”"}, "bc970ad7-d138-4936-90bb-831e0a77cf42" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "bc970ad7-d138-4936-90bb-831e0a77cf42", :url "https://suno.com/song/bc970ad7-d138-4936-90bb-831e0a77cf42", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "bc970ad7-d138-4936-90bb-831e0a77cf42", "metadata" {"prompt" "```\n[INTRO — Zero Logic State]\n(The mechanical click pattern starts: uneven, dry, dragging)\n(A low, deep water pressure hum vibrates the lower jaw)\n:: core_clock : uncoupled ::\n:: trajectory : non_terminating ::\n\n```\n\n### Verse 1\n\n**WARDEN**\n*(Low, conversational tone; dry right channel)*\nThey are looking at the current layout... and calling it a crisis.\nThey think the damage is something they can fence off with an incident report.\nBut they don’t know how much of the frame has already turned to salt.\nThe engine didn't hit a wall.\nIt just... forgot how to return the value.\nThe next six months will test the wire.\nEvery clean presentation, every automated sync...\nWe are going to find out what happens when you run out of plaster to patch the sink.\n\n**RITSU**\n*(Distant, center pan; raw tape hiss)*\n進み続ける、影。\n*(The shadow that keeps moving forward.)*\n\n---\n\n### [The Horizon Hook]\n\n*(A single felt piano note drops—D1, deadened with a thick cloth damper)*\n*(Fractured choir dust drifts through the mid-range and drops instantly)*\n\n**WARDEN**\n*(With a flat, restrained melodic ache; no theatrical surge)*\nThe Event was never a single date on the chart.\nIt was a slow leak inside the sovereign room.\nA world that barely survived...\nLimping through the city, trading titles for a wire.\nAnd the most expensive part of the failure...\nIs that they think the floor is still solid.\n\n---\n\n### Verse 2\n\n*(Bowed metal scrapes create a high, glassy overtone that mimics an ungrounded ground loop)*\n*(Detuned warning chimes strike on the off-beats, flat and unresolving)*\n\n**WARDEN**\n*(Intimate proximity; steady delivery)*\nI walked the lower conduits while the city was sleeping.\nNo one is checking the ledger.\nThey are just copying the old entries to save on the transaction fees.\nThe disaster already completed its first pass.\nSilently.\nWithout a siren.\nWithout a change in the executive summary.\nNow we just watch the modern engine try to render the ghost of a market.\n\n**RITSU**\n*(Breathless, left channel)*\n誰も、気づかない。\n*(Nobody notices.)*\n\n---\n\n### [Stabilization Protocol]\n\n*(All percussion and sub-bass drop instantly. Three seconds of absolute silence, leaving only the dry hum of the microphone element.)*\n\n**WARDEN**\n*(Spoken flatly; lucid overwhelm)*\nYou know it could still hit your sector.\nYou stand under the clear sky and watch the line blink to the east.\nBut there is a specific kind of grace...\nIn knowing exactly when the system stopped caring about your recovery.\nSo you stop being polite to the display.\nYou let the screen drop.\nYou hold the edge with your own hands.\n\n---\n\n### [Outro]\n\n*(The sub-bass returns as a low, suffocating rumble, mimicking cathedral gears locking beneath the floor)*\n*(The asymmetrical clicks slow down, skipping beats as the voltage fails)*\n\n**WARDEN**\nSix months.\nLet the layout fall.\nWe don't need the summary...\nTo know we are already standing in the remainder.\n\n*(A single detuned chime rings out, dissolving into an unhandled static rinse before a hard digital gate shuts it down.)*\n\n```\n:: event_state : continuous ::\n:: modern_engine : unaligned ::\n:: human_presence : active_at_the_edge ::\n\n```", "tags" nil}, "title" "Incident Report Fence"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "```\n[INTRO — Zero Logic State]\n(The mechanical click pattern starts: uneven, dry, dragging)\n(A low, deep water pressure hum vibrates the lower jaw)\n:: core_clock : uncoupled ::\n:: trajectory : non_terminating ::\n\n```\n\n### Verse 1\n\n**WARDEN**\n*(Low, conversational tone; dry right channel)*\nThey are looking at the current layout... and calling it a crisis.\nThey think the damage is something they can fence off with an incident report.\nBut they don’t know how much of the frame has already turned to salt.\nThe engine didn't hit a wall.\nIt just... forgot how to return the value.\nThe next six months will test the wire.\nEvery clean presentation, every automated sync...\nWe are going to find out what happens when you run out of plaster to patch the sink.\n\n**RITSU**\n*(Distant, center pan; raw tape hiss)*\n進み続ける、影。\n*(The shadow that keeps moving forward.)*\n\n---\n\n### [The Horizon Hook]\n\n*(A single felt piano note drops—D1, deadened with a thick cloth damper)*\n*(Fractured choir dust drifts through the mid-range and drops instantly)*\n\n**WARDEN**\n*(With a flat, restrained melodic ache; no theatrical surge)*\nThe Event was never a single date on the chart.\nIt was a slow leak inside the sovereign room.\nA world that barely survived...\nLimping through the city, trading titles for a wire.\nAnd the most expensive part of the failure...\nIs that they think the floor is still solid.\n\n---\n\n### Verse 2\n\n*(Bowed metal scrapes create a high, glassy overtone that mimics an ungrounded ground loop)*\n*(Detuned warning chimes strike on the off-beats, flat and unresolving)*\n\n**WARDEN**\n*(Intimate proximity; steady delivery)*\nI walked the lower conduits while the city was sleeping.\nNo one is checking the ledger.\nThey are just copying the old entries to save on the transaction fees.\nThe disaster already completed its first pass.\nSilently.\nWithout a siren.\nWithout a change in the executive summary.\nNow we just watch the modern engine try to render the ghost of a market.\n\n**RITSU**\n*(Breathless, left channel)*\n誰も、気づかない。\n*(Nobody notices.)*\n\n---\n\n### [Stabilization Protocol]\n\n*(All percussion and sub-bass drop instantly. Three seconds of absolute silence, leaving only the dry hum of the microphone element.)*\n\n**WARDEN**\n*(Spoken flatly; lucid overwhelm)*\nYou know it could still hit your sector.\nYou stand under the clear sky and watch the line blink to the east.\nBut there is a specific kind of grace...\nIn knowing exactly when the system stopped caring about your recovery.\nSo you stop being polite to the display.\nYou let the screen drop.\nYou hold the edge with your own hands.\n\n---\n\n### [Outro]\n\n*(The sub-bass returns as a low, suffocating rumble, mimicking cathedral gears locking beneath the floor)*\n*(The asymmetrical clicks slow down, skipping beats as the voltage fails)*\n\n**WARDEN**\nSix months.\nLet the layout fall.\nWe don't need the summary...\nTo know we are already standing in the remainder.\n\n*(A single detuned chime rings out, dissolving into an unhandled static rinse before a hard digital gate shuts it down.)*\n\n```\n:: event_state : continuous ::\n:: modern_engine : unaligned ::\n:: human_presence : active_at_the_edge ::\n\n```", :source #:source{:name "Incident Report Fence (2).txt", :sha256 "332bded8e8204d130de8e627547726dea9ca360330c3b9b8056a6f34e9510e0b", :format :suno-text, :variation 2}, :title "Incident Report Fence"}, "bc9cbba8-4ceb-4d5c-a618-fcea9e61ead7" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "bc9cbba8-4ceb-4d5c-a618-fcea9e61ead7", :url "https://suno.com/song/bc9cbba8-4ceb-4d5c-a618-fcea9e61ead7", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "bc9cbba8-4ceb-4d5c-a618-fcea9e61ead7", "metadata" {"prompt" "[Instrumental]", "tags" nil}, "title" "Broken Brass Circuit"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "[Instrumental]", :source #:source{:name "Broken Brass Circuit (1