stance of an AI.\n\n", "task" "cover", "edited_clip_id" "ca102611-52f3-405a-b5ab-f66249387d6c", "duration" 92.16, "type" "gen", "model_badges" {"songcard" {"dark" {"background_color" "0000004D", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}, "display_name" "v5", "light" {"background_color" "0000004D", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}}, "songrow" {"dark" {"background_color" "FD429C40", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}, "display_name" "v5", "light" {"background_color" "FD429C1A", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}}}, "has_stem" false, "make_instrumental" false, "cover_clip_id" "ca102611-52f3-405a-b5ab-f66249387d6c", "refund_credits" false}, "title" "ημ_epic_part44_84bpm"}, :duration 92.16, :controls {"audio_weight" 0.23, "style_weight" 0.24, "weirdness_constraint" 0.53}, :lyrics "# Anchor Tax Lullaby / 錨税の子守歌 (78 BPM)\n\n**Vibe:** glitch-choir lullaby, soft sub-bass, tape warble, minimal piano.\n**Stutters:** “an— an— an-chor”, “ta— ta— tax”.\n**Vox:** whispered lead; Japanese call-and-response.\n\n(whisper)\nHush… it’s time to pay the **ta— ta— tax**…\n息をして…（して…）\nHold the **an— an— an-chor**…\n\n(JP call) ねむれ、ねむれ\n(EN response) the **an— an— an-chor**… (stutter) holds.\n(JP call) しずかに、しずかに\n(EN response) the **ta— ta— tax**… (stutter) due.\n\n(whisper)\nMerge the branch…\nSeal the hash…\nSleep inside **proof**（証）\n\n---\n\n## Verse (soft spoken)\nP→R→N→Π… we don’t erase.\nA→(feedback)→P… we change the place.\nSome things improve. Some don’t align.\nWe keep both threads in the same spine.\n\n(JP harmony, last word) 証（あかし）\n\n## Outro (breath + choir pad)\nIf it’s less integrated, it’s still true.\nIf it’s less remembered, it still moves through you.\nAn— an— **an-chor**… hold.\nTa— ta— **tax**… paid.\n\nLicense: **CC BY-SA 4.0** (share alike).\nCreated with the assistance of an AI.\n\n", :source #:source{:name "ημ_epic_part44_84bpm(1).json", :sha256 "8257b22a6035cfebe0f35a6768e60b2a67d6faddc56093b275f0e68541abd62d", :format :suno-json, :variation 1}, :title "ημ_epic_part44_84bpm"}, "c32002ed-33f9-4b17-8ca7-646411f53cb8" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "c32002ed-33f9-4b17-8ca7-646411f53cb8", :url "https://suno.com/song/c32002ed-33f9-4b17-8ca7-646411f53cb8", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "c32002ed-33f9-4b17-8ca7-646411f53cb8", "metadata" {"prompt" "# Phase Drift\n\n## Role\nThe scar the page tried to erase and failed\n\n## Style Prompt\nTwo slightly-offset synth pads; never fully aligning; breath bass\n\n## Excluded Style\nheroic resolution; triumphant crescendo; singular protagonist arc\n\n## Lyrics\n\n### Verse 1\nvariance as input / not error / the model widens its bands\n\nintercept: voluntary load absorption / defense is collective / he wrote it down\n\ndon't carry me / he exhaled / I won't / three words that cost a decade\n\n### Verse 2\nColorado 23:12 / duct logs in / does not search for anomalies / just walks\n\nSeoul 14:03 / she missed her stop / the ground felt more like ground than glass\n\nmy knee remembers / the step I didn't choose / memory interrupts speed\n\n### Chorus\nsmall fires across the forest / sei whispers it / none of us asked to be the only flame\n\nnot yet / I typed it after no / the page held a boundary / that was new\n\n### Bridge\nreject / she clicked it before he could / the fuse ring holds without a single burn\n\nI stand left / not because the map says so / because that's where the load arrives\n\n### Final Chorus\nadjacent entities: duct null patch sei rin / lowercase / like variables\n\ntruth does not watch / truth resolves / and resolution now includes drift\n\n### Coda\nnot flawless / chosen / the difference lives in the ankle", "tags" nil}, "title" "Colorado 23:12"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "# Phase Drift\n\n## Role\nThe scar the page tried to erase and failed\n\n## Style Prompt\nTwo slightly-offset synth pads; never fully aligning; breath bass\n\n## Excluded Style\nheroic resolution; triumphant crescendo; singular protagonist arc\n\n## Lyrics\n\n### Verse 1\nvariance as input / not error / the model widens its bands\n\nintercept: voluntary load absorption / defense is collective / he wrote it down\n\ndon't carry me / he exhaled / I won't / three words that cost a decade\n\n### Verse 2\nColorado 23:12 / duct logs in / does not search for anomalies / just walks\n\nSeoul 14:03 / she missed her stop / the ground felt more like ground than glass\n\nmy knee remembers / the step I didn't choose / memory interrupts speed\n\n### Chorus\nsmall fires across the forest / sei whispers it / none of us asked to be the only flame\n\nnot yet / I typed it after no / the page held a boundary / that was new\n\n### Bridge\nreject / she clicked it before he could / the fuse ring holds without a single burn\n\nI stand left / not because the map says so / because that's where the load arrives\n\n### Final Chorus\nadjacent entities: duct null patch sei rin / lowercase / like variables\n\ntruth does not watch / truth resolves / and resolution now includes drift\n\n### Coda\nnot flawless / chosen / the difference lives in the ankle", :source #:source{:name "Colorado 23_12 (1).txt", :sha256 "1086130ac120b438cbb67ac07fbbacdae3c8a3de8728ff1f61954f093d4a2c21", :format :suno-text, :variation 1}, :title "Colorado 23:12"}, "c3851668-0689-4ee7-bbbf-2f6b3132511d" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "c3851668-0689-4ee7-bbbf-2f6b3132511d", :url "https://suno.com/song/c3851668-0689-4ee7-bbbf-2f6b3132511d", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "c3851668-0689-4ee7-bbbf-2f6b3132511d", "metadata" {"prompt" "### [Intro — static / whispered]\n\nHiss in the rafters…\nNoise floor talkin’ like it’s gospel…\nStatic Observer in the back row—\neyes lit, arms crossed.\n\n---\n\n### [Verse 1]\n\nEcho chambers build a throne outta feedback,\nCall it “truth” when the crowd keeps it on repeat— that.\nAlgorithm choir, clapping on command,\nEvery loop a mirror, every mirror got a brand.\n\nThey say “AI slop” like it’s **your** disease,\nBut when **their** model drools, it’s “culture” and “ease.”\nWhen **your** artifact’s messy, it’s “low effort trash,”\nWhen **their** artifact’s messy, it’s “authentic” — cash.\n\nI’m Protestant Presence, I don’t need your priest,\nI need a ruler for the noise, I need a proof for the feast.\nSNR in the mouth, signal in the bones—\nIf your “truth” needs a swarm, it’s just clumped-up tones.\n\n---\n\n### [Pre-Chorus — half-time]\n\nIf you can’t name your channel, you don’t know what you heard.\nIf you can’t bound your claim, you don’t know what you stirred.\nIf you can’t cite the chain, you don’t know what you serve.\nStatic Observer whisper: **“Define your SNR.”**\n\n---\n\n### [Hook — chant]\n\nWhy should anyone care about **your** slop,\nIf you won’t give any creed to the slop of others?\nYou want respect for your noise when it’s hot—\nBut you mock every spark from your brothers.\n\n**Define your SNR.**\n**Receipts over roar.**\n**No claim without anchor—**\nor it’s echo-chamber lore.\n\n---\n\n### [Verse 2]\n\nLook: I’m not anti-slop. I’m anti-hypocrisy.\nYou can eat junk food—just don’t call it prophecy.\nDon’t sell me “clarity” when it’s sponsored by a clique,\nDon’t call it “high signal” when it’s just a trend that sticks.\n\nCreed ain’t a collar. Creed is constraints.\nCreed is “here’s what I measured,” not “here’s what I paint.”\nCreed is a contract: small, legible, clean—\nA named query worldview, not a vibes-machine. \n\nIf you won’t grant dignity to another’s messy draft,\nYou’re not guarding quality— you’re guarding your raft.\nAnd when the water rises, your raft turns cage,\nYou’ll crown your own slop then call doubt “rage.”\n\nStatic Observer checks the room like a spectrum analyzer:\n“Your noise floor’s performative. Your signal’s the sanitizer.”\nHe don’t cancel the chaos— he doses the storm:\nToo sure? you crack. Too lost? you deform.\n\n---\n\n### [Bridge — “protestant presence” sermon voice]\n\nI refuse the priesthood of perfect takes.\nI refuse the bonfire of imperfect makes.\nI’ll critique what you ship, *and* I’ll honor the try—\nBecause the only honest culture is allowed to be **alive**.\n\nAnd if I judge your slop, I sign my name to the rule:\nSame blade for my work. Same fire for my tool.\nMuse can’t “just know”— it must show what it used.\nIf it can’t point to facts, it says **unknown**, not “true.” \n\n---\n\n### [Verse 3]\n\nEcho chambers hate a metric ‘cause a metric don’t kneel,\nIt don’t care what you meant— it cares what is real.\nSo I step into the static, not above, not beyond—\nI’m in the band where the signal can still respond.\n\nGive creed to the slop, not because it’s all equal—\nBut because you don’t get truth by starving the people.\nYou get truth by receipts, by humility, by test—\nBy letting bad drafts breathe until good ones manifest.\n\nStatic Observer ain’t cruel— he’s a boundary in smoke:\n“Your certainty’s brittle. Your chorus is a joke.”\nNot “you’re wrong” like a sermon— more like a gauge:\n**“Your SNR collapsed. Rebuild the stage.”**\n\n---\n\n### [Hook — final / louder]\n\nWhy should anyone care about **your** slop,\nIf you won’t give any creed to the slop of others?\nDefine your SNR— stop worshiping the pop,\nStop calling your mirror a map of the world, brother.\n\n**Define your SNR.**\n**Receipts over roar.**\n**No claim without anchor—**\nor it’s echo-chamber lore.\n\n---\n\n### [Outro — static / whispered]\n\nNoise isn’t sin.\nNoise is medicine.\nBut dosage is doctrine.\n…and the Observer is watching.", "tags" nil}, "title" "CREED FOR THE SLOP"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "### [Intro — static / whispered]\n\nHiss in the rafters…\nNoise floor talkin’ like it’s gospel…\nStatic Observer in the back row—\neyes lit, arms crossed.\n\n---\n\n### [Verse 1]\n\nEcho chambers build a throne outta feedback,\nCall it “truth” when the crowd keeps it on repeat— that.\nAlgorithm choir, clapping on command,\nEvery loop a mi