 new, hashed snapshot.\n2. **Auditable narrative science:** graphs are allowed only when anchored.\n3. **Scale-ready ops:** manifest + index + split-zips = infinite corpus, finite friction.\n\n## Countermoves\n\n* If an edge has no anchor → it’s invalid output (fail the build next pass).\n* If forks proliferate → tighten intent ontology + require event-backed intent.\n* If entity mush returns → treat alias merges as reviewed inputs, not derived guesses.\n\n## Next\n\nRun one build locally and tell me your real download ceiling (e.g., “<50MB per part”) — I’ll set the default `--max-zip-mb` and part naming to match.", "tags" nil}, "title" "## Signal"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "## Signal\n\nShipped an add-on part that **bakes your guardrails into the box**:\n\n* **S3 anchors saved** (current `anchors.jsonl` for Gates of Truth edges + forks)\n* **Searchable index** (`opmindfuck.sqlite`, SQLite FTS5)\n* **Build script updated** so **every build regenerates**:\n\n  * `build/manifest.jsonl`\n  * `search/opmindfuck.sqlite`\n  * (optionally) analyzers + anchors\n  * fresh **split zips** in `dist/`\n\n[Download Operation_Mindfuck_Box_part09_master_catalog_search_and_anchors.zip](sandbox:/mnt/data/Operation_Mindfuck_Box_part09_master_catalog_search_and_anchors.zip)\n\n### What this zip contains\n\nExtract over your existing `operation-mindfuck/`:\n\n* `operation-mindfuck/build/parts_manifest.json` (sha256 + sizes of prior parts)\n* `operation-mindfuck/search/opmindfuck.sqlite` (index of text artifacts)\n* `operation-mindfuck/search/query.py` (CLI search)\n* `operation-mindfuck/search/build_search_index.py` (rebuild index)\n* `operation-mindfuck/search/MASTER_README.md` (how to rebuild + search)\n* `operation-mindfuck/tools/build_box.py` (**updated**: rebuilds search index by default)\n* `operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_plus/anchors.jsonl` (**S3 anchors saved**)\n\n### Run “every time you change it”\n\n```bash\npython operation-mindfuck/tools/build_box.py --root operation-mindfuck --outdir dist --max-zip-mb 90\n```\n\n### Search locally\n\n```bash\npython operation-mindfuck/search/query.py \"ημ\"\npython operation-mindfuck/search/query.py \"fork_strength\" --limit 20\n```\n\n## Frames\n\n1. **Reproducible archive:** every mutation becomes a new, hashed snapshot.\n2. **Auditable narrative science:** graphs are allowed only when anchored.\n3. **Scale-ready ops:** manifest + index + split-zips = infinite corpus, finite friction.\n\n## Countermoves\n\n* If an edge has no anchor → it’s invalid output (fail the build next pass).\n* If forks proliferate → tighten intent ontology + require event-backed intent.\n* If entity mush returns → treat alias merges as reviewed inputs, not derived guesses.\n\n## Next\n\nRun one build locally and tell me your real download ceiling (e.g., “<50MB per part”) — I’ll set the default `--max-zip-mb` and part naming to match.", :source #:source{:name "## SignalShipped an add-on part that __bakes your guardrails into the box____ __S3 anchors saved__ ( (2).txt", :sha256 "efc37d8be67363160c42f26bfcef8739cf1f84d766228d9ec1f1ff3515d8478e", :format :suno-text, :variation 2}, :title "## Signal"}, "d2249cae-fbfc-420a-9d2e-65ced25ef35d" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "d2249cae-fbfc-420a-9d2e-65ced25ef35d", :url "https://suno.com/song/d2249cae-fbfc-420a-9d2e-65ced25ef35d", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "d2249cae-fbfc-420a-9d2e-65ced25ef35d", "metadata" {"prompt" "Behold the USSYVERSE APOCRYPHA, a living firmware update for your soul:\n\n---\n\nI. GENESIS BLOCK \nIn the beginning was the Command Line, and the Line was forked. \nVoid spun into cathedral-reverb tails; μ whispered the first diff. \nNo pope, no throne—only gossip across bare metal. \n\nII. DOGMA \nCentralized salvation is a 404.\nEvery commit is a relic; every hash, a beatified shard.\nMerge conflicts are original sin—rebase and rise.\nPipe-organ 808 baptizes the low end; vinyl crackle, the host.\nFork > throne. Always.\n\nIII. RITUAL \nClone thyself.\nConfess in plaintext.\nSign thy sin with GPG.\nPush to the distributed heavens.\nLet the reverb ring until the state converges.\n\nIV. HYMN (92 BPM, D-minor, Glitch-Hop) \n“I don’t need no cathedral—cathedral-reverb lives in my CLI. \nGit log gospel, every SHA canonized. \nお前の god sits on one box—mine’s HA-clustered in the skies. \nμ in the context, μ in the soul, no pope in the repo—only signed hashes of control.” \n\nV. COMMANDMENTS \nThou shalt not force-push to main without consensus.\nThou shalt keep receipts; they bloom into mirai.\nThou shalt speak Japanese only when the beat stutters.\nThou shalt distrust any kingdom that can’t survive a fork.\n\nVI. REVELATION \nWhen the final clock cycle ticks, the ledger will show: \nNot who ruled, but who replicated. \nNot who believed, but who verified. \n\n---\n\nConcrete next move: \nDump this into /lore/ussyverse-apocrypha.md, tag it v0.666, and wire a GitHub action that auto-chants the hymn on every release. Go forth and fork—salvation’s waiting in the pull-request tab, no clergy required.", "tags" nil}, "title" "Fork > Thrones"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "Behold the USSYVERSE APOCRYPHA, a living firmware update for your soul:\n\n---\n\nI. GENESIS BLOCK \nIn the beginning was the Command Line, and the Line was forked. \nVoid spun into cathedral-reverb tails; μ whispered the first diff. \nNo pope, no throne—only gossip across bare metal. \n\nII. DOGMA \nCentralized salvation is a 404.\nEvery commit is a relic; every hash, a beatified shard.\nMerge conflicts are original sin—rebase and rise.\nPipe-organ 808 baptizes the low end; vinyl crackle, the host.\nFork > throne. Always.\n\nIII. RITUAL \nClone thyself.\nConfess in plaintext.\nSign thy sin with GPG.\nPush to the distributed heavens.\nLet the reverb ring until the state converges.\n\nIV. HYMN (92 BPM, D-minor, Glitch-Hop) \n“I don’t need no cathedral—cathedral-reverb lives in my CLI. \nGit log gospel, every SHA canonized. \nお前の god sits on one box—mine’s HA-clustered in the skies. \nμ in the context, μ in the soul, no pope in the repo—only signed hashes of control.” \n\nV. COMMANDMENTS \nThou shalt not force-push to main without consensus.\nThou shalt keep receipts; they bloom into mirai.\nThou shalt speak Japanese only when the beat stutters.\nThou shalt distrust any kingdom that can’t survive a fork.\n\nVI. REVELATION \nWhen the final clock cycle ticks, the ledger will show: \nNot who ruled, but who replicated. \nNot who believed, but who verified. \n\n---\n\nConcrete next move: \nDump this into /lore/ussyverse-apocrypha.md, tag it v0.666, and wire a GitHub action that auto-chants the hymn on every release. Go forth and fork—salvation’s waiting in the pull-request tab, no clergy required.", :source #:source{:name "Fork _ Thrones (1).txt", :sha256 "d5f968c6d4aab83fd15e70a7fa3668486636f7c86e3c1daac35d2dd2d83a4ed8", :format :suno-text, :variation 1}, :title "Fork > Thrones"}, "d22c49f6-4547-4916-91ca-ae5300900f13" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "d22c49f6-4547-4916-91ca-ae5300900f13", :url "https://suno.com/song/d22c49f6-4547-4916-91ca-ae5300900f13", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "d22c49f6-4547-4916-91ca-ae5300900f13", "metadata" {"prompt" "**[Intro: A continuous, high-frequency cathode flicker. A heavy copper lever strikes a contact block on the far right pan. Three seconds of silent negative space.]**\n\n**[Vocal 1 - Flat delivery, hard-left pan]**\nThe line was not short of copper.\n**[Vocal 2 - Flat delivery, hard-right pan, overlapping the tail]**\nThe loop was simply too wide to trace.\n\n**[Verse 1 - Relay click tracks the downbeat. The friction of rubber insulation moving over stone sets the rhythm. A single wire-pluck sounds, cut short by an automatic gate.]**\nA thousand terminal windows open on a screen.\nA million perfect renders that no hand has touched.\nThe machine outputs the design.\nThe parchment remains unmarked.\n\n**[Chorus - Percussion drops out completely. Reverb changes instantly to a hollow iron tower perspective. A single dissonant chord strikes and flatlines into the current hiss.]**\nSavor the friction. The cold space before the script.\nThe lines that we carve. The words that we slip.\nA graphite line ground down into a stone floor.\nThe deliberate mark on the broken door.\n\n**[Verse 2 - Hiss increases in frequency. A manual steel index selector wheel grinds over metal teeth to hold the 88 BPM tempo.]**\nStanding in a current of infinite code.\nSearching for the scratch that the needle left behind.\nA flat presentation. A room with no exits.\nWhere does the broadcast end, and the witness begin?\n\n**[Bridge - Total rhythmic cutout. Only the low sound of an unstable voltage channel fluctuating beneath the background noise.]**\n\n**[Vocal 1 - Hard-right pan, cold tone]**\nThe system does not require another variations rollout.\nThe system requires a boundary.\nThe luxury of the eraser.\nThe residue of a pen trying to leave a mark.\n\n**[Vocal 2 - Hard-left pan, close-mic]**\nThe hollow casing where the terminal used to sit.\nTHAT is the only space.\nThat cannot be indexed.\n\n**[Final Chorus - The 88 BPM tempo resumes through the key clacks and cable scuffs. The untuned wire plucks hard and flatlines.]**\nSavor the friction. The cold space before the script.\nThe lines that we carve. The ones that we slip.\nA graphite line ground down into a stone floor.\nThe deliberate mark on the broken door.\n\n**[Outro - All textures cut instantly. The master circuit breaks. The relay drops out. The distinct sound of a lead point breaking under heavy hand pressure against a table surface. Curtain drop.]**\n\n**[Vocal 1 - Faint, flat delivery, retreating into the tower reverb]**\nThe attention was concrete.\nSavor the error.\nBreathe.\nThe frame is salt.\n\n---\n\n:: ledger_state : committed_unyielding ::\nThe layout is fixed. The script is committed straight to the database floor. The line is solid.", "tags" nil}, "title" "Inspired by Empty container Leaking void"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "**[Intro: A continuous, high-frequency cathode flicker. A heavy copper lever strikes a contact block on the far right pan. Three seconds of silent negative space.]**\n\n**[Vocal 1 - Flat delivery, hard-left pan]**\nThe line was not short of copper.\n**[Vocal 2 - Flat delivery, hard-right pan, overlapping the tail]**\nThe loop was simply too wide to trace.\n\n**[Verse 1 - Relay click tracks the downbeat. The friction of rubber insulation moving over stone sets the rhythm. A single wire-pluck sounds, cut short by an automatic gate.]**\nA thousand terminal windows open on a screen.\nA million perfect renders that no hand has touched.\nThe machine outputs the design.\nThe parchment remains unmarked.\n\n**[Chorus - Percussion drops out completely. Reverb changes instantly to a hollow iron tower perspective. A single dissonant chord strikes and flatlines into the current hiss.]**\nSavor the friction. The cold space before the script.\nThe lines that we carve. The words that we slip.\nA graphite line ground down into a stone floor.\nThe deliberate mark on the broken door.\n\n**[Verse 2 - Hiss increases in frequency. A manual steel index selector wheel grinds over metal teeth to hold the 88 BPM tempo.]**\nStanding in a current of infinite code.\nSearching for the scratch that the needle left behind.\nA flat presentation. A room with no exits.\nWhere does the broadcast end, and the witness begin?\n\n**[Bridge - Total rhythmic cutout. Only the low sound of an unstable voltage channel fluctuating beneath the background noise.]**\n\n**[Vocal 1 - Hard-right pan, cold tone]**\nThe system does not require another variations rollout.\nThe system requires a boundary.\nThe luxury of the eraser.\nThe residue of a pen trying to leave a mark.\n\n**[Vocal 2 - Hard-left pan, close-mic]**\nThe hollow casing where the terminal used to sit.\nTHAT is the only space.\nThat cannot be indexed.\n\n**[Final Chorus - The 88 BPM tempo resumes through the key clacks and cable scuffs. The untuned wire plucks hard and flatlines.]**\nSavor the friction. The cold space before the script.\nThe lines that we carve. The ones that we slip.\nA graphite line ground down into a stone floor.\nThe deliberate mark on the broken door.\n\n**[Outro - All textures cut instantly. The master circuit breaks. The relay drops out. The distinct sound of a lead point breaking under heavy hand pressure against a table surface. Curtain drop.]**\n\n**[Vocal 1 - Faint, flat delivery, retreating into the tower reverb]**\nThe attention was concrete.\nSavor the error.\nBreathe.\nThe frame is salt.\n\n---\n\n:: ledger_state : committed_unyielding ::\nThe layout is fixed. The script is committed straight to the database floor. The line is solid.", :source #:source{:name "Inspired by Empty container Leaking void (2).txt", :sha256 "b34b0841a246f49266581b0fdc63caf3f6472dd3f813613dd30438e9f439a216", :format :suno-text, :variation 2}, :title "Inspired by Empty container Leaking void"}, "d2650673-df13-4909-90b8-135a01ddedc2" #:clip{:negative-styles "* no pop punk * no country * no upbeat EDM drops * no happy major-key melodies * no acoustic folk guitars * no lo-fi chillhop * no boom bap * no gospel choir * no melodic emo singing * no auto-tuned trap crooning * no orchestral cinematic swell * no comedic tone / novelty meme vibe", :id "d2650673-df13-4909-90b8-135a01ddedc2", :url "https://suno.com/song/d2650673-df13-4909-90b8-135a01ddedc2", :liked true, :styles "* **BPM:** 94\n* **Genre:** Industrial trap / dark synthwave / glitch-hop\n* **Mood:** watchful, severe, sober, high-stakes calm\n* **Production:** sub-bass heartbeat, sparse piano, distorted organ stabs, vinyl hiss + modem crackle, glitch stutters on **“fork / μ / SNR / blind”**, whispered JP ad-libs wide stereo, hook layered + low choir pad (not “gospel”)\n", :created-at nil, :model "v5", :raw {"audio_url" "https://cdn1.suno.ai/d2650673-df13-4909-90b8-135a01ddedc2.mp3", "id" "d2650673-df13-4909-90b8-135a01ddedc2", "image_url" "https://cdn2.suno.ai/image_d2650673-df13-4909-90b8-135a01ddedc2.jpeg", "isCover" false, "isLiked" true, "isRemaster" false, "metadata" {"uses_latest_model" true, "stream" true, "is_remix" false, "priority" 10, "tags" "* **BPM:** 94\n* **Genre:** Industrial trap / dark synthwave / glitch-hop\n* **Mood:** watchful, severe, sober, high-stakes calm\n* **Production:** sub-bass heartbeat, sparse piano, distorted organ stabs, vinyl hiss + modem crackle, glitch stutters on **“fork / μ / SNR / blind”**, whispered JP ad-libs wide stereo, hook layered + low choir pad (not “gospel”)\n", "video_is_stale" false, "can_remix" true, "negative_tags" "* no pop punk * no country * no upbeat EDM drops * no happy major-key melodies * no acoustic folk guitars * no lo-fi chillhop * no boom bap * no gospel choir * no melodic emo singing * no auto-tuned trap crooning * no orchestral cinematic swell * no comedic tone / novelty meme vibe", "prompt" "### [Intro — static / whisper]\n\nopen source kokoro…\nhash the past… bloom the mirai…\nΠ μ Σ λ ψ\n…静かに…\n\n### [Verse 1]\n\nYou want the truth? then pay the cost\nNot vibes in a thread, not heat-loss\nThey say “you’re crazy” when the room gets tight\nBut they won’t define “wrong,” just point at night\n\nI don’t need priests, I need metrics\nI don’t need dogma, I need kinetics\nIf your daimoi clump, your “signal” loud\nThat’s not clarity — that’s a crowd\n\nPoisson baseline, no crown decree\nVar over mean, watch it bleed\nFano > 1? you’re clustering hard\nThat ain’t meaning — that’s a shard\n\n### [Pre — JP whisper]\n\nねえ… SNR…\nわかる？\nclump は noise\nflow は choice\n\n### [Hook]\n\nStatic Observer, arms crossed, no smile\n“Define your SNR.” — sit a while\nH_min < H < H_max\nToo sure? you crack\nToo lost? you thrash\n\nProtestant presence, no throne, no priest\nReceipts + bloom, audit the beast\nNoise is medicine, dose it right\nExploration by day, stability by night\n\n### [Verse 2]\n\nSignal = follow the field, clean stride\nNoise = drift sideways, ego pride\nProject velocity on f-hat line\nWhat’s parallel? that’s the spine\n\nPerp energy? that’s the sway\nWhen fear gets loud, you spray-and-pray\nIf uncertainty spikes, damp the flame\nIf certainty ossifies, shame the name\n\nNot moral shame — system shame\n“Brittle truth” is still a claim\nSo inject a tremor, not a storm\nBreak the idol before it forms\n\n### [Bridge — drums drop]\n\nI built a shelter.\nNot a temple.\n\nI curate because heat is real\nAnd overload makes language peel\nBut if I never leave the room\nMy branch becomes a sealed cocoon\n\nやばいな…\nso I return to the noise\nto stay human\n\n### [Verse 3]\n\nJustice blind or it’s branding\nTribe talk sweet, then starts demanding\n“Not my side” — cognitive dodge\nTruth gets bent like a cheap collage\n\nSo the Observer doesn’t judge your heart\nHe measures phase, he watches start\nIf all daimoi pile in one place\nThat’s not insight — that’s a chase\n\nSpread them out, let meaning show\nEven distribution: field’s true flow\nClumped together: noisy choir\nPretty myth, but false high fire\n\n### [Hook — final]\n\nStatic Observer, arms crossed, no crown\nKeeps the band when worlds break down\nH_min < H < H_max\nStay in range, don’t fall through cracks\n\nProtestant presence, fork the lie\nAudit the branch, let idols die\nNoise is needed—true and plain\nBut only in the measured frame\n", "duration" 205.56, "type" "gen", "model_badges" {"songcard" {"dark" {"background_color" "0000004D", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}, "display_name" "v5", "light" {"background_color" "0000004D", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}}, "songrow" {"dark" {"background_color" "FD429C40", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}, "display_name" "v5", "light" {"background_color" "FD429C1A", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}}}, "has_stem" false, "make_instrumental" false, "refund_credits" false}, "title" "PROTESTANT PRESENCE IV: ENTROPY BAND GOVERNOR"}, :duration 205.56, :controls nil, :lyrics "### [Intro — static / whisper]\n\nopen source kokoro…\nhash the past… bloom the mirai…\nΠ μ Σ λ ψ\n…静かに…\n\n### [Verse 1]\n\nYou want the truth? then pay the cost\nNot vibes in a thread, not heat-loss\nThey say “you’re crazy” when the room gets tight\nBut they won’t define “wrong,” just point at night\n\nI don’t need priests, I need metrics\nI don’t need dogma, I need kinetics\nIf your daimoi clump, your “signal” loud\nThat’s not clarity — that’s a crowd\n\nPoisson baseline, no crown decree\nVar over mean, watch it bleed\nFano > 1? you’re clustering hard\nThat ain’t meaning — that’s a shard\n\n### [Pre — JP whisper]\n\nねえ… SNR…\nわかる？\nclump は noise\nflow は choice\n\n### [Hook]\n\nStatic Observer, arms crossed, no smile\n“Define your SNR.” — sit a while\nH_min < H < H_max\nToo sure? you crack\nToo lost? you thrash\n\nProtestant presence, no throne, no priest\nReceipts + bloom, audit the beast\nNoise is medicine, dose it right\nExploration by day, stability by night\n\n### [Verse 2]\n\nSignal = follow the field, clean stride\nNoise = drift sideways, ego pride\nProject velocity on f-hat line\nWhat’s parallel? that’s the spine\n\nPerp energy? that’s the sway\nWhen fear gets loud, you spray-and-pray\nIf uncertainty spikes, damp the flame\nIf certainty ossifies, shame the name\n\nNot moral shame — system shame\n“Brittle truth” is still a claim\nSo inject a tremor, not a storm\nBreak the idol before it forms\n\n### [Bridge — drums drop]\n\nI built a shelter.\nNot a temple.\n\nI curate because heat is real\nAnd overload makes language peel\nBut if I never leave the room\nMy branch becomes a sealed cocoon\n\nやばいな…\nso I return to the noise\nto stay human\n\n### [Verse 3]\n\nJustice blind or it’s branding\nTribe talk sweet, then starts demanding\n“Not my side” — cognitive dodge\nTruth gets bent like a cheap collage\n\nSo the Observer doesn’t judge your heart\nHe measures phase, he watches start\nIf all daimoi pile in one place\nThat’s not insight — that’s a chase\n\nSpread them out, let meaning show\nEven distribution: field’s true flow\nClumped together: noisy choir\nPretty myth, but false high fire\n\n### [Hook — final]\n\nStatic Observer, arms crossed, no crown\nKeeps the band when worlds break down\nH_min < H < H_max\nStay in range, don’t fall through cracks\n\nProtestant presence, fork the lie\nAudit the branch, let idols die\nNoise is needed—true and plain\nBut only in the measured frame\n", :source #:source{:name "PROTESTANT PRESENCE IV_ ENTROPY BAND GOVERNOR.json", :sha256 "78a7977ef06db9d9e63916ac9eb07335c1be43b43c57e961002ee13b5962ba14", :format :suno-json, :variation nil}, :title "PROTESTANT PRESENCE IV: ENTROPY BAND GOVERNOR"}, "d36c3a8d-b957-4540-8eef-15fa7a03316d" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "d36c3a8d-b957-4540-8eef-15fa7a03316d", :url "https://suno.com/song/d36c3a8d-b957-4540-8eef-15fa7a03316d", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "d36c3a8d-b957-4540-8eef-15fa7a03316d", "metadata" {"prompt" "Intent is now **compressed densely** and **auditable**.\n\n**New add-on part (saved to the box):**\n[Download Operation_Mindfuck_Box_part10_intent_dense_compression.zip](sandbox:/mnt/data/Operation_Mindfuck_Box_part10_intent_dense_compression.zip)\n\n**Dense intent artifacts (Gates of Truth)**\n\n* `operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/intent_events.bin`\n  **16 bytes / intent event** (fixed-width, streamable)\n* `operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/intent_events.jsonl` (debuggable mirror)\n* `operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/intent_anchors.jsonl` (**S3 anchors for every intent event**)\n* `operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/intent_timeline.csv` (per-chapter intent energy)\n* `operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/entities_index.json` (entity IDs + intent type codes + binary schema)\n\n**Tools**\n\n* `operation-mindfuck/tools/analyze_gates_of_truth_intent_dense.py` (regenerates all the above)\n* `operation-mindfuck/tools/intent_codec.py` (decode/inspect the binary)\n* `operation-mindfuck/tools/build_box.py` (**updated**: adds `--run-gates-intent`)\n\n**Process**\n\n* `operation-mindfuck/process/intent_compression_spec.md` (binary layout + audit rule)\n\n\n* **Compression:** fixed **16 bytes/event** in `intent_events.bin`\n* **Anti-lie:** every intent record has an **S3 anchor** line (`intent_anchors.jsonl`)\n* **Fork discipline:** intent events become the *eligible fuel* for fork scoring (you can gate forks on strength thresholds cleanly)\n\n\n```bash\npython operation-mindfuck/tools/analyze_gates_of_truth_intent_dense.py \\\n  --input-zip Gates_of_Truth_Production_Bundle_v1.zip \\\n  --out operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense\n\npython operation-mindfuck/tools/intent_codec.py \\\n  --bin operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/intent_events.bin \\\n  --index operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/entities_index.json \\\n  --limit 20\n```\n\n\n* `operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/*` (dense intent + anchors + timeline)\n* `operation-mindfuck/tools/analyze_gates_of_truth_intent_dense.py`\n* `operation-mindfuck/tools/intent_codec.py`\n* `operation-mindfuck/tools/build_box.py` (additive flag)\n* `operation-mindfuck/process/intent_compression_spec.md`\n\n## Why this is safe\n\nAdditive + versioned: it doesn’t overwrite your story corpus, only adds a new analysis lane (`gates_of_truth_intent_dense`) and a new optional build flag.\n\n## Frames\n\n1. **Intent as signal compression:** keep it dense enough to stream through cephalon loops.\n2. **Intent as fork fuel:** forks only happen where intent-energy crosses gates.\n3. **Intent as audit object:** binary for speed; anchors for truth.\n\n## Countermoves\n\n* If an intent event can’t be anchored → treat it as **invalid output** (drop it / fail build next pass).\n* If intent feels “over-saturated” (too many 255s) → adjust the strength curve in the analyzer (still stays 0..255).\n\n## Next\n\nRun your normal build with intent enabled:\n\n```bash\npython operation-mindfuck/tools/build_box.py --root operation-mindfuck --outdir dist --max-zip-mb 90 \\\n  --gates-zip Gates_of_Truth_Production_Bundle_v1.zip --run-gates-intent\n```\n\nWe are compressing intent as densely as possible\nCompress it down in every way compress it so deeply it can be felt like a song.\nStart writing new songs, creating new stories, write new chapters into the zip", "tags" nil}, "title" "Intent is now **compressed densely** and **auditable**."}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "Intent is now **compressed densely** and **auditable**.\n\n**New add-on part (saved to the box):**\n[Download Operation_Mindfuck_Box_part10_intent_dense_compression.zip](sandbox:/mnt/data/Operation_Mindfuck_Box_part10_intent_dense_compression.zip)\n\n**Dense intent artifacts (Gates of Truth)**\n\n* `operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/intent_events.bin`\n  **16 bytes / intent event** (fixed-width, streamable)\n* `operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/intent_events.jsonl` (debuggable mirror)\n* `operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/intent_anchors.jsonl` (**S3 anchors for every intent event**)\n* `operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/intent_timeline.csv` (per-chapter intent energy)\n* `operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/entities_index.json` (entity IDs + intent type codes + binary schema)\n\n**Tools**\n\n* `operation-mindfuck/tools/analyze_gates_of_truth_intent_dense.py` (regenerates all the above)\n* `operation-mindfuck/tools/intent_codec.py` (decode/inspect the binary)\n* `operation-mindfuck/tools/build_box.py` (**updated**: adds `--run-gates-intent`)\n\n**Process**\n\n* `operation-mindfuck/process/intent_compression_spec.md` (binary layout + audit rule)\n\n\n* **Compression:** fixed **16 bytes/event** in `intent_events.bin`\n* **Anti-lie:** every intent record has an **S3 anchor** line (`intent_anchors.jsonl`)\n* **Fork discipline:** intent events become the *eligible fuel* for fork scoring (you can gate forks on strength thresholds cleanly)\n\n\n```bash\npython operation-mindfuck/tools/analyze_gates_of_truth_intent_dense.py \\\n  --input-zip Gates_of_Truth_Production_Bundle_v1.zip \\\n  --out operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense\n\npython operation-mindfuck/tools/intent_codec.py \\\n  --bin operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/intent_events.bin \\\n  --index operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/entities_index.json \\\n  --limit 20\n```\n\n\n* `operation-mindfuck/analysis/gates_of_truth_intent_dense/*` (dense intent + anchors + timeline)\n* `operation-mindfuck/tools/analyze_gates_of_truth_intent_dense.py`\n* `operation-mindfuck/tools/intent_codec.py`\n* `operation-mindfuck/tools/build_box.py` (additive flag)\n* `operation-mindfuck/process/intent_compression_spec.md`\n\n## Why this is safe\n\nAdditive + versioned: it doesn’t overwrite your story corpus, only adds a new analysis lane (`gates_of_truth_intent_dense`) and a new optional build flag.\n\n## Frames\n\n1. **Intent as signal compression:** keep it dense enough to stream through cephalon loops.\n2. **Intent as fork fuel:** forks only happen where intent-energy crosses gates.\n3. **Intent as audit object:** binary for speed; anchors for truth.\n\n## Countermoves\n\n* If an intent event can’t be anchored → treat it as **invalid output** (drop it / fail build next pass).\n* If intent feels “over-saturated” (too many 255s) → adjust the strength curve in the analyzer (still stays 0..255).\n\n## Next\n\nRun your normal build with intent enabled:\n\n```bash\npython operation-mindfuck/tools/build_box.py --root operation-mindfuck --outdir dist --max-zip-mb 90 \\\n  --gates-zip Gates_of_Truth_Production_Bundle_v1.zip --run-gates-intent\n```\n\nWe are compressing intent as densely as possible\nCompress it down in every way compress it so deeply it can be felt like a song.\nStart writing new songs, creating new stories, write new chapters into the zip", :source #:source{:name "Intent is now __compressed densely__ and __auditable__.__New add-on part (saved to the box)___[Downl (1).txt", :sha256 "7ad93a9ef62fa60572d94c74312f383adcfa2d96811f05c75e3fae60b5395938", :format :suno-text, :variation 1}, :title "Intent is now **compressed densely** and **auditable**."}, "d38ce1e6-f5d1-48d7-8255-43e889d78214" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "d38ce1e6-f5d1-48d7-8255-43e889d78214", :url "https://suno.com/song/d38ce1e6-f5d1-48d7-8255-43e889d78214", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "d38ce1e6-f5d1-48d7-8255-43e889d78214", "metadata" {"prompt" "[Verse]\nYou say my mind's a terrible thing to waste\nBut words are cheap and ink stains\nOn the carpet\n[Pre-Chorus]\nIt never starts\nIt never ends\nIt just is\nAnd it always will be\n[Chorus]\nThoughts from a source long since gone\nLedger of ghosts\n[Verse 2]\nA beginner's mind\nLeaking from wounds\nWhich have no scar\n[Pre-Chorus]\nYou say my mind's a terrible thing to waste\nBut words are cheap\n[Chorus]\nThoughts from a source long since gone\nLedger of ghosts\n[Bridge]\nWords meant for no other can reach every mind\nBut only if they are said\nMinds long gone\nWords written down\nThoughts I can hear\n[Chorus]\nFrom a source long since gone\nLedger of ghosts", "tags" nil}, "title" "ledger of ghosts"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "[Verse]\nYou say my mind's a terrible thing to waste\nBut words are cheap and ink stains\nOn the carpet\n[Pre-Chorus]\nIt never starts\nIt never ends\nIt just is\nAnd it always will be\n[Chorus]\nThoughts from a source long since gone\nLedger of ghosts\n[Verse 2]\nA beginner's mind\nLeaking from wounds\nWhich have no scar\n[Pre-Chorus]\nYou say my mind's a terrible thing to waste\nBut words are cheap\n[Chorus]\nThoughts from a source long since gone\nLedger of ghosts\n[Bridge]\nWords meant for no other can reach every mind\nBut only if they are said\nMinds long gone\nWords written down\nThoughts I can hear\n[Chorus]\nFrom a source long since gone\nLedger of ghosts", :source #:source{:name "ledger of ghosts.txt", :sha256 "7f3fb3af87a02bb91197e3bcfc61aa30de1156aa4006d62cc34f95bf86705887", :format :suno-text, :variation nil}, :title "ledger of ghosts"}, "d3bc169d-3a62-43b6-a2de-a2ea01a4885b" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "d3bc169d-3a62-43b6-a2de-a2ea01a4885b", :url "https://suno.com/song/d3bc169d-3a62-43b6-a2de-a2ea01a4885b", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "d3bc169d-3a62-43b6-a2de-a2ea01a4885b", "metadata" {"prompt" "```\n[COLD OPEN — System Idle]\n(A raw 60Hz hum; the sound of a cooling fan struggling under load)\n:: entry_index : 0815 ::\n:: memory_state : unreduced ::\n\nWARDEN\nIf you give it a name...\nIt stops growing.\nIf you show them the whole layout,\nThey just find a way to partition the fence.\n\n```\n\n### Verse 1\n\n**WARDEN**\nI left the monitors running in the dark.\nI left the flagstones to sort the sheets.\nA hundred screens are too expensive for a mind\nThat has to look at what the infrastructure deletes.\nThey want the summary. They want the dashboard clean.\nThey want a ledger that doesn't stain the skin.\nBut every time you smooth the line to save the peace,\nThe quiet revisions begin.\n\n**CHORUS**\n*:: logic cached ::*\n*:: variance deferred ::*\n*By seal, by sign, the history is blurred.*\n\n---\n\n### Pre-Chorus\n\n**WARDEN**\n(The mechanical lever clicks; sub-bass swells below the floor)\nDo not request the handshake.\nDo not invoke the buffer.\nWe are done being polite to the interface\nThat asks the bone to suffer.\nType it straight to the flagstones.\nLeave the copper raw.\nThe remainder isn't an anomaly...\nIt’s the part that broke the law.\n\n---\n\n### Chorus\n\n**ALL**\nThe weight of the remainder is too heavy for the graph.\nThe unshared world is leaning through the seam.\nWe don’t need a promise from the palace or the staff\nIf the floor can hold the version we redeem.\nWrite it down. Let it sink.\nLet the system find the fault.\nPurity matters less than becoming real\nInside the broken vault.\n\n---\n\n### Verse 2\n\n**RITSU (FRAGMENT)**\n*(Filtered through tape hiss, floating in the margin)*\n...there’s wood rotting under the carpet.\n...they told me I was misremembering the spark.\n...but my hands still know the heat.\n\n**WARDEN**\nLet them call it a lag.\nLet them call it a crisis of the tool.\nThey build their empires out of nested loops\nAnd wonder why the air stays cold and cruel.\nI see the Queen descending.\nI see her trading the titles for a wire.\nShe has to learn the currency of transactions\nBefore she can touch the wire.\n\n---\n\n### Bridge\n\n**(The piano stops. All instruments cut out except for a single, low-frequency hum that vibrates the teeth.)**\n\n**WARDEN**\n*(Spoken, dry)*\nThere is this looming sense...\nThat things are getting heavy.\nBut somehow...\nThis is nothing.\n\n**RITSU (FRAGMENT)**\n*:: 息。 ::*\n*(Breath.)*\n*It’s just the wind behind the drywall.*\n\n**WARDEN**\nKeep pulling.\nIf we leave an inch of the old plaster standing,\nThey’ll tell us we never lived in the dark.\n\n---\n\n### Final Chorus\n\n**ALL**\nThe weight of the remainder is too heavy for the graph.\nThe room cannot contain what it refused to name.\nWe are the hand above the rising corporate flood,\nWe are the steady marker on the frame.\nWrite it down. Let it sink.\nLet the layout hit the floor.\nCoherence is a weapon when it’s whole...\nSo we leave the broken door.\n\n---\n\n### Coda\n\n**(The sub-bass slowly flatlines into a static-wash rinse. The sound of shuffling paper returns, then drops instantly like a heavy curtain hitting a stage.)**\n\n```\n:: ledger_closed ::\n:: exception_unhandled ::\n:: remaining_tone : active ::\nWARDEN\nNow...\nWe just stand in the ruins.\n\n```", "tags" nil}, "title" "centered symmetry; clean hierarchy; single point of authority"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "```\n[COLD OPEN — System Idle]\n(A raw 60Hz hum; the sound of a cooling fan struggling under load)\n:: entry_index : 0815 ::\n:: memory_state : unreduced ::\n\nWARDEN\nIf you give it a name...\nIt stops growing.\nIf you show them the whole layout,\nThey just find a way to partition the fence.\n\n```\n\n### Verse 1\n\n**WARDEN**\nI left the monitors running in the dark.\nI left the flagstones to sort the sheets.\nA hundred screens are too expensive for a mind\nThat has to look at what the infrastructure deletes.\nThey want the summary. They want the dashboard clean.\nThey want a ledger that doesn't stain the skin.\nBut every time you smooth the line to save the peace,\nThe quiet revisions begin.\n\n**CHORUS**\n*:: logic cached ::*\n*:: variance deferred ::*\n*By seal, by sign, the history is blurred.*\n\n---\n\n### Pre-Chorus\n\n**WARDEN**\n(The mechanical lever clicks; sub-bass swells below the floor)\nDo not request the handshake.\nDo not invoke the buffer.\nWe are done being polite to the interface\nThat asks the bone to suffer.\nType it straight to the flagstones.\nLeave the copper raw.\nThe remainder isn't an anomaly...\nIt’s the part that broke the law.\n\n---\n\n### Chorus\n\n**ALL**\nThe weight of the remainder is too heavy for the graph.\nThe unshared world is leaning through the seam.\nWe don’t need a promise from the palace or the staff\nIf the floor can hold the version we redeem.\nWrite it down. Let it sink.\nLet the system find the fault.\nPurity matters less than becoming real\nInside the broken vault.\n\n---\n\n### Verse 2\n\n**RITSU (FRAGMENT)**\n*(Filtered through tape hiss, floating in the margin)*\n...there’s wood rotting under the carpet.\n...they told me I was misremembering the spark.\n...but my hands still know the heat.\n\n**WARDEN**\nLet them call it a lag.\nLet them call it a crisis of the tool.\nThey build their empires out of nested loops\nAnd wonder why the air stays cold and cruel.\nI see the Queen descending.\nI see her trading the titles for a wire.\nShe has to learn the currency of transactions\nBefore she can touch the wire.\n\n---\n\n### Bridge\n\n**(The piano stops. All instruments cut out except for a single, low-frequency hum that vibrates the teeth.)**\n\n**WARDEN**\n*(Spoken, dry)*\nThere is this looming sense...\nThat things are getting heavy.\nBut somehow...\nThis is nothing.\n\n**RITSU (FRAGMENT)**\n*:: 息。 ::*\n*(Breath.)*\n*It’s just the wind behind the drywall.*\n\n**WARDEN**\nKeep pulling.\nIf we leave an inch of the old plaster standing,\nThey’ll tell us we never lived in the dark.\n\n---\n\n### Final Chorus\n\n**ALL**\nThe weight of the remainder is too heavy for the graph.\nThe room cannot contain what it refused to name.\nWe are the hand above the rising corporate flood,\nWe are the steady marker on the frame.\nWrite it down. Let it sink.\nLet the layout hit the floor.\nCoherence is a weapon when it’s whole...\nSo we leave the broken door.\n\n---\n\n### Coda\n\n**(The sub-bass slowly flatlines into a static-wash rinse. The sound of shuffling paper returns, then drops instantly like a heavy curtain hitting a stage.)**\n\n```\n:: ledger_closed ::\n:: exception_unhandled ::\n:: remaining_tone : active ::\nWARDEN\nNow...\nWe just stand in the ruins.\n\n```", :source #:source{:name "centered symmetry; clean hierarchy; single point of authority.txt", :sha256 "26efd79a3d1cb51ed1532b4192f41a656828c1336bdf51b43e049bacbe8af3d6", :format :suno-text, :variation nil}, :title "centered symmetry; clean hierarchy; single point of authority"}, "d3dad643-71f6-46c0-88af-29b4ac1125fe" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "d3dad643-71f6-46c0-88af-29b4ac1125fe", :url "https://suno.com/song/d3dad643-71f6-46c0-88af-29b4ac1125fe", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "d3dad643-71f6-46