 out\nif the name is not known\n\n[STAGGERED ROUND]\nleave the key out\n             key out\n                    out\n\n[VERSE]\n\nNo mark on the door\nis not a mark that says empty\nNo hand on the wire\nis not a hand saying no\n\nI can still reach the room\nif I don't forge the number\nI can still find the row\nif I don't fill what I don't know\n\n[ROUND]\n\nwhat is missing\n        is not empty\n               not empty\n\n[REFRAIN]\n\nNil is still a lock\nwhen you write it in the key\nNil is still a lock\non a room you meant to leave free\n\nLeave the key out\nlet the unknown keep its width\nLeave the key out\nlet the evidence attach\n\n[CHOIR, LOW]\n\nわからない\nない、じゃない\n\n[VERSE]\n\nThe work was there first\nbefore the proof could name it\nThe proof can bind the work\nit does not get to make it\n\nA page I cannot read\nis still a page in the ledger\nA witness can go dark\nwithout the row going with it\n\n[STAGGERED ROUND]\n\nstill there\n       still there\n             even when the witness isn't\n\n[REFRAIN — MUTATION]\n\nNil is still a lock\nwhen absence gets a value\nNil is still a lock\nwhen the search becomes a cell\n\nI don't need to call it empty\njust because I cannot tell\nI don't need to close the doorway\nto admit I cannot tell\n\n[CHOIR, THIN]\n\nわからない\nない、じゃない\n\n[VERSE]\n\nKeep the source edge open\nkeep the rendered edge the same\nIf the proof names these bytes\nthen the body keeps its shape\n\nDo not flatten all the spaces\njust to make the checksum neat\nMany rooms can share a hallway\nwithout becoming one room\n\n[ROUND, TIGHTENING]\n\nproof attaches\n       work remains\nproof attaches\n       work remains\n\n[FINAL REFRAIN]\n\nLeave the key out\nif the name is not known\nLeave the key out\nand the room stays findable\n\nNil is still a lock\nbut the missing key is not\n\n[STAGGERED OUTRO]\n\nnot empty\n      not gone\n            still reachable\n\nわからない\nない、じゃない\n\nleave the key out\n             key out\n                    out", "tags" nil},