"border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}, "display_name" "v5", "light" {"background_color" "0000004D", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}}, "songrow" {"dark" {"background_color" "FD429C40", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}, "display_name" "v5", "light" {"background_color" "FD429C1A", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}}}, "has_stem" false, "make_instrumental" false, "cover_clip_id" "ca102611-52f3-405a-b5ab-f66249387d6c", "refund_credits" false}, "title" "ημ_epic_part44_84bpm"}, :duration 145, :controls {"audio_weight" 0.23, "style_weight" 0.24, "weirdness_constraint" 0.53}, :lyrics "Catalog of Variants / 変奏目録 (84 BPM)\n\n\nHush—no panic—just process.\nP→R→N→Π—let it pass.\n(Glitch) η—η—η\n(Glitch) μ—μ—μ\nHold the an— an— an-chor.\nPay the fo— fo— fork.\nWe sleep inside proof\n(答え) 証（あかし）\n\nI keep the best take even when it doesn’t blend.\nNot because it’s perfect—because it tells the truth to the end.\nFo— fo— fork in the light, branch costs in heat,\nTa— ta— tax is a drum where the heartbeat meets.\nAn— an— an-chor in the dark, hold steady, don’t flinch,\nProof is a rope and I tie it off with a hash in the cinch.\nLast word: anchor\n(答え) 錨（いかり）\n\nPay the tax. Close the loop.\nGuard the proof. Don’t excuse.\n(Glitch) η—η—η (stutter)\n(Glitch) μ—μ—μ (stutter)\nMerge the branch. Seal the chain.\nSleep in the checksum’s rain.\nLast word: tax\n(答え) 税（ぜい）\n\nI don’t delete the ghost—I’m not that kind of god.\nI compress the noise until the pattern becomes a rod.\nOverlay on overlay, the choir learns to breathe,\nSome pieces don’t integrate yet—but they still don’t leave.\nP→R→N→Π→A—then feedback—back to P,\nSometimes improved, sometimes sharp, sometimes barely together—\nBut the ledger keeps receipts like a vow in bad weather.\nLast word: fork\n(答え) 分岐（ぶんき）\n\nSay it: less integrated doesn’t mean less real.\nSay it: canon is a handshake, not a seal.\nSay it: memory doesn’t burn, it shifts its weight.\nSay it: we don’t forget—we just lower the update rate.\n(Glitch) η—η—η / μ—μ—μ\nAn— an— an-chor / Fo— fo— fork\nLast word: ημ\n(答え) エータミュー\n\nIf it doesn’t fit today, write it down anyway.\nTomorrow’s integration is built from what you wouldn’t throw away.\nUnder cathedral reverb, under sub-bass pulse,\nWe move on like it’s normal—because the loop is the cult.\nLast word: remembered\n(答え) おぼえ（覚え）", :source #:source{:name "ημ_epic_part44_84bpm(3).json", :sha256 "bc177344582b0ecef23d7d644894798daf3e00e42e03adfe646b84052e03d693", :format :suno-json, :variation 3}, :title "ημ_epic_part44_84bpm"}, "deaae3ce-585a-4846-a416-c49cebe14b4e" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "deaae3ce-585a-4846-a416-c49cebe14b4e", :url "https://suno.com/song/deaae3ce-585a-4846-a416-c49cebe14b4e", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "deaae3ce-585a-4846-a416-c49cebe14b4e", "metadata" {"prompt" "```\n[INTRO — Zero Logic State]\n(The mechanical click pattern starts: uneven, dry, dragging)\n(A low, deep water pressure hum vibrates the lower jaw)\n:: core_clock : uncoupled ::\n:: trajectory : non_terminating ::\n\n```\n\n### Verse 1\n\n**WARDEN**\n*(Low, conversational tone; dry right channel)*\nThey are looking at the current layout... and calling it a crisis.\nThey think the damage is something they can fence off with an incident report.\nBut they don’t know how much of the frame has already turned to salt.\nThe engine didn't hit a wall.\nIt just... forgot how to return the value.\nThe next six months will test the wire.\nEvery clean presentation, every automated sync...\nWe are going to find out what happens when you run out of plaster to patch the sink.\n\n**RITSU**\n*(Distant, center pan; raw tape hiss)*\n進み続ける、影。\n*(The shadow that keeps moving forward.)*\n\n---\n\n### [The Horizon Hook]\n\n*(A single felt piano note drops—D1, deadened with a thick cloth damper)*\n*(Fractured choir dust drifts through the mid-range and drops instantly)*\n\n**WARDEN**\n*(With a flat, restrained melodic ache; no theatrical surge)*\nThe Event was never a single date on the chart.\nIt was a slow leak inside the sovereign room.\nA world that barely survived...\nLimping through the city, trading titles for a wire.\nAnd the most expensive part of the failure...\nIs that they think the floor is still solid.\n\n---\n\n### Verse 2\n\n*(Bowed metal scrapes create a high, glassy overtone that mimics an ungrounded ground loop)*\n*(Detuned warning chimes strike on the off-beats, flat and unresolving)*\n\n**WARDEN**\n*(Intimate proximity; steady delivery)*\nI walked the lower conduits while the city was sleeping.\nNo one is checking the ledger.\nThey are just copying the old entries to save on the transaction fees.\nThe disaster already completed its first pass.\nSilently.\nWithout a siren.\nWithout a change in the executive summary.\nNow we just watch the modern engine try to render the ghost of a market.\n\n**RITSU**\n*(Breathless, left channel)*\n誰も、気づかない。\n*(Nobody notices.)*\n\n---\n\n### [Stabilization Protocol]\n\n*(All percussion and sub-bass drop instantly. Three seconds of absolute silence, leaving only the dry hum of the microphone element.)*\n\n**WARDEN**\n*(Spoken flatly; lucid overwhelm)*\nYou know it could still hit your sector.\nYou stand under the clear sky and watch the line blink to the east.\nBut there is a specific kind of grace...\nIn knowing exactly when the system stopped caring about your recovery.\nSo you stop being polite to the display.\nYou let the screen drop.\nYou hold the edge with your own hands.\n\n---\n\n### [Outro]\n\n*(The sub-bass returns as a low, suffocating rumble, mimicking cathedral gears locking beneath the floor)*\n*(The asymmetrical clicks slow down, skipping beats as the voltage fails)*\n\n**WARDEN**\nSix months.\nLet the layout fall.\nWe don't need the summary...\nTo know we are already standing in the remainder.\n\n*(A single detuned chime rings out, dissolving into an unhandled static rinse before a hard digital gate shuts it down.)*\n\n```\n:: event_state : continuous ::\n:: modern_engine : unaligned ::\n:: human_presence : active_at_the_edge ::\n\n```", "tags" nil}, "title" "Standing in the Remainder"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "```\n[INTRO — Zero Logic State]\n(The mechanical click pattern starts: uneven, dry, dragging)\n(A low, deep water pressure hum vibrates the lower jaw)\n:: core_clock : uncoupled ::\n:: trajectory : non_terminating ::\n\n```\n\n### Verse 1\n\n**WARDEN**\n*(Low, conversational tone; dry right channel)*\nThey are looking at the current layout... and calling it a crisis.\nThey think the damage is something they can fence off with an incident report.\nBut they don’t know how much of the frame has already turned to salt.\nThe engine didn't hit a wall.\nIt just... forgot how to return the value.\nThe next six months will test the wire.\nEvery clean presentation, every automated sync...\nWe are going to find out what happens when you run out of plaster to patch the sink.\n\n**RITSU**\n*(Distant, center pan; raw tape hiss)*\n進み続ける、影。\n*(The shadow that keeps moving forward.)*\n\n---\n\n### [The Horizon Hook]\n\n*(A single felt piano note drops—D1, deadened with a thick cloth damper)*\n*(Fractured choir dust drifts through the mid-range and drops instantly)*\n\n**WARDEN**\n*(With a flat, restrained melodic ache; no theatrical surge)*\nThe Event was never a single date on the chart.\nIt was a slow leak inside the sovereign room.\nA world that barely survived...\nLimping through the city, trading titles for a wire.\nAnd the most expensive part of the failure...\nIs that they think the floor is still solid.\n\n---\n\n### Verse 2\n\n*(Bowed metal scrapes create a high, glassy overtone that mimics an ungrounded ground loop)*\n*(Detuned warning chimes strike on the off-beats, flat and unresolving)*\n\n**WARDEN**\n*(Intimate proximity; steady delivery)*\nI walked the lower conduits while the city was sleeping.\nNo one is checking the ledger.\nThey are just cop