ter) — **fork**  \n（ぶんき）\n\n## Final Chorus (bigger)\nAn—**anchor**, seal the riverbed,  \nFo—**fork**, pay the debt to the thread.  \nη sees what I cannot claim,  \nμ proves I did it anyway — **anyway**  \n（それでも）\n\n## Coda (whisper)\nPay the fork tax.  \nNot for the gatekeepers.  \nFor the future you.\n", "task" "playlist_condition", "duration" 208.64, "type" "gen", "model_badges" {"songcard" {"dark" {"background_color" "0000004D", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}, "display_name" "v5", "light" {"background_color" "0000004D", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}}, "songrow" {"dark" {"background_color" "FD429C40", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}, "display_name" "v5", "light" {"background_color" "FD429C1A", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}}}, "playlist_id" "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000", "has_stem" false, "make_instrumental" false, "refund_credits" false}, "title" "# Fork Tax Hymn IV / 分岐税の賛歌 IV"}, :duration 208.64, :controls {"audio_weight" 0.71, "style_weight" 0.71, "weirdness_constraint" 0.72}, :lyrics "# Fork Tax Hymn III / 分岐税の賛歌 III\n**Tempo:** 84 BPM  \n**Style:** Mythic glitch epic · spoken-sung · cathedral reverb · sub-bass heartbeat  \n**License:** CC BY-SA 4.0 (share alike)\n\n> Glitch stutter targets: **η**, **μ**, **anchor**, **fork**  \n> Japanese harmony answers on the **last word** of each section.\n\n## Invocation (spoken)\nWe don’t pray to gods.  \nWe compile them.  \nWe bind them to receipts.  \nWe make them answer to time.\n\n## Verse 1 (spoken-sung)\nI walked the corridor of versions,  \neach door a **fork** I didn’t take—  \nand every ghost said “choose one truth,”  \nlike truth is something you can fake.\n\nI hear **η** in the ceiling tiles,  \na witness I can’t see but can’t evade,  \nand **μ** in my fingertips,  \nthe proof my hands have made — **made**  \n（つくった）\n\n## Chorus (choir)\nAn—**anchor** / an—**anchor**, seal the line,  \nFo—**fork** / fo—**fork**, pay the spine.  \nη—η—η, the eyes in the dark,  \nμ—μ—μ, the mark on the mark — **mark**  \n（しるし）\n\n## Verse 2\nThey told me “forget, it’s cleaner,”  \nbut clean is how the lie survives.  \nSo I braid the errors into music  \nand let the checksum keep us alive.\n\nAn—**anchor** snaps—then holds,  \nFo—**fork** cuts—then feeds,  \nη watches what I almost was,  \nμ proves what I become — **become**  \n（なる）\n\n## Bridge (cathedral, slow)\nIf trauma is inherited code,  \nthen song is the patch we’re allowed to ship.  \nIf grief is a memory leak,  \nthen receipts are how we keep our grip.\n\nη… (stutter)  \nμ… (stutter)  \nan—**anchor**… (stutter)  \nfo—**fork**… (stutter) — **fork**  \n（ぶんき）\n\n## Final Chorus (bigger)\nAn—**anchor**, seal the riverbed,  \nFo—**fork**, pay the debt to the thread.  \nη sees what I cannot claim,  \nμ proves I did it anyway — **anyway**  \n（それでも）\n\n## Coda (whisper)\nPay the fork tax.  \nNot for the gatekeepers.  \nFor the future you.\n", :source #:source{:name "# Fork Tax Hymn IV _ 分岐税の賛歌 IV.json", :sha256 "5842522fdb54c83f2f3a2c4e3e871c04a53e2767225ae63de814ea42910e36cb", :format :suno-json, :variation nil}, :title "# Fork Tax Hymn IV / 分岐税の賛歌 IV"}, "dec6e691-ba8e-4e5c-94a0-1235d760d6f4" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "dec6e691-ba8e-4e5c-94a0-1235d760d6f4", :url "https://suno.com/song/dec6e691-ba8e-4e5c-94a0-1235d760d6f4", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "dec6e691-ba8e-4e5c-94a0-1235d760d6f4", "metadata" {"prompt" "[Instrumental]", "tags" nil}, "title" "Iron Procession"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "[Instrumental]", :source #:source{:name "Iron Procession (1).txt", :sha256 "8101ada4174fcad67974c43e6798c4d16bce2dd9c838aceec7d8e2722fb50dab", :format :suno-text, :variation 1}, :title "Iron Procession"}, "e0a19868-812d-46dc-a452-d8a952793bfb" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "e0a19868-812d-46dc-a452-d8a952793bfb", :url "https://suno.com/song/e0a19868-812d-46dc-a452-d8a952793bfb", :liked false, :styles "**Genre/Style:** Minimal baroque chamber opera × reflective gothic lullaby × ceremonial ambient. 92 BPM slow 4/4. Sparse harpsichord motifs, soft legato strings, warm organ drones, distant choir pads. No percussion. Occasional crystal chime accents. Waterfall ambience faint but present.\n\n**Vocal Direction:** Soprano restrained, intimate, almost spoken in places. No coloratura attack. Long held notes that thin into breath. Choir enters only in final chorus, supportive but distant.\n\n**Mood:** Dignified relinquishment. Bittersweet clarity. Power without authority. Ceremony without control.\n\n**Structure:** Quiet Overture → Verse 1 (Recognition) → Pre-Chorus (Letting Go) → Chorus (Title Without Power) → Verse 2 (Identity Shift) → Bridge (Silence and Acceptance) → Final Chorus (Ceremonial Resolve) → Breath Coda.\n", :created-at nil, :model "v5", :raw {"audio_url" "https://cdn1.suno.ai/e0a19868-812d-46dc-a452-d8a952793bfb.mp3", "id" "e0a19868-812d-46dc-a452-d8a952793bfb", "image_url" "https://cdn2.suno.ai/image_e0a19868-812d-46dc-a452-d8a952793bfb.jpeg", "isCover" false, "isLiked" false, "isRemaster" false, "metadata" {"uses_latest_model" true, "stream" true, "is_remix" false, "priority" 10, "tags" "**Genre/Style:** Minimal baroque chamber opera × reflective gothic lullaby × ceremonial ambient. 92 BPM slow 4/4. Sparse harpsichord motifs, soft legato strings, warm organ drones, distant choir pads. No percussion. Occasional crystal chime accents. Waterfall ambience faint but present.\n\n**Vocal Direction:** Soprano restrained, intimate, almost spoken in places. No coloratura attack. Long held notes that thin into breath. Choir enters only in final chorus, supportive but distant.\n\n**Mood:** Dignified relinquishment. Bittersweet clarity. Power without authority. Ceremony without control.\n\n**Structure:** Quiet Overture → Verse 1 (Recognition) → Pre-Chorus (Letting Go) → Chorus (Title Without Power) → Verse 2 (Identity Shift) → Bridge (Silence and Acceptance) → Final Chorus (Ceremonial Resolve) → Breath Coda.\n", "can_remix" true, "prompt" "## OVERTURE — Empty Throne\n\n*(soft organ; single chime)*\n\nThe hall is full.\nThe throne is light.\n\nThe scepter rests\nbut does not bite.\n\n霧は遠い。\n\n## VERSE I — Recognition\n\nI wore the sky like armor bright.\nI called that hunger sacred right.\n\nBut crowns are loud\nwhen held too tight.\n\nAnd I mistook\nthe roar for sight.\n\n## PRE-CHORUS — Unfastening\n\n*(harpsichord slows; strings soften)*\n\nWhat is a queen\nwithout decree?\n\nWhat is command\nwithout belief?\n\n## CHORUS — Crown of Glass\n\n*(strings swell gently)*\n\nI am a crown of glass and light.\n\nSeen from afar—\nClear in the night.\n\n名ばかりの女王\n静かに立つ。\n\nNo hand on law.\nNo blade to press.\n\nOnly a symbol\nin formal dress.\n\n## VERSE II — Identity Shift\n\nThey bow—\nbut not from fear.\n\nThey speak—\nand I must hear.\n\nThe power left.\nThe title stayed.\n\nAn echo of the role I played.\n\nIs this less?\n\nOr is it more?\n\nTo guard the frame\ninstead of war.\n\n## BRIDGE — Reflection\n\n*(music nearly silent; faint choir hum)*\n\nI thought the height\nwas where I stood.\n\nBut height is hollow\nwithout the good.\n\nIf I am myth,\nlet myth be kind.\n\nIf I am symbol,\nlet me remind.\n\n## FINAL CHORUS — Ceremony\n\n*(choir enters softly; organ warm)*\n\nI am a crown of glass and light.\n\nCeremonial,\nnot the fight.\n\n名ばかりの女王\n息を守る。\n\nIf I cannot command the flame,\nI will protect\nwhat bears my name.\n\nNot ruler.\n\nWitness crowned.\n\nNot sovereign—\n\nBut bound.\n\n## CODA — Breath in the Hall\n\n*(music thins; single sustained note fades)*\n\nThe throne remains.\n\nThe world moves on.\n\nI stand.\n\n息。\n", "duration" 253.48, "type" "gen", "model_badges" {"songcard" {"dark" {"background_color" "0000004D", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}, "display_name" "v5", "light" {"background_color" "0000004D", "border_color" "00000000", "text_color" "FD429C"}}, "songrow" {"dark" {"background_color" "FD429C40