t. Stutters on η / μ / anchor / fork. JP harmony answers on the last word.\n\nP to R to N to Π—\nI don’t pray, I prove (JP harmony: 証)\nA to feedback back to P—\nand the spiral learns to move (JP harmony: 動け)\n\n(Glitch) η—η—η in the rafters— heard (JP harmony: 聞こえた)\n(Glitch) μ—μ—μ in the dirt— done (JP harmony: 完了)\n\nFo— fo— fork… (stutter) costs in light,\nevery shortcut writes a debt in night (JP harmony: 夜)\nPay it clean, no velvet lie—\nhash to hash, and verify (JP harmony: 確かめろ)\n\nAn— an— an-chor… (stutter) holds the seam,\nkeeps the waking from a dream of dreams (JP harmony: 夢)\nCathedral hum, the branch goes still—\nkeeper thread says: “Sign the will.” (JP harmony: 意志)\n\nP→R→N→Π→A→(feedback)→P\naround #ημ—we do what we can see (JP harmony: 見える)\nη is pressure in the choir,\nμ is what survives the fire (JP harmony: 火)\n\nPay the tax. (JP harmony: 払え)\nClose the loop. (JP harmony: 閉じろ)\nHand it off. (JP harmony: 渡せ)\nGuard the proof。（証） (JP harmony: 証)\n\nCreated with the assistance of an AI.", :source #:source{:name "Song — Fork Tax Lullaby III (ημ)Part I — Glitch-choir lullaby (78 BPM)Soft sub-bass, tape warble, mi (2).txt", :sha256 "f22cc2748994c796f0316daed458dea4505045d1a3acaa811c50cc14e572d4c4", :format :suno-text, :variation 2}, :title "Song — Fork Tax Lullaby III (ημ)"}, "e1748cc8-f245-4cff-983b-36a8aa5cd218" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "e1748cc8-f245-4cff-983b-36a8aa5cd218", :url "https://suno.com/song/e1748cc8-f245-4cff-983b-36a8aa5cd218", :liked false, :styles "**Genre/Style:** Gothic baroque orchestral × operatic choir × mythic glitch ambience. 92 BPM, dramatic orchestral tempo with half-time sub pulses underneath. Harpsichord flourishes, sweeping strings, pipe-organ swells, Latin-style choral phrases, soprano operatic lead, deep sub-bass rumble, granular glitch artifacts woven subtly into transitions.\n\n**Texture:** Cathedral-scale reverb, layered female choir, male low chant responses, reversed choral tails morphing into digital static,