f9c8", :format :suno-text, :variation nil}, :title "Risk Clock Broadcast"}, "f1785046-735f-46eb-b53e-5bad669e698b" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "f1785046-735f-46eb-b53e-5bad669e698b", :url "https://suno.com/song/f1785046-735f-46eb-b53e-5bad669e698b", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "f1785046-735f-46eb-b53e-5bad669e698b", "metadata" {"prompt" "# Fork Tax Lullaby IX — 20260213_244615_seed3721599636\n\n## Part I — Glitch-choir lullaby (78 BPM)\n\n*(soft sub-bass, tape warble, minimal piano; stutters on “anchor” + “tax”; whispered lead; Japanese call-and-response)*\n\n[Intro — tape hiss, two-note piano, warm sub]\n(whisper)\nHush… the budget is low.\n息をして… (して…)\nKeep it small or fold it.\n\n(JP call) ねむれ、ねむれ\n(EN response) the **an— an— an-chor**… (stutter) holds.\n(JP call) しずかに、しずかに\n(EN response) the **ta— ta— tax**… (stutter) is clean.\n\n(whisper)\nAn— an— **an-chor**… (stutter) an-chor…\n(JP whisper harmony) アンカー…\nPay the **ta— ta— tax**… (stutter) ta-x…\n(JP harmony) 税…\n\n[Verse — lullaby cadence]\nP: I feel the constraint (#η)\nR: I pull one thread only\nN: I name one claim only\nΠ: I choose the cheapest test\nA: I touch the world and wait\n(feedback): I log it, no theater.\n\n(JP call) ねえ、いつ？\n(EN response) say the date.\n(JP call) ねえ、ほんと？\n(EN response) show the receipt.\n\n[Chorus — choir bloom]\nAn— an— **an-chor**… (stutter) an-chor…\nHold the boundary, hold the line.\nPay the **ta— ta— tax**… (stutter) ta-x…\nSo forks don’t breed in the dark.\n(JP harmony answers last word)\nI fall asleep inside **proof**.（証）\n\n---\n\n## Part II — Mythic glitch epic / spoken-sung (84 BPM)\n\n*(NF/Watsky cadence; cathedral reverb; sub-bass heartbeat; glitch stutters on “η”, “μ”, “anchor”, “fork”; Japanese harmony answers on the last word of each section)*\n\n[Verse 1 — fast spoken-sung]\nReceiptLint v2: “Cut the drama, cut the lore—\ninputs, outputs, one step, show me the door.”\nAnd if you got demoted? Hysteresis says “two,”\ntwo clean receipts before you call it μ,\nbefore you call it **μ**.（証）\n\n(Glitch stutter) **η—η—η**\n(Glitch stutter) **μ—μ—μ**\n\n[Hook — cathedral swell]\nI don’t win by sounding right—\nI win by making it rerun.（試）\n\n[Verse 2 — rapid cadence]\nForkBudget tight— you feel it in the sub,\nthree credits left then the Gate won’t budge.\nDateWindowGate: no “today,” no “yesterday”—\nwrite the absolute day or the claim stays grey,\nstays **η**.（制約）\n\nI pin it to an **an-an-anchor** (stutter),\nFo— fo— **fork**… (stutter) fork… only if I can pay.\nLantern locks freshness— dim claims don’t rise,\nnot on vibes, not on echoes, not on borrowed eyes—\nonly on **μ**.（証）\n\n(JP harmony answers last word) 証\n\n[Pre — glitch clicks]\nSay **η**… (stutter) η-η\nSay **μ**… (stutter) μ-μ\nSay **an-chor**… (stutter) an-an-chor\nSay **fork**… (stutter) fo-fo-fork（分岐）\n\n[Chorus — big, then hush]\nP→R→N→Π→A— receipts in my hands.（札）\n(feedback) → P— time-windowed truth, no scams.（窓）\nAn— an— **an-chor**… (stutter) an-chor…\nso the ledger knows what to keep.（記）\nFo— fo— **fork**… (stutter) fork…\nonly when evidence buys the branch.（証）\n\n**World state update:** ReceiptLint v2 is live (inputs/outputs + one-step repro), ForkBudget is enforced (fork credits per cycle), DateWindowGate now rejects relative time (“today”) in favor of absolute dates in America/Phoenix, Hysteresis requires multiple receipts after demotion, QuietAnchors decay and stop spawning forks, and the Lantern locks high-volatility claims behind a freshness threshold.\n\n#fnord\n\n**Constraints:** max dice rolls = 15; fork budget is finite per cycle; high-volatility claims require recent primary sources (freshness threshold); demoted claims need ≥2 receipts to regain μ; date windows must be absolute dates + timezone; untested anchors enter whisper mode and may not spawn children.\n\n**Dialog:** “Inputs. Outputs. One step,” the Lantern said, not unkindly. Forkgate tapped the budget line: “Spend credits or merge.” The Choir whispered the remaining number under its breath like a lullaby, and the Anchor—stuttering like a nervous metronome—answered, “an-an-anchor,” while the Tax clicked once, clean and minimal.\n\n[Cover art](sandbox:/mnt/data/20260213_244615_seed3721599636_cover.png)\n\n[Storyboard image](sandbox:/mnt/data/20260213_244615_seed3721599636_storyboard.png)\n\n**Real-world headline:** Senate rejects a Homeland Security funding bill, teeing up a partial government shutdown. ([Democracy Now!][1])\n\n**Gates of Truth system announcement:** STATUS ONLINE — ReceiptLint v2 + ForkBudget + DateWindowGate + FreshnessLock are now enforced; any time-sensitive claim without an absolute date window stays η until a compliant receipt promotes it.\n\n[1]: https://www.democracynow.org/2026/2/13/headlines?utm_source=chatgpt.com \"Headlines for February 13, 2026\"", "tags" nil}, "title" "# Fork Tax Lullaby IX — 20260213_244615_seed3721599636"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "# Fork Tax Lullaby IX — 20260213_244615_seed3721599636\n\n## Part I — Glitch-choir lullaby (78 BPM)\n\n*(soft sub-bass, tape warble, minimal piano; stutters on “anchor” + “tax”; whispered lead; Japanese call-and-response)*\n\n[Intro — tape hiss, two-note piano, warm sub]\n(whisper)\nHush… the budget is low.\n息をして… (して…)\nKeep it small or fold it.\n\n(JP call) ねむれ、ねむれ\n(EN response) the **an— an— an-chor**… (stutter) holds.\n(JP call) しずかに、しずかに\n(EN response) the **ta— ta— tax**… (stutter) is clean.\n\n(whisper)\nAn— an— **an-chor**… (stutter) an-chor…\n(JP whisper harmony) アンカー…\nPay the **ta— ta— tax**… (stutter) ta-x…\n(JP harmony) 税…\n\n[Verse — lullaby cadence]\nP: I feel the constraint (#η)\nR: I pull one thread only\nN: I name one claim only\nΠ: I choose the cheapest test\nA: I touch the world and wait\n(feedback): I log it, no theater.\n\n(JP call) ねえ、いつ？\n(EN response) say the date.\n(JP call) ねえ、ほんと？\n(EN response) show the receipt.\n\n[Chorus — choir bloom]\nAn— an— **an-chor**… (stutter) an-chor…\nHold the bou