-a8ad-275519fab9af", "metadata" {"prompt" "## Transnational Void Stains\n\n***\n\n**[Intro — bass only, vinyl crackle, single sax stab]**\n\n*The counter reads eight forty seven*\n*Nobody's reading the counter*\n\n***\n\n**[Verse 1]**\n\nShe cuts left through the static field\nHands that learned to move before the mind could yield\nBody memory, no — body treaty\nThe thing she's in does what she tells it\nmost of the time\n\nHe's already on the left\ndidn't ask, doesn't explain\nmoral geometry, standing where the load comes in\nguilt that feels irrational\nis still real as rain\n\n***\n\n**[Pre-Chorus — electric piano clusters, blues bends entering]**\n\nMy mom said I was dramatic\nMy dad said I was overthinking\nSame ceiling, different words\nSame move to stop you speaking\n\nYou noticed something\nthey didn't want to deal with\nYou carried something\nthey called it a feeling\n\n***\n\n**[Chorus — full alloy, sax over riff, slap bass, tom fill]**\n\nBut Truth resolves\nTruth resonates\nThe world gets clearer\naround the things that stay\nThe riff comes down like a shutter closing\non everything we couldn't say\n\nTruth renders high\naround the ones who don't look away\nWe're still in it\nstill playing\nstill here\nstill in the fray\n\n***\n\n**[Verse 2 — resolution climbing, jazz harmony bleeding in]**\n\nShe says I don't remember\nwhen my body stopped being the problem\njust became the place I live\nthe contract I keep\nthe thing that holds the bottom\n\nHe says I used to think\nthe guilt was about specific things\nthen I realized it was a posture\nalways braced\nalways listening\nfor what the next wave brings\n\n***\n\n**[Pre-Chorus 2]**\n\nSame posture, different wound\nSame flinch before the motion\nWe learned it young\nwe wore it long\nwe're still learning\nwhat we're owed in\n\nYou carried something\nthey called it a problem\nYou built something\nthey called it a symptom\n\n***\n\n**[Chorus]**\n\nBut Truth resolves\nTruth resonates\nThe world gets clearer\naround the things that stay\nThe riff comes down like a shutter closing\non everything we couldn't say\n\nTruth renders high\naround the ones who don't look away\nWe're still in it\nstill playing\nstill here\nstill in the fray\n\n***\n\n**[Bridge — stripped to bass and piano, granular delay, the pocket held open]**\n\nThe horde keeps coming\nthe loot keeps dropping\nreceipts for every moment\nwe didn't stop\n\nThe wave resets\nthe sector clears\nthe amber marker\nglows ahead\n\nNeither of us moves yet\n\n*You want to keep going?*\n\n***\n\n**[Guitar and sax dialogue — no lyrics, just the instruments talking]**\n\n*blues bend answers the sax line*\n*sax finds the note between major and minor*\n*which is the most honest thing*\n*an instrument can do*\n\n***\n\n**[Final Chorus — everything additive, nothing removed]**\n\nTruth resolves\nTruth resonates\nThe world gets clearer\naround the things that stay\nThe riff comes down like a shutter closing\non all the weight we learned to name\n\nTruth renders high\naround the ones who chose to stay\nWe're still in it\nstill playing\nstill moving\ntoward the amber light\ntoday\n\n***\n\n**[Outro — bass locks back in, 170 BPM, swung triplet, vinyl crackle underneath]**\n\n*The counter resets*\n*She's already walking*\n*He's already left*\n*The world stays the same*\n\n*The resolution stays high*\n\n*They keep playing*", "tags" nil}, "title" "Transnational Void Stains"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "## Transnational Void Stains\n\n***\n\n**[Intro — bass only, vinyl crackle, single sax stab]**\n\n*The counter reads eight forty seven*\n*Nobody's reading the counter*\n\n***\n\n**[Verse 1]**\n\nShe cuts left through the static field\nHands that learned to move before the mind could yield\nBody memory, no — body treaty\nThe thing she's in does what she tells it\nmost of the time\n\nHe's already on the left\ndidn't ask, doesn't explain\nmoral geometry, standing where the load comes in\nguilt that feels irrational\nis still real 