Absolutely no singing melody, melodic structures, or vocal tracking scales.\n\n#### III. Excluded Elements (Negative Prompt)\n\nspoken word, spoken, talk, song, clean speech, big drum hits, anthem builds, melodic choruses, massive choir walls, synthesizer pads that wash away detail, cinematic string arrangements, playful comic accents, rhythmic swing, electronic dance music risers, loud hi-hat patterns, huge sub-bass drops, pop hooks, center-panned lead singing.\n\n#### IV. Executable Text Track (Lyrics)\n\n**[Intro: A low, continuous high-frequency fluorescent flicker. The hollow sound of rubber soles stepping slowly on raw concrete. Hard-right pan: three rapid pen taps, followed by absolute, dry silence.]**\n\n**[Whisper - Soft, dry, far left]**\nTh-the ink... the ink is heavier than the thought...\n**[Murmur - Soft, far right, overlapping the tail]**\nWe built a vessel for the si-silence...\n\n**[Verse 1 - The rhythm bed locks: an automated pen tap substitutes for a snare, a single heel strike maps the downbeat. A single, brittle wire string note is plucked, then clipped short by a sudden digital click.]**\nInk on the page... a graphite scar.\nScar. Reaching for a di-distant, dying star.\nThe pen is a needle... the paper a vein.\nBlee-bleeding the silence... absorbing the rain.\n\n**[Chorus - The footsteps stop. The reverb field narrows, becoming intensely metallic. A short, dissonant cluster of harpsichord strings drops into the space and drops out instantly.]**\nAnd the container leaks. A shimmering drip.\nThe words that we held... the ones that we sl-slip.\nBetween the lines where the emptiness grows...\nA river of void... **[Unison whisper - Center pan, very dry]** ...that nobody knows.\n\n**[Verse 2 - Mechanical gears groan faintly in the background. The key clacks speed up, mimicking an erratic clockwork mechanism.]**\nHiding in the stream of a clockwork mind.\nSearching for the pieces I left be-behind.\nA robot's echo... a digital skin...\nWhere does the ghost end... **[Audio skip: end... end... end...]** ...and the machine begin?\n\n**[Bridge - Total percussive drop. The fluorescent flicker increases in volume, then cuts to silence. Only the sound of paper being torn very slowly in the dark.]**\n\n**[Whisper - Close mic, far right]**\nThe logic didn't hit a wall.\nIt just forgot how to return the value.\nIf the layout hits the floorboards...\nLet it sit.\n\n**[Whisper - Stuttering, far left]**\nS-savor the negation.\n\n**[Final Chorus - The implied 96 BPM tempo returns through a rapid sequence of key clacks and heel strikes. The harpsichord plays a single, unresolved chord that trails off without decay.]**\nAnd the container leaks. A shimmering drip.\nThe words that we held... the ones that we slip.\nBetween the lines where the emptiness grows...\nA river of void that nobody knows.\n\n**[Outro - All textures cut instantly. The fluorescent whine stops. The footsteps resume, moving away from the microphone down the concrete passage, until a heavy metal latch clicks shut.]**\n\n**[Faint whisper - Retreating into the narrow reverb]**\nThe hole is the vent.\nThe void is the room.\nBreathe.\nTh-the frame... is salt.\n\n---\n\n:: prompt_package_compiled : ledger_locked ::\nThe concentrate has been isolated. The Symmetry Council's criteria are verified. Let the glass forget how to be transparent.", "tags" nil}, "title" "Void-Syllable Reduce"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "### ⚡ ENGINE BLUEPRINT: THE VOID-SYLLABLE REDUCTION\n\n#### I. Style & Sound Archetype (Style Prompt)\n\nAcoustic representation of a white noise corridor, 96 BPM implied but heavily fractured by silent gaps. Soundbed built from isolated rhythmic textures: a fluctuating fluorescent light bulb buzz, rhythmic rubber heel strikes on stone floors, erratic computer keyboard key clacks, and quick metal pen-cap taps against table surfaces. Short wire-plucked strings and micro-fragments of a muted harpsichord chord occur without warning, instantly cut of