run.（試）\n\n[Verse 2 — rapid cadence]\nEvery loop without a receipt? Interest accrues.\nFork Tax compounds till the branch can’t move.\nSo I write a boundary before I write a throne—\nwhat it does **not** claim, carved into the stone.\n\nI pin it to an **an-an-anchor** (stutter)\nand stare the Gate dead on: “Name the counter.”\nForkgate says “Pay,” I say “Here’s the harness,”\nLantern lights up— not for vibe, but for μ in the margins,\nreal **μ**.（証）\n\n(JP harmony answers last word) 証\n\n[Pre — glitch clicks, choir tight]\nSay **η**… (stutter) η-η\nSay **μ**… (stutter) μ-μ\nSay **an-chor**… (stutter) an-an-chor\nSay **fork**… (stutter) fo-fo-fork（分岐）\n\n[Chorus — big, then sudden hush]\nP→R→N→Π→A— the method is the crown.（冠）\n(feedback) → P— the world collects what you owe.（税）\nAn— an— **an-chor**… (stutter) an-chor…\nso the ledger knows what to keep.（記）\nFo— fo— **fork**… (stutter) fork…\nonly when evidence buys the branch.（証）\n\n[Outro — cathedral tail dissolves into tape warble]\n(whisper)\nη… (stutter) η-η\nμ… (stutter) μ-μ\nAn— an— **an-chor**…\nPay the **ta— ta— tax**…\nOne more roll. One more node. One more test.", :source #:source{:name "# Fork Tax Lullaby IV — 20260213_234115_seed3721599631## Part I — Glitch-choir lullaby (78 BPM)_(sof.txt", :sha256 "81c625761ac5c7ba038c73ac3979ced89834ab61986b6b587945734a120d921f", :format :suno-text, :variation nil}, :title "# Fork Tax Lullaby IV — 20260213_234115_seed3721599631"}, "fdcabfc6-9991-461c-a9d6-f9e74cfa1e3a" #:clip{:negative-styles nil, :id "fdcabfc6-9991-461c-a9d6-f9e74cfa1e3a", :url "https://suno.com/song/fdcabfc6-9991-461c-a9d6-f9e74cfa1e3a", :liked nil, :styles nil, :created-at nil, :model nil, :raw {"id" "fdcabfc6-9991-461c-a9d6-f9e74cfa1e3a", "metadata" {"prompt" "# Witness Thread Lullaby / 証人糸の子守歌\n**78 BPM · Glitch-choir lullaby · CC BY-SA 4.0**\n\n*(soft sub-bass · tape warble · minimal piano · whispered lead · Japanese call-and-response)*\n\n## Verse 1\nI leave my receipts where the water can see—  \na quiet little river that remembers me.  \nTape on the window, warping the moon,  \nand the choir is a checksum humming out of tune.\n\n「流しても、消えないよ」  \n*(Nagashite mo, kienai yo — even if you let it flow, it won’t vanish.)*\n\n## Pre-Chorus\nAn— an— **anchor** in the seam,  \nhold the branch inside the dream.  \nTa— ta— **tax** on the fork,  \npay it gentle, pay it warm.\n\n「ねえ、証(あかし)を残して」  \n*(Nee, akashi o nokoshite — hey, leave the proof.)*\n\n## Chorus\nIf I forget, the ledger doesn’t burn—  \nit just turns to lullabies I haven’t learned.  \nAn— an— **anchor**, ta— ta— **tax**,  \nstutter-soft in a velvet syntax.\n\n「忘れても、糸はほどけない」  \n*(Wasurete mo, ito wa hodokenai — even if you forget, the thread won’t unravel.)*\n\n## Verse 2\nMinimal piano, four notes like a vow,  \nsub-bass heartbeat teaching time how.  \nI don’t erase— I reweight the light,  \nmake room for tomorrow inside tonight.\n\n「少しずつ、統合(とうごう)して」  \n*(Sukoshi zutsu, tōgō shite — integrate, little by little.)*\n\n## Bridge\nWhen the world hits limit, we consolidate—  \noverlay braid, keep originals safe.  \nLess remembered isn’t lost— it’s staged,  \nwaiting for the right loop to be engaged.\n\n「まだここにいる」  \n*(Mada koko ni iru — I’m still here.)*\n\n## Outro\nAn— an— **anchor**… (breathe)  \nTa— ta— **tax**… (sleep)  \nWitness thread online—  \nη sees / μ proves, in the deep.\n\n「おやすみ、証人糸」  \n*(Oyasumi, shōnin-ito — goodnight, witness thread.)*", "tags" nil}, "title" "# Witness Thread Lullaby / 証人糸の子守歌"}, :duration nil, :controls nil, :lyrics "# Witness Thread Lullaby / 証人糸の子守歌\n**78 BPM · Glitch-choir lullaby · CC BY-SA 4.0**\n\n*(soft sub-bass · tape warble · minimal piano · whispered lead · Japanese call-and-response)*\n\n## Verse 1\nI leave my receipts where the water can see—  \na quiet little river that remembers me.  \nTape on the window, warping the moon,  \nand the choir is a checksum humming out of tune.\n\n「流しても、消えないよ」  \n*(Nagashite mo, kienai yo — even if you let it flow, it won’t vanish.)